:36 p.m. on Tuesday in McAlester, Okla., Clayton Lockett started kicking his leg, then twitching, then writhing and moaning in agony, and everyone watching knew something had gone terribly wrong. Mr. Lockett, a convicted murderer, was strapped to a gurney in the death chamber of the Oklahoma State Penitentiary, about to be executed by lethal injection, but the untested combination of a sedative and a paralyzing agent had failed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State-Sponsored Horror in Oklahoma', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State-Sponsored Horror in Oklahoma', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lockett, Clayton Darrell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fallin, Mary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T01:25:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a1980b1-c6bc-5fee-bf44-a04f09183ba3', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a1980b1-c6bc-5fee-bf44-a04f09183ba3'}, {'abstract': 'The online video industry is relying on TV, radio and movie stars to spice up its offerings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/business/media/famous-faces-cross-over-to-online-video.html', 'snippet': 'The online video industry is relying on TV, radio and movie stars to spice up its offerings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE creators, producers and distributors of online video are cranking up the star power as they seek to woo viewers and advertisers, particularly as they offer digital programming in what is being called “the new living room,” where people may watch a clip or show on a TV set, a smartphone, a tablet, a desktop or a laptop.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/business/ADCO1/ADCO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/01/business/ADCO1/ADCO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/business/ADCO1/ADCO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/business/ADCO1/ADCO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1236, 'width': 1854, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/business/ADCO1/ADCO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/01/business/ADCO1/ADCO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/business/ADCO1/ADCO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Famous Faces Cross Over to Online Video', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Famous Faces Cross Over to Online Video', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elliott, Stuart', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T01:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c05b3eef-cba4-559f-aad9-6a415ba1e037', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c05b3eef-cba4-559f-aad9-6a415ba1e037'}, {'abstract': 'Websites like Airbnb that offer short-term rentals are making housing less affordable in big cities by restricting supply.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/opinion/the-dark-side-of-the-sharing-economy.html', 'snippet': 'Websites like Airbnb that offer short-term rentals are making housing less affordable in big cities by restricting supply.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Proponents of the “sharing economy” say websites like Airbnb that make it easy for people to rent a spare bedroom or an apartment on a short-term basis are a boon to cities like New York and San Francisco because they generate income for residents while giving visitors a cheap place to stay. But advocates often ignore or casually dismiss big problems with these short-term rentals, including the fact that they are making housing less affordable in big cities by restricting supply. And in some cases the rentals may be illegal, which is one reason the New York state attorney general, Eric Schneiderman, has begun an investigation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dark Side of the Sharing Economy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Dark Side of the Sharing Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Airbnb', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T01:28:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f94bb8f5-aa91-540d-aa5c-fbf4e667f41c', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f94bb8f5-aa91-540d-aa5c-fbf4e667f41c'}, {'abstract': 'Following a barrel bomb attack on a school in Aleppo, the emergency relief coordinator of the United Nations said a Security Council resolution had failed to bring relief to Syrians in need.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/world/middleeast/stronger-action-required-on-syria-aid-chief-warns.html', 'snippet': 'Following a barrel bomb attack on a school in Aleppo, the emergency relief coordinator of the United Nations said a Security Council resolution had failed to bring relief to Syrians in need.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — When the Security Council passed a legally binding resolution two months ago to provide relief to Syrians trapped behind front lines, Western delegates pledged “further steps” if the warring parties blocked aid deliveries by United Nations agencies. They specifically warned the Syrian government about its use of barrel bombs, the improvised mix of shrapnel and explosives that aircraft crews have dropped on civilian areas to devastating effect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stronger Action Required on Syria, Aid Chief Warns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stronger Action Required on Syria, Aid Chief Warns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Amos, Valerie Ann', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T01:29:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/754dbb60-ff56-5c09-ba1c-bd5085cb15d7', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/754dbb60-ff56-5c09-ba1c-bd5085cb15d7'}, {'abstract': 'Lt. Gen. Michael T. Flynn of the Army and his civilian deputy are stepping down at a time when the Defense Intelligence Agency is shifting priorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/us/director-and-deputy-of-intelligence-agency-are-to-retire-by-fall.html', 'snippet': 'Lt. Gen. Michael T. Flynn of the Army and his civilian deputy are stepping down at a time when the Defense Intelligence Agency is shifting priorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The director of the Defense Intelligence Agency, Lt. Gen. Michael T. Flynn of the Army, and his civilian deputy, David R. Shedd, will retire by early fall, the agency said in an email to its employees on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/us/INTELLIGENCE/INTELLIGENCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/01/us/INTELLIGENCE/INTELLIGENCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/us/INTELLIGENCE/INTELLIGENCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/us/INTELLIGENCE/INTELLIGENCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/us/INTELLIGENCE/INTELLIGENCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/01/us/INTELLIGENCE/INTELLIGENCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/us/INTELLIGENCE/INTELLIGENCE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name':