ite artists and songs in this first-time awards ceremony, broadcast live from the Shrine Auditorium in Los Angeles. Nominees include Imagine Dragons (above), Justin Timberlake, Macklemore & Ryan Lewis, Maroon 5 and Rihanna for artist of the year; Florida Georgia Line, Icona Pop, Imagine Dragons, Lorde, Macklemore & Ryan Lewis, and Passenger for best new artist; and, in the most voted-on category, “Holy Grail” and “Suit & Tie,” both by Jay Z and Mr. Timberlake; “Stay,” by Rihanna and Mikky Ekko; “The Monster,” by Eminem and Rihanna; and “Timber,” by Pitbull and Kesha, for best collaboration. Blake Shelton, Drake, Kendrick Lamar, Pharrell Williams, Pitbull, Shakira, Thirty Seconds to Mars, Luke Bryan, Arcade Fire, Ed Sheeran and Ariana Grande will perform at the auditorium and in locations around Los Angeles, including the Roxy and the Hotel Cafe. Red-carpet coverage begins at 7 on E!', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T05:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb9f7790-cd9c-55bf-9a96-b2b8b183d81d', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb9f7790-cd9c-55bf-9a96-b2b8b183d81d'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor of Toronto quietly exited his home and entered rehab after a video surfaced that appeared to show him smoking crack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/world/americas/toronto-mayor-takes-leave.html', 'snippet': 'The mayor of Toronto q