p-o/', 'snippet': 'Chatter ahead of Alibaba’s I.P.O. | A look at why only one top banker has gone to jail after the financial crisis. | A federal regulator says banks erred on troubled mortgages. | Facebook changes its rules for log-ins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Alibaba Group, the Chinese Internet giant that is about to go public in the United States, is said to be in talks with its Alipay payment affiliate about regaining a stake in the business, Michael J. de la Merced writes in DealBook. The two sides have been in talks for nearly a year and a half, and no agreement is imminent. In any case, the possibility that Alibaba could be formally reunited with its payment division would be of great interest to the company’s future shareholders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Awaiting Alibaba’s I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T12:19:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a454d977-aab5-50d7-acef-7bb65992c0fc', 'word_count': 2006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a454d977-aab5-50d7-acef-7bb65992c0fc'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A U.P.S. delivery clerk explained the options to a customer whose package to London had been turned away.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/a-royal-rejection/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A U.P.S. delivery clerk explained the options to a customer whose package to London had been turned away.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Royal Rejection', 'kicker': 'Ci