mbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Woman’s Wish List Against Street Harassment', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T14:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a09ac34-bfc0-5c06-8565-2e7b8f5e61c0', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a09ac34-bfc0-5c06-8565-2e7b8f5e61c0'}, {'abstract': 'Plenty of parents don’t manage to set aside money, but that doesn’t mean their children will be shut out of degrees from great schools.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/eight-tips-for-parents-who-have-saved-nothing-for-college/', 'snippet': 'Plenty of parents don’t manage to set aside money, but that doesn’t mean their children will be shut out of degrees from great schools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of days ago, a post here by a mother in Maine lamenting her lack of savings for her son’s college education inspired an outpouring of comments. A number of people questioned her and her husband’s decision to raise six children. Others thought she might have been better off putting money aside years ago instead of paying for music lessons and sports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/30/us/motherlode-berklee/motherlode-berklee-articleLarge.png', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/04/30/us/motherlode-berklee/motherlode-berklee-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth