ould buy the British television group Channel 5 Broadcasting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Viacom, the media powerhouse that includes the movie studio Paramount and cable television channels like MTV, Comedy Central and Nickelodeon, generated $502 million in profit for its latest fiscal quarter, driven by increased advertising and higher affiliate fees for its television outlets, the company reported on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Television Revenue Helps Profit at Viacom to Rise 4%', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television Revenue Helps Profit at Viacom to Rise 4%', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Viacom Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Channel 5', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paramount Pictures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dauman, Philippe P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T14:45:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edca1216-784e-563f-ab57-a4d98de66ed5', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edca1216-784e-563f-ab57-a4d98de66ed5'}, {'abstract': 'A video documents the transformation of the decommissioned St. Agnes church into a nexus of contemporary art and culture.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/st-agnes-church-berlin-germany-now-art-gallery-space/', 'snippet': 'A video documents the transformation of the decommissioned St. Agnes church into a nexus of contemporary art and culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the 32-year-old German gallerist Johann König, art is religion.\xa0His father, Kasper, is one of the most respected curators in Europe; his mother, Ilke, and uncle, Walter, are leaders in art-book publishing and his older half-brother, Leo, is a noted Manhattan art dealer.\xa0And so, when several years ago, the architect Arno Brandlhuber approached König with the idea of leasing a decommissioned Catholic church called St. Agnes — a striking example of Brutalist architecture in the Berlin neighborhood of Kreuzberg — König signed a nearly century-long lease, despite the fact that the building (which included a nursery school, offices and a courtyard along with the church itself) was too big for his gallery alone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Matters | A Decommissioned Catholic Church in Berlin is Reborn as a Hub of Creativity', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Churches (Buildings)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T15:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gisela Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gisela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d934e26e-c898-5d64-b466-e5b047d64da3', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d934e26e-c898-5d64-b466-e5b047d64da3'}, {'abstract': 'This Poetry Pairing features “Sweeping the States” by 