aragraph': 'TIMES INSIDER — Welcome to the May 2014 Times Premier Puzzle Pack. This month, we’re celebrating the arrival of spring.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Has Sprung', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T16:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60629269-afab-5ea8-a899-bc21717c5222', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60629269-afab-5ea8-a899-bc21717c5222'}, {'abstract': 'Neither doctors nor medical students can solve a patient’s financial problems on the spot. Yet any one of us can be the first to detect a problem.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/doctors-not-asking-about-money/', 'snippet': 'Neither doctors nor medical students can solve a patient’s financial problems on the spot. Yet any one of us can be the first to detect a problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the doorway, my patient looked pregnant — but his protuberant belly was actually a sign of serious liver disease that had quickly worsened. Given the fluid pressing on his abdomen, he was no doubt in pain. Yet his spirits were high, and raucous laughter often accompanied his nearly toothless smile.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/10/health/10well_bond/10well_bond-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/