ub_date': '2014-05-01T19:22:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Hughes and Neil Unmack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Unmack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52ca2e11-1743-57fa-855b-982be2cccef9', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52ca2e11-1743-57fa-855b-982be2cccef9'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Rosenthal helped bring the 20th century to the National Gallery of Art in Washington and the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/arts/nan-rosenthal-curator-who-championed-modern-art-dies-at-76.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Rosenthal helped bring the 20th century to the National Gallery of Art in Washington and the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nan Rosenthal, a curator who helped bring the 20th century to the National Gallery of Art in Washington and the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York, died on Sunday at her home in Manhattan. She was 76.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/rosenthalobit/rosenthalobit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/rosenthalobit/rosenthalobit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 614}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/rosenthalobit/rosenthalobit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/rosenthalobit/rosenthalobit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/rosenthalobit/rosenthalobit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/rosenthalobit/rosenthalobit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/rosenthalobit/rosenthalobit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nan Rosenthal, Curator Who Championed Modern Art, Dies at 76', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nan Rosenthal, 76, Advocate of 20th-Century Artworks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenthal, Nan (1937-2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Margalit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Gallery of Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T19:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ccdeea8-b2a3-55ad-8174-b735ac380a51', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ccdeea8-b2a3-55ad-8174-b735ac380a51'}, {'abstract': 'Venture off the eastern coast of Tanzania to stroll through historic Stone Town, listen to a celebrated local music genre and sample one of Zanzibar’s spectacular beaches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/travel/36-hours-in-zanzibar-tanzania.html', 'snippet': 'Venture off the eastern coast of Tanzania to stroll through historic Stone Town, listen to a celebrated local music genre and sample one of Zanzibar’s spectacular beaches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The name Zanzibar conjures up visions of sultans’ palaces, paradisiacal beaches and winding alleyways leading to spice-filled bazaars. Indeed, this coral archipelago in the Indian Ocean, 23 miles off the eastern coast of Tanzania, still has many of the features that it did when it was an important trading center and its historic Stone Town served as the capital of an Omani sultanate. Zanzibar’s largest island, Unguja, is home to most of the cultural attractions, many of them found in beguiling Stone Town, which was awarded Unesco World Heritage status in 2000. In recent years, there’s been a concerted effort to restore and give new life to the city’s distinctive structures. Palaces have been turned into museums and cultural centers, and grand Swahili mansions have been reborn as restaurants and boutique hotels. Yet the coast still offers the “delicious view” that the explorer Sir Richard Burton recorded, of a “cocoa-fringed shore of purest white, and the sea blue as a slab of lapis lazuli.” (Note: Prices in Zanzibar are routinely quoted in dollars — alongside, or occasionally instead of, the island’s official currency, the Tanzanian shilling.)', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/travel/04-hours-span-sf/04-hours-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/travel/04-hours-span-sf/04-hours-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 538}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/travel/04-hours-span-sf/04-hours-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/travel/04-hours-span-sf/04-hours-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1836, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/travel/04-hours-span-sf/04-hours-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/04/travel/04-hours-span-sf/04-hours-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/travel/04-hours-span-sf/04-hours-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Zanzibar, Tanzania', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Zanzibar, Tanzania', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doyle, Rachel B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zanzibar (Tanzania)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T19:34:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel B. Doyle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c082d1c5-db1d-54ac-ba56-112cf47e718d', 'word_count': 1450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c082d1c5-db1d-54ac-ba56-112cf47e718d'}, {'abstract': 'The Municipal Art Society is offering more than 100 free walking tours across the five boroughs on Saturday and Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/arts/design/walking-tours-in-the-spirit-of-jane-jacobs.html', 'snippet': 'The Municipal Art Society is offering more than 100 free walking tours across the five boroughs on Saturday and Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jane Jacobs’s 1961 book, “The Death and Life of Great American Cities,” a sweeping critique of the modern metropolis, was both a best seller and quite contentious. What set Jacobs apart from many of her critics, including her archnemesis Robert Moses, was that as lofty as her ideas and prose could be, they sprang from, and remained rooted in, the street. So it’s easy to imagine her feeling honored to have inspired Jane’s Walk, an annual series of free guided walking tours across all five boroughs, organized by the Municipal Art Society of New York.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02MISER/MISER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02MISER/MISER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur