Joan Robinson get into this discussion?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/hangups-of-the-heterodox-vaguely-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'How did Joan Robinson get into this discussion?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Palley and Simon Wren-Lewis have been having a back and forth over heterodox economics versus garden-variety saltwater economics, and their role in making sense of the economic crisis. Palley accuses Wren-Lewis and me of “flimflam”; Wren-Lewis wonders what he’s talking about.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hangups of the Heterodox (Vaguely Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T19:41:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/572864a3-6848-5644-b739-62baee5625a8', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/572864a3-6848-5644-b739-62baee5625a8'}, {'abstract': 'Tickets for the Yankees’ first 13 home games were up nearly 10 percent from last year, and ratings on YES were up 38 percent. Mets’ ticket sales were up, too, but their TV ratings were down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/sports/baseball/yankees-attendance-and-ratings-rebound-but-mets-are-mixed.html', 'snippet': 'Tickets for the Yankees’ first 13 home games were up nearly 10 percent from last year, and ratings on YES were up 38 percent. Mets’ ticket sales were up, too, but their TV ratings were down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees, built on winning and the star system, are benefiting from the return of Derek Jeter and the addition of Masahiro Tanaka and Jacoby Ellsbury.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees’ Attendance and Ratings Rebound, but the Mets’ Are Mixed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees’ Attendance and Ratings Rebound, but the Mets’ Are Mixed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SNY Network', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YES Network', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T19:42:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d359e7e7-e5ea-5375-9182-5114212ff44c', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d359e7e7-e5ea-5375-9182-5114212ff44c'}, {'abstract': 'Hairstyle rules seemed to imply that the Army preferred chemically straightened hair for black women.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/eurocentric-beauty-ideals-in-the-military/', 'snippet': 'Hairstyle rules seemed to imply that the Army preferred chemically straightened hair for black women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People of African descent have been tyrannized for centuries by a Eurocentric aesthetic that deems light skin and straight hair beautiful and that casts dark skin, African features and kinky hair as undesirable, if not ugly. This bias is less potent than it was, say, 50 years ago. (Movies, advertisements and prime-time television clearly show that.) But it still weighs heavily in judgments about what is beautiful\xa0 and what is not; it also limits the opportunities of people whose appearances place them far from the Eurocentric ideal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eurocentric Beauty Ideals in the Military', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty (Concept)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T19:44:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/986d5402-b810-5d2e-a3a2-cd47753d2f58', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/986d5402-b810-5d2e-a3a2-cd47753d2f58'}, {'abstract': 'Chevrolet introduces a police version of its Silverado pickup; the federal government says it lost $11.2 billion in bailing out General Motors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/automobiles/wheelies-the-police-truck-edition.html', 'snippet': 'Chevrolet introduces a police version of its Silverado pickup; the federal government says it lost $11.2 billion in bailing out General Motors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A roundup of motoring news from the web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge'