_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/32197e10-5211-53aa-9f7d-1d66d14fa76e'}, {'abstract': 'The rentier class, the minimum wage, and different paths to helping the working class.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/donald-sterling-and-the-inequality-debate/', 'snippet': 'The rentier class, the minimum wage, and different paths to helping the working class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turning from the controversies of Roman Catholicism back to the ongoing inequality conversation, I highly recommend this post from Reihan Salam\xa0on Donald Sterling, the disgraced owner of the Los Angeles Clippers, and the interesting ways that Sterling’s career as a Southern Californian slumlord is entangled both with the phenomenon of “petits rentiers” (Thomas Piketty’s term for the capital-accumulating mass upper class) and with America’s ongoing debates (which Piketty’s “Capital” seems to have\xa0gotten a bit wrong) over whether and how high to raise the minimum wage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Sterling and the Inequality Debate', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piketty, Thomas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salam, Reihan', 'rank': 10, '