.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/our-bookshelves-on-display/', 'snippet': 'Here are a few of our bookshelves, with brief descriptions of their organizational principles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the magazine’s most recent Riff,\xa0Mireille Silcoff notes that although e-books are outselling their physical counterparts on Amazon, the latter still remain objects of desire for the average consumer — just not for the reasons you might think.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/magazine/BooksAmy/BooksAmy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/01/magazine/BooksAmy/BooksAmy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/magazine/BooksAmy/BooksAmy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/magazine/BooksAmy/BooksAmy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/magazine/BooksAmy/BooksAmy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/01/magazine/BooksAmy/BooksAmy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/magazine/BooksAmy/BooksAmy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Way to Organize Bookshelves?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T20:26:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannie Choi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Choi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25b7226f-85f2-52fb-8bea-82fd0d057087', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25b7226f-85f2-52fb-8bea-82fd0d057087'}, {'abstract': 'A new edition of Fitzgerald’s story collection “Taps at Reveille” includes versions that hew more closely to the author’s original typescripts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/f-scott-fitzgerald-uncut-in-a-new-edition-of-short-stories/', 'snippet': 'A new edition of Fitzgerald’s story collection “Taps at Reveille” includes versions that hew more closely to the author’s original typescripts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When “Taps at Reveille” was published in 1935, it marked the end of F. Scott Fitzgerald’s career as a short-story writer. It was his fourth collection and his last. Now, it turns out, a lot of the words were missing, excised by editors at The Saturday Evening Post, where all 18 stories in the collection first appeared.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/01/arts/01artsbeat-fitz/01artsbeat-fitz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/01/arts/01artsbeat-fitz/01artsbeat-fitz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 830}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption':