/279f119a-7fb5-5bed-9263-bb2f3b6900d9'}, {'abstract': 'Beyond renowned landmarks like the Chrysler Building, New York offers a dizzying array of Art Deco-style night spots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/arts/design/a-sampling-of-20s-and-30s-style-bars-clubs-and-restaurants.html', 'snippet': 'Beyond renowned landmarks like the Chrysler Building, New York offers a dizzying array of Art Deco-style night spots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NIGHT and day, New York reveals itself as the Art Deco capital of the world. I don’t mean just the obvious treasures — the Chrysler Building, Radio City Music Hall, Rockefeller Center — but the Deco surprises that decorate just about every other block.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1004, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 1331, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2/20140502-ARTDECO-slide-MWJ2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Password Is Deco', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where the Password Is Deco', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ART DECO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Twenties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T22:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Stapinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stapinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a07ba5c-77db-5e2c-9589-3e9d2f8dedfe', 'word_count': 2880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a07ba5c-77db-5e2c-9589-3e9d2f8dedfe'}, {'abstract': 'Hildreth Meière is not exactly a household name, but her Art Deco mosaics and murals live on landmarks in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/arts/design/hildreth-meiere-the-forgotten-art-deco-artist.html', 'snippet': 'Hildreth Meière is not exactly a household name, but her Art Deco mosaics and murals live on landmarks in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOW many worshipers, at the 1920s Temple Emanu-El in Manhattan, or St. Bartholomew’s Church, the Episcopal bastion nearby, realize — if they notice them at all — that the intricate mosaic ornamentations in these contrasting houses of faith were produced by a singular vision? The same sensibility distinguishes an altar in St. Patrick’s Cathedral, and the glistening red mosaic walls at One Wall Street, which turn to orange the higher they go. If audiences dashing to Radio City Music Hall tilted their heads back, they would suddenly be struck by brightly colored figurative roundels on the 50th Street facade. From one coast to the other are many more instances of the same artist’s remarkable decorative work, forgotten in plain sight.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If These Walls Could Speak, They’d Say Her Name', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If These Walls Could Speak, They’d Say Her Name', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ART DECO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meiere, Hildreth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Temple Emanu-el', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St Bartholomew's Church (Manhattan, NY)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio City Music Hall', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T22:02:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Celia McGee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Celia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33022a49-48c4-5c0a-8a23-f55dbb9bc394', 'word_count': 1418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33022a49-48c4-5c0a-8a23-f55dbb9bc394'}, {'abstract': 'Howard Norman’s novel “Next Life Might Be Kinder” is about a man whose dead wife talks to him, makes love with him, arranges books and takes dance lessons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/books/howard-normans-novel-next-life-might-be-kinder.html', 'snippet': 'Howard Norman’s novel “Next Life Might Be Kinder” is about a man whose dead wife talks to him, makes love with him, arranges books and takes dance lessons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The premise of Howard Norman’s new novel is eerie enough to make the skin crawl. “Next Life Might Be Kinder” is narrated by a blocked, troubled writer named Sam Lattimore, who delivers an opening sentence worthy of the Noir Hall of Fame. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02BOOKNORMAN/BOOKNORMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 963, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02BOOKNORMAN/BOOKNORMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 963}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02BOOKNORMAN/BOOKNORMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 639, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02BOOKNORMAN/BOOKNORMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1614, 'width': 1006, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02BOOKNORMAN/02BOOKNORMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02BOOKNORMAN/02BOOKNORMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02BOOKNORMAN/02BOOKNORMAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Ghosts Have Hobbies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Ghosts Have Hobbies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norman, Howard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T22:03:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/86a91c92-d098-5005-b6c6-59f4b6d5fbdc', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86a91c92-d098-5005-b6c6-59f4b6d5fbdc'}, {'abstract': 'A critical guide to performances of classical music in the New York City area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/arts/music/opera-classical-music-listings-for-may-2-8.html', 'snippet': 'A critical guide to performances of classical music in the New York City area.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Full reviews of recent classical performances: nytimes.com/classical. A searchable guide to these and other performances is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opera & Classical Music Listings for May 2-8', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Classical', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-01T22:04:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/74cfe71c-787e-5e9e-a2e6-7d4fb4f6da1b', 'word_count': 1727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74cfe71c-787e-5e9e-a2e6-7d4fb4f6da1b'}, {'abstract': '“Belle” is a period film in the Merchant-Ivory style about a biracial woman raised as part of a lord and lady’s family in 18th-century England.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/movies/belle-centers-on-a-biracial-aristocrat-in-the-18th-century.html', 'snippet': '“Belle” is a period film in the Merchant-Ivory style about a biracial woman raised as part of a lord and lady’s family in 18th-century England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No bodices seem to have been harmed, much less ripped, during the making of “Belle,” a period film at once sweeping and intimate, about an 18th-century Englishwoman who transcends her historical moment. Even so, peekaboo bosoms tremble throughout the movie amid the rustle of luxurious gowns and the gasps of polite company as conventions are crushed underfoot. Melodramatic and grounded in history, “Belle” is enough of an old-fashioned entertainment that it could have been made in classic Hollywood. Well, except for one little thing that would have probably given old studio suits apoplexy: The movie’s prettily flouncing title character is biracial. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02JUMPBELLE/JUMPBELLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02JUMPBELLE/JUMPBELLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02JUMPBELLE/JUMPBELLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02JUMPBELLE/JUMPBELLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1061, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02JUMPBELLE/02JUMPBELLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02JUMPBELLE/02JUMPBELLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02JUMPBELLE/02JUMPBELLE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To the Manner Born?', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To the Manner Born?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mbatha-Raw, Gugu', 'rank': 2, 'ma