anyone who still associates Austrian cinema with Michael Haneke’s dour, stringent visions, “Blood Glacier,” from the Vienna-born filmmaker Marvin Kren, presents a rousing alternative, complete with giant flying insects. In Mr. Kren’s enjoyably committed and splattery creature feature, scientists and visitors at an Alpine weather station fend off mutant beasts that materialize after the discovery of a sprawling, rust-colored hunk of ice.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_BLOOD_SPAN/02RDP_ALTERED_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_BLOOD_SPAN/02RDP_ALTERED_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_BLOOD_SPAN/02RDP_ALTERED_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_BLOOD_SPAN/02RDP_ALTERED_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1149, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_BLOOD_SPAN/02RDP_ALTERED_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_BLOOD_SPAN/02RDP_ALTERED_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_BLOOD_SPAN/02RDP_ALTERED_SPAN-thu