raph': 'The flashier of the two stories in “Unclaimed,” Michael Jorgensen’s intensely moving documentary, is about a man claiming to be a long-missing Vietnam War veteran. Quietly shadowing this central identity quest, however, is a less attention-grabbing but perhaps even more compelling tale of how one man from a broken home finds peace and purpose in reconstructing the home of another.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_UNCLAIMED/02RDP_UNCLAIMED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_UNCLAIMED/02RDP_UNCLAIMED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_UNCLAIMED/02RDP_UNCLAIMED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_UNCLAIMED/02RDP_UNCLAIMED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1153, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_UNCLAIMED/02RDP_UNCLAIMED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_UNCLAIMED/02RDP_UNCLAIMED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/arts/02RDP_UNCLAIMED/02RDP_UNCLAIMED-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_na