bia, and rescuers were searching for other miners believed to be missing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/world/americas/at-least-3-die-in-collapse-of-gold-mine.html', 'snippet': 'The collapse of the illegal gold mine occurred late Wednesday night in western Colombia, and rescuers were searching for other miners believed to be missing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — At least three people were killed in the collapse of an illegal gold mine in western Colombia, and rescuers were searching for other miners believed to be missing, officials said on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Least 3 Die in Collapse of Gold Mine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Least 3 Die in Collapse of Gold Mine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T01:13:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32e83ee7-342a-53ca-9460-c38aeaef0092', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32e83ee7-342a-53ca-9460-c38aeaef0092'}, {'abstract': 'Alan Rothenberg, a longtime sports lawyer who has known Donald Sterling for decades, said, “He’ll fight as hard as he can legally.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/sports/basketball/little-recourse-for-sterling.html', 'snippet': 'Alan Rothenberg, a longtime sports lawyer who has known Donald Sterling for decades, said, “He’ll fight as hard as he can legally.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'N.B.A. Commissioner Adam Silver handed down a lifetime ban to the Los Angeles Clippers owner Donald Sterling this week for racist comments he made during a recorded conversation. Silver also vowed he would force Sterling to sell the team and fined him $2.5 million. No one knows quite where it will lead. As Alan Rothenberg, a longtime sports lawyer who has known Sterling for decades said, “Donald is hugely litigious.” He added, “He’ll fight as hard as can legally.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Little Recourse for Sterling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Little Recourse for Sterling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sterling, Donald', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Adam (1962- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T01:16:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fcd22c9-79ad-59fb-812b-d7f5e8f54011', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fcd22c9-79ad-59fb-812b-d7f5e8f54011'}, {'abstract': 'The dangers of nuclear power are real, but policy makers should not be spooked into shutting down a vital source of clean energy in a warming world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/opinion/the-right-lessons-from-chernobyl.html', 'snippet': 'The dangers of nuclear power are real, but policy makers should not be spooked into shutting down a vital source of clean energy in a warming world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty-eight years after Unit 4 at the Chernobyl power plant in what was then Soviet Ukraine erupted into a volcano of radioactivity, its name has become synonymous with the nightmarish side of nuclear power. It is also the site today of an extraordinary international project, the construction of a vast steel shield to cover the leaky concrete ‘‘sarcophagus’’ in which the highly radioactive remains of the reactor are to be entombed for at least 100 years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Right Lessons From Chernobyl', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Right Lessons From Chernobyl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chernobyl (Ukraine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T01:16:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e06a76a-67fe-5b7c-b9ab-218080202b66', 'wo