la-worthy-looks.html', 'snippet': 'On the occasion of the forthcoming “Charles James: Beyond Fashion” show at the Metropolitan Museum of Art’s new Anna Wintour Costume Center, T rounds up midcentury glam designs reminiscent of the designer’s own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next week, the Metropolitan Museum of Art reopens the doors to its Costume Institute, now dubbed the Anna Wintour Costume Center, with a show dedicated to the works of the Anglo-American couturier Charles James. The inaugural exhibition, “Charles James: Beyond Fashion,” will of course inform the dress code for the fashion flock attending the opening gala on Monday evening — the designer’s classic style (think: society balls and Hollywood starlets) marking a complete departure from last year’s garbage-bag gowns and safety-pin-fastened concert tees for the “Punk: Chaos to Couture” event. In anticipation of one of fashion’s biggest nights of the year, we’ve curated some modern black-tie-appropriate designs that nod to the midcentury glamour that James helped define. In case your golden ticket got lost in the mail, now’s as good a time as any to make Monday evening plans worthy of floral-printed opera gloves and statement diamond earrings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/t-magazine/02market-gilchrist/02market-gilchrist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/t-magazine/02market-gilchrist/02market-gilchrist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/t-magazine/02market-gilchrist/02market-gilchrist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 