rticle', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Felisko', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Felisko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e6452e0-3f2c-5632-a0a1-1dbb987c740c', 'word_count': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e6452e0-3f2c-5632-a0a1-1dbb987c740c'}, {'abstract': 'Now that China is planning to loosen its animal testing requirement, a government training program in alternative testing methods is so popular it has had to turn away applicants.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/interest-grows-in-animal-testing-alternatives/', 'snippet': 'Now that China is planning to loosen its animal testing requirement, a government training program in alternative testing methods is so popular it has had to turn away applicants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With China planning to relax its requirement that cosmetics and other personal care products be tested on animals before they can go to market, a government training program in alternative testing methods is suddenly so popular it has had to turn away applicants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Interest Grows in Animal Testing Alternatives', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Product Tests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Avon Products Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Humane Society International', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute for In Vitro Sciences', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangdong Province (China)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangzhou (China)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T04:21:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaojie Huang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaojie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/885f8a3d-72a6-5312-b2f7-645a4b82cfaa', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/885f8a3d-72a6-5312-b2f7-645a4b82cfaa'}, {'abstract': 'New commercial satellite imagery shows that North Korea is expanding its main rocket-launching site and testing engines of what is believed to be its first road-mobile intercontinental ballistic missile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/world/asia/north-korea-activity-at-a-missile-site.html', 'snippet': 'New commercial satellite imagery shows that North Korea is expanding its main rocket-launching site and testing engines of what is believed to be its first road-mobile intercontinental ballistic missile.', 'lead_paragraph': ' New commercial satellite imagery shows that North Korea is expanding its main rocket-launching site and testing engines of what is believed to be its first road-mobile intercontinental ballistic missile, a website specializing in the North said Thursday. The reported activities at the Sohae Satellite Launching Station in Tongchang-ri near North Korea’s western border with China come amid fears that the North may be preparing for another nuclear test. In recent days, more activity has been reported at an underground nuclear test site in Punggye-ri in northeastern North Korea. The website, 38 North, which is run by the U.S.-Korea Institute at Johns Hopkins University, said its analysis of satellite images of Tongchang-ri showed that North Korea conducted “one and maybe more engine tests of what is probably the first stage of a KN-08 road-mobile intercontinental ballistic missile” in late March to early April. “With this latest activity, three KN-08 rocket engine test series have been identified for the first and possibly second stages dating back to mid-2013,” the website said. “As this effort progresses, the next technically logical step in the missile’s development would be a flight test of the entire system.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea: Activity at a Missile Site', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea: Activity at a Missile Site', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Satellites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'US-Korea Institute', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T04:22:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/39f3d64a-f208-5736-a1a3-64ceeb8880fd', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39f3d64a-f208-5736-a1a3-64ceeb8880fd'}, {'abstract': 'Reasons to visit Brooklyn’s Homecrest include a house that doubles as a shrine to the opera icon Enrico Caruso, and the restaurant Pirosmani.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/nyregion/pagliacci-by-appointment-only.html', 'snippet': 'Reasons to visit Brooklyn’s Homecrest include a house that doubles as a shrine to the opera icon Enrico Caruso, and the restaurant Pirosmani.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Italian heritage of Brooklyn’s Homecrest is evinced by the Virgin Mary statuettes on the block that is home to the Enrico Caruso Museum of America. A tidy house at 1942 East 19th Street, owned by Aldo Mancusi since 1956, doubles as a shrine to the opera icon. “A hobby gone crazy,” Mr. Mancusi said, his silver mustache as neatly pruned as the yard’s hedges.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04REASONDS1/04REASONDS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04REASONDS1/04REASONDS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04REASONDS1/04REASONDS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04REASONDS1/04REASONDS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1318, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04REASONDS1/04REASONDS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'lega