e died, two of them believed to have been the attackers, who also set off an explosive device. The one suspect the police identified, a 39-year-old man, has a name that suggests he belonged to the Uighur ethnic group, once the dominant people in Xinjiang, who after decades of migration by ethnic Han Chinese are now a minority.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/world/02sino-Xinjiang/02sino-Xinjiang-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/world/02sino-Xinjiang/02sino-Xinjiang-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/world/02sino-Xinjiang/02sino-Xinjiang-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/world/02sino-Xinjiang/02sino-Xinjiang-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/world/02sino-Xinjiang/02sino-Xinjiang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/02/world/02sino-Xinjiang/02sino-Xinjiang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/world/02sino-Xinjiang/02sino-Xinjiang-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q & A: Nicholas Bequelin on Why Tensions Are Rising in Xinjiang and Beyond', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Han Chinese (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indigenous People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tohti, Ilham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashgar (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kunming (China)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tiananmen Square (Beijing)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Urumqi (China)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T13:07:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Forsythe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Forsythe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e8213ef-ca75-551c-8b33-7f20c3aaf295', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e8213ef-ca75-551c-8b33-7f20c3aaf295'}, {'abstract': 'At first glance, the new reading on the nation’s employment situation is shout-from-the-roof-tops, pop-the-Champagne fantastic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/03/upshot/jobs-report-looks-great-but-looks-are-deceiving.ht