': 'nyt://article/85871657-61a5-58b5-8685-753c08235452'}, {'abstract': 'While official figures show scant economic growth, a confidence survey seems to show enthusiasm for proposals by the Italian government and relief that the euro crisis has eased.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/03/business/economy/optimism-grows-in-italy-defying-the-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'While official figures show scant economic growth, a confidence survey seems to show enthusiasm for proposals by the Italian government and relief that the euro crisis has eased.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Italian economy has been a laggard for years. In the final quarter of 2013, it registered scant growth of just 0.3 percent at an annual rate, and that was a great improvement. Before that, it had shrunk for nine consecutive quarters. The economy remains smaller than it was 14 years ago. Unemployment has climbed to nearly 13 percent, twice its level in early 2008.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Confidence Undimmed by Statistics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italian Confidence Undimmed by Statistics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T15:46:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', 