rticle', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Engber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Engber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8755f33f-466c-5bde-ae1e-9cf400a07b71', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8755f33f-466c-5bde-ae1e-9cf400a07b71'}, {'abstract': 'Smoke, smoke, smoke that cigarette. Or not.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/magazine/brother-can-you-spare-some-emphysema.html', 'snippet': 'Smoke, smoke, smoke that cigarette. Or not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t smoke, but once or twice a year I have a cigarette with old friends. I bought a pack for one such evening, and only a few were consumed. On my way to work the next morning, I was about to throw it away, but then I saw a group of homeless people on the sidewalk. I gave the pack to the only woman in the bunch, and she accepted it with gratitude. Should I have thrown them away? MARK LESSARD, BROOKLYN', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/magazine/04ethicist1/04ethicist1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/magazine/04ethicist1/04ethicist1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/magazine/04ethicist1/04ethicist1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 510, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/magazine/04ethicist1/04ethicist1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 5