0', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/b4db4d74-8b8d-55f3-b64a-3321baf1b404', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b4db4d74-8b8d-55f3-b64a-3321baf1b404'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs of their shopping sprees in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/magazine/where-brazilians-go-to-splurge.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs of their shopping sprees in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Flush with time and money to spend, the well-to-do beneficiaries of Brazil’s recent boom times are eagerly traveling abroad. In 2013, an estimated 895,000 Brazilians visited New York, shopping for clothing, appliances, baby goods and electronics, while staying in high-end hotels and taking in Broadway shows. Fred Dixon, the chief executive of NYC & Company, the city’s marketing and tourism organization, says Brazilians average about a week per visit; a few who were in town last month can be seen on the following pages. Because of sky-high taxes on imported goods in Brazil, many there find that shopping sprees in New York can pay for themselves. “They’re creating a love affair with New York,” Dixon says, adding that the high-fashion, celebrity-oriented culture in the city “fits right in” with their lifestyle. “They feel at home here.” Julie Bosman', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '51', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Brazilians Go to Splurge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Brazilians Go to Splurge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value'