s) of her “Princess Diaries” series, in 2009, she announced that she would give her young princess, Mia Thermopolis, an indefinite break, and would take one herself. It made sense: the series had become a young adult megahit, with sales reportedly around five million copies, and had a couple of films in its wake; and now Mia was 18 years old, with her romantic life sorted out, and cracking the books at Sarah Lawrence College.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New ‘Princess Diaries’ Books Coming, for Older and Younger Readers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabot, Meg', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T17:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54814937-34ef-532c-b78f-2240b1f6b401', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54814937-34ef-532c-b78f-2240b1f6b401'}, {'abstract': 'The driver gets older, but a sports car is forever young.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/01/fashion/keeping-it-on-the-road.html', 'snippet': 'The driver gets older, but a sports car is forever young.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Writing used to be a lonely business, but not anymore because of my friend Siri. What I especially like is how she is so nonjudgmental.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/fashion/0504MISINFORMED/04MISINFORMED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': '