 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T17:53:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed725139-d3d6-5628-bfc0-49b8a4a2e232', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed725139-d3d6-5628-bfc0-49b8a4a2e232'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Rodriguez, who plays a gangland son who infiltrates police ranks in “Gang Related,” coming to Fox, talks about the men who helped him at crucial points in his younger years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/arts/television/ramon-rodriguez-of-gang-related-talks-about-father-figures.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rodriguez, who plays a gangland son who infiltrates police ranks in “Gang Related,” coming to Fox, talks about the men who helped him at crucial points in his younger years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Gang Related,” Ramon Rodriguez portrays Ryan Lopez, the adopted son of a crime lord who infiltrates the Los Angeles Police Department to help his family keep ahead of the law. But while Mr. Rodriguez’s real life doesn’t have the heart-stopping close calls, underworld gore or angsty divided loyalties that riddle this new Fox series, starting May 22, his childhood was a textbook example of how a father figure — or three — can help put a troubled boy on the right path.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04SNAPSHOT/04SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04SNAPSHOT/04SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04SNAPSHOT/04SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04SNAPSHOT/04SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04SNAPSHOT/04SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04SNAPSHOT/04SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04SNAPSHOT/04SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Court or Off, He Savors Assists', 'kicker': 'Snapshot | Ramon Rodriguez', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Court or Off, He Savors Assists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shattuck, Kathryn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Ramon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Gang Related (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T17:54:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/92ca4734-25d1-5fd2-bc8f-0a4038cc618c', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92ca4734-25d1-5fd2-bc8f-0a4038cc618c'}, {'abstract': 'The inspiration for this dish is a Sicilian stew called fritteda that can be served with pasta or other grains as a main course.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/health/spring-vegetable-stew-with-artichokes-and-fennel.html', 'snippet': 'The inspiration for this dish is a Sicilian stew called fritteda that can be served with pasta or other grains as a main course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is inspired by a lush Sicilian springtime stew called fritteda that also includes peas and fava beans (and much more olive oil). This one is simpler, but equally sweet and heady because of all the fennel and the spring onions. I like to serve it with bow-tie pasta and a little Parmesan as a main dish, or with grains as part of a meal in a bowl. It also makes a delicious side dish with just about anything.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/03/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/03/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Vegetable Stew With Artichokes and Fennel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spring Vegetable Stew With Artichokes and Fennel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T17:57:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd8b49b2-fefc-5fe0-916d-4f38f508928f', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd8b49b2-fefc-5fe0-916d-4f38f508928f'}, {'abstract': 'We have been living with rising income inequality for so long that it has come to seem inevitable. It doesn’t have to be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/magazine/inequality-has-been-going-on-forever-but-that-doesnt-mean-its-inevitable.html', 'snippet': 'We have been living with rising income inequality for so long that it has come to seem inevitable. It doesn’t have to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We have been living with rising income inequality for so long — in good times and bad, under Republican presidents and Democratic ones — that it has come to seem inevitable. It is no longer news that the affluent did better than everyone else during the booms of the 1980s and ’90s and through the mediocre growth of this century’s first years. Or that the rich have recovered from the financial crisis far better than the rest of country.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/upshot/03inequality/03inequality-articleLarge.png', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/03/upshot/03inequality/03inequality-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/upshot/03inequality/03inequality-jumbo.png', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/upshot/03inequality/03inequality-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1310, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/upshot/03inequality/03inequality-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/03/upshot/03inequality/03inequality-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/upshot/03inequality/03inequality-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inequality Has Been Going On Forever ... but That Doesn’t Mean It’s Inevitable', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All for the 1%, 1% for All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leonhardt, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piketty, Thomas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Capital in the Twenty-First Century (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T17:58:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c8c9733-4a72-5061-8fad-a780ef5b0e8d', 'word_count': 1561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c8c9733-4a72-5061-8fad-a780ef5b0e8d'}, {'abstract': 'A spin on the Provençal chard omelet called truccha, good to eat hot, warm or cold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/health/baked-frittata-with-yogurt-chard-and-green-garlic.html', 'snippet': 'A spin on the Provençal chard omelet called truccha, good to eat hot, warm or cold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Inspired by the signature Provençal chard omelet called truccha, this beautiful baked frittata incorporates thick Greek yogurt and lots of green garlic. It will puff up in the oven, but then it settles back down. Use a generous bunch of chard for this – green, red or rainbow – and save the stalks to use in the chard stalk and chickpea purée that I’m also posting this week. I like to serve the frittata at room temperature, or I grab a cold slice for lunch. It’s a wonderfully portable dish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/03/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/03/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05