pring-onions-green-garlic-and-tofu.html', 'snippet': 'Juicy springtime ginger, onions and green garlic elevate this stir-fry featuring baby turnips and their bitter greens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fresh ginger I’m finding at springtime farmers’ markets is new and juicy, like the spring garlic and onions. I’m sure this is going to be just one of many springtime stir-fries, but right now it’s a favorite. It’s inspired by an irresistible bunch of baby turnips I bought at a Sunday farmers’ market. The turnips were no bigger than a small round radish, but their greens were lush – I had about 6 cups of leaves after I’d stripped them from the stems. Sweet spring onions and green garlic contrast beautifully with the bitter flavor of the turnip greens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/09recipehealth/09recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/03/science/09recipehealth/09recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/09recipehealth/09recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/09recipehealth/09recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/09recipehealth/09recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/03/science/09recipehealth/09recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/09recipehealth/09recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stir-Fried Baby Turnips With Spring Onions, Green Garlic and Tofu', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T18:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65f2aa5c-6bf4-58ae-af7b-a71dbf0a0a9b', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65f2aa5c-6bf4-58ae-af7b-a71dbf0a0a9b'}, {'abstract': 'An economical dip that is a cross between hummus and the classic Middle Eastern dip called silq bil tahina.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/health/chard-stalk-chickpea-tahini-and-yogurt-dip.html', 'snippet': 'An economical dip that is a cross between hummus and the classic Middle Eastern dip called silq bil tahina.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you’ve bought a bunch of Swiss chard and used the leaves for another dish, like an oven-baked frittata with yogurt, Swiss chard and green garlic, save the stems. Then you can make this dip, which is a cross between hummus and classic Middle Eastern dip called silq bil tahina, made with chard stalks and tahini. I’ve added lots of yogurt to the mix. I love to use some red chard stalks because they give the dip a beautiful pale pink hue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/03/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/03/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chard Stalk, Chickpea, Tahini and Yogurt Dip', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T18:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63a5b0fe-14d4-5fc4-93b7-5c29a0d95bc1', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63a5b0fe-14d4-5fc4-93b7-5c29a0d95bc1'}, {'abstract': 'A new book argues that more people can and should become angel investors, but that they must expect plenty of failures along with the rare big win.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/03/your-money/angel-investors-need-a-high-risk-tolerance-not-billions.html', 'snippet': 'A new book argues that more people can and should become angel investors, but that they must expect plenty of failures along with the rare big win.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUST about every major tech success — from Facebook to LinkedIn to Instagram — started with angel investors taking a chance. These risk takers ended up being richly rewarded for their early investments, and no doubt they have inspired would-be angels to search for the next big thing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/your-money/03wealth/03wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/03/your-money/03wealth/03wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/your-money/03wealth/03wealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/your-money/03wealth/03wealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/your-money/03wealth/03wealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/03/your-money/03wealth/03wealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/your-money/03wealth/03wealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Billions Not Required for Angel Investing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Billions Not Required for Angel Investing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, David S (1957- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T18:02:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02c2454e-d282-5519-bed5-90ce21e3d867', 'word_count': 1583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02c2454e-d282-5519-bed5-90ce21e3d867'}, {'abstract': 'Lygia Clark is not well known in the United States, a circumstance that should be corrected by a new exhibition at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/arts/design/see-it-feel-it-touch-it-be-healed.html', 'snippet': 'Lygia Clark is not well known in the United States, a circumstance that should be corrected by a new exhibition at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though she was one of Brazil’s most celebrated artists of the post-World War II era, Lygia Clark (1920-88) is not well known in the United States, a circumstance that should be corrected by “Lygia Clark: The Abandonment of Art, 1948-1988,” beginning Saturday at the Museum of Modern Art. Clark started out as a maker of geometric abstractions under the influences of Klee, Mondrian and Léger. In the 1960s she was associated with Neo-Concretism, the Brazilian movement that insisted on the sensual and material — as opposed to intellectual — properties of paintings and sculpture, sometimes encouraging viewer interaction with objects and installations. After 1966, Clark claimed to have abandoned art. She shifted her approach away from creating conventional forms and toward a kind of art therapy that involved the application of materials and devices directly to the people’s bodies. Art was treated as a form of psychological healing. Her late works should be of particular interest to fans of socially engaged and otherwise participatory types of art making. (Through Aug. 24, 11 West 53rd Street, 212-708-9400, moma.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE2/04GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 523, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE2/04GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 523}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE2/04GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 892, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE2/04GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1785, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE2/04GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE2/04GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE2/04GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'See It, Feel It, Touch It, Be Healed', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'See It, Feel It, Touch It, Be Healed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T18:09:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9364323f-ed84-5f12-946b-2886a9b86842', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9364323f-ed84-5f12-946b-2886a9b86842'}, {'abstract': 'A new-music great and a rising star both have tantalizing concerts on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/arts/music/two-generations-of-new-music-stars.html', 'snippet': 'A new-music great and a rising star both have tantalizing concerts on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new-music great and a rising star both have tantalizing concerts on Saturday. The pianist Peter Serkin, 66, fresh off a recent Bartok triumph with the New York Philharmonic, arrives at the 92nd Street Y with a characteristically varied program. Stretching from the early Baroque composer Jan Pieterszoon Sweelinck to three recent works by Charles Wuorinen, the evening also includes Carl Nielsen and Beethoven. (8 p.m., Lexington Avenue at 92nd Street, 212-415-5500, 92y.org.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE3/04GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 906, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE3/04GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 906}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE3/04GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 679, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE3/04GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1357, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name':