oves! Dance Festival, now in its ninth year, featuring more than 50 local and international artists (through May 25). In the first week, the festival hosts a benefit concert, “Dancing for Japan 2014” (Wednesday), to support victims of the 2011 Tohoku earthquake and tsunami. Next, Miki Orihara, a longtime dancer for the Martha Graham Dance Company, will perform “Resonance,” a series of solos by modern-dance pioneers and contemporary choreographers (Thursday through May 11).', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType'