': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landslides and Mudslides', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Badakhshan Province (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T19:37:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed and Haris Kakar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Haris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89b5546d-1f87-52e9-996a-e2ad2486246d', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89b5546d-1f87-52e9-996a-e2ad2486246d'}, {'abstract': 'Five years after first trying it, two critics again offer advice to everyone involved in the making, distributing and watching of movies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/movies/critics-weigh-in-on-patriarchy-and-the-vanished-film-print.html', 'snippet': 'Five years after first trying it, two critics again offer advice to everyone involved in the making, distributing and watching of movies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer is sequel season, when the movie studios celebrate their lack of imagination by disguising it as populism. Why should movie critics be any different? Five years ago, we published the first installment of our “Memos to Hollywood,” in which we presumed to give advice to everyone involved in the making, distributing and watching of movies. And now we’re back with another spectacular, game-changing, blockbuster episode. This time, they’ll pay attention.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04HOLLYWOOD-ILLO/04HOLLYWOD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04HOLLYWOOD-ILLO/04HOLLYWOD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 778}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04HOLLYWOOD-ILLO/04HOLLYWOD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04HOLLYWOOD-ILLO/04HOLLYWOD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1580, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04HOLLYWOOD-ILLO/04HOLLYWOOD-ILLO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04HOLLYWOOD-ILLO/04HOLLYWOOD-ILLO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04HOLLYWOOD-ILLO/04HOLLYWOOD-ILLO-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Memos to Hollywood', 'kicker': 'Summer Movies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Memos to Hollywood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T19:39:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis and A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f4d4b53-af13-59d4-8432-476195378486', 'word_count': 2195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f4d4b53-af13-59d4-8432-476195378486'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Forman, 72, whom a parole official once told he “could have made millions as a salesman,” was recently released from prison and is again accused of taking money under false pretenses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/03/nyregion/a-long-and-questionable-record-in-sales.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Forman, 72, whom a parole official once told he “could have made millions as a salesman,” was recently released from prison and is again accused of taking money under false pretenses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sign on the door of the building on Eighth Avenue hard by Pennsylvania Station reads “Vigilant Hotel.” It is handwritten on cardboard. The Vigilant is a men’s-only, single-room-occupancy dwelling, the sort that lined the Bowery and its skid row a generation ago. Rooms go for $150 a week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/nyregion/03CRIMESCENE/03CRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 208, 'width': 156, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/nyregion/03CRIMESCENE/03CRIMESCENE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 208, 'width': 156, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'sup