tencing, while black judges vote differently from whites on issues involving civil rights and affirmative action. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GRAY/04GRAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 782, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GRAY/04GRAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 782}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GRAY/04GRAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 786, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GRAY/04GRAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1571, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GRAY/04GRAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GRAY/04GRAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GRAY/04GRAY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Not to Pick Judges', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Not to Pick Judges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T19:46:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maya Sen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5befe8af-7458-5102-abd7-431bf52eb79f', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5befe8af-7458-5102-abd7-431bf52eb79f'}, {'abstract': 'In John Carney’s new film, “Begin Again,” he has tried to shoot in parts of New York that are recognizable to residents, not tourists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/movies/begin-again-is-set-in-a-real-new-york-of-real-musicians.html', 'snippet': 'In John Carney’s new film, “Begin Again,” he has tried to shoot in parts of New York that are recognizable to residents, not tourists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2006, while the Irish writer-director John Carney was promoting his indie musical film “Once,” he fell hard for New York City. Literally. “Cycling around, going the wrong way down one-way streets, I got the feel of living here,” Mr. Carney said, adding that when he crashed that bike, he admired the efficiency with which New Yorkers stopped “for the minimal amount of time to make sure I wasn’t dead.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/arts/04LOGANHILL1/04LOGANHILL1-articleLarg