m/2014/05/02/week-in-pictures-for-may-2/', 'snippet': 'A slide show of photographs of the past week in New York City and the region includes an amusement park in Rye, N.Y.; a prayer service for Sherpa guides; and storm clouds over the Brooklyn Bridge.', 'lead_paragraph': '.media.slideshow.in-page-player .headline { display: none; } ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week in Pictures for May 2', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T21:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fae6ea2-861b-5aef-a95e-d82be3a1c03b', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fae6ea2-861b-5aef-a95e-d82be3a1c03b'}, {'abstract': 'Though imperfect, the agreement is a good deal for the city and its students.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/03/opinion/a-teachers-contract-for-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Though imperfect, the agreement is a good deal for the city and its students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was no snarling at City Hall when Mayor Bill de Blasio and the teachers’ union announced a very significant labor agreement on Thursday. Dispensing with the unproductive tension that tarnished the Bloomberg administration, the two sides showed that real progress can be made — on both the fiscal and the educational sides of the contract — when there is good will instead of disdain. On the whole, the agreement represents a good deal for the city and its students, though there were several missed opportunities and unanswered questions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Teachers’ Contract for New York', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Teachers’ Contract for New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Federation of Teachers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T21:08:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/20b77445-a673-506b-9c33-313d88b536d5', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20b77445-a673-506b-9c33-313d88b536d5'}, {'abstract': 'In memory of Jerry Goodman.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/friday-night-music-alison-krauss/', 'snippet': 'In memory of Jerry Goodman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Too busy to post much. But on Wednesday there was a lovely memorial event for Jerry (George W) Goodman, aka Adam Smith, that among other things highlighted his love of music, and included performances of some of his favorites — including this piece.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Alison Krauss', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-02T21:10:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67e32024-c35a-531c-a8fb-9557c3639e47', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67e32024-c35a-531c-a8fb-9557c3639e47'}, {'abstract': 'Watch our exclusive clip of Richard Ayoade’s new film “The Double,” which hits theaters next week. Jesse Eisenberg plays two identical-looking characters with opposite luck and temperament.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/02/richard-ayoade-the-double-jesse-eisenberg/', 'snippet': 'Watch our exclusive clip of Richard Ayoade’s new film “The Double,” which hits theaters next week. Jesse Eisenberg plays two identical-looking characters with opposite luck and temperament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Richard Ayoade’s film, “The Double,” the quiet, self-conscious office clerk Simon James (played by Jesse Eisenberg) is struggling through a work day when he is suddenly confronted with his doppelgänger: exact in physique, but opposite in temperament. Arrogant, suave and irresistible to women, James Simon (also played by Eisenberg) glides into Simon’s life, throwing light on his weaknesses and self-loathing, and preying on his love interest Hannah (played by Mia Wasikowska). Nothing ever seems to go right for Simon, while everything is perfect for James. Based on Fyodor Dostoyevsky’s novella, the story delves into questions of identity, psychosis and self-preservation with absurd and sometimes agonizing humor. A seasoned comedian, the British director can draw a link between Dostoyevsky’s piercing insight and Larry David’s brazen style: “He’s really willing to go to un-noble places in people.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't