eing hit by vehicles made a lasting impact on them.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Dance with me, baby,” the night nurse crooned to me. Despite the morphine-induced fog clouding my brain that first week after the accident, I understood that she meant I was to collapse into her arms. Then, holding me like a limp rag doll, she lifted me upright and held my full weight. The new perspective was dizzying, since I’d been on my back, looking up, since the cops and the medics got to me.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04HIT1sub3/04HIT1sub3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 323, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04HIT1sub3/04HIT1sub3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 323}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04HIT1sub3/04HIT1sub3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 551, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04HIT1sub3/04HIT1sub3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1103, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04HIT1sub3/04HIT1sub3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04HIT1sub3/04HIT1sub3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04HIT1sub3/04HIT1sub3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Struck on the Street: Four Survivors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Struck on the Street', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abramson, Jill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montclair (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuhs, Denise', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kueneman, Andrew', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sussman, Mick', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMSON, JILL', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-03T01:34:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jill Abramson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abramson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd4bd8f6-34ac-5b5e-ab1a-17efc0e00f16', 'word_count': 3329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd4bd8f6-34ac-5b5e-ab1a-17efc0e00f16'}, {'abstract': 'A casino license, particularly within a leisurely drive of New York City, could be a golden ticket to billions in profits in one of the last underdeveloped gambling markets in the nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/03/nyregion/bidders-lining-up-lobbyists-in-fight-for-new-york-casinos.html', 'snippet': 'A casino license, particularly within a leisurely drive of New York City, could be a golden ticket to billions in profits in one of the last underdeveloped gambling markets in the nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — The 22 entities vying to build casinos in New York State include operators of some of the flashiest gambling palaces, from Las Vegas to Singapore. Others are mysterious paper-only creatures with no websites, no offices and not so much as a slot machine to call their own.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/nyregion/03JPCASINOS/03JPCASINOS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/03/nyregion/03JPCASINOS/03JPCASINOS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/nyregion/03JPCASINOS/03JPCASINOS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/nyregion/03JPCASINOS/03JPCASINOS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/nyregion/03JPCASINOS/03JPCASINOS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/03/nyregion/03JPCASINOS/03JPCASINOS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/03/nyregion/03JPCASINOS/03JPCASINOS-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bidders Lining Up Lobbyists in Fight for New York Casinos', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bidders Lining Up Lobbyists in Fight for New York Casinos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKinley, Jesse', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Gaming Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-03T01:34:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley and Charles V. Bagli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Bagli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7eb2e6e-faa1-543e-b899-f864c69a854e', 'word_count': 1434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7eb2e6e-faa1-543e-b899-f864c69a854e'}, {'abstract': 'The week’s two major events seemed to challenge the popular image of a linear march of human progress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/opinion/sunday/celebrating-sainthood-and-witnessing-barbarity.html', 'snippet': 'The week’s two major events seemed to challenge the popular image of a linear march of human progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Catholic Church’s canonization of two of its recent popes and the grotesquely botched execution of a murderer in Oklahoma last week stood at opposite ends of the moral scale. Yet there was something about the two events — the public affirmation of a religious order in the one and the medieval barbarity of the other — that seemed to challenge the popular image of a linear march of human progress.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04QUICK/04QUICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04QUICK/04QUICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04QUICK/04QUICK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04QUICK/04QUICK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04QUICK/04QUICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04QUICK/04QUICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04QUICK/04QUICK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating Sainthood and Witnessing Barbarity', 'kicker