inal': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e9a7aa9-5828-56a9-aefe-0d5e80d5d33a', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e9a7aa9-5828-56a9-aefe-0d5e80d5d33a'}, {'abstract': 'A tactile acrostic by Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/03/variety-a-tactile-acrostic/', 'snippet': 'A tactile acrostic by Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE — Today’s quote is from a fascinating look into the world of synesthesia, a neurological condition that involves a blending of sensations that are normally experienced separately. Some synesthetes, for example, report that they experience numbers as “colors, shapes or motions,” as the author of “Born on a Blue Day” confirms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: A Tactile Acrostic', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acrostic Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-03T16:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6fe03b2-6de9-599c-8b70-ed5ea64b9e90', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6fe03b2-6de9-599c-8b70-ed5ea64b9e90'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Joe discusses Pfizer’s desire to acquire AstraZeneca and move to the U.K.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/03/joe-on-wnycs-money-talking-may-1-2014/', 'snippet': 'This week, Joe discusses Pfizer’s desire to acquire AstraZeneca and move to the U.K.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York-based pharmaceutical giant Pfizer revealed a multi-billion dollar offer to acquire British rival AstraZeneca, and if the acquisition is successful, Pfizer plans to reincorporate in the United Kingdom. Doing so would lower the company’s tax rate by 7 percent and allow it to avoid paying U.S. taxes on profits made overseas. This week on Money Talking, Rana Foroohar and Joe Nocera discuss whether Pfizer could inspire other U.S.-based, international companies to pursue a similar path. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/opinion/pfizer/pfizer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/opinion/pfizer/pfizer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/opinion/pfizer/pfizer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/opinion/pfizer/pfizer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/opinion/pfizer/pfizer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/02/opinion/pfizer/pfizer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':