 series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/sports/hockey/falling-behind-in-nhl-playoffs-is-no-reason-to-lose-hope.html', 'snippet': 'In the first round there were 29 comeback victories in 48 games, but no big upsets in any of the series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Stanley Cup playoffs’ wild first round was a reminder of just how improbable hockey can be. San Jose trounced Los Angeles in their first three games, and then the Kings trounced the Sharks in the last four. The Pittsburgh Penguins advanced, even though Sidney Crosby did not score a goal. The Rangers extended their 12-game losing streak while holding a series lead, but then won their fourth straight Game 7. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Falling Behind in N.H.L. Playoffs Is No Reason to Lose Hope', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Falling Behind Is No Reason to Lose Hope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keenan, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Jon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suter, Ryan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Linden, Trevor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-03T18:24:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36927ca6-6adb-53a6-bc45-2d806470bb07', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36927ca6-6adb-53a6-bc45-2d806470bb07'}, {'abstract': 'Forget what you know about what grows where.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/opinion/sunday/gardening-for-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'Forget what you know about what grows where.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLUMBIA, S.C. — THIS past winter was a tough one in our backyard. Where we live, about a hundred miles inland from the South Carolina coast, winter is normally a good time to make changes, like the swath of turf I removed from our front yard this year and replaced with perennial flowers and small tufts of native grass. But what is normal now in the garden? One week I’m sweating, the bees are buzzing, buds are breaking; the next, the birdbath is frozen and there’s snow on the ground.  ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GARDENING/04GARDENING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GARDENING/04GARDENING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GARDENING/04GARDENING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GARDENING/04GARDENING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1289, 'width': 1289, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/sunday-review/04GARDENING/04GARDENING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05