 Obama has opened himself to criticism that he is not articulating a strong, overarching blueprint for the exercise of American power and has not been able to bend authoritarian leaders to his will.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Obama and the World', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Obama and the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-03T18:33:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b03ab90f-a1c7-5fb5-b4d7-215692f817fe', 'word_count': 1802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b03ab90f-a1c7-5fb5-b4d7-215692f817fe'}, {'abstract': 'Controlling the message that’s getting out to the public reaches a new level that’s great for public relations but troubling for journalists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/opinion/sunday/when-sources-set-the-ground-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Controlling the message that’s getting out to the public reaches a new level that’s great for public relations but troubling for journalists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOMETIMES a single sentence can be a window into a world.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Sources Set the Ground Rules', 'kicker'