ine': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, May 4', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-03T19:21:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elena Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/095dc8cc-c21a-5d9d-85c6-82ff64b3da65', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/095dc8cc-c21a-5d9d-85c6-82ff64b3da65'}, {'abstract': 'The blimp providing a heightened vantage point for CBS’s broadcasting of PGA Tour events has become, along with its pilots, a crucial part of the telecast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/sports/golf/metlife-blimp-becomes-an-integral-part-of-pga-tour-telecasts.html', 'snippet': 'The blimp providing a heightened vantage point for CBS’s broadcasting of PGA Tour events has become, along with its pilots, a crucial part of the telecast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABOARD SNOOPY ONE, above Charlotte, N.C. — Like scores of other golf spectators at a PGA Tour event, Andrew Murray chooses where to position himself by consulting a course map. By the end of the week, his legs are leaden from the effort of tracking the leaders.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fairways From the Air', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fairways From the Air', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRSHIPS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Sports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MetLife Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-03T19:34:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ed3639c-b7fe-588e-88aa-95dfb3dd3bc1', 'word_count': 1125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ed3639c-b7fe-588e-88aa-95dfb3dd3bc1'}, {'abstract': 'Officials removed some of the cars involved in the derailment on Friday, which injured 19 people, and restored service to the lines, though more disruptions were planned to remove the remaining cars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/nyregion/partial-service-resumes-after-subway-derailment.html', 'snippet': 'Officials removed some of the cars involved in the derailment on Friday, which injured 19 people, and restored service to the lines, though more disruptions were planned to remove the remaining cars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Partial service was temporarily restored to subway lines running along Queens Boulevard on Saturday afternoon, a day after 19 people were injured in the worst derailment in the New York City subway system in over two decades.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Partial Service Resumes After Subway Derailment in Queens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Subway Service Partially Resumes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Woodside (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-03T19:46:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da50d344-5f47-5bd6-951b-fadf249ee85d', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da50d344-5f47-5bd6-951b-fadf249ee85d'}, {'abstract': 'The prevalence of both Type 1 and Type 2 diabetes drastically increased among youth across racial groups from 2001 to 2009, a study found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/us/study-reveals-sizable-increase-in-diabetes-among-children.html', 'snippet': 'The prevalence of both Type 1 and Type 2 diabetes drastically increased among youth across racial groups from 2001 to 2009, a study found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years doctors have warned of a rising epidemic of diabetes among children. Yet there has been surprisingly little firm data on the extent of this disease among younger Americans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Reveals Sizable Increase in Diabetes Among Children', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Reveals Sizable Increase in Diabetes Among Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saint Louis, Catherine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of the American Medical Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-03T20:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c69d7115-cd5b-55ae-b670-7ae056d2a8c3', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c69d7115-cd5b-55ae-b670-7ae056d2a8c3'}, {'abstract': 'The backdrop on my column about the kidnapped Nigerian school girls', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/03/standing-with-the-kidnapped-girls-in-nigeria/', 'snippet': 'The backdrop on my column about the kidnapped Nigerian school girls', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column is about the girls kidnapped from their school in northeastern NIgeria nearly three weeks ago. I wrote the column partly to apply more pressure on the Nigerian authorities, who seem uninterested in the case, to try to rescue these girls, and partly because I’m offended by the contrast between the global media focus on the missing MH370 flight and the uninterest in the even greater number of missing schoolgirls in Nigeria. It’s also important to note that what’s at stake isn’t just these girls: If they’re not recovered soon, then no parents are going to send girls or boys to school in the area again. And the area, where as it is only half of adults are literate, will slide into greater illiteracy, economic difficulty and backwardness. Education isn’t just about building schools, it’s also about ensuring security so that parents feel safe sending their children to school.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Standing with the Kidnapped Girls in Nigeria', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-03T20:08:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0430cd31-63d5-5718-b199-304224582368', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0430cd31-63d5-5718-b199-304224582368'}, {'abstract': 'Abu Malek, 25, the commander of a band of Al-Quds Brigades — the armed wing of Islamic Jihad — discusses his troops’ readiness to respond to any Israeli incursions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/100000002833651/islamic-jihad-on-defending-gaza.html', 'snippet': 'Abu Malek, 25, the commander of a band of Al-Quds Brigades — the armed wing of Islamic Jihad — discusses his troops’ readiness to respond to any Israeli incursions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Abu Malek, 25, the commander of a band of Al-Quds Brigades — the armed wing of Islamic Jihad — discusses his troops’ readiness to respond to any Israeli incursions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/18/multimedia/gaza-islamic-jihad/gaza-islamic-jihad-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/04/18/multimedia/gaza-islamic-jihad/gaza-islamic-jihad-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 