, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc9e1f5c-feac-5653-b683-92e7297b93eb', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc9e1f5c-feac-5653-b683-92e7297b93eb'}, {'abstract': 'Owned by two electrical engineers, Kibberia Restaurant and Cafe in Westport offers food well-suited to snacks or a light lunch or dinner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/04/nyregion/a-review-of-kibberia-restaurant-and-cafe-in-westport.html', 'snippet': 'Owned by two electrical engineers, Kibberia Restaurant and Cafe in Westport offers food well-suited to snacks or a light lunch or dinner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kibberia Restaurant and Cafe opened in Westport in late August 2013. This modest Lebanese place, more of a cafe than a restaurant, fills a need for falafel, hummus, kibbe (the ground meat and bulgur wheat patty from which the cafe derives its name), kebabs and other Mediterranean and Middle Eastern favorites — all while keeping prices low enough to entice families on a budget.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04DINECT3/04DINECT3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 521, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04DINECT3/04DINECT3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 521}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04DINECT3/04DINECT3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 890, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/04/nyregion/04DINECT3/04DINECT3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1780, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJu