y', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a0a444d-8e72-55f1-8824-7ad0f90a55fb', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a0a444d-8e72-55f1-8824-7ad0f90a55fb'}, {'abstract': 'Amid speculation that President Joseph Kabila might have the Constitution amended so that he could run again, Secretary of State John Kerry asked him “to put the country on a continued path to democracy.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/world/africa/kerry-urges-congolese-leader-not-to-run-for-third-term.html', 'snippet': 'Amid speculation that President Joseph Kabila might have the Constitution amended so that he could run again, Secretary of State John Kerry asked him “to put the country on a continued path to democracy.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'KINSHASA, Democratic Republic of Congo — Secretary of State John Kerry on Sunday publicly urged the president of the Democratic Republic of Congo to respect his nation’s Constitution and not run for another term in 2016.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/05/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/0