cd-6dcd-58e2-96e0-2a809cb4e8dc'}, {'abstract': 'Criminal sentences should be determined by the defendant’s role in the operation rather than the weight of the narcotics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/opinion/we-need-al-capone-drug-laws.html', 'snippet': 'Criminal sentences should be determined by the defendant’s role in the operation rather than the weight of the narcotics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EDINA, Minn. — AFTER a ruinous 30-year experiment in harsh sentences for narcotics trafficking resulting in mass incarceration, policy makers are having second thoughts. Many states, including Texas, have reformed their laws to shorten sentences. Congress is giving serious consideration to the Smarter Sentencing Act, which would do the same. The United States Sentencing Commission has just adopted a proposal to revise federal guidelines. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We Need Al Capone Drug Laws', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Need Al Capone Drug Laws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osler, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-04T23:15:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Osler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Osler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c96c3aee-20ae-5d4f-89a2-c2003246edb2', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c96c3aee-20ae-5d4f-89a2-c2003246edb2'}, {'abstract': 'We moved much more slowly to confront the dangers of smoking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/opinion/finally-some-optimism-about-obesity.html', 'snippet': 'We moved much more slowly to confront the dangers of smoking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EARLIER this year, we got what seemed like the first good news on obesity rates: A study in JAMA found that there had been a 43 percent drop in the obesity rates of 2- to 5-year-old children in the last decade. But then, last month, that news was contradicted by researchers at the University of North Carolina who used the same data to find that obesity rates had remained flat after all. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/opinion/0503OPEDisland/0503OPEDisland-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/05/opinion/0503OPEDisland/0503OPEDisland-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 748}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/opinion/0503OPEDisland/0503OPEDisland-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 822, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/opinion/0503OPEDisland/0503OPEDisland-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1735, 'width': 1392, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/opinion/0503OPEDisland/0503OPEDisland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/05/opinion/0503OPEDisland/0503OPEDisland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidt