 Gov. Mario M. Cuomo’s final term. Through it all, he has been a Democrat — and a liberal one at that — with Republicans as his usual adversaries. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/nyregion/05KOPPELL/05KOPPELL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 573, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/nyregion/05KOPPELL/05KOPPELL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 573, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/nyregion/05KOPPELL/05KOPPELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/05/nyregion/05KOPPELL/05KOPPELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/nyregion/05KOPPELL/05KOPPELL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooperation With G.O.P. Puts Senator in a Primary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cooperation With G.O.P. Puts Senator in a Primary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKinley, Jesse', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, State Legislature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koppell, G Oliver', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeffrey D', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T00:59:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18c2cb06-aa6e-5b12-a25c-4f43dacac1c2', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18c2cb06-aa6e-5b12-a25c-4f43dacac1c2'}, {'abstract': 'Three theater organizations have agreed to provide listening devices, like headsets or hearing loops, to audience members with hearing loss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/theater/hearing-help-in-theaters.html', 'snippet': 'Three theater organizations have agreed to provide listening devices, like headsets or hearing loops, to audience members with hearing loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attorney General Eric T. Schneiderman of New York announced on Sunday that three theater organizations — the Manhattan Theater Club, the Atlantic Theater Company and the School of Visual Arts Theater — have agreed to provide listening devices, like headsets or hearing loops, to audience members with hearing loss. As part of the Americans With Disabilities Act, theater companies that use microphones or have amplified sound during performances are to grant equal access to those who are hard of hearing, but the attorney general’s office received complaints from individuals and disability rights organizations that some Off Broadway theaters were not following those guidelines. An investigation by attorney general’s Civil Rights Bureau found that the three theater companies were not providing listening devices, and the bureau is working with other theaters to ensure their compliance with the law.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hearing Help in Theaters', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hearing Help in Theaters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manhattan Theater Club', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'School of Visual Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic Theater Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMERICANS WITH DISABILITIES ACT', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deafness', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ears and Hearing', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T01:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f35b986f-71da-5391-a506-a6cb6b48f10a', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f35b986f-71da-5391-a506-a6cb6b48f10a'}, {'abstract': 'While conceding he was “terrified” going into the deal, David Karp says he is happy with the autonomy the microblogging service has under its new owner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/technology/no-regrets-for-the-founder-of-tumblr-after-yahoo-sale.html', 'snippet': 'While conceding he was “terrified” going into the deal, David Karp says he is happy with the autonomy the microblogging service has under its new owner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Yahoo bought Tumblr for $1.1 billion a year ago, it sent a ripple of excitement — and anxiety — through the tech industry. Would Yahoo and its recently arrived chief executive, Marissa Mayer, breathe new life into Tumblr? Or would Yahoo smother the start-up, as it did after acquiring popular young services like GeoCities and Flickr?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/business/TUMBLR1/TUMBLR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/05/business/TUMBLR1/TUMBLR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/business/TUMBLR1/TUMBLR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/business/TUMBLR1/TUMBLR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/business/TUMBLR1/TUMBLR1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/05/business/TUMBLR1/TUMBLR1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/business/TUMBLR1/TUMBLR1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Regrets for the Founder of Tumblr After Yahoo Sale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Regrets for the Founder of Tumblr After Yahoo Sale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tumblr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wortham, Jenna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karp, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T01:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96cb81a6-a5c4-5b97-8e94-b1bc53d7653e', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96cb81a6-a5c4-5b97-8e94-b1bc53d7653e'}, {'abstract': 'Loaded with treasure, the S.S. Central America sank in 1857 during a hurricane near South Carolina. After years of legal battles, a private company is finally excavating the ship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/us/x-still-marks-sunken-spot-and-gold-awaits.html', 'snippet': 'Loaded with treasure, the S.S. Central America sank in 1857 during a hurricane near South Carolina. After years of legal battles, a private company is finally excavating the ship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The discovery of sunken gold conjures up visions of instant riches: Swiss bank accounts and lazy afternoons on faraway beaches, daiquiris in hand.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/0