00', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/06077f81-d3e0-50ab-8398-0ea9dcac9d1d', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06077f81-d3e0-50ab-8398-0ea9dcac9d1d'}, {'abstract': 'Congress should raise the gas and diesel taxes to pay for the upkeep of federal interstate highways, not end the ban on tolls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/opinion/the-toll-of-no-new-taxes.html', 'snippet': 'Congress should raise the gas and diesel taxes to pay for the upkeep of federal interstate highways, not end the ban on tolls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the nation’s highway system frayed and running short of funds, the Obama administration has asked Congress to end the current ban on states’ charging tolls to pay for the upkeep of federal interstate highways. The proposal would reverse a proud policy dating to the system’s creation in 1956, when the postwar automobile boom left government flush with fuel taxes and ever bigger highway plans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Toll of ‘No New Taxes’', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Toll of ‘No New Taxes’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gasoline Tax (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Highway Trust Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tolls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T01:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c2d3c05-8e14-5408-a82a-6dac2aac1d2f', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c2d3c05-8e14-5408-a82a-6dac2aac1d2f'}, {'abstract': 'After losing three straight games at Coors Field, the Mets got six scoreless innings from Dillon Gee, who won his third game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/sports/baseball/gee-stymies-colorado-to-help-prevent-a-four-game-sweep.html', 'snippet': 'After losing three straight games at Coors Field, the Mets got six scoreless innings from Dillon Gee, who won his third game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — The Mets finally shook the demons that had haunted them at Coors Field this weekend, getting a masterly pitching performance and enough offense for a 5-1 victory against the Colorado Rockies.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/sports/METS/METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 548, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/05/sports/METS/METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 548}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/sports/METS/METS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 934, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/sports/METS/METS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1869, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't