e really needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Police Department has been doing more with less for over a decade, with a force that is down about 6,000 uniformed officers from a peak of 40,710 in 2001. During that time crime in the city has fallen to record lows, and New Yorkers’ real worries about their safety have been replaced by more hypothetical jitters — can the trend possibly continue, and do we have enough officers to make sure it does? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Policing, on the Safe Side', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Policing, on the Safe Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bratton, William J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T01:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4f48aa7-296a-572a-aa99-fb53110e89a6', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4f48aa7-296a-572a-aa99-fb53110e89a6'}, {'abstract': 'April was the best month for job growth in quite a while, but recovery is still painfully slow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/opinion/a-better-economy-still-far-from-good.html', 'snippet': 'April was the best month for job growth in quite a while, but recovery is still painfully slow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The good news from last week’s economic reports is this: April was the best month for job growth in quite a while. Employers added 288,000 jobs, bringing the average for the last three months to a respectable 238,000. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Better Economy, Still Far From Good', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Better Economy, Still Far From Good', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T01:23:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f0ac832-ce34-5870-b2db-a23895cf9fe9', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f0ac832-ce34-5870-b2db-a23895cf9fe9'}, {'abstract': 'For Rand Paul, the would-be presidential candidate, and Rupert Murdoch, one of the most powerful Republican brokers, Saturday marked a potential turn in the 2016 campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/us/politics/at-derby-day-with-murdoch-rand-paul-goes-through-his-paces.html', 'snippet': 'For Rand Paul, the would-be presidential candidate, and Rupert Murdoch, one of the most powerful Republican brokers, Saturday marked a potential turn in the 2016 campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOUISVILLE, Ky. — On the afternoon of the Kentucky Derby, Rand Paul, the state’s junior Republican senator and likely presidential candidate, spilled out of an elevator in the exclusive Jockey Club Suites of Churchill Downs with an entourage of women with flower-adorned hats, men in seersucker suits