pet': 'The accused spy was contacted through an online messaging service and asked to pass along military journals available only to domestic Chinese subscribers, according to a state-run newspaper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man in the southern province of Guangdong who sent military documents and photos of military bases overseas has been sentenced to 10 years in prison on a spying conviction, state media has reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Sentences Accused Spy to 10-Year Prison Term', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xue Feng', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Daily", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T06:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eb8f8e5-d0ee-5886-8866-9c608829a867', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eb8f8e5-d0ee-5886-8866-9c608829a867'}, {'abstract': 'New equipment will be deployed with help from outside groups and companies to examine the ocean floor for debris from Malaysia Airlines Flight 370.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/world/asia/missing-malaysia-flight-370.html', 'snippet': 'New equipment will be deployed with help from outside groups and companies to examine the ocean floor for debris from Malaysia Airlines Flight 370.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SYDNEY, Australia — With nothing tangible to show for nearly two months of searching for Flight 370, officials and experts from Malaysia, China, Australia and other countries plan to meet on Wednesday in Canberra, the Australian capital, to sort out what to do next, officials said Monday. The focus will be on intensively examining the floor of the Indian Ocean looking for debris.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/06PLANE/06PLANE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/06PLANE/06PLANE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/06PLANE/06PLANE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/06PLANE/06PLANE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1309, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/06PLANE/06PLANE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/06PLANE/06PLANE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailhei