', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a721430-548f-5d24-bedb-5408ce62dc69', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a721430-548f-5d24-bedb-5408ce62dc69'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn Academy of Music is offering a monthlong program celebrating the cinema of rock ‘n’ roll’s greatest female rebels. Here, T checks in with the long-off-the-radar Linda Manz, the feisty star of Dennis Hopper’s 1980 classic “Out of the Blue.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/now-screening-catching-up-with-the-original-punk-rock-girl-of-film/', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn Academy of Music is offering a monthlong program celebrating the cinema of rock ‘n’ roll’s greatest female rebels. Here, T checks in with the long-off-the-radar Linda Manz, the feisty star of Dennis Hopper’s 1980 classic “Out of the B...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starting May 7 at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, a series called “Punk Rock Girls” will showcase the women of the movement in all their pierced, ripped, hairsprayed glory. “The theme is so resonant,” says the programmer Nellie Killian, who conceived the monthlong event as a valentine to the era. “Especially for female viewers, it’s so important to have these types of girl characters, and we wanted to put in the lineage of movies of girls carving out a space for themselves within alternative culture.” Highlights will include a rubber-braceleted, Danceteria-era Madonna brazenly appropriating the Port Authority hand dryers (“Desperately Seeking Susan”); Diane Lane and friends, in slashes of scarlet eye shadow and skunk-striped hair, stepping up to the mike (“Ladies and Gentlemen, the Fabulous Stains”); and Robin Johnson and Trini Alvarado hurling TV sets off Manhattan rooftops (“Times Square”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05punk-bengal/05punk-bengal-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05punk-bengal/05punk-bengal-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05punk-bengal/05punk-bengal-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05punk-bengal/05punk-bengal-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1146, 'width': 1530, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05punk-bengal/05punk-bengal-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05punk-bengal/05punk-bengal-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05punk-bengal/05punk-bengal-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Screening | Catching Up With the Original Punk Rock Girl of Film', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T16:30:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Bengal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bengal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a162d34-6fb3-548b-99b2-ce79a16a8c31', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a162d34-6fb3-548b-99b2-ce79a16a8c31'}, {'abstract': 'The University of Chicago economist had the audacity to suggest that virtually every aspect of human behavior was subject to economic analysis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/upshot/how-gary-becker-transformed-the-social-sciences.html', 'snippet': 'The University of Chicago economist had the audacity to suggest that virtually every aspect of human behavior was subject to economic analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gary Becker was the most important social scientist in the past 50 years and possibly longer, in my view. He was my intellectual hero, and I want to explain why.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/upshot/06UP-Becker-copy/06UP-Becker-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 895, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/06/upshot/06UP-Becker-copy/06UP-Becker-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 895}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/upshot/06UP-Becker-copy/06UP-Becker-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/upshot/06UP-Becker-copy/06UP-Becker-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1373, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/upshot/06UP-Becke