y.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/michelle-obama-joins-in-a-salute-to-anna-wintour/', 'snippet': 'The first lady attended a dedication ceremony at the Metropolitan Museum of Art for the newly renamed Anna Wintour Costume Center. “Two first ladies in one room at the same time,” Marc Jacobs observed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday morning, from the Temple of Dendur at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, the Vogue editor Anna Wintour proved yet again that she can get the entire fashion world to show up. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michelle Obama Joins in a Salute to Anna Wintour', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wintour, Anna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Costume Institute', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T18:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Koblin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koblin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c36abeeb-5e3c-573f-ba8c-4048bacd0cee', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c36abeeb-5e3c-573f-ba8c-4048bacd0cee'}, {'abstract': 'The designer, who penned the introduction to the Met’s catalog for James, says he and the late couturier were cut from the same cloth.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/ralph-rucci-charles-james-beyond-fashion-metropolitan-museum-of-art/', 'snippet': 'The designer, who penned the introduction to the Met’s catalog for James, says he and the late couturier were cut from the same cloth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charles James was one of American fashion’s first couturiers, as well as one of its most influential designers and most notorious perfectionists. His contemporaries, such as Christian Dior and Mainbocher, venerated him; Balenciaga famously called him the world’s best and only dressmaker, and both Elsa Schiaparelli and Coco Chanel wore his designs. Tonight, The Costume Institute of The Metropolitan Museum of Art will pay tribute to the late master’s 30-year career with the gala for “Charles James: Beyond Fashion,” which opens to the public May 8. Nearly 75 of the 200 designs ever completed by James will be on display at the newly christened Anna Wintour Costume Center and first-floor Special Exhibition Galleries. And to accompany this retrospective, an eponymous book has been written by its curators Harold Koda and Jan Glier Reeder, cataloguing the work on view.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05james-curkin2/05james-curkin2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05james-curkin2/05james-curkin2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 789}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05james-curkin2/05james-curkin2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 779, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/t-magazine/05james-curkin2/05james-curkin2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1558, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': Non