309e6e-d6e9-5e02-9b88-4de9bf7f9225'}, {'abstract': 'Tear-drinking in the wild may be common, but isn’t seen often, says an aquatic ecologist in Costa Rica who witnessed just that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/science/butterfly-and-bee-stop-at-crying-croc-for-a-drink.html', 'snippet': 'Tear-drinking in the wild may be common, but isn’t seen often, says an aquatic ecologist in Costa Rica who witnessed just that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A butterfly and a bee were seen, above, sipping the tears of a spectacled caiman (Caiman crocodilus) along the Río Puerto Viejo in northeastern Costa Rica. The insects were probably seeking protein and salt. Tear drinking in the wild may be common but not often seen, said Carlos de la Rosa, an aquatic ecologist at La Selva Biological Station in Costa Rica who witnessed the event.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06FLOA/06FLOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06FLOA/06FLOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06FLOA/06FLOA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06FLOA/06FLOA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06FLOA/06FLOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', '