': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a642b458-3289-5556-ba00-2b07a15b8f22', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a642b458-3289-5556-ba00-2b07a15b8f22'}, {'abstract': 'Officials in Englewood Cliffs, N.J., are considering a master zoning plan that would allow even more high-rise developments of up to 150 feet in the area near the LG headquarters.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/05/more-blight-for-the-palisades/', 'snippet': 'Officials in Englewood Cliffs, N.J., are considering a master zoning plan that would allow even more high-rise developments of up to 150 feet in the area near the LG headquarters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LG Electronics USA has been facing a growing outcry about the company’s plan to build a 143-foot tall headquarters along the Palisades Park in New Jersey. That tower, which will stretch far above the tree line, will permanently deface the view along a once-protected stretch of the Hudson River. Politicians, environmentalists, architectural critics, outraged citizens\xa0and even potential\xa0LG customers have appealed to the company to lower this tower to the traditional limit of 35 feet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Blight for the Palisades?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LG Electronics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Palisades (Hudson River)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T20:16:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eleanor Randolph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eleanor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Randolph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt:/