ct their salivary glands. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06SUBGLOBAL/06global-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06SUBGLOBAL/06global-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06SUBGLOBAL/06global-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06SUBGLOBAL/06global-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1076, 'width': 1496, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06SUBGLOBAL/06global-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06SUBGLOBAL/06global-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/science/06SUBGLOBAL/06global-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Goal to Combat Malaria With the Help of a Robot', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Goal to Combat Malaria With the Help of a Robot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanaria Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-05T20:56:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a448b302-ebe5-5044-89fc-5fc2097f6ea2', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a448b302-ebe5-5044-89fc-5fc2097f6ea2'}, {'abstract': '“Homefront & Battlefield: Quilts and Context in the Civil War,” at the New-York Historical Society, makes clear that textiles were at the heart of the conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/arts/design/homefront-and-battlefield-looks-at-civil-war-quilts.html', 'snippet': '“Homefront & Battlefield: Quilts and Context in the Civil War,” at the New-York Historical Society, makes clear that textiles were at the heart of the conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance, this exhibition might seem a bit quaint, its subject — textiles and the Civil War — evoking Americana more than American history. But this show, “Homefront & Battlefield: Quilts and Context in the Civil War,” which opened last month at the New-York Historical Society after originating at the American Textile History Museum in Lowell, Mass., does much more: It turns Americana back into history. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/arts/06QUILTS1/06QUILTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name'