olice chief on Monday, prompting the City Council to end debate on a charter amendment that would transfer authority for picking the police chief from the mayor to voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/us/new-mexico-new-protests-against-albuquerque-police.html', 'snippet': 'Protesters in Albuquerque threw fake arrest warrants at the police chief on Monday, prompting the City Council to end debate on a charter amendment that would transfer authority for picking the police chief from the mayor to voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Protesters in Albuquerque threw fake arrest warrants at the police chief on Monday, prompting the City Council to end debate on a charter amendment that would transfer authority for picking the police chief from the mayor to voters. The protest came two days after an officer fatally shot Armand Martin, the 25th person killed by the police here since January 2010. The Justice Department recently released a report rebuking the Police Department for systematically using excessive force. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Mexico: New Protests Against Albuquerque Police', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Mexico: New Protests Against Albuquerque Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBUQUERQUE (NM)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T02:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Jennings', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jennings', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_