/2014/05/06/t-magazine/murray-moss-tertium-quid-book-hauser-wirth.html', 'snippet': 'Murray Moss, the man behind the now-shuttered Manhattan design boutique Moss, has embarked on an unexpected side project in which he pairs vintage press photos that suggest bizarre new narratives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the veteran design entrepreneur Murray Moss, 2012 was a year of turning points. It saw the closing of his fabled SoHo boutique Moss, and it was also the year he was diagnosed with Parkinson’s. He soon discovered that his medication had a number of side effects. “They keep me up late at night,” he says, “and they increase my already compulsive nature.” He sought to turn these new traits to his advantage by combing through hundreds of vintage press photos in the wee hours, and combining them to create surprising, often funny visual conversations. “This is what I used to do, literally daily, for 18 years, with the objects I displayed at the store,” Moss says. “Now I exercise this obsession with juxtapositions I make with press photographs instead of objects. It’s like making a movie and filming multiple endings.” His efforts are showcased in his new book, “Tertium Quid” ($75), due out later this month in a limited print run.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Design Curator Murray Moss, a Book of Unexpected Juxtapositions', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Rubinstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubinstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0dd1c2b-efba-5956-93fc-a5536bee3420', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0dd1c2b-efba-5956-93fc-a5536bee3420'}, {'abstract': 'In an exclusive video interview, the chef discusses Basque cuisine and the importance of family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/t-magazine/elena-arzak-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'In an exclusive video interview, the chef discusses Basque cuisine and the importance of family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week we introduced readers to Elena Arzak, one of only two women chefs named to the 2014 World’s 50 Best Restaurants list for her family’s restaurant, Arzak, which she runs with her father Juan Mari Arzak. Here, Elena invites T into her restaurant, perfectly located, she says in the above video, in the seaside town of San Sebastián. Step into her beautifully orchestrated kitchen as she discusses Basque cuisine, the creative and modern influence El Bulli had on her regional cooking and the importance of family — from her secret to working seamlessly with her chef father to the value of a balanced and lip-smacking staff meal. “The staff meal or family meal is really important,” she says. “It has to be very well made, very well cooked, no different from what goes out to the restaurant.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside Elena Arzak’s Kitchen', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9ee2f05-727d-5093-8791-c0b14aef312f', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9ee2f05-727d-5093-8791-c0b14aef312f'}, {'abstract': 'The Getty Foundation is announcing the 40 grant recipients for its $5 million Latin American art project.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/arts/design/getty-to-jump-start-latin-american-art-research-in-california.html', 'snippet': 'The Getty Foundation is announcing the 40 grant recipients for its $5 million Latin American art project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The ambitious regionwide arts collaboration known as Pacific Standard Time, which three years ago focused on Southern California art from 1945 to 1980, will have for its sequel a broader but still relatively underexamined field: Latin American art.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getty to Jump-Start Latin American Art Research in California', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Latin American Art Receives Support From Getty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finkel, Jori', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Getty, J Paul, Trust', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T04:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jori Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4d55bc8-b20b-5b9a-a5ce-0b1e70710a17', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4d55bc8-b20b-5b9a-a5ce-0b1e70710a17'}, {'abstract': 'One of the civilian divers searching for victims of the South Korean ferry disaster died on Tuesday after losing consciousness underwater, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/world/asia/south-korea-ferry-diver-dies.html', 'snippet': 'One of the civilian divers searching for victims of the South Korean ferry disaster died on Tuesday after losing consciousness underwater, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' One of the civilian divers searching for victims of the South Korean ferry disaster died on Tuesday\xa0after losing consciousness underwater, officials said. The diver, identified as Lee Gwang-ok, 53, was employed by a salvage company that worked with Navy divers in the now three-week-old effort to recover bodies from the 6,825-ton ferry Sewol, which capsized and sank off southwestern South Korea on April 16. The divers have struggled against strong currents and poor visibility to reach the ship and then make their way through a dark maze of corridors and cabins clogged with debris. As of\xa0Tuesday, 39 people remained missing, with 263 confirmed dead. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Korea: Ferry Diver Dies', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea: Ferry Diver Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ferries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T04:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/494e2804-d6ad