ical class.” And making a killing in the media instead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike Rogers keeps telling me how fed up he is with all of the “brand identity politicians” he is serving alongside in the United States Congress. And by this, the Republican from Michigan means those colleagues who would rather raise their profiles and get into the media and “do that celebrity thing” than, say, pass bills or help constituents or win the respect of peers. “They are all about their brand,” Rogers laments, drawing out the word with an extra disdainful beat: “BRAAH-und.” This, of course, is one reason that Rogers has decided to cede his chairmanship of the House Intelligence Committee, and all the loudmouths in the People’s Chamber that come with it, for his very own talk-radio show. In March, he announced his decision to leave behind the “whole celebrity political class in Washington, D.C.” for what is expected to be a nationally syndicated gig with Cumulus Media. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11politics/mag-11Politics-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11politics/mag-11Politics-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11politics/mag-11Politics-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11politics/mag-11Politics-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbna