onal Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chappatte, Patrick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T11:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e21f1ab8-06bd-52bc-98ed-717b32aeda9b', 'word_count': 8, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e21f1ab8-06bd-52bc-98ed-717b32aeda9b'}, {'abstract': 'Hedge fund managers are getting richer. | Bayer is buying Merck’s consumer care business. | At Berkshire Hathaway, a culture of trust. | Barclays’ first-quarter earnings declined.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/morning-agenda-a-haul-for-hedge-fund-moguls/', 'snippet': 'Hedge fund managers are getting richer. | Bayer is buying Merck’s consumer care business. | At Berkshire Hathaway, a culture of trust. | Barclays’ first-quarter earnings declined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hedge fund managers, who heavily populate the so-called 1 percent in the United States, are getting richer. The 25 highest-earning hedge fund managers in the United States took home a total of $21.15 billion in compensation in 2013, according to an annual ranking published on Tuesday by Institutional Investor’s Alpha magazine, DealBook’s Alexandra Stevenson writes. The payday, earned in a year when most hedge fund managers fell short of market performance, is the highest since 2010 and 50 percent more than in 2012. No women placed among the top 50.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Big Haul for Hedge Fund Moguls', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T11:49:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8ff57ec-dccf-536a-ad16-f051bb3aeff1', 'word_count': 1854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8ff57ec-dccf-536a-ad16-f051bb3aeff1'}, {'abstract': 'At one time, “deep-pocketed” may have seemed like a fresh and clever alternative to “wealthy.” That was probably quite a while ago.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/words-we-love-too-much-12/', 'snippet': 'At one time, “deep-pocketed” may have seemed like a fresh and clever alternative to “wealthy.” That was probably quite a while ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A colleague noted six uses of the description “deep-pocketed” in our copy in a single week not long ago. There were four more appearances during another recent week: “deep-pocketed investors,” “deep-pocketed donors” and “deep-pocketed tobacco companies” (twice).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Words We Love Too Much', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T12:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By PHILIP B. CORBETT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5645dbc6-3a44-556c-bb08-8d0283f9ada6', 'word_count': 1160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5645dbc6-3a44-556c-bb08-8d0283f9ada6'}, {'abstract': 'The actress sings the number “I Can’t Give You Anything but Love” from the Broadway musical revue “After Midnight.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/in-performance-vanessa-williams-of-after-midnight/', 'snippet': 'The actress sings the number “I Can’t Give You Anything but Love” from the Broadway musical revue “After Midnight.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s video features the actress Vanessa Williams singing the number “I Can’t Give You Anything but Love,” written by Dorothy Fields and Jimmy McHugh, from the Broadway musical revue “After Midnight.” Ms. Williams is performing in the show at the Brooks Atkinson Theater through May 11.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Vanessa Williams of ‘After Midnight’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fields, Dorothy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Vanessa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T12:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c751826-503f-5411-bf30-a6bdb377947e', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c751826-503f-5411-bf30-a6bdb377947e'}, {'abstract': 'The company has created an app that has a large following among professional photographers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/vsco-a-digital-photography-company-raises-40-million-from-accel-partners/', 'snippet': 'The company has created an app that has a large following among professional photographers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chances are, if you have used Instagram, you have come across the hashtag #VSCO or #VSCOCam.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None,