f unseasonal rain and hailstorms, the ban comes as further bad news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUMBAI, India — The Indian mango, and in particular the Alphonso, is a much-coveted and much-fetishized fruit by Indians, loved as much for its flavor as for its scarcity. Because of its rarity the fruit has achieved\xa0near-mythical importance\xa0in India, where access to mangoes early in the season is a sign of prestige.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/05-mangoes-IndiaInk/05-mangoes-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/05-mangoes-IndiaInk/05-mangoes-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/05-mangoes-IndiaInk/05-mangoes-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/05-mangoes-IndiaInk/05-mangoes-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/05-mangoes-IndiaInk/05-mangoes-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/05-mangoes-IndiaInk/05-mangoes-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/05/world/asia/05-mangoes-IndiaInk/05-mangoes-IndiaInk