, 'snippet': '“Breastmilk,” an agenda-free documentary by Dana Ben-Ari, observes the nursing journeys of five new mothers in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether spraying or leaking, massaged by hand or pumped by machine, the breasts of the young mothers in “Breastmilk” are arguably more active than the infants they nourish. Cheerfully exposed or decorously veiled, the functioning of these workhorses may be life-sustaining, but, as Dana Ben-Ari’s admirably agenda-free documentary reveals, it can also be shockingly stressful.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/arts/07BREASTMILK/07BREASTMILK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/07/arts/07BREASTMILK/07BREASTMILK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/arts/07BREASTMILK/07BREASTMILK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/arts/07BREASTMILK/07BREASTMILK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1008, 'width': 1548, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/arts/07BREASTMILK/07BREASTMILK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/07/arts/07BREASTMILK/07BREASTMILK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/arts/0