N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T23:37:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh and Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/726a9bc0-7843-57e0-895c-af366fd12da8', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/726a9bc0-7843-57e0-895c-af366fd12da8'}, {'abstract': 'Kara Goucher, a two-time Olympian, is the only top professional runner to represent two major sponsors, one for shoes and one for clothing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/sports/second-top-runner-is-signed-by-skechers.html', 'snippet': 'Kara Goucher, a two-time Olympian, is the only top professional runner to represent two major sponsors, one for shoes and one for clothing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks after Meb Keflezighi won the Boston Marathon in Skechers, the brand added another distance star, Kara Goucher, to its sponsorship roster. The deal gives the shoe line, more commonly known for its fashion footwear, two of America’s most established and popular distance runners. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Second Top Runner Is Signed by Skechers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Skechers Signs Another Top Runner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crouse, Lindsay', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skechers USA Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goucher, Kara', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keflezighi, Mebrahtom', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sneakers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T23:37:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f41eda7-84f5-50ce-a5fb-596aee2ee55e', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f41eda7-84f5-50ce-a5fb-596aee2ee55e'}, {'abstract': 'The two science academies under Pope Francis hold a rare joint meeting to chart paths to sustainable development.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/06/can-a-pope-help-sustain-humanity-and-ecology/', 'snippet': 'The two science academies under Pope Francis hold a rare joint meeting to chart paths to sustainable development.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — For four long days, several dozen physical, environmental and social scientists hunkered here with theologians, philosophers, economists and a poverty campaigner to explore ways to balance human ambitions with the planet’s limits. The rare joint meeting of the Pontifical Academy of Sciences and Pontifical Academy of Social Sciences — “Sustainable Humanity, Sustainable Nature, Our Responsibility” — helped demarcate where science leaves off and the rest of society, including organized religion, plays a role in shaping the quality of human life and environmental conditions in this century.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/blogs/dotpope/dotpope-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/06/blogs/dotpope/dotpope-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/blogs/dotpope/dotpope-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/blogs/dotpope/dotpope-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/blogs/dotpope/dotpope-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/06/blogs/dotpope/dotpope-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/06/blogs/dotpope/dotpope-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can a Pope Help Sustain Humanity and Ecology?', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vatican City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-06T23:42:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/413807c1-a779-5181-a6ce-0cfee1a6a8e8', 'word_count': 1856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/413807c1-a779-5181-a6ce-0cfee1a6a8e8'}, {'abstract': 'The Vatican presented itself as a model of reform before a United Nations committee reviewing the Holy See’s compliance with an international treaty prohibiting torture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/world/europe/vatican-tells-of-848-priests-ousted-in-last-decade.html', 'snippet': 'The Vatican presented itself as a model of reform before a United Nations committee reviewing the Holy See’s compliance with an international treaty prohibiting torture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The Vatican has dismissed more than 800 priests for sexual abuse of children in the past decade and paid billions of dollars in compensation, senior Vatican officials told a United Nations panel on Tuesday, presenting the Roman Catholic Church as a model of reform but drawing the ire of victims’ groups that said it still seeks to dodge responsibility for the harm that priests continue to inflict.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/world/VATICAN/VATICAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/07/world/VATICAN/VATICAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'ca