 None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29f42ea6-5167-5689-abce-3d1deba3668d', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29f42ea6-5167-5689-abce-3d1deba3668d'}, {'abstract': 'For the upcoming art and design fairs in New York and the sixth annual Monumenta art exhibition in the Grand Palais in Paris, art-inspired designs make for obvious outfits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/t-magazine/art-and-fashion-are-at-it-again.html', 'snippet': 'For the upcoming art and design fairs in New York and the sixth annual Monumenta art exhibition in the Grand Palais in Paris, art-inspired designs make for obvious outfits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last October, in Paris, Karl Lagerfeld transformed the Grand Palais into a white-walled art gallery filled with Chanel-themed paintings and sculptures for his spring/summer 2014 runway — a motif which seemed to officially set up this year’s warm-weather fashion landscape as one intertwined and imbued with art. And now that the season has arrived, the connection is undeniable. As fashion editors gear up for art and design shows opening both here and there — New York’s Collective 2 design fair on Thursday and Frieze Art Fair on Friday, and Paris’s Monumenta art exhibition at the Grand Palais on Saturday — obvious outfit choices abound, from artist’s-sketch-covered separates to sculptural bangles fit for a ceramist’s studio.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07market-gilchrist/07market-gilchrist-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07market-gilchrist/07market-gilchrist-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07market-gilchrist/07market-gilchrist-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07market-gilchrist/07market-gilchrist-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07market-gilchrist/07market-gilchrist-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07market-gilchrist/07market-gilchrist-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07market-gilchrist/07market-gilchrist-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art and Fashion Are at It Again', 'kicker': 'Market Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TCulture', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d4b7b56-3ed0-5b36-a34e-6ea6def1ce1c', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d4b7b56-3ed0-5b36-a34e-6ea6def1ce1c'}, {'abstract': 'The ambitious second edition of the fair at Moynihan Station, featuring an international roster of galleries and talent, opens tomorrow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/t-magazine/collective-2-fair-frieze-new-york-nada-hella-jongerius.html', 'snippet': 'The ambitious second edition of the fair at Moynihan Station, featuring an international roster of galleries and talent, opens tomorrow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend sees the return of two hugely successful contemporary art fairs to New York, Frieze New York and NADA, which are set to fill the streets with collectors and fashionable folk from across the globe. But it also marks the kick-off for a month-long marathon of design events, openings, fairs, conferences and parties. The first is Collective 2, the second annual collectible design fair, which was started last year by the architect Steven Learner. It opens tomorrow at Moynihan Station.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07collective-rubinstein1/07collective-rubinstein1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07collective-rubinstein1/07collective-rubinstein1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07collective-rubinstein1/07collective-rubinstein1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07collective-rubinstein1/07collective-rubinstein1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07collective-rubinstein1/07collective-rubinstein1-th