nk': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajagopal, P', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T04:11:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rollo Romig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rollo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55e60dbc-59c6-58d2-acb0-b3e201682e99', 'word_count': 4507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55e60dbc-59c6-58d2-acb0-b3e201682e99'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on May 7, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/pageoneplus/corrections-may-7-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on May 7, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: May 7, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T04:38:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/250385e3-fc27-5a1f-93b7-4ed979737c84', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/250385e3-fc27-5a1f-93b7-4ed979737c84'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:50 P.M. (Starz Cinema) FAREWELL, MY QUEEN (2012) Sidonie Laborde (Léa Seydoux, above left, with Julie-Marie Parmentier), the reader to Marie Antoinette (Diane Kruger) at Versailles, watches as the French monarchy falls in this drama directed by Benoît Jacquot from a novel by Chantal Thomas. Noémie Lvovsky portrays the queen’s lady-in-waiting; Virginie Ledoyen is the woman rumored to be the queen’s lover. “If the rules and the players of this continuing, increasingly dangerous court intrigue remain obscure, it’s because ‘Farewell, My Queen’ is told through Sidonie’s eyes,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “Tapping her palace sources, notably an archivist (Michel Robin) and a dressmaker (Anne Benoît), Sidonie learns of news known only to the nobility and their trusted stewards: that the Bastille has been seized.” Mr. Jacquot, she added, “has always been a sensitive director of actresses, his sympathies evident in his caressing, sometimes ogling camerawork and the time and space he gives women and their stories. That sympathy is evident here too, though crucially, while he doesn’t demonize Marie Antoinette, he doesn’t turn her into a spurious feminist martyr.” In French, with English subtitles.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T05:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa2c4841-38ec-5221-b659-ef2ea962f816', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa2c4841-38ec-5221-b659-ef2ea962f816'}, {'abstract': 'Hiroki Kuroda allowed just one earned run over seven and two-thirds innings, and Brian Roberts broke a 3-3 tie with a homer in the ninth to salvage a win in Anaheim.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/sports/baseball/late-homer-by-roberts-carries-yankees-past-angels.html', 'snippet': 'Hiroki Kuroda allowed just one earned run over seven and two-thirds innings, and Brian Roberts broke a 3-3 tie with a homer in the ninth to salvage a win in Anaheim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANAHEIM, Calif. — When Brian Roberts came to the plate with two outs in the ninth inning, the game tied and the Yankees in fairly urgent need of a win, he did not require any fancy scouting reports on the opposing pitcher, the fastball artist Ernesto Frieri. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strong Start by Kuroda and Late Homer by Roberts Lift Yankees', 'kicker': 'Yankees 4, Angels 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strong Start by Kuroda and Late Homer by Roberts Lift Yankees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Brian (1977- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T05:31:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbb337f4-b9b1-5a53-a46c-7f6ee872af61', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbb337f4-b9b1-5a53-a46c-7f6ee872af61'}, {'abstract': 'Polls suggested that President Jacob Zuma’s African National Congress will steamroll to victory, but with less support than in the past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/world/africa/south-africans-vote-as-president-zuma-seeks-second-term.html', 'snippet': 'Polls sugges