'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4cd172b-2be4-5968-94a7-cf4c595fc78d', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4cd172b-2be4-5968-94a7-cf4c595fc78d'}, {'abstract': 'Citing restructuring and other charges, AOL said its first-quarter profit dropped to $9.3 million, or 11 cents a share, from $25.9 million a year earlier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/business/media/aol-revenue-increases-but-special-charges-depress-profit.html', 'snippet': 'Citing restructuring and other charges, AOL said its first-quarter profit dropped to $9.3 million, or 11 cents a share, from $25.9 million a year earlier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Armstrong, the chief executive of AOL, the giant media and advertising technology company, has said that it was poised for significant long-term growth. On Wednesday investors displayed their skepticism — resoundingly. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/AOL/AOL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1462, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/business/AOL/AOL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1462}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/AOL/AOL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 421, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/AOL/AOL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 841, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/AOL/AOL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/08/business/AOL/AOL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/AOL/AOL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'AOL Profit Slides 64%, Sending Its Shares Down 20%', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'AOL Profit Slides 64%, Sending Its Shares Down 20%', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaufman, Leslie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AOL Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T13:58:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cd7eb66-a61b-5a10-818e-9249e549df97', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cd7eb66-a61b-5a10-818e-9249e549df97'}, {'abstract': 'Republican concern is similar to that in the Middle East. Democratic concern is closer to Europe’s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/upshot/on-climate-republicans-and-democrats-are-from-different-continents.html', 'snippet': 'Republican concern is similar to that in the Middle East. Democratic concern is closer to Europe’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans are less worried about climate change than the residents of any other high-income country, as my colleague Megan Thee-Brennan wrote Tuesday. When you look at the details of these polls, you see that American exceptionalism on the climate stems almost entirely from Republicans. Democrats and independents don’t look so different from people in Japan, Australia, Canada and across Europe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Climate, Republicans and Democrats Are From Different Continents', 'kicker': 'Debate That Divides', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T13:58:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c67a4101-0520-5ab6-8627-0c390312aa81', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c67a4101-0520-5ab6-8627-0c390312aa81'}, {'abstract': 'Hispanics are expected to make up the majority of American Catholics in the next two decades, but more Hispanics are also forsaking Catholicism and becoming religiously unaffiliated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/upshot/even-as-hispanics-lift-catholicism-theyre-leaving-it.html', 'snippet': 'Hispanics are expected to make up the majority of American Catholics in the next two decades, but more Hispanics are also forsaking Catholicism and becoming religiously unaffiliated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By all accounts, Hispanics are the future of Catholicism in America. Already, most young Roman Catholics in the United States are Hispanic, and soon that will be true of the overall Catholic population. But the Hispanicization of American Catholicism faces a big challenge: Hispanics are leaving Catholicism at a striking rate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/upshot/08UP-Hispanic/08UP-Hispanic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/07/upshot/08UP-Hispanic/08UP-Hispanic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/upshot/08UP-Hispanic/08UP-Hispanic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/upshot/08UP-Hispanic/08UP-Hispanic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/upshot/08UP-Hispanic/08UP-Hispanic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/07/upshot/08UP-Hispanic/08UP-Hispanic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima