ntended to continue the stimulus campaign that it considered at least partly responsible.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/Yellen/Yellen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 263, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/business/Yellen/Yellen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 263}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/Yellen/Yellen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/Yellen/Yellen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 898, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/Yellen/Yellen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/08/business/Yellen/Yellen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/Yellen/Yellen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yellen Won’t Be Pinned Down on Plans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yellen Won’t Be Pinned Down on Plans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appelbaum, Binyamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T14:14:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcc6e6f4-5ee5-5ebc-b5d5-3572e8c8e6fd', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcc6e6f4-5ee5-5ebc-b5d5-3572e8c8e6fd'}, {'abstract': 'Thom Tillis, who just won the state’s Republican primary, has been the point-man in a sadly effective anti-government project.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/there-are-no-mainstream-republicans-left-in-north-carolina/', 'snippet': 'Thom Tillis, who just won the state’s Republican primary, has been the point-man in a sadly effective anti-government project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The national Republican Party is exulting that the “establishment” won in North Carolina’s Senate primary yesterday. That’s only because they have redefined the term “Republican establishment” to include adamant adherents of a far-right ideology.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There Are No Mainstream Republicans Left in North Carolina', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tillis, Thomas R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T14:18:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c6dfe15-6b44-5fd8-b2c8-d7a0f9243ee9', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c6dfe15-6b44-5fd8-b2c8-d7a0f9243ee9'}, {'abstract': 'Four artists have been nominated for the £25,000 (or $42,428) prize, given annually to an artist who is either British or living in Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/turner-prize-nominees-announced-2/', 'snippet': 'Four artists have been nominated for the £25,000 (or $42,428) prize, given annually to an artist who is either British or living in Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Dances, screen prints, YouTube clips and slideshows are all elements used in the work of this year’s Turner Prize nominees, who were announced on Wednesday by Tate Britain, where an exhibition of the four artists’ work will take place from Sept. 30 to Jan. 4.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turner Prize Nominees Announced', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turner Prize', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tate Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T14:19:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4aca9fb3-d561-57d3-8884-de074b039233', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4aca9fb3-d561-57d3-8884-de074b039233'}, {'abstract': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia pressed pause on Wednesday in what had begun to look like an inevitable march toward war in Ukraine, but world leaders questioned whether it was a feint.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/world/europe/Putin-Russia-Ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia pressed pause on Wednesday in what had begun to look like an inevitable march toward war in Ukraine, but world leaders questioned whether it was a feint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — President Vladimir V. Putin, faced with rising violence in southeastern Ukraine that threatened to draw in the Russian Army at great cost and prompt severe new Western economic sanctions, pressed pause on Wednesday in what had started to look like an inevitable march toward war.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/world/08putin1_now/08putin1_now-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/world/08putin1_now/08putin1_now-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/world/08putin1_now/08putin1_now-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/world/08putin1_now/08putin1_now-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1342, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/world/08putin1_now/08putin1_now-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/08/world/08putin1_now/08putin1_now-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/world/08putin1_now/08putin1_now-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putin Announces Pullback From Ukraine Border', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putin Hits Pause in Ukraine Crisis Amid Skepticism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crimea (Ukraine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T14:35:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d90a444-d017-5914-8057-6890ea781688', 'word_count': 1636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d90a444-d017-5914-8057-6890ea781688'}, {'abstract': 'Just in time for Mother’s Day, the natural dye guru Jane Palmer and the artist Christy Matson have collaborated on a new series of luxurious — and socially and environmentally virtuous — home accessories.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/feeling-for-decadent-cashmere-blankets-with-a-planet-friendly-pedigree/', 'snippet': 'Just in time for Mother’s Day, the natural dye guru Jane Palmer and the artist Christy Matson have collaborated on a new series of luxurious — and socially and environmentally virtuous — home accessories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just how much good karma can be packed into a single home accessory? Quite a bit, as evidenced by a new series of limited-edition cashmere blankets made by Jane Palmer of Noon Design Studio — the fashion industry’s eminent natural dye house, which is also known for its popular indigo kits and decorative housewares — and the artist Christy Matson. Carpet-thick yet feather-light, the blankets are hand-loomed by Matson in Los Angeles on the same jacquard machine she uses in her fine-art practice. The lofty cashmere yarn is not only hand-twisted by members of a women’s cooperative in Afghanistan, but also — two degrees of virtuousness — sourced directly from fashion houses that would otherwise have discarded it. The rich, variegated colors are hand-dyed by Palmer using flowers, leaves and minerals; the jet-black hue comes from a dye recipe of roots, bark and indigo that dates back to medieval times. Each is one of a kind; custom designs are also available by special order. Palmer and Matson have set aside a small number of the blankets for T readers, and can ship overnight — just in time for a (very decadent) last-minute Mother’s Day gift.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08noon-hartman/08noon-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08noon-hartman/08noon-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08noon-hartman/08noon-hartman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08noon-hartman/08noon-hartman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08noon-hartman/08noon-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08noon-hartman/08noon-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08noon-hartman/08noon-hartman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | Decadent Cashmere Blankets With a Planet-Friendly Pedigree', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'By Design: Soft but Strong', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T14:44:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7f991d0-ee54-5b27-8789-7f7a9b61ace7', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7f991d0-ee54-5b27