aid the charges were a political vendetta brought on by his plans to publish a book condemning the Chinese Communist Party leader, Xi Jinping.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hong Kong Publisher’s Prison Sentence Is Called a Political Vendetta', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Hong Kong Publisher Planning Critical Book Is Sentenced in Smuggling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yiu Mantin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shenzhen (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T18:53:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45aa777b-effb-5cd1-a093-905d664d68e6', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45aa777b-effb-5cd1-a093-905d664d68e6'}, {'abstract': 'Ruth Reichl, the food writer and former Gourmet editor, discusses her newfound love of Twitter. But her tweets are written in a style that is all her own.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/can-you-tweet-like-ruth-reichl/', 'snippet': 'Ruth Reichl, the food writer and former Gourmet editor, discusses her newfound love of Twitter. But her tweets are written in a style that is all her own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the magazine’s most recent Talk column, Ruth Reichl, the food writer and former Gourmet editor, discusses her newfound love of Twitter. “I discovered that I really loved the discipline of 140 characters,” she says. “It was a complete surprise to me that you could really paint a portrait of a moment.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/magazine/Reichl1/Reichl1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/07/magazine/Reichl1/Reichl1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/magazine/Reichl1/Reichl1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/magazine/Reichl1/Reichl1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/magazine/Reichl1/Reichl1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/07/magazine/Reichl1/Reichl1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/magazine/Reichl1/Reichl1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can You Tweet Like Ruth Reichl?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reichl, Ruth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T18:54:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannie Choi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Choi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/780373d2-fea7-5d44-95b7-522409982ffb', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/780373d2-fea7-5d44-95b7-522409982ffb'}, {'abstract': 'Sue Townsend’s Italian line of scented luxury products, Ortigia, is ideal for Mother’s Day gifting.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/ortigia-beauty-products-sue-townsend-mothers-day/', 'snippet': 'Sue Townsend’s Italian line of scented luxury products, Ortigia, is ideal for Mother’s Day gifting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sue Townsend, one of the original founders of Britain’s Crabtree & Evelyn,\xa0lives in a\xa015th-century palazzo in Florence\xa0and creates handsome-smelling products under her luxury beauty label Ortigia. Unlike Townsend, everything about the line is truly Sicilian, from the indigenous, natural ingredients to the scents, which evoke the Mediterranean landscape. Some embody local flora —\xa0the slightly stringent yet delicate Zagara, infused with orange blossoms, or the Sicilian Jasmine, distilled from local white flowers — while others transport, like the musky but honeysuckle-sweet Ambra Nera, infused with patchouli and vetiver and evocative of a warm, amorous night on the island. The calming Fico D’India scent is inspired by the cactus of the same name that grows wild along the beaches of Sicily.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07ortigia-beddie/07ortigia-beddie-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07ortigia-beddie/07ortigia-beddie-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07ortigia-beddie/07ortigia-beddie-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07ortigia-beddie/07ortigia-beddie-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07ortigia-beddie/07ortigia-beddie-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07ortigia-beddie/07ortigia-beddie-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07ortigia-beddie/07ortigia-beddie-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | Beauty Products to Whisk Mom Off to the Beaches of Sicily', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty (Concept)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Mother's Day", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T19:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2eb4072d-1b90-5f6d-a0d7-047828044a9c', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2eb4072d-1b90-5f6d-a0d7-047828044a9c'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Sam, a defensive end from Missouri who is openly gay, is considered a middle-round to late-round N.F.L. draft pick, and may not be drafted at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/sports/football/michael-sam-adds-a-gay-subplot-to-the-nfl-draft.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Sam, a defensive end from Missouri who is openly gay, is considered a middle-round to late-round N.F.L. draft pick, and may not be drafted at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.F.L. draft, an auction of athletic aptitude with primeval roots and prime-time appeal, will begin Thursday night with an unprecedented subplot. An openly gay player with impressive credentials is in the pool of candidates, casting the usually myopic, football-centric draft in a societywide spotlight with resonant cultural significance.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/sports/08sam1/08sam1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/sports/08sam1/08sam1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/sports/08sam1/08