_id': 'nyt://article/605ad405-70ea-526c-97de-19f461bd2135', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/605ad405-70ea-526c-97de-19f461bd2135'}, {'abstract': 'When a company moves its annual meeting far from its home base, it might be an effort to blunt adverse publicity, according to new research.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/business/beware-when-the-annual-meeting-is-in-moosejaw.html', 'snippet': 'When a company moves its annual meeting far from its home base, it might be an effort to blunt adverse publicity, according to new research.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A handful of annual company meetings draw attention because they are unusually celebratory, like Berkshire Hathaway’s huge gathering in Omaha each May, or because shareholders are able to mount public efforts to curb executive pay or objectionable practices. But most such gatherings are carefully scripted so there are no hiccups.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beware When the Annual Meeting Is in Moosejaw', 'kicker': 'Business Travel', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beware When the Annual Meeting Is in Moosejaw', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Elizabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T20:10:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Olson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ffcd961-bb5e-50ee-9b66-690d4251e125', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ffcd961-bb5e-50ee-9b66-690d4251e125'}, {'abstract': 'While citing “considerable progress” in strengthening the financial sector, the Financial Stability Oversight Council cautioned that threats remain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/business/economy/financial-oversight-council-warns-of-lingering-weak-spots-and-new-risks.html', 'snippet': 'While citing “considerable progress” in strengthening the financial sector, the Financial Stability Oversight Council cautioned that threats remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Some of the same weaknesses that contributed to the disastrous 2008 financial crisis persist today, the Financial Stability Oversight Council said in its 2014 annual report to Congress.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Financial Regulators See Progress and Threats', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Financial Regulators See Progress and Threats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowrey, Annie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Stability Oversight Council', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T20:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcbeb9dd-e08d-58a8-b3e5-d01b4c97516e', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcbeb9dd-e08d-58a8-b3e5-d01b4c97516e'}, {'abstract': 'Rivka Galchen’s collection, “American Innovations,” features tales inspired by classic short stories by writers including James Thurber, Nikolai Gogol and Jorge Luis Borges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/books/american-innovations-by-rivka-galchen.html', 'snippet': 'Rivka Galchen’s collection, “American Innovations,” features tales inspired by classic short stories by writers including James Thurber, Nikolai Gogol and Jorge Luis Borges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stories in “American Innovations,” the new collection by Rivka Galchen, the author of the 2008 novel “Atmospheric Disturbances,” don’t behave like typical short stories. Sure, they bear strong physical resemblances to selections you would find in an anthology with the words “Best American” in its title. Though Ms. Galchen favors misdirection and indirection, her writing is skillful, imaginative, often funny. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/arts/book/book-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/arts/book/book-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 766}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1718, 'width': 1345, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 