: [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corkery', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01982781-a510-5693-912e-3e66362d0e9d', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01982781-a510-5693-912e-3e66362d0e9d'}, {'abstract': '“The Fabulous Miss Marie,” a 1971 play revived by Woodie King Jr., features a former showgirl married to a parking valet, and a prodigious amount of drinking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/theater/fabulous-miss-marie-drinks-and-dances-at-castillo-theater.html', 'snippet': '“The Fabulous Miss Marie,” a 1971 play revived by Woodie King Jr., features a former showgirl married to a parking valet, and a prodigious amount of drinking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the title character of Ed Bullins’s “The Fabulous Miss Marie,” Tonya Pinkins wears a series of dresses cut low and slit high. One gown has leopard spots, another tiger stripes. (Perhaps her ocelot frock is at the dry cleaner’s?) Ms. Pinkins slinks around the Castillo Theater stage, yowling and purring as she sips Ambassador Scotch. When she sees a handsome young man, she toys with him for a while. Then she pounces.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/arts/fabulous/fabulous-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/arts/fabulous/fabulous-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 685}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/arts/fabulous/fabulous-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 898, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N