ing, once a rarity in China, is becoming more commonplace as increasing exposure to less physically reserved cultures lowers resistance to warm embraces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all the changes to sweep China since the death of Mao Zedong in 1976 — stock markets, private cars, fashion — one thing seemed not to have changed: No hugging. Chinese were physically reserved.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/world/07sino-hug/07sino-hug-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/07/world/07sino-hug/07sino-hug-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/world/07sino-hug/07sino-hug-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/world/07sino-hug/07sino-hug-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1324, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/world/07sino-hug/07sino-hug-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/07/world/07sino-hug/07sino-hug-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/world/07sino-hug/07sino-hug-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Hugs Please, We’re Chinese', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cautious Chinese Gain Comfort With Hugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Daily', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East China Sea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North America', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T22:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2284833d-3b59-5f40-aef2-3be68a3790a9', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2284833d-3b59-5f40-aef2-3be68a3790a9'}, {'abstract': 'The third edition of the art fair imported from London hits Randall’s Island this weekend, and features a host of compelling programs inside the tent and out.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/frieze-new-york-randalls-island/', 'snippet': 'The third edition of the art fair imported from London hits Randall’s Island this weekend, and features a host of compelling programs inside the tent and out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The third iteration of Frieze New York, which opens to V.I.P.s on Thursday and to the general public on Friday with more than 190 contemporary art galleries from 28 countries, is one of the world’s epicenters of pleasure for profit. So perhaps it’s fitting that this year the fair’s organizers embraced the pursuit of leisure via the complementary programming installed in and around the tent. “We wanted to interrupt the rhythms of the fair, going from booth to booth,” says Cecilia Alemani, the curator of Frieze Projects, the annual array of artworks commissioned for the fair, and Frieze Sounds, a series of audio works looped in the fair’s V.I.P. shuttles. “It is a marketplace, and we wanted to create a platform where what could be exchanged was also ideas.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07frieze-wu-slide-E5BD/07frieze-wu-slide-E5BD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07frieze-wu-slide-E5BD/07frieze-wu-slide-E5BD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07frieze-wu-slide-E5BD/07frieze-wu-slide-E5BD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07frieze-wu-slide-E5BD/07frieze-wu-slide-E5BD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1181, 'width': 1618, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/07/t-magazine/07frieze-wu-slide-E5BD/07frieze-wu-slide-E5BD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width':