: 'Studeman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/063e327e-4e8d-5c6f-aa85-0a9789b13dc9', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/063e327e-4e8d-5c6f-aa85-0a9789b13dc9'}, {'abstract': 'Who wore whom to the ball this year? A sampling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/fashion/the-met-gala-by-the-labels.html', 'snippet': 'Who wore whom to the ball this year? A sampling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a night when the Metropolitan Museum of Art was honoring Charles James, a designer known for his dramatic, structurally inventive ball gowns, it was not surprising that many of the guests, including two of the evening’s hosts, Sarah Jessica Parker and Aerin Lauder, chose to wear Oscar de la Renta, a designer whose work seems all but ready for a museum retrospective of its own. Or that Marchesa and Zac Posen, both operating in the less-is-never-more school of fashion design, would be well represented. But who would have guessed that Stella McCartney would come close to stealing the night with a posse of young stars, Rihanna and Reese Witherspoon among them, who turned the red carpet into their own personal party, or that the British retailer Topshop would have as many red-carpet credits as Prada? A selective look at who wore what on Monday night.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/fashion/08METBYNUMB2/08METBYNUMB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/fashion/08METBYNUMB2/08METBYNUMB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/fashion/08METBYNUMB2/08METBYNUMB2-