_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Milioti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Milioti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d878b262-beb1-576f-8485-9204a575029f', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d878b262-beb1-576f-8485-9204a575029f'}, {'abstract': 'Other Criteria, a shop that sells designs by the artist and his peers, just opened in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/garden/damien-hirst-plants-a-flag-in-soho.html', 'snippet': 'Other Criteria, a shop that sells designs by the artist and his peers, just opened in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Damien Hirst has brought his ebullient gestures to New York, with the Tuesday opening of Other Criteria, the retail arm of the British arts-based publishing company of the same name. The two-level 3,500-square-foot SoHo boutique was designed by Michel Schranz and is the first Other Criteria shop to break out of Britain (there are two in London, and one in Devon). Jason Beard, the creative director, said SoHo was chosen over other neighborhoods because: “It feels like London. It feels like home.” The shop features versions of Mr. Hirst’s spin art applied to rugs ($66,700), skulls and guitars. It also sells works by 35 other artists, including Gary Hume, Sarah Lucas, Peregrine Honig and Thomas Scheibitz. Offerings extend from tourist bait like key chains to prints, jewelry and artist-designed wallpaper and vases. A dollar will buy you an “I spot DH” pin. 458 Broome Street (Mercer Street). Information: 646-762-0123 or othercriteria.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/garden/08CURREVENTS/08CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/garden/08CURREVENTS/08CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/garden/08CURREVENTS/08CURR5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 882, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/garden/08CURREVENTS/08CURR5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 882, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/garden/08CURREVENTS/08CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/08/garden/08CURREVENTS/08CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/garden/08CURREVENTS/08CURR5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Damien Hirst Plants a Flag in SoHo', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Damien Hirst Plants a Flag in SoHo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suqi, Rima', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirst, Damien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Other Criteria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T22:57:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/240356f1-9320-5c37-bdfe-e508c68b72c7', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/240356f1-9320-5c37-bdfe-e508c68b72c7'}, {'abstract': '“Goodnight Nanny-Cam” pokes gently fun at the anxieties of modern parents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/garden/a-classic-again-ripe-for-an-update.html', 'snippet': '“Goodnight Nanny-Cam” pokes gently fun at the anxieties of modern parents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lizzy Ratner is a contributor to the Nation, reporting on serious subjects like politics, education and the economy. Jen Nessel is also a journalist, a former political organizer and the communications coordinator at the Center for Constitutional Rights. They are the mothers of Elias, 4, and Oscar, 8, and the authors of “Goodnight Nanny-Cam,” a new parody of the much-parodied children’s book (remember “Goodnight Keith Moon”?) that was first born as an essay in The New Yorker two years ago to skewer the affectations and anxieties of modern parenting.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/garden/08CURR6/08CURR6-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/garden/08CURR6/08CURR6-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/garden/08CURR6/08CURR6-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo',