 'snippet': 'Rashid Rehman, a human rights activist who had received threats for defending people charged under Pakistan’s blasphemy laws, was killed in his office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAHORE, Pakistan — Rashid Rehman, a veteran Pakistani human rights activist who had received threats for defending people charged under the country’s blasphemy laws, was shot dead on Wednesday night in his office in the southern city of Multan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistani Activist Shot Dead; Aided Blasphemy Suspects', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistani Activist Shot Dead; Aided Blasphemy Suspects', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rehman, Rashid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T23:39:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Waqar Gillani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Waqar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d465560-dd83-539c-8704-6d52d285d4e7', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d465560-dd83-539c-8704-6d52d285d4e7'}, {'abstract': '] The United States has closed its embassy in Yemen to the public because of security concerns, the State Department said in a statement on Wednesday, citing recent attacks against Western interests in Yemen as the reason for temporarily suspending operations at the embassy in Sana.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/world/americas/washington-embassy-in-yemen-shut.html', 'snippet': '] The United States has closed its embassy in Yemen to the public because of security concerns, the State Department said in a statement on Wednesday, citing recent attacks against Western interests in Yemen as the reason for temporarily suspendin...', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States has closed its embassy in Sana, the Yemeni capital, to the public because of security concerns, the State Department said on Wednesday, citing recent attacks against Western interests in Yemen as the reason for temporarily suspending operations. Embassy personnel are not being evacuated, but the closing will stop the processing of visas and other services. The department did not say how long the embassy would be closed to the public but stated that the potential threat to the embassy would be evaluated daily. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Embassy in Yemen Is Closed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Embassy in Yemen Is Closed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T23:43:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc3c575b-a136-5635-bf2e-19db7a90d9fb', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc3c575b-a136-5635-bf2e-19db7a90d9fb'}, {'abstract': 'PTSD never goes away. On bad days, it’s so close you can’t breathe. On good days, it’s off in the distance like a gathering storm.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/07/a-soldier-fights-off-the-cold/', 'snippet': 'PTSD never goes away. On bad days, it’s so close you can’t breathe. On good days, it’s off in the distance like a gathering storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — On Aug. 4, 2004, while in my Stryker combat vehicle battling insurgents for control of a street in Mosul, Iraq, I was struck by a rocket-propelled grenade. The core of the rocket, a solid piece of metal only a few inches long, sliced open my stomach from right to left, filled my legs and face with shrapnel, tore my intestines, lacerated my liver, destroyed my spleen, punctured my diaphragm, flattened my lungs, shattered my ribs and ruptured discs in my back. As I struggled to remove my smoldering body armor, I watched my stomach tear open and my intestines begin to push their way out. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/opinion/08PRIVATELIVES/08PRIVATELIVES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/opinion/08PRIVATELIVES/08PRIVATELIVES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 738}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/opinion/08PRIVATELIVES/08PRIVATELIVES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 833, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/opinion/08PRIVATELIVES/08PRIVATELIVES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1846, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/opinion/08PRIVATELIVES/08PRIVATELIVES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/08/opinion/08PRIVATELIVES/08PRIVATELIVES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/opinion/08PRIVATELIVES/08PRIVATELIVES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Soldier Fights Off the Cold', 'kicker': 'Private Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Soldier Fights Off the Cold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T23:43:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damon T. Armeni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damon', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Armeni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63838e57-c828-5a1b-b6d3-8ded745dacc5', 'word_count': 1380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63838e57-c828-5a1b-b6d3-8ded745dacc5'}, {'abstract': 'By the end of April, the Beijing government had collected 88 million renminbi, or $14 million, in fines levied during the first three months of this year against companies caught violating pollution standards, according to a news release from Beijing officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/world/asia/china-pollution-fines-multiply.html', 'snippet': 'By the end of April, the Beijing government had collected 88 million renminbi, or $14 million, in fines levied during the first three months of this year against companies caught violating pollution standards, according to a news release from Beij...', 'lead_paragraph': ' By the end of April, the Beijing government had collected 88 million renminbi, or $14 million, in fines levied during the first three months of this year against companies caught violating pollution standards, according to a news release from Beijing officials and a report on Wednesday in Beijing News, a daily newspaper. The amount is 10 times the total levied in the same period in 2013. More than 7,000 companies were fined in the first three months of this year by Beijing environmental protection officials, compared with 2,000 in the same period last year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Pollution Fines Multiply', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Pollution Fines Multiply', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beijing News, The', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-07T23:45:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': 