arming and can no longer be ignored.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/opinion/climate-disruptions-close-to-home.html', 'snippet': 'A new report on the effects of global warming on the United States is alarming and can no longer be ignored.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apart from the disinformation sowed by politicians content with the status quo, the main reason neither Congress nor much of the American public cares about global warming is that, as problems go, it seems remote. Anyone who reads the latest National Climate Assessment, released on Tuesday, cannot possibly think that way any longer. The report is exhaustive and totally alarming. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Disruptions, Close to Home', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Climate Disruptions, Close to Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'US Global Change Research Program (USGCRP)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T01:09:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/76510cc6-8347-51b4-909e-26ba4fc2469b', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76510cc6-8347-51b4-909e-26ba4fc2469b'}, {'abstract': 'Boko Haram, the Nigerian group that has carried out mass kidnappings, was rejected long ago by mainstream Muslims