sion to study building a women’s history museum in Washington, advancing an effort that has been stalled in Congress for more than a decade. Drafted by Representatives Carolyn B. Maloney, Democrat of New York, and Marsha Blackburn, Republican of Tennessee, the bill would create an eight-member panel to examine potential locations, including on or near the National Mall, and construction and maintenance details. The bill must be approved by the Senate, and the museum itself would require congressional approval. Some critics do not want to use taxpayer money on the project, and several conservatives groups have pressured lawmakers to oppose it because they believe it will reflect a liberal bias. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Approves Panel to Study Building Women’s Museum', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Approves Panel to Study Women’s Museum Despite Concerns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huetteman, Emmarie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'History (Academic Subject)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maloney, Carolyn B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blackburn, Marsha', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T02:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname':