rd_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38fd5dc5-7d4e-5422-beb8-81d5e4946e77'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese authorities, who are wary of dissent as the occasion approaches, arrested the outspoken Gao Yu under a state secrets law that critics call vague and overly broad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/world/asia/dissident-journalist-held-ahead-of-tiananmen-anniversary.html', 'snippet': 'Chinese authorities, who are wary of dissent as the occasion approaches, arrested the outspoken Gao Yu under a state secrets law that critics call vague and overly broad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An outspoken Chinese journalist who was jailed after the armed crackdown of 1989 has been detained in Beijing on charges of obtaining and leaking a confidential Communist Party document, a state-run news agency reported\xa0on Thursday. The report said the journalist, Gao Yu, had admitted to the crime and was “willing to accept legal punishment.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dissident Journalist Held Ahead of Tiananmen Anniversary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dissident Journalist Held Ahead of Tiananmen Anniversary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gao Yu', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tiananmen Square (Beijing)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T03:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cb511c0-c522-502d-815f-d86c3d85297c', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cb511c0-c522-502d-815f-d86c3d85297c'}, {'abstract': 'It was another bumpy night at the spring auctions, the second of the week’s evening sales of Impressionist and modern art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/nyregion/mediocre-night-at-sothebys-as-one-third-of-the-art-does-not-sell.html', 'snippet': 'It was another bumpy night at the spring auctions, the second of the week’s evening sales of Impressionist and modern art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was another bumpy night at the spring auctions, the second of the week’s evening sales of Impressionist and modern art. On Wednesday, many in the art world converged upon Sotheby’s, where nearly a third of the art went unsold. Paintings and sculptures by masters like Degas, Renoir and Picasso were either overpriced or were just not good enough to tempt buyers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty