ern; Julia Louis-Dreyfus, for Nicole Holofcener’s film “Enough Said” and the HBO series “Veep”; “The Colbert Report”; Jason Bateman, for Netflix’s “Arrested Development”; “Louis C.K.: Oh My God”; and “Bound 3,” starring James Franco and Seth Rogen. Bill Hader, Johnny Knoxville, Leslie Mann, Stephen Merchant, Aubrey Plaza and J. B. Smoove are among the presenters. The house band is Craig Robinson & the Nasty Delicious.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T05:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/422090b8-f973-5dff-a3f3-cdd4edc825ac', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/422090b8-f973-5dff-a3f3-cdd4edc825ac'}, {'abstract': 'With 83 percent of the votes counted, interim figures showed the party was in danger of winning a smaller share of the vote than it did in 2009.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/world/africa/south-african-vote.html', 'snippet': 'With 83 percent of the votes counted, interim figures showed the party was in danger of winning a smaller share of the vote than it did in 2009.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — South Africa’s long-ruling African National Congress was headed to another big victory in national elections on Thursday, though it appeared to fall short of President Jacob G. Zuma’s goal of a two-thirds majority, incomplete results showed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New Yo