'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0971a2a-17f9-51c9-a114-8da12bdf3c9c', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0971a2a-17f9-51c9-a114-8da12bdf3c9c'}, {'abstract': 'A mansion above the shores of Lake Geneva is to become “Chaplin’s World,” a museum dedicated to Charlie Chaplin.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/charlie-chaplins-home-in-switzerland-to-become-a-museum/', 'snippet': 'A mansion above the shores of Lake Geneva is to become “Chaplin’s World,” a museum dedicated to Charlie Chaplin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charlie Chaplin spent the last 25 years of his life in Corsier-sur-Vevey, above the shores of Lake Geneva in Switzerland. In an 18th-century mansion on a 35-acre estate he gardened, made films, composed music, wrote books and spent time with his wife, Oona Chaplin, and their eight children. Now three of those children — Michael, Eugene and Victoria Chaplin — have announced their partnership in a new museum, called “Chaplin’s World” in their former family home, The Associated Press reported.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charlie Chaplin’s Home in Switzerland to Become a Museum', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chaplin’s Swiss Home To Become a Museum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaplin, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T13:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'f