ic paper says. It was found in a construction site in Ganzhou in southeastern China in 2010, stuffed into bags and assembled two years l...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientists have discovered a new species of dinosaur, a relative of the ferocious Tyrannosaurus rex, according to a report in Nature Communications. The story of the discovery of the 30-foot-long Qianzhousaurus sinensis, which began more than three years ago in a construction site in southeastern China, is one of drama and luck, as well as science.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Pinocchio Rex,’ China’s New Dinosaur', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dinosaurs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fossils', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Communications (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Edinburgh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Edinburgh (Scotland)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T13:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c5f5ea4-b551-584e-9682-597090148f4e', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c5f5ea4-b551-584e-9682-597090148f4e'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department