rising-visits-from-washington-and-radcliffe.html', 'snippet': 'They weren’t nominating many movie stars for Tony Awards this year, maybe because those celebrities did such a good job of working like real actors instead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may be that Denzel Washington and Daniel Radcliffe have been doing their jobs too well. As the leading men of the hit Broadway revivals of Lorraine Hansberry’s “A Raisin in the Sun” (Mr. Washington) and Martin McDonagh’s “The Cripple of Inishmaan” (Mr. Radcliffe), they are both offering affecting and astute interpretations — in the case of Mr. Radcliffe, what is surely his best stage work to date.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11BRANTLEY1/11BRANTLEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11BRANTLEY1/11BRANTLEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11BRANTLEY1/11BRANTLEY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11BRANTLEY1/11BRANTLEY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11BRANTLEY1/11BRANTLEY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11BRANTLEY1/11BRANTLEY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 