//article/9a1bca45-5419-5a3f-992f-47a80466ed4f'}, {'abstract': 'In interviews with Andrew Ross Sorkin, Timothy Geithner discussed his tenure in government and his prescriptions for solving financial crises.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/5-takeaways-from-magazine-article-on-geithner-and-the-financial-crisis/', 'snippet': 'In interviews with Andrew Ross Sorkin, Timothy Geithner discussed his tenure in government and his prescriptions for solving financial crises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Timothy F. Geithner is finally going public. Since Mr. Geithner stepped down as Treasury secretary last year, he has remained largely out of the public eye. Now, with the publication of his book, “Stress Test: Reflections on Financial Crises,” to be published next week, Mr. Geithner is breaking his silence. I caught up with him last month as he was putting the finishing touches on the book. We discussed — and debated — his tenure in government and his prescriptions for solving financial crises. During a series of interviews, he was surprisingly frank. The result of those interviews — and an early look at his book — appear as the cover story in the coming issue of The New York Times Magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/dbpix-sorkin2/dbpix-sorkin2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/business/dbpix-sorkin2/dbpix-sorkin2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 751}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/dbpix-sorkin2/dbpix-sorkin2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 818, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/dbpix-sorkin2/dbpix-sorkin2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1636, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/dbpix-sorkin2/dbpix-sorkin2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/08/business/dbpix-sorkin2/dbpix-sorkin2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/business/dbpix-sorkin2/dbpix-sorkin2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '5 Takeaways From Magazine Article on Geithner and the Financial Crisis', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Economic Stabilization Act (2008)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Summers, Lawrence H', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T17:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d16c8da-8bbc-5bbb-911e-04b308841621', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d16c8da-8bbc-5bbb-911e-04b308841621'}, {'abstract': 'Another possible interpretation of the Romneycare mortality data.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/medicaid-and-mortality-2/', 'snippet': 'Another possible interpretation of the Romneycare mortality data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My post yesterday on the new study of post-Romneycare mortality rates in Massachusetts set up a contrast between two policy scenarios: One in which health insurance expansions have a substantial effect on health (as the Massachusetts mortality data suggests), and another in which insurance’s connection to public health is much more limited (as the data from the Oregon Medicaid experiment had indicated).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicaid, Romneycare and Mortality', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T17:02:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51ba2fe5-b036-5712-84c0-b6161a60b507', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51ba2fe5-b036-5712-84c0-b6161a60b507'}, {'abstract': 'The mobile messaging service Snapchat settled with the Federal Trade Commission over charges that the service inaccurately claimed that, once sent, messages disappeared.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/03/14/technology/snapchat-ftc-settlement.html', 'snippet': 'The mobile messaging service Snapchat settled with the Federal Trade Commission over charges that the service inaccurately claimed that, once sent, messages disappeared.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mobile messaging service Snapchat settled with the Federal Trade Commission over charges that the service inaccurately claimed that, once sent, messages disappeared.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/technology/snapchat-ftc-settlement-poster/snapchat-ftc-settlement-poster-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/technology/snapchat-ftc-settlement-poster/snapchat-ftc-settlement-poster-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/technology/snapchat-ftc-settlement-poster/snapchat-ftc-settlement-poster-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/technology/snapchat-ftc-settlement-poster/snapchat-ftc-settlement-poster-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/technology/snapchat-ftc-settlement-poster/snapchat-ftc-settlement-poster-thumbSt