name': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/027e7cb8-aed8-57a0-9cf7-6d01874928af', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/027e7cb8-aed8-57a0-9cf7-6d01874928af'}, {'abstract': 'A dispute in England over a Banksy work found near a boys club is resolved after a letter from the artist supporting the club’s plan to auction it.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/banksy-emerges-from-shadows-to-weigh-in-on-dispute-over-work/', 'snippet': 'A dispute in England over a Banksy work found near a boys club is resolved after a letter from the artist supporting the club’s plan to auction it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Banksy, the mercurial street artist, typically keeps clear of the disputes that break out when his graffiti artworks are removed from the walls and doorways where he painted them — and sometimes later sold for enormous prices. But the case of the piece now known as “Mobile Lovers” –\xa0 a door-size painting of an embracing couple checking their cellphones behind each other’s backs, painted on plywood and screwed to a wall – has brought the secretive artist out of hiding for long enough to leave a typed, signed note for one of the piece’s potential beneficiaries, the BBC reported.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banksy Emerges From Shadows to Weigh In on Dispute Over Work', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Banksy Comments On Dispute Over Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banksy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bristol (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T18:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name':