on of the annual art exhibition called Monumenta, the sprawling nave in the Grand Palais in Paris becomes a blank canvas for an internationally-renowned artist. In years past, large-scale installations like Anish Kapoor’s enormous balloon sculpture and Christian Boltanski’s mountain of clothing have filled the room. And this Saturday, the Russian-born, Long Island, N.Y.-based artist couple Ilya and Emilia Kabakov will unveil “The Strange City” there for the show’s sixth iteration, which will be on view through June 22.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08kabakov-gassmann2/08kabakov-gassmann2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08kabakov-gassmann2/08kabakov-gassmann2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 801}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08kabakov-gassmann2/08kabakov-gassmann2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08kabakov-gassmann2/08kabakov-gassmann2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1827, 'width': 1369, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08kabakov-gassmann2/08kabakov-gassmann2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08kabakov-gassmann2/08kabakov-gassmann2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None,