ion_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'Vikram Singh, Rajneesh Bhandari and Taige Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikram', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rajneesh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bhandari', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Taige', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/13368536-285d-5960-a994-2be4a208455d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/13368536-285d-5960-a994-2be4a208455d'}, {'abstract': 'Out of the minimalist space of El Rey Coffee Bar and Luncheonette on the Lower East Side comes mostly comfort food, unobtrusively finessed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/dining/hungry-city-el-rey-coffee-bar-and-luncheonette-on-the-lower-east-side.html', 'snippet': 'Out of the minimalist space of El Rey Coffee Bar and Luncheonette on the Lower East Side comes mostly comfort food, unobtrusively finessed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no falafel on the falafel plate at El Rey Coffee Bar and Luncheonette. This is not an error. What appears instead could be described on the menu (but thankfully isn’t) as “evanescence of falafel,” and may be the most low-key — and satisfying — example of culinary deconstruction in the city. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Afternoon at the Improv', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Afternoon at the Improv', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishan, Ligaya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Rey Coffee Bar and Luncheonette (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T19:26:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d913ad8a-e8e8-548c-9b6d-dd58c8ec2a31', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d913ad8a-e8e8-548c-9b6d-dd58c8ec2a31'}, {'abstract': 'The designer Miguel Hurtado created his new bag line Able Archer to allow photographers to carry equipment into the field without looking like a target.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/able-archer-camera-bag-designed-to-keep-photojournalists-safe-miguel-hurtado/', 'snippet': 'The designer Miguel Hurtado created his new bag line Able Archer to allow photographers to carry equipment into the field without looking like a target.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The designer Miguel Hurtado’s a-ha moment took place one afternoon five years ago during a visit to Bahia, in northern Brazil. He was snapping pictures at Carnival when a young boy ran up to him and grabbed his camera. The kid wasn’t a thief; he was trying to telegraph a warning to Hurtado that there were some bad guys in the area and that he should put the camera away because he was about to be robbed. Immediately, Hurtado stashed his gear in his potato-shaped canvas Domke, a camera bag that advertises to the world, “I am currently in possession of a very expensive camera.” “Right there I started to wonder, why does a camera bag have to scream luxury?” Hurtado recalls. “Why does it have to make you a mark?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08archer-french/08archer-french-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08archer-french/08archer-french-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08archer-french/08archer-french-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08archer-french/08archer-french-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 795, 'width': 1192, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08archer-french/08archer-french-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08archer-french/08archer-french-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/t-magazine/08archer-french/08archer-french-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making Of | A Camera Bag Designed to Keep Photojournalists Safe', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T19:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex French', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'French', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6360792-a49f-5170-955f-776c8dc75de9', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6360792-a49f-5170-955f-776c8dc75de9'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement to drop the terms “all natural” and “nothing artificial” from some products is included in a settlement of a class-action lawsuit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/business/kellogg-agrees-to-change-labeling-on-kashi-line.html', 'snippet': 'The agreement to drop the terms “all natural” and “nothing artificial” from some products is included in a settlement of a class-action lawsuit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Kellogg Company, maker of some of the country’s most familiar breakfast cereals, said on Thursday that it had agreed to drop the terms “all natural” and “nothing artificial” from some products in its Kashi line as part of a settlement agreement ending a class-action lawsuit.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kellogg Agrees to Alter Labeling on Kashi Line', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kellogg Agrees to Alter Labeling on Kashi Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strom, Stephanie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kellogg Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kashi Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cereals', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T19:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53daf0a4-7929-59a0-bb01-6a84edb198dc', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53daf0a4-7929-59a0-bb01-6a84edb198dc'}, {'abstract': 'AstraZeneca’s board would do well to evaluate whether the company’s progress will continue under Pfizer’s management, Bill George, a professor at Harvard Business School, writes in the Another View column.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/a-case-for-rejecting-pfizers-bid-for-astrazeneca/', 'snippet': 'AstraZeneca’s board would do well to evaluate whether the company’s progress will continue under Pfizer’s management, Bill George, a professor at Harvard Business School, writes in the Another View column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill George is professor of management practice at Harvard Business School, former chairman and chief executive of Medtronic and author of “True North,” a book about authentic leadership. He serves on the boards of ExxonMobil, Goldman Sachs and the Mayo Clinic. In the past two years, he has taught custom leadership programs at Harvard for AstraZeneca executives and consulted with the company in 2012-13. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/business/dbpix-pfizer1/dbpix-pfizer1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/09/business/dbpix-pfizer1/dbpix-pfizer1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/business/dbpix-pfizer1/dbpix-pfizer1-jumbo.jpg', 'he