ocial Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Chris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vitale, Ami', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Press Photographers Assn', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guinea-Bissau', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T20:40:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/053b34fa-9ccd-583a-b67e-4885fd75b85e', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/053b34fa-9ccd-583a-b67e-4885fd75b85e'}, {'abstract': 'Getting mad at cancer is pointless, but now I have another target for my anger: the negligent care my friend received.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/living-with-cancer-careless-care/', 'snippet': 'Getting mad at cancer is pointless, but now I have another target for my anger: the negligent care my friend received.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I consider what happened to an esteemed friend and colleague, I fume at the mayhem that ovarian cancer wreaks and at the deficient care she received at a university hospital in another town. Do instances of medical negligence sometimes go unnoticed because patients are so debilitated that they cannot testify — especially if they are still in treatment? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit'