from. The hesitation in the clerk’s reply was enough to unleash Stroman’s hatred for Muslims, whom he referred to as people with “shawls on their face.” Stroman pulled the trigger, but his victim, Raisuddin Bhuiyan, an enterprising immigrant from Bangladesh — and a Muslim, indeed — would survive. The other two victims from the fortnight’s vigilante shooting spree, immigrants from India and Pakistan, would not. So begins Anand Giridharadas’s “The True American,” a richly detailed, affecting account of two men bound, as it turned out, by more than just an act of violence.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/books/review/0511-bks-Akhtar/0511-bks-Akhtar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/books/review/0511-bks-Akhtar/0511-bks-Akhtar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 763}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/books/review/0511-bks-Akhtar/0511-bks-Akhtar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 806, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/books/review/0511-bks-Akhtar/0511-bks-Akhtar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1798, 'width': 1414, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/books/review/0511-bks-Akhtar/0511-bks-Akhtar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/11/books/review/0511-bks-Akhtar/0511-bks-Akhtar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/books/review/0511-bks-Akhtar/0511-bks-Akhtar-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pledges of Allegiance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pledges of Allegiance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giridharadas, Anand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T20:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ayad Akhtar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ayad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akhtar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d0d0456-b57b-5eb0-84b9-eebe6f60c5ca', 'word_count': 1080, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d0d0456-b57b-5eb0-84b9-eebe6f60c5ca'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time since 2010, New York audiences had the chance to take in work by Christian Rizzo, at the French Institute Alliance Française and at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/arts/dance/lyon-opera-ballet-dances-a-work-by-christian-rizzo.html', 'snippet': 'For the first time since 2010, New York audiences had the chance to take in work by Christian Rizzo, at the French Institute Alliance Française and at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christian Rizzo last presented his choreography in New York in 2010, and the afterimage of that ravishing experience, at least for me, remains firmly etched. In “b.c, janvier 1545, fontainebleau,” Mr. Rizzo created a stark black-and-white landscape in which a series of repetitive angled positions grew into a hypnotic movement meditation for the sleek, high-heeled dancer Julie Guibert. Mr. Rizzo, as an interloper or part of the set, wore a rabbit mask.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09RIZZO_SPAN/RIZZO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09RIZZO_SPAN/RIZZO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09RIZZO_SPAN/RIZZO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09RIZZO_SPAN/RIZZO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09RIZZO_SPAN/09RIZZO_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09RIZZO_SPAN/09RIZZO_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09RIZZO_SPAN/09RIZZO_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Surreal Dream, Dark and Deeply Melancholy', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Surreal Dream, Dark and Deeply Melancholy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lyon Opera Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T20:54:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/87f40096-ced9-5e75-ad3e-3a12cbd5c459', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87f40096-ced9-5e75-ad3e-3a12cbd5c459'}, {'abstract': 'In “Fed Up,” a documentary investigation into why people are getting fatter, the filmmakers explore who’s killing our health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/movies/fed-up-descends-on-villains-in-the-battle-of-the-bulge.html', 'snippet': 'In “Fed Up,” a documentary investigation into why people are getting fatter, the filmmakers explore who’s killing our health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are interested in learning the latest on fighting what’s called the obesity epidemic, you may want to avoid the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention’s website. There, in a section about balancing calories (“Healthy Weight — it’s not a diet, it’s a lifestyle!”), amid tips on reducing and exercising, you can read that “a calorie is a calorie regardless of its source.” The page also features a graphic of a scale with the words “calories in” and “calories out,” as if all calories were equal. The American Beverage Association, as it happens, pretty much says the same thing on its website: “Quite simply, overweight and obesity are a result of an imbalance between calories consumed and calories burned.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/fed-span/fed-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 331, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/fed-span/fed-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 331}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/fed-span/fed-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 564, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/fed-span/fed-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 950, 'width': 1724, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/fed-span/fed-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/fed-span/fed-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/fed-span/fed-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sugar, Come Out With Your Hands Up', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sugar, Come Out With Your Hands Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fed Up (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soechtig, Stephanie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Couric, Katie', 'rank': 