is workplace demands his ID every morning, and a co-worker cheerfully describes poor Simon as “a bit of a nonperson, really.” His boss (Wallace Shawn) has a vague idea of who he is, as does Hannah (Mia Wasikowska), a fellow employee as well as a neighbor. Simon is hopelessly in love with her, in a creepy way that is also kind of sweet.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09DOUBLE/DOUBLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09DOUBLE/DOUBLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09DOUBLE/DOUBLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09DOUBLE/DOUBLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1444, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09DOUBLE/09DOUBLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09DOUBLE/09DOUBLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09DOUBLE/09DOUBLE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Competing Against a Doppelgänger Who Spells Trouble', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Competing Against a Doppelgänger Who Spells Trouble', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenberg, Jesse', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wasikowska, Mia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayoade, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shawn, Wallace', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Double (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T21:07:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebec3318-f874-585a-9b5b-09b352f851f4', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebec3318-f874-585a-9b5b-09b352f851f4'}, {'abstract': 'The NBC mini-series “Rosemary’s Baby” reimagines the 1968 Polanski movie in Paris, where a sophisticated French couple befriends two young expatriates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/arts/television/rosemarys-baby-is-remade-into-a-mini-series.html', 'snippet': 'The NBC mini-series “Rosemary’s Baby” reimagines the 1968 Polanski movie in Paris, where a sophisticated French couple befriends two young expatriates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People moving into new apartments in New York City dread brash, nosy neighbors. In Paris, the nightmare next door is more likely to be an elegant, worldly couple with irreproachable manners. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09JPROSEMARY/09JPROSEMARY-articleLarge-v2.