ragraph': 'The costumes were almost as loud as the music when Tune-Yards performed at Rough Trade Records on Wednesday night. Merrill Garbus, the Oakland, Calif.-based songwriter who records as Tune-Yards, was in a dress that was part red vinyl, part patterned turquoise fabric and part gold lamé, along with high sequined boots. Her band members were in a mélange of brightly colored, clashing patterns, not to mention the fluorescent face paint. Ms. Garbus also had a streak of glitter under one eye. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09TUNEYARDS/TUNEYARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09TUNEYARDS/TUNEYARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09TUNEYARDS/TUNEYARDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09TUNEYARDS/TUNEYARDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1406, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09TUNEYARDS/TUNEYARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09TUNEYARDS/TUNEYARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09TUNEYARDS/TUNEYARDS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'widt