{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Homs (Syria)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-08T22:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/382b3aa1-781f-5448-ad4d-1e23082a8b42', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/382b3aa1-781f-5448-ad4d-1e23082a8b42'}, {'abstract': 'A listing of discussions, film screenings, cultural activities and walking tours in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/arts/spare-times-for-may-9-15.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of discussions, film screenings, cultural activities and walking tours in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York Bicycle Jumble (Saturday) On the heels — or wheels — of last weekend’s TD Five Boro Bike Tour, this stationary event in Park Slope, Brooklyn, will set cyclists’ hearts racing in a different way. For the sixth year, buyers can browse new and used bicycles and accessories, as well as clothing, collectibles and other items offered by vendors from across the country. Guests can talk shop with representatives from the Bicycle Messenger Foundation; the environmental organization Times Up!; and We Bike NYC, a biking group for women. They can even take a potential purchase out for a spin. (This is the first of three such planned events in Brooklyn; the others will be in Red Hook on June 1 and Park Slope in the fall.) From 10 a.m. to 4 p.m., Old Stone House at Washington Park, Third Street, between Fourth and Fifth Avenues; nybikejumble.com; free. Squeaky wheels are welcome. (Anne Mancuso)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for May 9-15', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keyword