a star-studded drama set in Philadelphia, is the actor John Slattery’s feature film directorial debut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The occasional narrator of “God’s Pocket” is a Philadelphia newspaper columnist and Jimmy Breslin type who is the beloved voice of the city’s blue collar class. Describing the residents of the rough, seedy South Philadelphia neighborhood that gives the movie its name, this local celebrity, Richard (Richard Jenkins), muses out loud with barbed affection: “Everyone here has stolen something from someone else, or when they were kids, they set someone’s house on fire. They know who cheats at cards and who slaps their kids around. The one thing they can’t forgive is not being from God’s Pocket.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09GODS/GODS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09GODS/GODS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 250}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09GODS/GODS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09GODS/GODS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 852, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09GODS/GODS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/09/arts/09GODS/GODS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype