ial killer stalking the young campers at a summer getaway for aspiring theater stars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Canadian musical comedy “Stage Fright” unveils its lone showstopping number early on, as a bus full of kids pulls into theater camp: the one place they aren’t outcasts. As a sad sack sings of being “beaten up a dozen times for singing Stephen Sondheim’s rhymes,” the film offers a glimpse of exactly the sort of demented, toe-tapping sensibility you’d expect from a tuneful summer camp farce — in which a serial killer is on the loose.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some High Notes Are Just Screams', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stage Fright', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Driver, Minnie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meat Loaf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Stage Fright (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sable, Jerome', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T00:52:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/96d41872-b1b7-5855-aec6-b6b4a3a8ace9', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96d41872-b1b7-5855-aec6-b6b4a3a8ace9'}, {'abstract': 'The state-controlled news agency directed racist and suggestive language toward President Obama and President Park Geun-hye of South Korea, who together recently issued stern warnings to North Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/world/asia/ugly-words-from-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'The state-controlled news agency directed racist and suggestive language toward President Obama and President Park Geun-hye of South Korea, who together recently issued stern warnings to North Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — After President Obama and South Korea’s president, Park Geun-hye, warned North Korea of harsher sanctions if it continued pursuing nuclear weapons, the North has responded with harsh invective against both leaders. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ugly Words From North Korea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ugly Words From North Korea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Korean Central News Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Geun-hye', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T00:53:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d0119a7-636f-573b-aa25-3b300a956e43', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d0119a7-636f-573b-aa25-3b300a956e43'}, {'abstract': 'The board of the broken Massachusetts health insurance exchange voted to buy new software to help people enroll in coverage, while preparing to join the federal marketplace if necessary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/us/massachusetts-pushes-fix-for-state-health-exchange.html', 'snippet': 'The board of the broken Massachusetts health insurance exchange voted to buy new software to help people enroll in coverage, while preparing to join the federal marketplace if necessary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The board of the broken Massachusetts health insurance exchange voted on Thursday to support a state plan to buy new software to help people enroll in coverage, while also preparing to join the federal marketplace if the system is not ready by fall. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts Pushes Fix for State Health Exchange', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts Pushes Fix for State Health Exchange', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T00:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8595d34-efb5-5a12-acec-d6b6f3d98968', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8595d34-efb5-5a12-acec-d6b6f3d98968'}, {'abstract': 'Colorado has finalized plans to create the nation’s first financial cooperatives for the marijuana trade, even though few expect the necessary approval from the Federal Reserve.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/us/politics/marijuana-trade-offered-credit-relief-in-colorado.html', 'snippet': 'Colorado has finalized plans to create the nation’s first financial cooperatives for the marijuana trade, even though few expect the necessary approval from the Federal Reserve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — Seeking to move its growing marijuana industry away from the risk of using only cash, Colorado finalized plans this week to create the nation’s first financial cooperatives for the marijuana trade. But few expect the effort to gain the necessary approval of Federal Reserve officials leery of offering banking services to companies that grow and sell a federally controlled substance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/us/09colorado-1/09colorado-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/10/us/09colorado-1/09colorado-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/us/09colorado-1/09colorado-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/us/09colorado-1/09colorado-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/us/09colorado-1/09colorado-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/10/us/09colorado-1/09colorado-1-thumbSta