7', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10985944-b937-56c4-ab38-94bd911effa7'}, {'abstract': 'An awkward Boy Scouts policy — don’t-ask-don’t-tell silence on the one hand, and a supposedly welcoming embrace on the other, with an 18th birthday dividing the two — has emboldened and angered gay Scouts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/us/compromise-on-gays-pleases-no-one-scouts-are-learning.html', 'snippet': 'An awkward Boy Scouts policy — don’t-ask-don’t-tell silence on the one hand, and a supposedly welcoming embrace on the other, with an 18th birthday dividing the two — has emboldened and angered gay Scouts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — Pascal Tessier is a 17-year-old Eagle Scout in suburban Maryland who says scouting made him who he is today, with its lessons about morality, leadership and responsibility. And those very strengths, this openly gay high school senior said, are what compel and equip him to fight back now against Scout policies on gays that he believes are wrong.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Compromise on Gays Pleases No One, Scouts Are Learning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Compromise on Gays Pleases No One, Scouts Are Learning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Kirk', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boy Scouts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T01:30:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizatio