: 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garnett, Kevin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierce, Paul (1977- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T01:49:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c449d849-e2b6-5174-a471-240de14b3fb2', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c449d849-e2b6-5174-a471-240de14b3fb2'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Jerry Brown and state legislative leaders reached a deal to place a revised plan for a rainy-day fund on the ballot this fall; it would create a cushion against future economic downturns and allow the state to use extra cash to pay down long-term debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/us/politics/california-agreement-on-rainy-day-fund.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Jerry Brown and state legislative leaders reached a deal to place a revised plan for a rainy-day fund on the ballot this fall; it would create a cushion against future economic downturns and allow the state to use extra cash to pay down long-...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Jerry Brown and state legislative leaders reached a deal Thursday to place a revised plan for a rainy-day fund on the ballot this fall; it would create a cushion against future economic downturns and allow the state to use extra cash to pay down long-term debt. Mr. Brown, who is running for his fourth term this fall, has been pushing for the measure, which he says is the only way to bolster the state’s finances for the long term. Under the plan, spikes in money collected from capital gains taxes would be diverted to the fund, with some money set aside for debt payments on pensions. The Legislature would also be required to set aside 1.5 percent of general revenue for the fund each year, and money could be withdrawn from the fund only if overall revenue did not meet historic spending levels. The Legislature is expected to approve the proposal next week so that the measure can be placed on the November ballot. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Agreement on Rainy Day Fund', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Agreement on Rainy Day Fund', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T01:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b852d202-bd6e-58c6-9d1d-bc641471bc36', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b852d202-bd6e-58c6-9d1d-bc641471bc36'}, {'abstract': 'Friday fun with James Mulhern.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/digs-in-the-snow/', 'snippet': 'Friday fun with James Mulhern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY’S PUZZLE — Well, lookee here; a Friday puzzle that almost looks like it might have a theme. It’s a 68-worder, but take a gander at those long, horizontal entries. I looked at the blank grid before solving and thought, “Huh. A rule breaker.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'ma