181-07ace06df887'}, {'abstract': 'When the Big City Book Club convenes next, we’ll be reading Colm Toibin’s acclaimed 2009 novel, “Brooklyn.” The online discussion will take place on Monday, May 19, starting at 6:30 p.m.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/nyregion/big-city-book-club.html', 'snippet': 'When the Big City Book Club convenes next, we’ll be reading Colm Toibin’s acclaimed 2009 novel, “Brooklyn.” The online discussion will take place on Monday, May 19, starting at 6:30 p.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brooklyn today is a destination for celebrities and wealthy creative types, but not so long ago it was the default settlement for young immigrants without money. When the Big City Book Club convenes next, we’ll be reading Colm Toibin’s acclaimed 2009 novel, “Brooklyn,” the story of a young Irishwoman who leaves a fragile mother behind to find herself in Dodgerland in the early 1950s. Brooklyn College and the Fulton Mall both make appearances in a book that explores the conflict between familial obligation and one’s own youthful heart and promise. The online discussion will take place on Monday, May 19, starting at 6:30 p.m. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big City Book Club', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big City Book Club', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Clubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toibin, Colm', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T02:19:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4f940c6-5c71-5230-8d85-c18023446284', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4f940c6-5c71-5230-8d85-c18023446284'}, {'