'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9c254a7-32a6-5efe-b33b-818e34e1f83b', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9c254a7-32a6-5efe-b33b-818e34e1f83b'}, {'abstract': 'In court papers that attracted little attention, the Moreland Commission argued that it had “independent authority” beyond Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/nyregion/cuomo-and-panel-he-shut-differ-on-its-independence.html', 'snippet': 'In court papers that attracted little attention, the Moreland Commission argued that it had “independent authority” beyond Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, who has long cast himself as the man who would clean up Albany,\xa0offered a blunt defense last month to suggestions that his office had interfered with an anticorruption panel the governor formed last year, then shut down abruptly in March in exchange for enhancements to state ethics laws.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo and Panel He Shut Differ on Its Independence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo and Panel He Shut Differ on Its Independence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moreland Commission to Investigate Public Corruption (NYS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subpoenas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T03:18:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William K. Rashbaum and Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67d26303-1553-58bd-9e9c-5598efa43819', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67d26303-1553-58bd-9e9c-5598efa43819'}, {'abstract': 'The timing of China’s clash with Vietnam in the South China Sea is curious given that Asia’s leaders are meeting next week and China’s actions are likely to be a main topic.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/08/q-and-a-m-taylor-fravel-on-chinas-dispute-with-vietnam/', 'snippet': 'The timing of China’s clash with Vietnam in the South China Sea is curious given that Asia’s leaders are meeting next week and China’s actions are likely to be a main topic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The long-simmering territorial dispute between China and Vietnam in the South China Sea had one of its periodic eruptions this week, as Vietnamese vessels confronted Chinese ships that are trying to place an oil rig near the disputed Paracel Islands and off Vietnam’s coast. The rig is run by China National Offshore Oil Corporation, or Cnooc, and lies just 120 nautical miles off the main coastline of Vietnam. Chinese ships have fired water cannons at the Vietnamese vessels, and both sides have said their ships have been rammed by opposing forces. The Chinese military fought with units from South Vietnam over the southern Paracels in 1974, which led to China taking over the islands, though they remain uninhabited.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/world/09sino-tensions/09sino-tensions-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge