5th anniversary with a concert, taped last summer, at the music festival in western Massachusetts. “The interaction between the musicians,” Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim wrote in The New York Times when the ensemble played at Carnegie Hall in October, “turns any performance into a visual spectacle.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T05:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8b446a4-4dd9-5346-82bc-09432f6fe78c', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8b446a4-4dd9-5346-82bc-09432f6fe78c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Frank fought Washington State to honor treaties written in the 1850s giving Native Americans the right to fish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/us/billy-frank-jr-fighter-for-native-fishing-rights-dies-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Frank fought Washington State to honor treaties written in the 1850s giving Native Americans the right to fish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The crime was fishing. The year was 1945. The boy was 14. It was his first offense, but it would not be his last.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/us/FRANK-1-obit/FRANK-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/201