ouglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2e393c9-b74f-5d64-aef1-e1f404676ca5', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2e393c9-b74f-5d64-aef1-e1f404676ca5'}, {'abstract': 'The Global Times newspaper said that the lawyer, Pu Zhiqiang, had “clearly crossed the red line of law” by attending a meeting to commemorate the 1989 protest movement.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/communist-party-newspaper-denounces-detained-lawyer/', 'snippet': 'The Global Times newspaper said that the lawyer, Pu Zhiqiang, had “clearly crossed the red line of law” by attending a meeting to commemorate the 1989 protest movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A commentary in a Communist Party-run newspaper has criticized the prominent civil rights lawyer Pu Zhiqiang, who was detained in Beijing this week ahead of the 25th anniversary of the deadly crackdown on the Tiananmen Square protests. The article in the newspaper, Global Times, said that Mr. Pu had “clearly crossed the red line of law” by attending a meeting to commemorate the 1989 protest movement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/world/09sino-PuZhiqiang/09sino-PuZhiqiang-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/09/world/09sino-PuZhiqiang/09sino-PuZhiqiang-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/world/09sino-PuZhiqiang/09sino-PuZhiqiang-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subt