w-latest-report-on-new-delhis-pollution/', 'snippet': 'Indian government officials insist that the capital’s air pollution is not as bad as reports say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the World Health Organization’s recent report on air pollution, New Delhi ranks as the most polluted city in the world, writes Gardiner Harris of The New York Times, with air pollution far worse than that of Beijing, whose smoggy skies have grabbed much of the international attention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Denials Follow Latest Report on New Delhi’s Pollution', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Gardiner', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delhi (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T07:02:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79d5defd-bcc5-58ee-af95-509b7bcb40a6', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79d5defd-bcc5-58ee-af95-509b7bcb40a6'}, {'abstract': 'With ballots from all districts counted, the party led by President Jacob Zuma was only slightly down from its showing in 1994, the year it assumed power in the country’s first democratic election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/world/africa/south-africa-vote.html', 'snippet': 'With ballots from all districts counted, the party led by President Jacob Zuma was only slightly down from its showing in 1994, the year it assumed power in the country’s first democratic election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — As the final ballots of South Africa’s fifth post-apartheid election were tallied on Friday, the results handed the governing African National Congress a victory with 62 percent of the vote — nearly the same share it won in 1994, the year it assumed power under Nelson Mandela in the nation’s f irst truly democratic election.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/world/SAFRICA/SAFRICA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/10/world/SAFRICA/SAFRICA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/world/SAFRICA/SAFRICA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/world/SAFRICA/SAFRICA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/world/SAFRICA/SAFRICA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/10/world/SAFRICA/SAFRICA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/world/SAFRICA/SAFRICA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 15