er. The report was taken as a sign that conditions were improving in the steel industry, considered a proxy for overall economic activity.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recovering Steel Industry Lifts ArcelorMittal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recovering Steel Industry Lifts ArcelorMittal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Stanley', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ArcelorMittal SA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steel and Iron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Luxembourg', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mittal, Lakshmi N', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T08:46:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b3edb31-b577-5fdf-8e91-c75df297e6b0', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b3edb31-b577-5fdf-8e91-c75df297e6b0'}, {'abstract': 'The blaze and power failure came amid heightened tension in the Ukrainian capital on the anniversary of the end of World War II in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/world/europe/fire-kiev-ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'The blaze and power failure came amid heightened tension in the Ukrainian capital on the anniversary of the end of World War II in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIEV, Ukraine — A fire near a main broadcasting tower briefly disrupted some television service in the Ukrainian capital on Friday morning, as the authorities were on a heightened state of alert because of the country’s political crisis and a major national holiday celebrating victory in World War II.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fire Temporarily Knocks Out Broadcast Service in Kiev', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kiev (Ukraine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T08:53:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b0e06d4-a232-58ea-9caa-4a42f7ffea0f', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b0e06d4-a232-58ea-9caa-4a42f7ffea0f'}, {'abstract': 'A recent book chronicles the artistic and cultural efforts that were an essential – if overlooked – part of the civil rights movement.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/a-cultural-history-of-civil-rights/', 'snippet': 'A recent book chronicles the artistic and cultural efforts that were an essential – if overlooked – part of the civil rights movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two men sit inside a rural Mississippi community center. One of them, a black civil rights activist, has a shotgun at the ready. Their vigil — in a town where the Ku Klux Klan could strike at any moment — is in a makeshift library whose walls are covered with books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/0