he deal, which would also include the new Beats Music streaming service, would be the biggest acquisition in Apple’s history and could suggest an effort to shake up its approach to digital music.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple’s New Tune', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T11:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec05facf-fe9e-5c56-98b1-4da5633c647e', 'word_count': 1878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec05facf-fe9e-5c56-98b1-4da5633c647e'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese public security agents have detained Chen Guang, 43, a former soldier turned artist whose experiences during those tumultuous days have become a haunting inspiration for his work.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/chinese-artist-detained-before-tiananmen-anniversary/', 'snippet': 'Chinese public security agents have detained Chen Guang, 43, a former soldier turned artist whose experiences during those tumultuous days have become a haunting inspiration for his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With little more than three weeks remaining until the 25th anniversary of the Chinese Army’s bloody crackdown on the Tiananmen Square protests, the authorities are policing any attempt to commemorate the event — even those held in private. On Wednesday night, public security agents detained Chen Guang, 43, a former soldier turned artist whose experiences during those tumultuous days have become a haunting inspiration for his work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'cap