artists-photographs/', 'snippet': 'The Chicago-based artist and gallerist — who recently curated a floor at the Whitney Biennial and whose solo show opens in San Francisco next week — discusses her admiration for the photographer’s technically and conceptually rigorous work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this year, Michelle Grabner became the first artist to co-curate the Whitney Biennial since Gertrude Vanderbilt Whitney, the museum’s founder. The floor she organized was the popular favorite, lauded for its emphasis on mature female painters, like Amy Sillman and Louise Fishman, and lushly handmade objects, including several works by the textile artist Sheila Hicks. Grabner also runs two galleries with her husband, the artist Brad Killam: The Suburban, housed in two sheds in their Oak Park, Ill., backyard, and the\xa0Poor Farm, a larger space in rural Wisconsin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/t-magazine/09williams-kino2/09williams-kino2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/09/t-magazine/09williams-kino2/09williams-kino2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/t-magazine/09williams-kino2/09williams-kino2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/t-magazine/09williams-kino2/09williams-kino2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/t-magazine/09williams-kino2/09williams-k