'By Steve Almond', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Almond', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b8df851-cefc-571f-af06-e0a54d4640b8', 'word_count': 1868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b8df851-cefc-571f-af06-e0a54d4640b8'}, {'abstract': 'Truth in beer; expellable member; gimme shelters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/magazine/the-old-switch-a-brew.html', 'snippet': 'Truth in beer; expellable member; gimme shelters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sixty years ago, my father worked in a brewery, which produced a “premium” beer and a “regular” beer with a different name and a cheaper price. In actuality, the beers were identical, only with different bottles and labels. The “premium” buyers were getting what they were paying for — a premium beer. The “regular” beer drinkers were paying less for the same thing. While it doesn’t seem that anyone was hurt by the deception, does the fact that there was deceit involved make it unethical? NAME WITHHELD', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11ethicist/mag-11Ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11ethicist/mag-11Ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11ethicist/mag-11Ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11ethicist/mag-11Ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1546, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11ethicist/mag-11Ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11ethicist/mag-11Ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11ethicist/mag-11Ethicist-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Old Switch-a-Brew', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Old Switch-a-Brew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klosterman, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T14:45:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chuck Klosterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chuck', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klosterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa18ac0b-d9df-5694-ac39-1e010887a656', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa18ac0b-d9df-5694-ac39-1e010887a656'}, {'abstract': 'Caught between the dealers and the cops in Hazleton, Pa., is a woman with a bad habit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/magazine/addict-informant-mother.html', 'snippet': 'Caught between the dealers and the cops in Hazleton, Pa., is a woman with a bad habit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day last summer, Ann and her husband, Tom, walked two and a half hours to reach Hazleton, a onetime mining town in eastern Pennsylvania. They had lived there until July, when they were evicted and moved in with Ann’s mother in Sugarloaf, a more affluent township nearby. There was not much to miss about Hazleton, with its decaying downtown and its fading homes spotted with satellite dishes, but to Ann and Tom the town held a shimmering appeal: It had heroin, a lot of it. They had called the usual friends for a ride, with no luck, and their own car had been repossessed. So at midday, the two left Ann’s mother’s condominium by foot and followed the asphalt out of the valley all the way to Hazleton. Eventually they turned onto Alter Street, where, especially in summer, heroin dealers greeted customers outside a packed barbershop and a busy pawnshop, clustering around them, competing for business. Sometimes Ann and Tom joined other users they knew behind a building, where someone had left a tattered couch. Sometimes they got high in an abandoned garage on a side street. Though the walk that day to Alter Street was long, it was worth it to them both: Tom, especially, loved heroin, and Ann loved Tom, and the march to Hazleton was as much about need as it was about love.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11heroin1/11heroin1-articleLarge-v20.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11heroin1/11heroin1-articleLarge-v20.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11heroin1/11heroin1-jumbo-v20.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11heroin1/11heroin1-superJumbo-v20.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11heroin1/11heroin1-thumbStandard-v22.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11heroin1/11heroin1-thumbStandard-v22.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11heroin1/11heroin1-thumbLarge-v19.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Addict. Informant. Mother.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hooked', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heroin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hazleton (Pa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T14:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Dominus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dominus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3c70e69-1acc-5361-a9b8-a287ca31c964', 'word_count': 6878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3c70e69-1acc-5361-a9b8-a287ca31c964'}, {'abstract': 'But the high-wire artist is also a man of extremes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/magazine/philippe-petit-strikes-a-delicate-balance.html', 'snippet': 'But the high-wire artist is also a man of extremes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Your new book is called “Creativity: The Perfect Crime.” The first lines are “Make no mistake. I frown upon books about creativity.” How is yours different? Most books on creativity are written by an author who references all the great creators of humanity — very often Einstein, the Beatles. They’re not drawing from themselves, and these books are usually in the self-help department. And very often, at the end of a chapter, they have an exercise for you to do. I don’t frown upon them; let’s be frank, I hate them.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11talk/11talk-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 966, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11talk/11talk-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 966}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11talk/11talk-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 636, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/magazine/11talk/11talk-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1272, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'captio