iginal': 'By Holly Bass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a7fa751-468c-59af-b117-dacf58031222', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a7fa751-468c-59af-b117-dacf58031222'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s lesson students will read about the events in Nigeria and the subsequent Twitter campaign, deciding whether hashtag activism is worthwhile and designing ways to take action on an issue they care about.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/skills-and-strategies-engaging-in-causes-via-hashtag-activism/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s lesson students will read about the events in Nigeria and the subsequent Twitter campaign, deciding whether hashtag activism is worthwhile and designing ways to take action on an issue they care about.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update | May 14, 2014: We have added a contribution from 230 girls and their teachers at a school in Panama City, Panama. Scroll to the bottom of this post to see it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/world/NIGERIA-A1-LN/NIGERIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/08/world/NIGERIA-A1-LN/NIGERIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/world/NIGERIA-A1-LN/NIGERIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/08/world/NIGERIA-A1-LN/NIGERIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 987, 'width': 1590, 'subTyp