to enter the market at $12 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/realestate/upper-west-side-brownstone-with-modern-twists.html', 'snippet': 'A five-story townhouse that retains many original details, but also some bold, modern renovations, is poised to enter the market at $12 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A cleverly conceived hybrid townhouse — the pale front is a historically correct brownstone and the back a bold architectural grid of glass and steel — on a classic Upper West Side block near the American Museum of Natural History is poised to enter the market at $12 million. The annual taxes on the 19-foot-wide, circa-1900 property at 121 West 81st Street, between Columbus and Amsterdam Avenues, are $63,679.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upper West Side Brownstone With Modern Twists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Modern Twists Added', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, Robin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brownstones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T17:16:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4539db25-3144-5e27-a5c9-bfaf8a89d572', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4539db25-3144-5e27-a5c9-bfaf8a89d572'}, {'abstract': 'A Civil War photograph shows Union soldiers in a neat line — and, in the background, an early moment in baseball history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/upshot/the-national-pastime-amid-a-national-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'A Civil War photograph shows Union soldiers in a neat line — and, in the background, an early moment in baseball history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is one of the earliest photographs ever taken of a baseball game, and it happened by accident. The photographer, Henry P. Moore, of Concord, N.H., was focusing on the well-uniformed Union soldiers of the 48th New York State Volunteer Infantry, but he also captured their baseball-playing comrades in the background.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/upshot/10UP-Beschloss/10UP-Beschloss-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 456, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/09/upshot/10UP-Beschloss/10UP-Beschloss-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 456}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/upshot/10UP-Beschloss/10UP-Beschloss-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 779, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/upshot/10UP-Beschloss/10UP-Beschloss-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1494, 'width': 1965, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/09/upshot/10UP-Beschloss/10UP-Beschloss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/09/upshot/10UP-Beschloss/10UP-Beschloss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 