am Friedkin directed “The French Connection” and “The Exorcist” before a string of critical failures, including “Sorcerer,” which is now on Blu-ray.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/movies/homevideo/william-friedkin-before-and-after-the-hits.html', 'snippet': 'William Friedkin directed “The French Connection” and “The Exorcist” before a string of critical failures, including “Sorcerer,” which is now on Blu-ray.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a brief moment, between the ascension of Francis Ford Coppola and that of Steven Spielberg, Hollywood’s hottest young director was William Friedkin. The one-two punch of “The French Connection” (1971) and “The Exorcist” (1973) made the man nicknamed Hurricane Billy a gale-force talent. The successive failures of “Sorcerer” (1977), “The Brink’s Job” (1978) and “Cruising” (1980) sent Hurricane Billy out to sea.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11HOBERMAN/11HOBERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11HOBERMAN/11HOBERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11HOBERMAN/11HOBERMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11HOBERMAN/11HOBERMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/arts/11HOBERMAN/11HOBERMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75