Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Stop, Last Drop: Metro-North Bar Cars Chug Into History', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Last Stop, Last Drop: Bar Cars Chug Into Commuter History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro-North Commuter Railroad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T18:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d0956ba-4532-5052-9292-697e09b61c63', 'word_count': 1054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d0956ba-4532-5052-9292-697e09b61c63'}, {'abstract': 'Critics are correct that income inequality data leave out things like jobless benefits, food stamps and Medicaid, but they are missing a larger point.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/upshot/pikettys-arguments-still-hold-up-after-taxes.html', 'snippet': 'Critics are correct that income inequality data leave out things like jobless benefits, food stamps and Medicaid, but they are missing a larger point.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One critique of Thomas Piketty’s influential new book on wealth accumulation through the ages is that his analysis is solely of market incomes and wealth. He largely ignores systems of taxes and transfers and the extent to which they offset inequality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/upshot/10UP-TRANSFER-copy/10UP-TRANSFER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width