snippet': 'A bit of calm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I visited the art space for the first time a few weeks ago, and it made me think of this atmospheric performance:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Sarah Jarosz at Mass Moca', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T19:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7d1d93a-451a-51d5-8299-70c17f275c00', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7d1d93a-451a-51d5-8299-70c17f275c00'}, {'abstract': 'With a deadlocked Congress, President Obama risks leaving office in 2017 without a major accomplishment from his second term.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/us/obama-aggravated-by-gridlock-stresses-results-in-midterms.html', 'snippet': 'With a deadlocked Congress, President Obama risks leaving office in 2017 without a major accomplishment from his second term.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOUNTAIN VIEW, Calif. — On a fund-raising trip where President Obama acknowledged at one stop that the country was not going “to go where we need to go” despite his many executive actions, he was back in sales mode on Friday before returning to still-gridlocked Washington.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama, Aggravated by Gridlock, Stresses Results in Midterms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama, Aggravated by Gridlock, Stresses Results in Midterms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sc