like to believe that we are free from the racial and gender biases that afflict so many other people in society. But is this self-conception accurate?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11GRAY/11GRAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 990, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11GRAY/11GRAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 990}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11GRAY/11GRAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 621, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11GRAY/11GRAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1242, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11GRAY/11GRAY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11GRAY/11GRAY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11GRAY/11GRAY-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Professors Are Prejudiced, Too', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Professors Are Prejudiced, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T19:51:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dolly Chugh, Katherine L. Milkman and Modupe Akinola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dolly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chugh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Milkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Modupe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akinola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/53fa8d78-23ba-5e56-9fae-61ee074acf8f', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53fa8d78-23ba-5e56-9fae-61ee074acf8f'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine, which is ceasing print publication, was profoundly important at a time when the white press found black people of interest only if they committed crimes.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/when-jet-mattered/', 'snippet': 'The magazine, which is ceasing print publication, was profoundly important at a time when the white press found black people of interest only if they committed crimes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a grade school student in the late 1950s, I whiled away many Saturday mornings waiting to have my hair cut at Joseah’s Barbershop in Chester, Pa., the once-muscular factory town south of Philadelphia where I grew up. It is unremarkable today to see African-Americans and whites sitting side-by-side in hair salons. But in the age of American apartheid — even in the North — beauty and hair-care services were segregated by race.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When ‘Jet’ Mattered', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Segregation and Desegregation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, John H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Till, Emmett Louis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jet (Magazine)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T19:51:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce5145d7-8ede-5209-abea-7aa3861abf22', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce5145d7-8ede-5209-abea-7aa3861abf22'}, {'abstract': 'DealBook is attempting to fill in the gaps of Alibaba’s eagerly anticipated filing for a stock listing in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/09/weekend-reading-5-questions-for-alibabas-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'DealBook is attempting to fill in the gaps of Alibaba’s eagerly anticipated filing for a stock listing in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DealBook is attempting to fill in the gaps of Alibaba’s eagerly anticipated filing for a stock listing in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 