-ce2f6637b593', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f37e9f77-15c1-518a-a704-ce2f6637b593'}, {'abstract': 'For social-media users, a mass anxiety of approval seeking seems far more suited to a high school prom than a high-functioning society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/fashion/for-some-social-media-users-an-anxiety-from-approval-seeking.html', 'snippet': 'For social-media users, a mass anxiety of approval seeking seems far more suited to a high school prom than a high-functioning society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walking through an airport newsstand this year, I noticed a novelty. The covers of Inc., Fast Company and Time all had female executives on the covers: Sara Blakely, Angela Ahrendts and Janet L. Yellen. I quickly snapped a photo and sent out a tweet to my modest list of followers: “Women on the cover. Not just for girlie magazines anymore.” ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/11THISLIFE/11THISLIFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 188, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/11THISLIFE/11THISLIFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 188}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/11THISLIFE/11THISLIFE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/11THISLIFE/11THISLIFE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/11THISLIFE/11THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg',