re every May, but this year — because of the World Cup and a few impressive performances — the table has been set early. Several top leagues have crowned their champions, and the rest will do so in the next week before they send their best players home to pack for Brazil. Here’s a look at the status of the title races in Europe’s big-five leagues:', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'League Races in European Soccer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'League Races Reach Early End in Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T20:56:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce9bfa5b-a5ce-5391-8302-c20f917a981d', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce9bfa5b-a5ce-5391-8302-c20f917a981d'}, {'abstract': 'In Brooklyn they do drag a little differently, as Stephanie Keith found out when she shot the second annual Mr(s) Williamsburg competition, a nine-week extravaganza where anything goes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/nyregion/the-house-of-diy.html', 'snippet': 'In Brooklyn they do drag a little differently, as Stephanie Keith found out when she shot the second annual Mr(s) Williamsburg competition, a nine-week extravaganza where anything goes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The drag balls of Upper Manhattan are known for their celebrations of elegance, realness 