, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paris Wedding Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, Dickie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yang, Fiona', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T21:36:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Wall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2da6994a-0476-5fe2-8649-aa7abcea167a', 'word_count': 1257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2da6994a-0476-5fe2-8649-aa7abcea167a'}, {'abstract': 'The French choreographer Maud Le Pladec presented “Democracy,” a work laced with percussion and special lighting effects, at New York Live Arts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/arts/dance/maud-le-pladecs-percussive-democracy.html', 'snippet': 'The French choreographer Maud Le Pladec presented “Democracy,” a work laced with percussion and special lighting effects, at New York Live Arts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One by one, they arrived: nine people armed with sticks and facing off as if for a rumble. Rather than striking one another, though, they struck the cymbals on the four drum kits arrayed on the stage and kept striking them. Maud Le Pladec’s “Democracy” started not with one bang but with many.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Mosh Pit, or Maybe a Revolution', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Mosh Pit, or Maybe a Revolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Live Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Pladec, Maud', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T21:36:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc883825-5dbf-5f70-83bf-43a4431c6d11', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc883825-5dbf-5f70-83bf-43a4431c6d11'}, {'abstract': 'Major credit agencies are increasingly reporting the amount of borrowers’ payments, which experts say could soon be used in calculating credit risk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/your-money/for-better-credit-score-max-out-payments-not-the-card.html', 'snippet': 'Major credit agencies are increasingly reporting the amount of borrowers’ payments, which experts say could soon be used in calculating credit risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CREDIT reports, which track your management of credit cards and loans, increasingly include more details about when and how you pay your debts over time. Whether that extra information will eventually have a broad impact on your credit scores — the three-digit numbers that summarize your credit report and are used by lenders to size you up — remains to be seen.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Better Credit Score, Max Out Payments, Not the Card', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Better Credit Score, Max Out Payments, Not the Card', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrns, Ann', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fair Isaac Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equifax Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransUnion LLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Experian Group Ltd', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T21:36:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/454ed3e3-16e2-5ab0-9281-d9988ab7d2e8', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/454ed3e3-16e2-5ab0-9281-d9988ab7d2e8'}, {'abstract': 'Christian aTunde Adjuah, formerly known as Christian Scott, brought a 10-piece band and a new sound to the Harlem Jazz Shrines Festival on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/arts/music/christian-atunde-adjuah-brings-new-sound-to-a-jazz-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Christian aTunde Adjuah, formerly known as Christian Scott, brought a 10-piece band and a new sound to the Harlem Jazz Shrines Festival on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christian aTunde Adjuah has a firm, cold flash of a trumpet sound, like the glint off a brandished switchblade. For what seems like the entirety of his 