own this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Creativity brings disorientation — or vice versa? — in the music of two songwriters and sonic experimenters in town this week: Son Lux and Chad VanGaalen. Ryan Lott, who records as Son Lux, has collaborated widely with musicians like Sufjan Stevens and Lorde. In songs that lean toward the reflective — “What will we do now?/We’ve lost it to trying,” one goes — his music encompasses pinpoint orchestral arrangements as well as electronics that can be glitchy, glossy and dizzying. Son Lux appears Tuesday, sharing a bill with the guitarist Rafiq Bhatia as part of the Undead Music series. (8 p.m., Le Poisson Rouge, 158 Bleecker Street, near Thompson Street, Greenwich Village; 212-505-3474, lepoissonrouge.com.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Singular Sensations', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Singular Sensations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T23:02:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52216669-287f-5e84-9761-f168c9dbea1c', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52216669-287f-5e84-9761-f168c9dbea1c'}, {'abstract': 'Documentaries don’t come more disturbing than this examination of the confrontation between the police and the radical group MOVE in Philadelphia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/arts/television/in-a-blaze-of-confusion.html', 'snippet': 'Documentaries don’t come more disturbing than this examination of the confrontation between the police and the radical group MOVE in 