ac1688d4f'}, {'abstract': 'In their second union, the groom has to win over more than just the bride.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/fashion/weddings/a-second-union-to-a-commune-and-each-other.html', 'snippet': 'In their second union, the groom has to win over more than just the bride.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GUILFORD, Vt. — For Verandah Porche, there was never any question about where the wedding would take place. “This is home,” she said, waving an arm to encompass the rambling house, the rickety outbuildings, the steep fields and the gnarled orchard that make up Packer Corners, the storied commune that Ms. Porche helped found in 1968. It was also the site of her first marriage to the groom, Richard H. Coutant, in 1979. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/weddings/11VOWS1/11VOWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/weddings/11VOWS1/11VOWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/weddings/11VOWS1/11VOWS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/weddings/11VOWS1/11VOWS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1397, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/weddings/11VOWS1/11VOWS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/weddings/11VOWS1/11VOWS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/fashion/weddings/11VOWS1/11VOWS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Second Union, to a Commune and Each Other', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Second Union, to a Commune and Each Other', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vows (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T23:21:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marialisa Calta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marialisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1caa6bed-c479-5a76-a692-f26937327d70', 'word_count': 1605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1caa6bed-c479-5a76-a692-f26937327d70'}, {'abstract': 'The host of the Sirius XM satellite radio program “The Whoolywood Shuffle” spends Sundays on social media, and eats Frosted Flakes at night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/nyregion/dj-whoo-kid-a-social-media-butterfly.html', 'snippet': 'The host of the Sirius XM satellite radio program “The Whoolywood Shuffle” spends Sundays on social media, and eats Frosted Flakes at night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'D.J. Whoo Kid got his start making mixtapes, so long ago that he actually made them on tapes. He has D.J.’d for 50 Cent and G-Unit, and is currently the spicy-tongued host of the Sirius XM satellite radio program “The Whoolywood Shuffle,” where he interviews rap stars and entertainers as far afield as Willie Nelson (he asked the octogenarian Mr. Nelson whether he still got groupies). Born Yves Mondesir 42 years ago in Queens, he lives in Battery Park City and regularly spends time in New Jersey with his estranged wife and two teenage sons. “I haven’t been called by my real name in 20 years,” he said.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/nyregion/11ROUTINE1/11ROUTINE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/nyregion/11ROUTINE1/11ROUTINE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/nyregion/11ROUTINE1/11ROUTINE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/nyregion/11ROUTINE1/11ROUTINE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/nyregion/11ROUTINE1/11ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/11/nyregion/11ROUTINE1/11ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/nyregion/11ROUTINE1/11ROUTINE1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 