ge. Now, they can have their own coats of arms.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Step Forward Into Past for British Gay Couples: Coats of Arms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Step Forward Into Past for British Gay Couples: Coats of Arms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heraldry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Lords (Great Britain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'College of Arms (Great Britain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T23:45:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katrin Bennhold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78fe539b-753b-538e-b5e5-69d594e132dd', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78fe539b-753b-538e-b5e5-69d594e132dd'}, {'abstract': 'Two critics for The New York Times sample the world of contemporary work at the Frieze Art Fair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/arts/design/two-critics-sample-the-frieze-art-fair.html', 'snippet': 'Two critics for The New York Times sample the world of contemporary work at the Frieze Art Fair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The amazing spectacle that is Frieze New York is up and running on Randalls Island. With more than 190 contemporary art dealers from around the world inhabiting a temporary, quarter-mile-long white tent, it’s a dumbfounding display of human creative industry. Reasoning that in the time allowed, no one reviewer could hope to achieve a comprehensive overview of all there is to see, we both went to look and report. What follows is a sampler of things that caught our attention.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strolling an Island of Creativity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strolling an Island of Creativity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frieze Art Fair', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Randalls Island (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T23:47:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson and Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0322f4c2-9318-5c15-8836-c696b4fb5abd', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0322f4c2-9318-5c15-8836-c696b4fb5abd'}, {'abstract': 'Should the N.F.L. pool its resources and let players decide where to work, or will some teams inevitably gain an unfair competitive advantage?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2014/05/09/football-minus-the-draft/', 'snippet': 'Should the N.F.L. pool its resources and let players decide where to work, or will some teams inevitably gain an unfair competitive advantage?', 'lead_paragraph': 