government drastically increased the number of deaths. Two senior presidential aides met family representatives while hundreds of parents and their supporters staged a sit-in for 12 hours near the presidential palace. Meanwhile, prosecutors said Friday that they were seeking to arrest Kim Han-sik, the head of the Chonghaejin Marine Company, which operated the ferry, on charges of ignoring the overloading of the vessel. They were also looking into a family that owns a company that controls Chonghaejin Marine. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Korea: Victims’ Parents Assail President Over Government’s Response to Ferry Accident', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea: Victims’ Parents Assail President Over Government’s Response to Ferry Accident', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ferries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Geun-hye', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cheonghaejin Marine Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T23:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/486d7cfc-010a-5ea6-8648-f99bbf6fe90f', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/486d7cfc-010a-5ea6-8648-f99bbf6fe90f'}, {'abstract': 'Dodging a scrum of reporters, former Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy on Friday began serving his sentence for tax fraud at a nursing home outside Milan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/world/europe/italy-berlusconi-begins-his-community-service.html', 'snippet': 'Dodging a scrum of reporters, former Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy on Friday began serving his sentence for tax fraud at a nursing home outside Milan.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dodging a scrum of reporters, former Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy on Friday began serving his sentence for tax fraud at a nursing home outside Milan. Mr. Berlusconi, 77, was ordered to serve a year of community service, and he will spend four hours a week assisting Alzheimer’s patients. He did not stop to speak with reporters, slipping in and out of the nursing home, which is in Cesano Boscone. On Thursday, he told a radio station that he was certain that he would be able to help “those in need” and that the experience would enrich him. He also said that he had been studying the latest treatments for Alzheimer’s. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy: Berlusconi Begins His Community Service', 'kicker': 'World Briefing ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Berlusconi Begins His Community Service', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T23:56:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/59783b3c-2f07-5d45-adf8-733ae5ec91d9', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59783b3c-2f07-5d45-adf8-733ae5ec91d9'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican National Committee moved to reduce the number of presidential primary debates in 2016 and assert control over how they are run.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/us/politics/republicans-tighten-grip-on-debates-in-2016-race.html', 'snippet': 'The Republican National Committee moved to reduce the number of presidential primary debates in 2016 and assert control over how they are run.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEMPHIS — The Republican National Committee moved Friday to seize control of the presidential primary debates in 2016, another step in a coordinated effort by the party establishment to reshape the nominating process.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Tighten Grip on Debates in 2016 Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Tighten Grip on Debates in 2016 Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T23:56:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe01c238-a156-5dc7-81c0-94287e2be1c6', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe01c238-a156-5dc7-81c0-94287e2be1c6'}, {'abstract': 'Britain’s Defense Ministry said Friday that it had begun an investigation after graphic photos surfaced appearing to show at least one British service member posing next to the corpse of a Taliban fighter in Afghanistan in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/world/asia/afghanistan-british-military-to-investigate-photo-of-soldier-cavorting-next-to-dead-insurgent.html', 'snippet': 'Britain’s Defense Ministry said Friday that it had begun an investigation after graphic photos surfaced appearing to show at least one British service member posing next to the corpse of a Taliban fighter in Afghanistan in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Britain’s Defense Ministry said Friday that it had begun an investigation after graphic photos surfaced appearing to show at least one British service member posing next to the corpse of a Taliban fighter in Afghanistan in 2012. In one of the photos, a member of the military is kneeling next to a body and giving a thumbs-up sign, recalling some previous images of Western personnel in Afghanistan and Iraq that caused widespread offense in those countries. “This type of behavior is unacceptable and will not be tolerated,” said a statement from the Royal Air Force. A defense official confirmed news media reports in Britain that the incident took place after an attack by insurgents on Camp Bastion, the main British military base in Afghanistan’s Helmand Province. The photographs surfaced first on a website called Live Leak and were reproduced on many British newsweb sites with people’s faces concealed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan: British Military to Investigate Photo of Soldier Cavorting Next to Dead Insurgent', 'kicker': 'World Briefing ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan: British Military to Investigate Photo of Soldier Cavorting Next to Dead Insurgent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castle, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Air Force', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-09T23:59:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/efb74839-e3e9-5e5e-8937-ddbd8c55cbbb', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efb74839-e3e9-5e5e-8937-ddbd8c55cbbb'}, {'abstract': '“Family Reunion” in Briarcliff Manor is an evening of two British one-acts — “A Kind of Alaska” by Harold Pinter and “A Number” by Caryl Churchill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/nyregion/a-review-of-family-reunion-in-briarcliff-manor.html', 'snippet': '“Family Reunion” in Briarcliff Manor is an evening of two British one-acts — “A Kind of Alaska” by Harold Pinter and “A Number” by Caryl Churchill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They could have called it “Comas and Clones.” But Hudson Stage, presenting its last production in Briarcliff Manor before moving to Armonk this fall, has chosen a more dignified route and labeled its evening of two British one-acts — one by Harold Pinter and one by Caryl Churchill — “Family Reunion.” ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10',