 that you hardly know it’s there. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Big, Happy Budget', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Big, Happy Budget', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-10T01:09:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7fb599d-2254-53ad-b3cd-ed9521794c7c', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7fb599d-2254-53ad-b3cd-ed9521794c7c'}, {'abstract': 'At least twice in recent years, Beijing has sought to explore the South China Sea but backed down after protests by Vietnam. That good will evaporated this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/world/asia/in-high-seas-china-moves-unilaterally.html', 'snippet': 'At least twice in recent years, Beijing has sought to explore the South China Sea but backed down after protests by Vietnam. That good will evaporated this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — It is the pride of China’s state-run oil industry and the nation’s first deepwater drilling rig, a vessel as big as a football field and as tall as a 40-story building, with a $1 billion price tag. Last week, it crawled through the South China Sea, pulled by heavy-duty tugs, and parked in one of the most sensitive spots possible, about 17 miles off a speck of an island claimed by both China and Vietnam.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In High Seas, China Moves Unilaterally', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In High Seas, China Moves Unilaterally', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perlez, Jane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China National Offshore Oil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paracel Islands', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-10T01:10:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez and Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/919dbc80-76f7-5d4b-a2d4-19b40d6a0fb9', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/919dbc80-76f7-5d4b-a2d4-19b40d6a0fb9'}, {'abstract': 'A United States Special Operations commando and a C.I.A. officer killed two armed Yemeni civilians who tried to kidnap them in the capital two weeks ago, American officials said on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/world/middleeast/