f_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f52216c-4536-56f5-960f-a3db7ab60bf4', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f52216c-4536-56f5-960f-a3db7ab60bf4'}, {'abstract': 'It is impressive that prosecutors known as the “grandchildren generation” have opened investigations into dozens of long-dormant cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/opinion/germanys-pursuit-of-death-camp-guards.html', 'snippet': 'It is impressive that prosecutors known as the “grandchildren generation” have opened investigations into dozens of long-dormant cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With time running out, a new generation of criminal prosecutors in Germany has opened dozens of fresh investigations into long-dormant cases of death-camp guards suspected of culpable roles in the Nazi genocide machine. Men and women left to live in freedom for decades after World War II are finally being scrutinized for their work in the camps, with modern technology like 3-D visualizations of the camps being used to contradict their claims that they never were able to witness the ghastly routines of the Holocaust. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany’s Pursuit of Death Camp Guards', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany’s Pursuit of Death Camp Guards', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concentration Camps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Demjanjuk, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guards', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocid