ort by hundreds of names to qualify for the primary ballot in August.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Representative John Conyers Jr., who has represented the Detroit area in the House for almost 50 years, is in danger of not making the ballot for an August primary because his petitions may be disqualified for not containing enough signatures.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Signatures on Petitions for Conyers Fall Short', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Signatures on Petitions for Conyers Fall Short', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conyers, John Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congress', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheffield, Horace', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-10T04:54:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/962b7047-a3ce-5799-abb5-4ac03f5c349a', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/962b7047-a3ce-5799-abb5-4ac03f5c349a'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) PRISONERS (2013) Keller Dover (Hugh Jackman), a grief-stricken father in a small Pennsylvania town, contemplates the torture and murder of the man (Paul Dano, above right, with Mr. Jackman) he believes has kidnapped his daughter and her friend in this thriller, directed by Denis Villeneuve. Maria Bello plays Dover’s wife, submerged in despair; Viola Davis and Terrence Howard are the other girl’s parents, whose doubts about Dover’s means of extracting information strike him as weak and irrational; Melissa Leo is the suspect’s aunt, intent on shielding her mentally disabled nephew; and Jake Gyllenhaal is the tormented cop determined to solve the case. “\xa0‘Prisoners’ is the kind of movie that can quiet a room full of casual thrill-seekers,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “It absorbs and controls your attention with such assurance that you hold your breath for fear of distracting the people on screen, exhaling in relief or amazement at each new revelation. By the end you may be a little worn out, and perhaps also slightly let down by the fussily clever revelations that wrap up the story, but in the meantime you are a willing captive, unable to tell the difference between dread and delight.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-10T05:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a4733e6-5f66-5a03-bd18-380d4b1b1b2a', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a4733e6-5f66-5a03-bd18-380d4b1b1b2a'}, {'abstract': 'India Ink follows up with the television journalist, known for his aggressive interviews, after his one-on-one with Narendra Modi of the Bharatiya Janata Party.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/a-second-conversation-with-times-now-editor-arnab-goswami/', 'snippet': 'India Ink follows up with the television journalist, known for his aggressive interviews, after his one-on-one with Narendra Modi of the Bharatiya Janata Party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arnab Goswami, editor in chief of the Times Now television channel, is the only journalist to have interviewed the two main contenders in the Indian national elections: Rahul Gandhi, vice president of the Indian National Congress party, and Narendra Modi, prime ministerial candidate of the opposition Bharatiya Janata Party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/world/asia/12-arnab-indiaink/12-arnab-indiaink-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/12/world/asia/12-arnab-indiaink/12-arnab-indiaink-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/world/asia/12-arnab-indiaink/12-arnab-indiaink-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/world/asia/12-arnab-indiaink/12-arnab-indiaink-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1079, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/world/asia/12-arnab-indiaink/12-arnab-indi