icle/7bfcf9ec-4c9e-5d1a-9bcb-7f4e40c75de7', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bfcf9ec-4c9e-5d1a-9bcb-7f4e40c75de7'}, {'abstract': 'State Republicans are so determined to keep low-income people from getting Medicaid that they may copy their national counterparts and shut down the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/opinion/sunday/a-health-care-showdown-in-virginia.html', 'snippet': 'State Republicans are so determined to keep low-income people from getting Medicaid that they may copy their national counterparts and shut down the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Virginia, there are 400,000 low-income people who can’t afford health coverage but don’t qualify for federal insurance subsidies. If they lived across the state line in Maryland, West Virginia or Kentucky, which have expanded their Medicaid programs, they could get the coverage they need. Terry McAuliffe, the Virginia governor, campaigned on bringing an expanded Medicaid program to Virginia, too.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Health Care Showdown in Virginia', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Health Care Showdown in Virginia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAuliffe, Terry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-10T18:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1d50f19-1435-5ff7-9aff-e8e0f4f52c3c', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1d50f19-1435-5ff7-9aff-e8e0f4f52c3c'}, {'abstract': 'A metaphysical discussion of our place in the universe and the future of humankind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/opinion/sunday/of-humans-and-nature.html', 'snippet': 'A metaphysical discussion of our place in the universe and the future of humankind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A metaphysical discussion of our place in the universe and the future of humankind.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11LETTERSsub/11LETTERSsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11LETTERSsub/11LETTERSsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11LETTERSsub/11LETTERSsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-review/11LETTERSsub/11LETTERSsub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sunday-r