'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c55478d2-6f0a-5c9e-acc4-b131153de016', 'word_count': 2514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c55478d2-6f0a-5c9e-acc4-b131153de016'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Savage of Pittsburgh, who played for three programs in five years, was selected by the Texans. A punter who went to the Bears was the first special-teams player picked.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/sports/football/houston-is-next-for-a-nomadic-quarterback.html', 'snippet': 'Tom Savage of Pittsburgh, who played for three programs in five years, was selected by the Texans. A punter who went to the Bears was the first special-teams player picked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several notable quarterbacks came off the board during Day 3 of the N.F.L. draft Saturday, including Tom Savage of Pittsburgh, who went in the fourth round to the Houston Texans (135th over all). A few years ago, it would have been tough to imagine Savage’s being drafted, as he was in the middle of a meandering five-year career in which he played for three programs.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Houston Is Next for a Nomadic Quarterback', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Houston Is Next for a Nomadic Quarterback', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Texans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T00:06:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/503b125e-a9ca-53ef-9c41-c9e23d5cacb4', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/503b125e-a9ca-53ef-9c41-c9e23d5cacb4'}, {'abstract': 'Jordan Spieth finished the third round at TPC Sawgrass under par for the day, his one-under 71 giving him a share of the lead, at 12-under 204, with Martin Kaymer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/sports/golf/spieth-avoids-bogeys-to-claim-share-of-players-lead.html', 'snippet': 'Jordan Spieth finished the third round at TPC Sawgrass under par for the day, his one-under 71 giving him a share of the lead, at 12-under 204, with Martin Kaymer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PONTE VEDRA BEACH, Fla. — For Jordan Spieth, golf-course etiquette extends to how he refers to his elders, which includes everyone in this week’s Players Championship field. Grouped in the final twosome Saturday with the 29-year-old Martin Kaymer — or, as Spieth was tempted to call him, Mr. Kaymer — Spieth, 20, was as patient as a hunter in a deer blind. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sports/PGA-1/golf-1399765583039-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/sports/PGA-1/golf-1399765583039-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 560}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sports/PGA-1/golf-1399765583039-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/sports/PGA-1/golf-1399765583039