], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/86197a08-97ee-52b8-86db-40d5c8a8a6ce', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86197a08-97ee-52b8-86db-40d5c8a8a6ce'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, March 2, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/03/02/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-sunday-march-2-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, March 2, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The presence of Russian troops in Crimea now is unacceptable.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, March 2, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T05:41:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/46ce0d0e-5b41-5077-8546-1c9c47315aab', 'word_count': 19, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46ce0d0e-5b41-5077-8546-1c9c47315aab'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday March 1, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/03/01/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-saturday-march-01-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday March 1, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There will be costs.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday March 1, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T05:41:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/3766f25e-4cc0-54d7-93e4-f1cb5fbf3c61', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3766f25e-4cc0-54d7-93e4-f1cb5fbf3c61'}, {'abstract': 'Quotations of the Day for Wednesday, March 4, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/03/05/pageoneplus/quotations-of-the-day-for-wednesday-march-5-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotations of the Day for Wednesday, March 4, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It is not appropriate to invade a country and at the end of a barrel of a gun dictate what you are trying to achieve.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotations of the Day for Wednesday, March 5, 2014.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotations of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T05:42:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/dde8d4e9-249b-522f-98bb-e264d93690cb', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dde8d4e9-249b-522f-98bb-e264d93690cb'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/arts/television/whats-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (NBC) ROSEMARY’S BABY In this two-part remake of the 1968 Roman Polanski thriller, the director Agnieszka Holland transfers the setting from the Dakota on Central Park West to the Eighth Arrondissement of Paris, where Rosemary Woodhouse (Zoe Saldana, above) has moved with her husband, Guy (Patrick J. Adams), a writer with a teaching stint at the Sorbonne. Ms. Holland also transforms the dotty older couple next door, first played by Ruth Gordon and Sidney Blackmer, into French sophisticates (Carole Bouquet and Jason Isaacs) who offer the Americans their friendship and a spare apartment. This being Paris, they discuss the transaction in an elegant sex club. And when Rosemary, eager to get pregnant again after a miscarriage, visits an OBGYN, the examining room looks like the rare-books section of the Académie Française. “\xa0‘Rosemary’s Baby’ bends to current fashions, and, accordingly, is more straightforward and much gorier than the original film,” Alessandra Stanley wrote in The New York Times. “But partly because the story has been so altered, it still has mystery and suspense. And because it’s Paris, it is possible to wonder, at least for a while, if maybe the problem is Rosemary, not her neighbors, who seem so serenely superior and all knowing.” Part 2 will be shown on Thursday at 9.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T05:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/41a9c285-2a49-52d5-b299-dece638ea813', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41a9c285-2a49-52d5-b299-dece638ea813'}, {'abstract': 'Works performed by David Wampach and Claudia Triozzi at Abrons Arts Center focused as much on bodily sounds as they did on movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/10/arts/dance/at-abrons-arts-works-focusing-on-bodily-sounds.html', 'snippet': 'Works performed by David Wampach and Claudia Triozzi at Abrons Arts Center focused as much on bodily sounds as they did on movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Danse: A French-American Festival of Performance and Ideas is eclectic by design. Each of the institutions taking part in this citywide series has made its own programming choices. For the double bill it presented on Tuesday, Abrons Arts Center gravitated toward the outer edges of conventional definitions of dance. Both of the works — one by Claudia Triozzi, the other by David Wampach — were as focused on the sounds the body makes as on how a body might move. Both began with an open mouth, stretched as in the Munch painting, ready to scream. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/arts/TRIOZZI2/TRIOZZI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/15/arts/TRIOZZI2/TRIOZZI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/arts/TRIOZZI2/TRIOZZI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/arts/TRIOZZI2/TRIOZZI2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1269, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/arts/TRIOZZI2/TRIOZZI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/15/arts/TRIOZZI2/TRIOZZI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/arts/TRIOZZI2/TRIOZZI2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main'