d_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8bcdbed-47d2-5e7a-8b84-4f00c7694fe5'}, {'abstract': 'Families displaced 47 years ago worry that they will not be able to afford housing in a new development being built on the site of their old tenements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/nyregion/on-the-lower-east-side-rebuilding-a-neighborhood-but-not-a-community.html', 'snippet': 'Families displaced 47 years ago worry that they will not be able to afford housing in a new development being built on the site of their old tenements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like relics from a past civilization, tiny chunks of cracked tile and smashed bricks rest in the dirt of parking lots or empty lots along the south side of Delancey Street, near the corner of Clinton Street. They attest to a community on the Lower East Side of Manhattan that vanished 47 years ago, when some 1,800 families, mostly poor and Puerto Rican, were uprooted and their tenement homes demolished in the name of urban renewal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/nyregion/12SIDESTREETweb/12SIDESTREETweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/12/nyregion/12SIDESTREETweb/12SIDESTREETweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/nyregion/12SIDESTREETweb/12SIDESTREETweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/nyregion/12SIDESTREETweb/12SIDESTREETweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1273, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'r