-8f77-83012fcafb61'}, {'abstract': 'Conchita Wurst was the runaway winner of this year’s 59th annual Eurovision Song Contest in Copenhagen.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/austrian-singer-wins-eurovision-contest/', 'snippet': 'Conchita Wurst was the runaway winner of this year’s 59th annual Eurovision Song Contest in Copenhagen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — With a shimmering golden gown, trim dark beard and voice made for Broadway, an Austrian drag queen, Conchita Wurst, was the runaway winner of this year’s 59th annual Eurovision Song Contest on Saturday in Copenhagen.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Austrian Singer Wins Eurovision Contest', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Contest Winner With a Message', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eurovision Song Contest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T19:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dc14a91-d1d4-5ab3-977f-caf8782428b0', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dc14a91-d1d4-5ab3-977f-caf8782428b0'}, {'abstract': 'The No. 1 movie in the United States and Canada over the weekend was an R-rated comedy that rode strong reviews and a well-oiled marketing campaign to an astounding $51.1 million in ticket sales.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/11/neighbors-tops-weekend-box-office/', 'snippet': 'The No. 1 movie in the United States and Canada over the weekend was an R-rated comedy that rode strong reviews and a well-oiled marketing campaign to an astounding $51.1 million in ticket sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sorry, Spidey. A raunchy fraternity just threw a bong through your web. The No. 1 movie in the United States and Canada over the weekend was “Neighbors,” an R-rated comedy that rode strong reviews and a well-oiled marketing campaign to an astounding $51.1 million in ticket sales, trampling “The Amazing Spider-Man 2.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/movies/11neighbors/11neighbors-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/11/movies/11neighbors/11neighbors-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/movies/11neighbors/11neighbors-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/movies/11neighbors/11neighbors-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/movies/11neighbors/11neighbors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/11/movies/11neighbors/11neighbors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/11/movies/11neighbors/11neighbors-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_