t the Pennsylvania Ballet, a Director’s Choice program included works by Christopher Wheeldon and Robert Weiss and a world premiere by Trey McIntyre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — The Pennsylvania Ballet, celebrating its 50th anniversary this season, is in transition. Last weekend it presented what it called a Director’s Choice triple bill, which had been announced last year. Two weeks ago, the company said its artistic director, Roy Kaiser, would step down at the end of the season.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/SUBMCINTYRE/SUBMCINTYRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/SUBMCINTYRE/SUBMCINTYRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/SUBMCINTYRE/SUBMCINTYRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/SUBMCINTYRE/SUBMCINTYRE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/SUBMCINTYRE/SUBMCINTYRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/SUBMCINTYRE/SUBMCINTYRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/SUBMCINTYRE/SUBMCINTYRE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, '