: 'Walter Isaacson, the best-selling biographer and president of the Aspen Institute, will deliver the 43rd annual Jefferson Lecture on Monday night at the Kennedy Center in Washington. The lecture is sponsored by the National Endowment for the Humanities and considered the federal government’s highest honor in the humanities. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walter Isaacson to Deliver Jefferson Lecture', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Speaker for Annual Jefferson Lecture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isaacson, Walter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aspen Institute', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Endowment for the Humanities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T21:41:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a74046b-6e0e-5ed5-ad18-06ddec370d5d', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a74046b-6e0e-5ed5-ad18-06ddec370d5d'}, {'abstract': 'A shared program by the dancers Ashley Chen and Dylan Crossman at the Club at La MaMa on Friday was partly sophisticated and partly sophomoric.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/arts/dance/ashley-chen-and-dylan-crossman-at-the-club-at-la-mama.html', 'snippet': 'A shared program by the dancers Ashley Chen and Dylan Crossman at the Club at La MaMa on Friday was partly sophisticated and partly sophomoric.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sidewalk in front of the Club at La MaMa on Friday night was teeming with people needing a fix of Merce past. The lure was a shared program featuring Ashley Chen and Dylan Crossman, two much-admired former members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, in a dual presentation by Danse: A French-American Festival of Performance and Ideas, and La MaMa Moves! Dance Festival. Before the house opened, Mr. Chen joined the crowd to smoke a cigarette; as he put it, “It’s the French warm-up.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/CHEN/CHEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/CHEN/CHEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 357}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/CHEN/CHEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/CHEN/CHEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1220, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/CHEN/CHEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/CHEN/CHEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/arts/CHEN/CHEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Driven to Accumulate and Dancing Till Nothing’s Left', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Driven to Accumulate and Dancing Till Nothing’s Left', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, Ashley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crossman, Dylan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T21:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c451f493-ab32-5826-b5d8-68d63c16e331', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c451f493-ab32-5826-b5d8-68d63c16e331'}, {'abstract': 'Dance companies from France, The Hague and Denmark will appear in the Joyce Theater’s fall and winter lineup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/arts/dance/dance-lineups-announced.html', 'snippet': 'Dance companies from France, The Hague and Denmark will appear in the Joyce Theater’s fall and winter lineup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dance companies from France, The Hague and Denmark will appear in the Joyce Theater’s fall and winter lineup, said Joyce officials, who recently announced that the National Ballet of Canada would open the season on Sept. 9 with Christopher Wheeldon’s “Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland.” The schedule will also include Pacific Northwest Ballet performing works by Mr. Wheeldon and Alejandro Cerrudo (Oct. 8 to 12), the all-male company Les Ballets Trockadero de Monte Carlo (Dec. 16 to Jan. 4), and Royal Danish Ballet principals and soloists (Jan. 13 to 18). The French-Argentinean tango group Cia Unión Tanguera will perform from Sept. 23 to Oct. 5 as part of its “Nuit Blanche” North American tour, and the flamenco dancer Soledad Barrio is slated to bring her company, Noche Flamenca, to the Joyce from Oct. 29 to Nov. 9.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dance Lineups Announced', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance Lineups Announced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T21:48:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d8481b9-1f0a-5d20-b5d3-362ebb933926', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d8481b9-1f0a-5d20-b5d3-362ebb933926'}, {'abstract': 'Timothy F. Geithner, the former Treasury secretary, recounts his view of the financial crisis in “Stress Test.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/books/in-stress-test-timothy-f-geithner-recalls-crisis-days.html', 'snippet': 'Timothy F. Geithner, the former Treasury secretary, recounts his view of the financial crisis in “Stress Test.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'One afternoon in the summer of 2008, as the financial system was careening toward the abyss that would send the United States into the worst economic emergency \xa0since the Great Depression, Timothy F. Geithner — then president of the Federal Reserve Bank of New York, and later, President Obama’s Treasury secretary — tried to lighten the mood in his office with “an impromptu contest for the best metaphor for what was happening.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subty