, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T22:08:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c54e0f4-8074-5200-9791-73308aef715e', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c54e0f4-8074-5200-9791-73308aef715e'}, {'abstract': 'Jessica González-Rojas of the National Latina Institute for Reproductive Health responds to a news article.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/opinion/latinos-and-abortion.html', 'snippet': 'Jessica González-Rojas of the National Latina Institute for Reproductive Health responds to a news article.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Latinos and Abortion', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Latinos and Abortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T22:10:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/03e3be53-5103-5d08-b666-c2feadaef1bf', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03e3be53-5103-5d08-b666-c2feadaef1bf'}, {'abstract': '“The Events,” a drama by the Scottish playwright David Greig, will have its New York premiere at New York Theater Workshop next winter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/theater/a-new-york-premiere-for-a-scottish-play.html', 'snippet': '“The Events,” a drama by the Scottish playwright David Greig, will have its New York premiere at New York Theater Workshop next winter.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Events,” a moving drama by the Scottish playwright David Greig, about the aftermath and community response when a tragedy takes place in a small town, will have its New York premiere at New York Theater Workshop next winter, the theater planned to announce on Monday. The show, directed by Ramin Gray, was first presented at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe last summer, where it drew critical praise and won several awards, including the Carol Tambor Best of Edinburgh honor. In Edinburgh, a different local choir was featured at each performance, providing a musical element while also aiding the plot in other ways, much like a Greek chorus. New York Theater Workshop plans to take a similar approach. “The Events,” which makes its United States premiere in June at the International Festival of Arts and Ideas in New Haven, will come to New York in February. The show rounds out the previously announced New York Theater Workshop season.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New York Premiere for a Scottish Play', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New York Premiere for a Scottish Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McElroy, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Theater Workshop', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greig, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Events (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-11T22:10:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlenam