sports/football/questions-about-nfl-drafts-future-center-on-site-date-and-length.html', 'snippet': 'After a cramped event at Radio City Music Hall, the N.F.L. is considering other locations, as well as the addition of a fourth day and other changes.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0If the 2014 N.F.L. draft was the event’s swan song at Radio City Music Hall, it was quite a number. From the hysteria around Johnny Manziel on opening night to Michael Sam’s selection near the end of the third day, it was one of the most memorable of the nine consecutive drafts held at Radio City, the venerable theater in Midtown Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions About N.F.L. Draft’s Future Involve Location, Date and Length', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Questions About Draft’s Future Center on Site, Date and Length', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio City Music Hall', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-12T00:07:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3e4fc41-8f51-54f3-bc42-add122f88da1', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3e4fc41-8f51-54f3-bc42-add122f88da1'}, {'abstract': 'Last August, three men were arrested and accused of “illegal fund-raising,” charges that stemmed from their effort to finance a Uighur-language school in Xinjiang, China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/world/asia/a-devotion-to-language-proves-risky.html', 'snippet': 'Last August, three men were arrested and accused of “illegal fund-raising,” charges that stemmed from their effort to finance a Uighur-language school in Xinjiang, China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — A poet, linguist and globe-trotting polyglot, Abduweli Ayup had a passion for the spoken word, notably Uighur, the Turkic language spoken in his homeland in China’s far northwest. In 2011, soon after finishing his graduate studies in the United States, Mr. Ayup returned home to open a chain of “mother tongue” schools in Xinjiang, the vast Central Asian region whose forced marriage to the Han Chinese heartland has become increasingly tumultuous.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/world/JP-UIGHUR/JP-UIGHUR-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/12/world/JP-UIGHUR/JP-UIGHUR-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/world/JP-UIGHUR/JP-UIGHUR-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 603, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/world/JP-UIGHUR/JP-UIGHUR-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 603, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/world/JP-UIGHUR/JP-UIGHUR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'heig