er,” relegating me to an imagined intellectual wasteland of sippy cups and Legos. But being a mother animates and inspires my activism.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/why-i-play-the-mom-card/', 'snippet': 'When critics (usually men) want to delegitimize my views, they often refer to me as a “mommy blogger,” relegating me to an imagined intellectual wasteland of sippy cups and Legos. But being a mother animates and inspires my activism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago, I was named one of the “Top 15 Most Important Moms in the Food Industry” by an online women’s magazine. I was tickled by the recognition so I shared the link with my Twitter followers. But minutes later a fellow food-policy advocate, a woman with two advanced degrees and a book to her name (but no children), tweeted back archly: “Congrats. Does having a cat count?” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/us/Motherlode-gun-demo/COLORADO-2inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/us/Motherlode-gun-demo/COLORADO-2inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/us/Motherlode-gun-demo/COLORADO-2inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/us/Motherlode-gun-demo/COLORADO-2inline-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/us/Motherlode-gun-demo/COLORADO-2inline-thumbStandard.jpg'