r Watch column.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/pay-dispute-threatens-some-high-cost-legal-cases-in-britain/', 'snippet': 'A British court ruling in a fraud case could end up shifting some cases involving cross-border violations to the United States, Peter J. Henning writes in the White Collar Watch column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A ruling from a British court about the inability to find lawyers for a group of defendants charged with fraud calls into question whether the British authorities will be able to pursue complex white-collar crime prosecutions without paying more for lawyers to take such cases. The decision could end up shifting some cases to the United States, which does not face the same issues as Britain in paying for legal defense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/business/dealbook/dbpix-henning/dbpix-henning-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/12/business/dealbook/dbpix-henning/dbpix-henning-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/business/dealbook/dbpix-henning/dbpix-henning-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/business/dealbook/dbpix-henning/dbpix-henning-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/business/dealbook/dbpix-henning/dbpix-henning-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/12/business/dealbook/dbpix-henning/dbpix-henning-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/business/dealbook/dbpix-henning/dbpix-henning-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pay Dispute Threatens Some High-Cost Legal Cases in Britain', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-12T17:05:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/958f037a-e1ae-56f5-a77f-b7f68a54387c', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/958f037a-e1ae-56f5-a77f-b7f68a54387c'}, {'abstract': 'Within a 24-hour period during the Battle of Spotsylvania, North and South wracked up more than 15,000 casualties.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/general-barlow-and-the-bloody-angle/', 'snippet': 'Within a 24-hour period during the Battle of Spotsylvania, North and South wracked up more than 15,000 casualties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After being mauled by the Army of Northern Virginia in the Battle of the Wilderness, which took place in the dense central Virginia woods from May 5 to 7, 1864, Maj. Gen. Ulysses S. Grant pushed his troops southeast toward the small hamlet of Spotsylvania Court House, intending to get between the Confederates and their capital. But Robert E. Lee’s men won the race to the village, thwarting Grant’s designs and setting the stage for the Battle of Spotsylvania, which would rage for 12 days, one of the longest and bloodiest engagements of the war. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'General Barlow and the Bloody Angle', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Ulysses S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Robert E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of Northern Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of the Potomac', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-12T17:19:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard F. Welch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Welch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9176d781-545f-5a60-af77-0e8004e4cc76', 'word_count': 1632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9176d781-545f-5a60-af77-0e8004e4cc76'}, {'abstract': 'Coding is growing as a kids’ activity, but as trendy as it is, it’s not easy. Most children won’t seize on coding games with the same enthusiasm as they did Minecraft. To engage kids in what’s happening behind the screen takes work.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/when-kids-would-rather-play-computer-games-than-code-them/', 'snippet': 'Coding is growing as a kids’ activity, but as trendy as it is, it’s not easy. Most children won’t seize on coding games with the same enthusiasm as they did Minecraft. To engage kids in what’s happening behind the screen takes work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coding is trending. In schools. Twenty thousand teachers from kindergarten through 12th grade have introduced coding lessons, according to Code.org, a group backed by the tech industry that offers free curriculums. Thirty school districts, including New York City and Chicago, have agreed to add coding classes in the fall, mainly in high schools but in lower grades, too. At home, parents are downloading programs that promise to teach children coding basics, and toys that can be coded in various ways are lining up for the next holiday season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/us/motherlode-coding/motherlode-coding-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/13/us/motherlode-coding/motherlode-coding-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/us/motherlode-coding/motherlode-coding-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/us/motherlode-coding/motherlode-coding-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/us/motherlode-coding/motherlode-coding-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/13/us/motherlode-coding/motherlode-coding-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/us/motherlode-coding/motherlode-coding-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Kids Would Rather Play Computer Games Than Code Them', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Code.org', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-12T17:25:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2cd61e8-68c7-5d22-907b-1824731705f4', 'word_count': 1006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2cd61e8-68c7-5d22-907b-1824731705f4'}, {'abstract': 'The duo, featuring former members of Megafaun and Mountain Man, releases its first album tomorrow. An exclusive remix of their single “Coffee” is available here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/interview-sylvan-esso-exclusive-remix-coffee-song/', 'snippet': 'The duo, featuring former members of Megafaun and Mountain Man, releases its first album tomorrow. An exclusive remix of their single “Coffee” is available here.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Is it the kind of coffee that makes you feel like a crazy person?” asks Amelia Meath, one half of the Durham, N.C.-based electronic duo Sylvan Esso. The inquiry is directed toward a server at Café Stella, a Silver Lake bistro popular with the indie set (members of the bands Warpaint and the Afghan Whigs have also been known to dine there). “I have a problem with certain coffees,” Meath clarifies. “One sip and I know it’s going to turn me into a terrible person.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12esso-diehl/12esso-diehl-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12esso-diehl/12esso-diehl-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12esso-diehl/12esso-diehl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12esso-diehl/12esso-diehl-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1222, 'width': 917, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12esso-diehl/12esso-diehl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12esso-diehl/12esso-diehl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12esso-diehl/12esso-diehl-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Listen Up | Sylvan Esso’s Quirky, Caffeinated Synth-Pop', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-12T17:30:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By MATT DIEHL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DIEHL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45cb23e3-47e0-53e6-9382-92a8038a81d4', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45cb23e3-47e0-53e6-9382-92a8038a81d4'}, {'abstract': 'Forgo the automated apps for a month and see whether manually entering transactions sharpens your awareness of your budget, a financial planner suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/your-money/household-budgeting/a-slow-tech-approach-to-tracking-spending.html', 'snippet': 'Forgo the automated apps for a month and see whether manually entering transactions sharpens your awareness of your budget, a financial planner suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years ago, I tracked every penny of our family’s spending. That’s good, right? Over time, however, I lost sight of why I was doing it and eventually stopped. Recently, I decided to try it again, and I find myself having the same mental conversation every time I sit down with my receipts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/business/051214bucks-carl-sketch/051214bucks-carl-sketch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 326, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/12/business/051214bucks-carl-sketch/051214bucks-carl-sketch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 326}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/business/051214bucks-carl-sketch/051214bucks-carl-sketch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 556, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/business/051214bucks-carl-sketch/051214bucks-carl-sketch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1112, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/business/051214bucks-carl-sketch/051214bucks-carl-sketch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/12/business/051214bucks-carl-sketch/051214bucks-carl-sketch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/business/051214bucks-carl-sketch/051214bucks-carl-sketch-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Slow-Tech Approach to Tracking Spending', 'kicker': 'Sketch Guy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-12T17:49:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'subsection_name': 'Household Budgeting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/480f6b86-a782-557d-b9cb-2500925fea72', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/480f6b86-a782-557d-b9cb-2500925fea72'}, {'abstract': 'Lewis Hamilton won his fourth consecutive Formula One race this season; Jeff Gordon took a Nascar Sprint Cup win in Kansas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/automobiles/monday-motorsports-another-mercedes-1-2-finish-in-formula-one.html', 'snippet': 'Lewis Hamilton won his fourth consecutive Formula One race this season; Jeff Gordon took a Nascar Sprint Cup win in Kansas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lewis Hamilton and Nico Rosberg, teammates on the Mercedes-Benz Formula One team, finished one-two, a second apart, in the Spanish Grand Prix on Sunday, continuing Mercedes’s distinct superiority so far this season. Daniel Ricciardo, in the Red Bull Infiniti, came in a distant third, followed by Sebastian Vettel, his teammate and the defending series champion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/10/automobiles/10MOTORSPORTS-image1/10MOTORSPORTS-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/10/automobiles/10MOTORSPORTS-image1/10MOTORSPORTS-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, '