ebac7b', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a17cf0c5-fdd6-5eed-8995-034875ebac7b'}, {'abstract': 'A weekend in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/weekend-gun-report-may-9-11-2014/', 'snippet': 'A weekend in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last March, when Facebook promised to crack down on gun advertising by deleting posts from people looking to buy or sell guns without background checks, it was heralded as a victory by some gun-control groups. Others, however, hoped for the outright ban of gun ads, à la Craigslist and eBay. Instead, the social network said it would hide posts peddling guns from minors and remind users to follow local gun laws.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/opinion/love/love-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/12/opinion/love/love-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/opinion/love/love-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/opinion/love/love-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/opinion/love/love-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/12/opinion/love/love-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/opinion/love/love-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Gun Report: May 9-11, 2014', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-12T18:37:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9572a10d-0ae4-5adc-9351-a226f1f70bba', 'word_count': 4364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9572a10d-0ae4-5adc-9351-a226f1f70bba'}, {'abstract': 'Once again, the G.O.P.’s moderate wing is missing an opportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/12/republican-moderates-and-the-minimum-wage/', 'snippet': 'Once again, the G.O.P.’s moderate wing is missing an opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of my first columns for the Times was a non-requiem for Arlen Specter’s career as a moderate Republican, in which I argued that the G.O.P. desperately needed “a better sort of centrist” than the Specter-esque, “socially liberal, fiscally conservative” northeasterners to whom the label has usually been applied. One theme in that piece, which has run through my commentary on the Republican Party ever since, is that a moderate wing of the G.O.P. that just imitates the Democrats on a few issues where the liberal line is popular isn’t necessarily doing either its party or the country any great favors. To be truly constructive in their moderation, the G.O.P.’s centrists should be advancing alternatives to popular liberal ideas —\xa0trying to create a different center of political gravity, in effect, rather than just looking for ways to take some losing issues off the table.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Moderates and the Minimum Wage', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Specter, Arlen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Enterprise Institute for Public Policy Research', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-12T18:38:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9c7028e-cd23-5c5e-ac5b-2f396b6a7990', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9c7028e-cd23-5c5e-ac5b-2f396b6a7990'}, {'abstract': 'Plus how to back up an iPod Nano.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/technology/personaltech/saving-your-favorite-videos-on-youtube.html', 'snippet': 'Plus how to back up an iPod Nano.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. My YouTube mobile app has a nice “+” button for adding a video to my playlist of favorites, but I don’t see a similar button on the desktop browser version of YouTube. How do you do it from the computer?', 'print_section': 'B', 'p