/05/12/q-and-a-sterling-ruby-hauser-and-wirth-raf-simons-frieze-whitney-biennial/', 'snippet': 'The multidisciplinary star, whose new show opened at Hauser & Wirth last Friday, reflects on his place in the art world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Numerous New York galleries and museums synced their best shows to Frieze weekend, including Hauser & Wirth, which opened a much-anticipated new exhibition by the Los Angeles polymath Sterling Ruby at its newly renovated West 19th Street space last Friday. It’s Ruby’s first solo show in Chelsea since he parked two menacing, rectilinear forms (a bus and a big brick of human-size cages) inside the Pace Gallery four years ago. This new show, entitled “Sunrise, Sunset,” presents a dense cross-section of recent works the prolific and controversial artist has produced in his fabled studio-cum-industrial-complex on the outskirts of Downtown L.A. — where only weeks ago, a Mack truck veered off the road and through the wall of the building, destroying a number of mammoth spray paintings and Ruby’s studio manager’s car (fortunately, no one was injured). Though the accident was a setback, the grandiose, unexpected destruction of the incident aligned well with Ruby’s expansive practice. The exhibition is full of charged objects, including Corinthian columns dripping with lustrous red polyurethane, a super-size canary-yellow electric chair, infernal stoves and bleached fabrics that evoke everything from Rorschach tests to the American flag. Here, the artist reflects on his intentions for the show and his place in the art world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12ruby-mcgarry/12ruby-mcgarry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12ruby-mcgarry/12ruby-mcgarry-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12ruby-mcgarry/12ruby-mcgarry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12ruby-mcgarry/12ruby-mcgarry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12ruby-mcgarry/12ruby-mcgarry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12ruby-mcgarry/12ruby-mcgarry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/12/t-magazine/12ruby-mcgarry/12ruby-mcgarry-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. | Sterling Ruby on Making It in L.A., His New Show in New York and the Power of the Art Market', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruby, Sterling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-12T20:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb42b11e-508b-5785-b331-ebcfe5473237', 'word_count': 1142, 'uri': '