e proposal to decentralize the system to smaller stations that use solar or wind power could lead a national revolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In one of the most promising moves in the energy sector in years, New York State is proposing a way to get a head start on, and perhaps help lead, a revolution in the world of electricity generation. Starting this week, the main players in the state’s complex electricity business will be asked to comment on a new report from the state’s Public Service Commission that envisions more efficient and climate-friendly ways to produce electricity. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smarter Electricity in New York', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smarter Electricity in New York ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Service Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T01:10:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/46f7fab5-20c1-50ec-91ee-a4dce3937e30', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46f7fab5-20c1-50ec-91ee-a4dce3937e30'}, {'abstract': 'Rochelle Sterling, wife of the beleaguered Donald Sterling, said she would fight to maintain ownership of the franchise, saying, “If the roles were reversed, would they take the team away from the man?”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/sports/basketball/clippers-co-owner-rochelle-sterling-tells-her-side-of-the-story.html', 'snippet': 'Rochelle Sterling, wife of the beleaguered Donald Sterling, said she would fight to maintain ownership of the franchise, saying, “If the roles were reversed, would they take the team away from the man?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As co-owner of the Los Angeles Clippers for the past 33 years, Rochelle Sterling has been a largely silent partner. But now, as the N.B.A. pushes for the permanent removal of her husband, she does not want to go away quietly.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/sports/STERLING1/STERLING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/13/sports/STERLING1/STERLING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/sports/STERLING1/STERLING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/sports/STERLING1/STERLING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/sports/STERLING1/STERLING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/13/sports/STERLING1/STERLING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/sports/STERLING1/STERLING1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clippers’ Co-Owner: ‘I Didn’t Do Anything Wrong’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Her Side: ‘I Didn’t Do Anything Wrong’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sterling, Donald', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sterling, Rochelle', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Adam (1962- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T01:12:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3294709-1275-5a36-a5a2-f6d1444bdf71', 'word_count': 1602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3294709-1275-5a36-a5a2-f6d1444bdf71'}, {'abstract': 'President Vladimir Putin of Russia has much at stake in the Ukraine crisis and is going to have to support negotiations for a peaceful resolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/opinion/what-mr-putin-cant-control.html', 'snippet': 'President Vladimir Putin of Russia has much at stake in the Ukraine crisis and is going to have to support negotiations for a peaceful resolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there were questions about the legitimacy of the separatist referendums in eastern Ukraine, the farcical names of the entities on which people were asked to vote — the self-declared People’s Republics of Donetsk or Luhansk — surely answered them. But the gathering rumble of violence accompanying the votes is serious and is driving the Ukrainian crisis in a direction that before long no one — not President Vladimir Putin of Russia, not authorities in Kiev, not the West — will be able to control. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Mr. Putin Can’t Control', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Mr. Putin Can&#8217;t Control ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for Security and Cooperation in Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Luhansk (Ukraine)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Donetsk (Ukraine)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T01:16:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd813b79-6bb0-52ea-98d9-28f1d5722d45', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd813b79-6bb0-52ea-98d9-28f1d5722d45'}, {'abstract': 'A state panel announced capital requirements less than three weeks after 22 entities submitted application fees of $1 million to be considered as a full-scale casino operator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/nyregion/350-million-investment-needed-to-open-casino-closest-to-new-york-city-panel-says.html', 'snippet': 'A state panel announced capital requirements less than three weeks after 22 entities submitted application fees of $1 million to be considered as a full-scale casino operator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — A state gambling panel declared on Monday that business interests seeking to build a casino in Orange County, just an hour from New York City, would be required to invest a minimum of $350 million in capital. Casino industry experts say it is a surprisingly low buy-in for what could be a billion-dollar franchise, and one that could cause serious problems for casino proponents in the Catskills to the north.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$350 Million Investment Needed to Open Casino Closest to New York City, Panel Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State Panel Says $350 Million Investment Is Required to Open Casino Closest to City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKinley, Jesse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Orange County (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Gaming Facility Location Board', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T01:17:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://