oposal last week, Mayor Bill de Blasio repeatedly said it toed the line between fiscal prudence and progressiveness — assuring New Yorkers that teachers and other municipal employees who had long been working without a contract could be made whole, and then some, and that the city could afford the billions of dollars their raises and back pay would cost.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'De Blasio’s Budget Proposal Finds Critics at a Ratings Agency and in Accounting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayor’s Budget Proposal Finds Critics at a Ratings Agency and in Accounting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Investors Service Inc", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T02:48:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikita Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56f50771-a714-5ba3-91cb-edcdcb67ef3c', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56f50771-a714-5ba3-91cb-edcdcb67ef3c'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/nyregion/winning-lottery-numbers-for-may-12-2014.h