me': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Fran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evictions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T03:36:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt A.V. Chaban', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'V', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7de3ca8f-cb98-5c6b-a13c-e85175620de0', 'word_count': 1223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7de3ca8f-cb98-5c6b-a13c-e85175620de0'}, {'abstract': 'A regional politician from Spain’s governing Popular Party was shot dead in the northern city of León on Monday, prompting the country’s main parties to suspend campaigning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/world/europe/spain-provincial-council-leader-shot.html', 'snippet': 'A regional politician from Spain’s governing Popular Party was shot dead in the northern city of León on Monday, prompting the country’s main parties to suspend campaigning.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A regional politician from Spain’s governing Popular Party was shot dead in the northern city of León on Monday, prompting the country’s main parties to suspend campaigning ahead of the European parliamentary elections this month. Isabel Carrasco, the head of the provincial council in León, was shot at least three times as she crossed a bridge in the city’s downtown, according to local news media reports. Ms. Carrasco, 59, had been running the provincial council in Léon since 2007. The shooting in broad daylight was a shock in a country that has only recently emerged from decades of terrorist bombings and political killings by members of ETA, the Basque separatist group that declared a cease-fire in 2011. An unidentified woman arrested in connection with the crime, according to local news reports, is believed to have recently been fired from her council job. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spain: Provincial Council Leader Shot', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spain: Provincial Council Leader Shot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Leon (Spain)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Popular Party (Spain)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basques', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ETA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrasco, Isabel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T03:53:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/275aa9a7-0749-595f-8144-3e9a9adec885', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/275aa9a7-0749-595f-8144-3e9a9adec885'}, {'abstract': 'Eleven people have been confirmed dead and 20 others wounded after a car bomb exploded on Monday at a cafe frequented by government officials in the town of Baidoa, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/world/africa/somalia-attack-on-former-official-fails.html', 'snippet': 'Eleven people have been confirmed dead and 20 others wounded after a car bomb exploded on Monday at a cafe frequented by government officials in the town of Baidoa, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Eleven people have been confirmed dead and 20 others wounded after a car bomb exploded on Monday at a cafe frequented by government officials in the town of Baidoa, officials said. The suicide bomber was believed to have been targeting a former regional governor, Abdifatah Ibrahim Gesey, who survived the attack. No group has claimed responsibility. The Somali president, Hassan Sheik Mohamud, and the special representative of the United Nations secretary general for Somalia, Nicholas Kay, condemned the attack. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Somalia: Attack on Former Official Fails', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Somalia: Attack on Former Official Fails', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahim, Mohammed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohamoud, Hassan Sheik', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T03:53:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohamed Ibrahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohamed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ibrahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/74d18bdb-f216-5911-8ee8-8fb88104f153', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74d18bdb-f216-5911-8ee8-8fb88104f153'}, {'abstract': 'The White House moved Monday to fill the long vacant post of the United States ambassador to Egypt by nominating Robert Stephen Beecroft, a career diplomat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/world/africa/nominee-for-egypt-ambassador-post.html', 'snippet': 'The White House moved Monday to fill the long vacant post of the United States ambassador to Egypt by nominating Robert Stephen Beecroft, a career diplomat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House moved\xa0Monday\xa0to fill the long vacant post of the United States ambassador to Egypt by nominating Robert Stephen Beecroft, a career diplomat.\xa0Mr. Beecroft currently is the American ambassador to Iraq. Mr. Beecroft’s Iraq post, in turn, will be filled by Stuart E. Jones, the United States ambassador to Jordan, the White House said. Mr. Beecroft will take up his post in Cairo during a tumultuous period. Abdel Fattah el-Sisi, who led the ouster last year of the elected government in Egypt, is expected to be elected\xa0Egypt’s president next month. The Cairo post has been vacant since Anne Patterson left in August to become the top Middle East official at the State Department. \xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nominee for Egypt Ambassador Post', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nominee for Egypt Ambassador Post', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beecroft, Robert Stephen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank':