: None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d3c888a-3b6f-5544-bc4f-3f2d05afecc6', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d3c888a-3b6f-5544-bc4f-3f2d05afecc6'}, {'abstract': 'Of the 35 works for sale, only one failed to find a buyer, and the sale pulled in $134.6 million, about $10 million over its estimate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/arts/design/at-christies-auction-an-experiment-proves-fruitful.html', 'snippet': 'Of the 35 works for sale, only one failed to find a buyer, and the sale pulled in $134.6 million, about $10 million over its estimate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gambling on the boundless appetite and bottomless checkbooks of today’s contemporary art collectors, not to mention their quirky taste for macabre images — an electric chair, a canvas filled with dead flies, and an installation incorporating handcuffs and an illustrated guide to pistols — Christie’s staged a highly publicized experiment on Monday night that was a runaway success.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/13/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 820, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'super