dia vote.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/voting-for-change-india-goes-to-the-polls/', 'snippet': 'In this lesson we explore the complex web of issues, history and culture behind the India vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What happens when you ask 814 million people to decide the future of their country? The answer will be coming soon for India, which this week is concluding a huge, 35-day election for seats in the national Parliament. Observers say the results could be momentous, with polls suggesting that voters are fed up with slow economic or political progress and favor decisive change — even at the risk of upsetting the nation’s fragile balance between its religious and social groups.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voting for Change: Researching the Issues at Stake in India’s Election', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T17:27:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Marshall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marshall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17480a29-8378-527d-8890-6768c284a3ed', 'word_count': 1916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17480a29-8378-527d-8890-6768c284a3ed'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s edition of the long-running annual benefit for P.S. 122, the performance space in the East Village, honored the performance artists who lost their N.E.A. funding during the culture wars of the early ’90s.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/ps-122-auction-benefit-nea-four-michael-stipe-cecilia-dean/', 'snippet': 'This year’s edition of the long-running annual benefit for P.S. 122, the performance space in the East Village, honored the performance artists who lost their N.E.A. funding during the culture wars of the early ’90s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last night offered a classic instance of a time-honored Manhattan tradition: arty downtowners doing a little song and dance to extract crucial funding from monied uptowners. The setting was the opulent subterranean boîte the Diamond Horseshoe, which hosted its annual benefit for the not-for-profit performance space P.S. 122, which has been staging amazing and bizarre shows in the East Village for more than 30 years, with performers ranging from Eric Bogosian and John Leguizamo to Annie Dorsen and Young Jean Lee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Hours | A Ribald Downtown Auction on Behalf of Creative Freedom', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dean, Cecilia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Paige', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stipe, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diamond Horseshoe (Manhattan, NY, Nightclub)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Endowment for the Arts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'P S 122', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T17:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/699f8c69-c712-5063-acab-9f5386472d89', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/699f8c69-c712-5063-acab-9f5386472d89'}, {'abstract': 'A sampling of some of the best food halls in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/dining/so-much-food-it-fits-a-hall.html', 'snippet': 'A sampling of some of the best food halls in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Food halls are all about gratification, both immediate (a chorizo and potato taco to eat on the spot) and delayed (a chunky jar of anchovies to take home). These bounteous markets are not new to the city; Macy’s opened its Cellar nearly 40 years ago. In 1997, the former Nabisco factory was transformed into Chelsea Market on West 15th Street, setting off the modern proliferation of indoor markets.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/dining/14BURNER_MAINSPAN/14BURNER_MAINSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/14/dining/14BURNER_MAINSPAN/14BURNER_MAINSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/dining/14BURNER_MAINSPAN/14BURNER_MAINSPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/dining/14BURNER_MAINSPAN/14BURNER_MAINSPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/dining/14BURNER_MA