ub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zernike, Kate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drewniak, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'George Washington Bridge', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Lee (NJ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T18:38:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike and Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e874000-bc8b-5940-9407-700479bac54a', 'word_count': 996, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e874000-bc8b-5940-9407-700479bac54a'}, {'abstract': 'The L.A. design event, which took place last weekend, was a promenade for a kind of aesthetic — like the Source Family by way of Georgia O’Keefe — that is very much in style right now.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/echo-park-craft-fair-california-style-spirituality-rises-again/', 'snippet': 'The L.A. design event, which took place last weekend, was a promenade for a kind of aesthetic — like the Source Family by way of Georgia O’Keefe — that is very much in style right now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As far as Southern California festival style goes, the Echo Park Craft Fair is a long way from the bare midriffs and hippie posturing of Coachella. The biannual design and food festival, which celebrated its fifth anniversary last weekend, has evolved from an intimate backyard bazaar into the see-and-be-seen happening for a certain swath of the L.A. creative class. In a city without much pedestrian activity, the fair — which, despite its name, takes place in Silver Lake — generates plenty of it. And with all that foot traffic comes a uniquely Angeleno sort of fashion parade, one with a distinctly spiritual vibe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Observed | At the Echo Park Craft Fair, California-Style Spirituality Rises Once Again', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T18:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e426a1c-0500-5d61-955f-020593f26d85', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e426a1c-0500-5d61-955f-020593f26d85'}, {'abstract': 'The investment company Atlas Mara Co-Nvest plans to use the proceeds in part to support the growth of its first African venture, which operates the African bank BancABC.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/diamonds-new-venture-to-raise-400-million-in-private-placement/', 'snippet': 'The investment company Atlas Mara Co-Nvest plans to use the proceeds in part to support the growth of its first African venture, which operates the African bank BancABC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The investment company Atlas Mara Co-Nvest, backed by a former Barclays chief ex