astname': 'Wheeler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c7ea234-78fb-5756-ab02-d3d9962143ee', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c7ea234-78fb-5756-ab02-d3d9962143ee'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City Police Department announced it would no longer seize condoms for use in prostitution cases.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/13/get-rid-of-condom-policing/', 'snippet': 'The New York City Police Department announced it would no longer seize condoms for use in prostitution cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City drove down its H.I.V. infection rate in part by flooding the streets with millions upon millions of free condoms each year. At the same time, the police have undermined this effort by using condom possession as evidence to support prostitution charges — and by simply seizing condoms from sex workers and destroying them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Get Rid of ‘Condom Policing’', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condoms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T18:55:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c5c6278-e72f-5b53-bd14-5b9d384b01dc', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c5c6278-e72f-5b53-bd14-5b9d384b01dc'}, {'abstract': 'The port aims to win the job of breaking down the 950-foot-long wreck of the Italian cruise ship, whose captain had abandoned the ship after it hit a rock and capsized in 2012, killing 32 people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/world/europe/port-vies-to-dismantle-italian-cruise-ship.html', 'snippet': 'The port aims to win the job of breaking down the 950-foot-long wreck of the Italian cruise ship, whose captain had abandoned the ship after it hit a rock and capsized in 2012, killing 32 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PIOMBINO, Italy — Workers are hurriedly revamping the aged port in this smoggy Tuscan city, trucking in boulders to construct and fortify jetties, and enlarging its facilities to refit and dismantle ships. They are scheduled to dredge and deepen the harbor next month.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14concordia1/14concordia1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14concordia1/14concordia1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14concordia1/14concordia1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14concordia1/14concordia1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14concordia1/14concordia1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbn