omenade will open in June.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SURFACING1/18SURFACING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SURFACING1/18SURFACING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SURFACING1/18SURFACING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SURFACING1/18SURFACING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SURFACING1/18SURFACING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SURFACING1/18SURFACING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SURFACING1/18SURFACING1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Renaissance in Rapid City, S.D.', 'kicker': '5 Places', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Renaissance in a Resilient City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barone, Jeanine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rapid City (SD)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T20:56:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeanine Barone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeanine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a54bcfc-68ea-517e-94c6-afb4b213b71b', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a54bcfc-68ea-517e-94c6-afb4b213b71b'}, {'abstract': 'The Pulitzer Prize-winning author of “Lonesome Dove” talks about how the plains have affected him and reflects on the lonely landscapes that surface in his fiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/travel/larry-mcmurtry-on-the-power-of-the-plains.html', 'snippet': 'The Pulitzer Prize-winning author of “Lonesome Dove” talks about how the plains have affected him and reflects on the lonely landscapes that surface in his fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Larry McMurtry — the Pulitzer Prize-winning author of “Lonesome Dove” and co-author of the Oscar-winning screenplay for “Brokeback Mountain” — one of the most interesting, and overlooked, aspects of life in the Old West was just how profoundly isolating the “westering” experience could be. “Those plains, those mountains, those deserts were empty, except for the Indians, who didn’t make the settlers less lonely,” said Mr. McMurtry, 77.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18QNA1/18QNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18QNA1/18QNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jum