'lastname': 'Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/971dd305-3c80-5410-9b0d-2af3dc3ddb55', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/971dd305-3c80-5410-9b0d-2af3dc3ddb55'}, {'abstract': 'The Miller Theater at Columbia University will continue to emphasize its traditional strengths in its 2014-15 season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/arts/music/miller-theater-season.html', 'snippet': 'The Miller Theater at Columbia University will continue to emphasize its traditional strengths in its 2014-15 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miller Theater at Columbia University will continue to emphasize its traditional strengths — new music, early music and provocative combinations of the two — in its 2014-15 season. It will open Sept. 18 with “Heart and Breath,” a production by the new-music ensemble Eighth Blackbird in which the musicians play commedia dell’arte roles and perform 17th-century Italian music filtered through 21st-century sensibilities. The hall’s signature series, Composer Portraits, will offer overviews of the works of eight living composers, four of them women, representing an expansive array of contemporary styles. The series begins with an evening of recent works by Chou Wen-Chung, performed by the ensembles for which he wrote them — the Brentano String Quartet, Talujon and the New York New Music Ensemble. The International Contemporary Ensemble, with Steven Schick conducting, will devote a program to the Israeli experimentalist Chaya Czernowin, and the string quartet Ethel will perform the world premiere of a new work by Missy Mazzoli on a program that also includes her “Harp and Altar,” a paean to the Brooklyn Bridge. Other installments of Composer Portraits include programs devoted to Bernard Rands, Keeril Makan, Stefano Gervasoni, Augusta Read Thomas and Anna Clyne. The Miller’s program also includes a jazz series and occasional pop-up concerts (with free beer), which will announced closer to the performances. The full schedule is at millertheatre.com.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miller Theater Season', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Miller Theater Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miller Theater at Columbia University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-13T21:19:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/53acb885-fbfd-57e7-bc33-4f051a37dd2d', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53acb885-fbfd-57e7-bc33-4f051a37dd2d'}, {'abstract': 'Representative John Conyers Jr., a Democrat who has represented Detroit for nearly 50 years, lacks enough valid signatures on re-election petitions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/us/politics/filing-misstep-may-fell-house-veteran-conyers.html', 'snippet': 'Representative John Conyers Jr., a Democrat who has represented Detroit for nearly 50 years, lacks enough valid signatures on re-election petitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — For nearly 50 years, John Conyers Jr. has represented Detroit in the House of Representatives. He is the ranking Democrat on the House Judiciary Committee, a founder of the Congressional Black Caucus and the second-longest-serving member of Congress still holding office. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page'