-bc76-60b3d5a264b7', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cf7e9be-8102-55db-bc76-60b3d5a264b7'}, {'abstract': 'The military has made videotapes of military medical officials force-feeding detainees on hunger strikes at the prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, according to a court filing on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/us/videos-said-to-show-force-feeding-of-detainees-at-guantanamo-bay.html', 'snippet': 'The military has made videotapes of military medical officials force-feeding detainees on hunger strikes at the prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, according to a court filing on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The military has made videotapes of military medical officials force-feeding detainees on hunger strikes at the prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, according to a court filing on Tuesday. The filing asks a judge to issue an emergency order to the military requiring it to preserve the tapes. In 2007, it came to light that the C.I.A. had destroyed videotapes of its interrogation sessions showing the use of the suffocation technique called waterboarding. The military’s practice of force-feeding detainees has been a major issue in habeas corpus lawsuits. The procedure involves strapping a detainee into a restraint chair and inserting a gastric tube through the nose and down the throat, through which liquid nutritional supplement is poured into the stomach. In February, a federal appeals court in the District of Columbia ruled that the courts have jurisdiction to hear challenges of the conditions of confinement at Guantánamo as part of habeas corpus lawsuits. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Videos Said to Show Force-Feeding of Detainees at Guantánamo Bay', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Videos Said to Show Force-Feeding of Detainees at Guantánamo Bay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'