strayed too far from its modest roots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year, the National Puerto Rican Day Parade is returning to its roots. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Changes Announced to Puerto Rican Day Parade', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changes Announced to Puerto Rican Day Parade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puerto Ricans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mark-Viverito, Melissa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Velazquez, Nydia M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T03:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a6c65cf-0240-569a-875b-dbab0d341a04', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a6c65cf-0240-569a-875b-dbab0d341a04'}, {'abstract': 'The Chinese authorities said Mark Reilly, a Briton, had ordered his subordinates to form a “massive bribery network.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/business/international/glaxosmithkline-china.html', 'snippet': 'The Chinese authorities said Mark Reilly, a Briton, had ordered his subordinates to form a “massive bribery network.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — Chinese authorities sent a strong warning to the pharmaceutical industry on Wednesday, implicating a top Western executive at GlaxoSmithKline in a long-running bribery scheme. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Head of Glaxo in China Is Accused of Bribery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Head of Glaxo in China Is Accused of Bribery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barboza, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GlaxoSmithKline PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Katie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reilly, Mark', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhao Hongyan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Guowei', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T03:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza and Katie Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9ff03b4-57aa-5937-8ea0-f2c2f15fce68', 'word_count': 1011, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9ff03b4-57aa-5937-8ea0-f2c2f15fce68'}, {'abstract': 'In this exclusive video for T, the co-owners of the Little Flower School share their tricks to create a seasonal arrangement that looks as effortless and chic as an unruly garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/t-magazine/arrange-flowers-brooklyn-little-flower-school-nicolette-owen-sarah-ryhanen.html', 'snippet': 'In this exclusive video for T, the co-owners of the Little Flower School share their tricks to create a seasonal arrangement that looks as effortless and chic as an unruly garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Given the Brooklynization of the world, it’s no surprise that when the Little Flower School made its way from Brooklyn to London last month, formally trained florists from as far north as Scotland and as far south as Cornwall made the trek to learn how to craft the stunning, free-form arrangements coveted by New York’s creative elite and fashion set. Sarah Ryhanen and Nicolette Owen hosted the two-day immersive workshop to help British florists “break out of the dome” (think: those compact bridal bouquets). An old courtyard filled with 5,000 cut flowers set the scene for Ryhanen’s opening lecture, in which she challenged their 14 pupils to ditch the flower foam, show no fear and let their imaginations run wild with the bucketfuls of foxgloves and peonies before them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Arrange Flowers, the Brooklyn Way', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': "By Kate O'Brien", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Brien", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/597eade3-895f-57bc-9540-a3774d8a6ba0', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/597eade3-895f-57bc-9540-a3774d8a6ba0'}, {'abstract': 'Sight Unseen Offsite, a shoppable two-story exhibition in SoHo, brings the carefully curated vision of the design website Sight Unseen to New York Design Week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/t-magazine/sight-unseen-offsite-new-york-design-week.html', 'snippet': 'Sight Unseen Offsite, a shoppable two-story exhibition in SoHo, brings the carefully curated vision of the design website Sight Unseen to New York Design Week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If locals have one complaint about New York Design Week, it’s that the city can seem over-reliant on foreign brands and ho-hum showrooms for content. In 2010, Monica Khemsurov (a T contributor) and Jill Singer of the online magazine Sight Unseen founded the NoHo Design District to counteract that problem with a neighborhood-wide festival of quirky installations, events and pop-ups that ran during Design Week. The duo, known for their knack for identifying new talent, originally looked to create the same neighborhood feel they had experienced when attending other global design weeks in London and Milan. However, by last year, the trials of securing real estate in a booming market had become overwhelming. “In the end, it proved so difficult to find those spaces that we spent 80 percent of our time doing that, and zero percent curating,” says Khemsurov. “The only way for us to evolve was to let go of Noho and become nomadic.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fresh Hub for Young Talent at New York Design Week', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Rubinstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubinstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77b7f32d-72ea-5f32-822a-79ca960f36fc', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77b7f32d-72ea-5f32-822a-79ca960f36fc'}, {'abstract': 'In varying widths and fresh shades of blue, these patterned separates and accessories are the new summer neutrals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/t-magazine/easy-blue-and-white-stripes.html', 'snippet': 'In varying widths and fresh shades of blue, these patterned separates and accessories are the new summer neutrals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Memorial Day just around the corner, the promise of prolonged mornings spent luxuriating in pajamas and warm afternoon naps beneath a cool summer breeze is enough to inspire a wardrobe reinvention. And perhaps nothing says summertime more than stripes — but instead of the usual maritime take, we’re looking to swaths of pale and azure blues, in varying widths, contrasted with ample amounts of white. The effect is reminiscent of the parasols that pepper the beaches of the Italian Riviera. With light-as-air fabrics and loungewear-inspired designs, these little patterned numbers are as easy to wear as neutral basics — and will keep you feeling, and looking, cool all season long.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/t-magazine/14market-gilchrist/14market-gilchrist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/14/t-magazine/14market-gilchrist/14market-gilchrist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/t-magazine/14market-gilchrist/14market-gilchrist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/t-magazine/14market-gilchrist/14market-gilchrist-superJumbo.