ely as easy.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/plenty-of-words-for-indias-fallen-but-questions-are-met-with-silence/', 'snippet': 'Words about military deaths come free and easy to many people, especially to politicians seeking votes, but soldiers’ families often have questions for which answers are rarely as easy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In May 1999, Capt. Saurabh Kalia of the Indian Army’s 4 Jat Regiment, an officer from Himachal Pradesh, led a patrol of five soldiers along the heights above Kargil, in Kashmir. They disappeared.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plenty of Words for India’s Fallen but Questions Are Met With Silence', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singh, Jaswant', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aam Aadmi Party (India)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 15,