ff Vietnam’s coast.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/15/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/15/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China Targeted by Vietnamese in Fiery Riots', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Targeted by Vietnamese in Fiery Riots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doan, Chau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ho Chi Minh City (Vietnam)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T11:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley, Chau Doan and Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chau', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edfafb29-7265-531d-86ad-56e49fb9b20f', 'word_count': 1329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edfafb29-7265-531d-86ad-56e49fb9b20f'}, {'abstract': 'The theater will offer overviews of the works of eight living composers, four of them women, representing an expansive array of contemporary styles.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/new-music-meets-early-music-in-miller-theater-offerings/', 'snippet': 'The theater will offer overviews of the works of eight living composers, four of them women, representing an expansive array of contemporary styles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miller Theater will continue to emphasize its traditional strengths – new music, early music and provocative combinations of the two – in its 2014-15 season, which opens on Sept. 18 with “Heart and Breath,” a production by the new-music ensemble Eighth Blackbird, in which the musicians play commedia dell’arte roles and perform 17th-century Italian music filtered through 21st-century sensibilities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Music Meets Early Music in Miller Theater Offerings', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miller Theater at Columbia University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T12:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7126face-9407-5778-b9c6-f959353c37c2', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7126face-9407-5778-b9c6-f959353c37c2'}, {'abstract': 'The breakup of the Publicis-Omnicom merger offers some lessons about big deals. | A star banker at Goldman Sachs is leaving. | Citizens Bank is facing a stormy spinoff. | The maker of Botox faces more pressure about an unsolicited takeover bid.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/morning-agenda-lessons-from-a-breakup/', 'snippet': 'The breakup of the Publicis-Omnicom merger offers some lessons about big deals. | A star banker at Goldman Sachs is leaving. | Citizens Bank is facing a stormy spinoff. | The maker of Botox faces more pressure about an unsolicited takeover bid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a time when companies are reaching for ever bigger deals, the breakup of a $35 billion merger between two advertising giants offers some lessons, Steven M. Davidoff writes in the Deal Professor column. The deal between Publicis of France and Omnicom, based in New York, seemed at first to make good sense, creating a company that would become the largest ad agency in a world where bigger may be better for ad buying. But the merger also raised cultural and integration issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons From a Breakup', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T12:04:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08820ab5-6e22-53a0-a60c-98902f3e29d0', 'word_count': 2014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08820ab5-6e22-53a0-a60c-98902f3e29d0'}, {'abstract': 'A novelist, an astrobiologist and an ecologist explore the impact of centuries of rising seas.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/three-long-views-of-life-with-rising-seas/', 'snippet': 'A novelist, an astrobiologist and an ecologist explore the impact of centuries of rising seas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After finishing my post on the inevitability of substantial long-term sea-level rise from Antarctic ice loss, I sent this question to Curt Stager, a paleoclimatologist and author of “Deep Future,” Kim Stanley Robinson, the novelist focused on “cli fi” before that term was conceived, and the astrobiologist David Grinspoon:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/blogs/dotcities/dotcities-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/13/blogs/dotcities/dotcities-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/blogs/dotcities/dotcities-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/blogs/dotcities/dotcities-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/blogs/dotcities/dotcities-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/13/blogs/dotcities/dotcities-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/13/blogs/dotcities/dotcities-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Long Views of Life With Rising Seas', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coastal Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science Fiction', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volcanoes', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inslee, Jay', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Kim Stanley', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Paul Smith's College", 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T12:20:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15659d57-7f8e-5e0d-b5ef-7d484453373e', 'word_count': 1629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15659d57-7f8e-5e0d-b5ef-7d484453373e'}, {'abstract': 'Sylvia Mathews Burwell, the nominee for secretary of health and human services, was called “a force for bringing people together” at her Senate confirmation hearing Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/us/politics/health-human-services-nomination-hearing.html', 'snippet': 'Sylvia Mathews Burwell, the nominee for secretary of health and human services, was called “a force for bringing people together” at her Senate confirmation hearing Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Sylvia Mathews Burwell, President Obama’s nominee for secretary of health and human services, appeared Wednesday to be on a swift path to confirmation after she sailed through another cordial congressional hearing without promising significant changes in federal health policy or regulations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/15/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/15/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/us/HEALTH/HEALTH-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Breezy Hearing for Obama Health Pick', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Breezy Hearing for Oba