: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/books/queen-victorias-bathing-machine-and-elizabeth-queen-of-the-seas.html', 'snippet': 'In two new picture books, very different queens have trouble taking a swim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shouldn’t a queen have the right to swim wherever and whenever she likes? It ought to be a perk of the job. But in “Queen Victoria’s Bathing Machine,” by Gloria Whelan, with illustrations by Nancy Carpenter, and “Elizabeth, Queen of the Seas,” by Lynne Cox, illustrated by Brian Floca, two very different regents have trouble doing just that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/books/14childrens-2/14childrens-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 232, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/14/books/14childrens-2/14childrens-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 232}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/books/14childrens-2/14childrens-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/books/14childrens-2/14childrens-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/books/14childrens-2/14childrens-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/14/books/14childrens-2/14childrens-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/books/14childrens-2/14childrens-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suitable Swimming', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Floca, Brian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Lynne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carpenter, Nancy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whelan, Gloria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T14:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Harrison Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Harrison', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/50e9d6f2-c364-59fa-82ed-ddc692df2aa2', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50e9d6f2-c364-59fa-82ed-ddc692df2aa2'}, {'abstract': 'The Bolshoi Opera and Ballet filled in the details of performances scheduled for this summer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/casting-set-for-bolshoi-performances-at-lincoln-center-festival/', 'snippet': 'The Bolshoi Opera and Ballet filled in the details of performances scheduled for this summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Lincoln Center Festival announced its programming early this year, the Bolshoi Opera and Ballet, appearing in New York together for the first time, was clearly one of the major drawing cards. But though the programs were announced: The Bolshoi Opera would present a concert version of “The Tsar’s Bride,” a Rimsky-Korsakov work better known from recordings than from live performances — at least in the West — and the Bolshoi ballet would offer Khachauryan’s “Spartacus,” Tchaikovsky’s “Swan Lake” and Ludwig Minkus’s “Don Quichotte,” casting was a mystery. Even when the ballet company announced the casts for the first part of its American tour, not long after the Lincoln Center announcement, Lincoln Center was mum.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Casting Set for Bolshoi Performances at Lincoln Center Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Casting Set for Bolshoi at Lincoln Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bolshoi Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T14:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb89dfe0-51c0-505d-9974-3a55bc4b3de8', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb89dfe0-51c0-505d-9974-3a55bc4b3de8'}, {'abstract': 'Get ready for a world where your refrigerator, car and plant pots are all connected to the Internet and able to email and communicate with each other.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/some-predictions-about-the-next-decade-from-pew-research/', 'snippet': 'Get ready for a world where your refrigerator, car and plant pots are all connected to the Internet and able to email and communicate with each othe