ity.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/social-experiments-investigating-questions-related-to-personality-attributes/', 'snippet': 'In this lesson, students learn about current research on social structure and personality attributes in a type of communal spider, then design their own research questions related to personality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | What is the definition of personality, and how have scientists studied its attributes in animals? What can we learn about ourselves by studying the science behind personality? In this lesson, students learn about current research on social structure and personality attributes in a type of communal spider, then design their own research questions meant to investigate traits in humans like shyness, boldness or fear of the new.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Social Experiments: Investigating Questions Related to Personality Attributes', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T16:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Cutraro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cutraro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b101ecd-0f47-57a7-8a37-c42f75e9c66e', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b101ecd-0f47-57a7-8a37-c42f75e9c66e'}, {'abstract': 'Jaipur, the capital of the Indian state of Rajasthan, is one of the world’s most important centers for the cutting and polishing of precious and semiprecious gems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2014/05/06/style/international/15ACAJ-ESSAY.html', 'snippet': 'Jaipur, the capital of the Indian state of Rajasthan, is one of the world’s most impo