e', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T17:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c625f98b-b4e5-5b38-909f-71ad07e615b1', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c625f98b-b4e5-5b38-909f-71ad07e615b1'}, {'abstract': 'The new show “Just Jim Dale” will feature the titular star alone onstage, supported only by the pianist Mark York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/theater/that-funny-man-of-1000-faces.html', 'snippet': 'The new show “Just Jim Dale” will feature the titular star alone onstage, supported only by the pianist Mark York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title “Just Jim Dale” might seem to foretell something fairly straightforward. And, yes, this new show will feature the titular star alone onstage, supported only by the pianist Mark York. Yet the wide-ranging career of Mr. Dale has been anything but simple. He made his Broadway debut in “Scapino” in 1974, won a Tony for “Barnum” in 1980 and later appeared in the long-running hit “Me and My Girl.” More recently he was in the revival of Athol Fugard’s “Road to Mecca.” But did you know that Mr. Dale also wrote the lyrics for the title song of “Georgy Girl,” which won him an Oscar nomination in 1967?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/theater/18dale/18dale-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/theater/18dale/18dale-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 773}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/theater/18dale/18dale-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 795, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/theater/18dale/18dale-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1590, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/theater/18dale/18dale-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/18/theater/18dale/18dale-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/theater/18dale/18dale-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'That Funny Man of 1,000 Faces', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Funny Man of 1,000 Faces', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dale, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roundabout Theater Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Just Jim Dale (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T17:04:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': N