ation': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/7a7258a3-86f2-5ad4-b667-5323e070a704', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/7a7258a3-86f2-5ad4-b667-5323e070a704'}, {'abstract': 'The travel website Hipmunk has concluded that the best time to buy tickets for the July 4 weekend is the week beginning May 26.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/the-best-time-to-book-july-4-trips/', 'snippet': 'The travel website Hipmunk has concluded that the best time to buy tickets for the July 4 weekend is the week beginning May 26.', 'lead_paragraph': 'July 4 falls on a Friday this year, giving many a three-day holiday and time to travel. To get the best deal on Independence Day airfares in a potentially crowded season, the travel-planning website Hipmunk advises making plans by the end of May.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Time to Book July 4 Trips', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Independence Day (US) (July 4)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T19:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07b8e412-40d7-5fb2-aa2d-1ef311e6fabf', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07b8e412-40d7-5fb2-aa2d-1ef311e6fabf'}, {'abstract': 'Several apps will help you turn your pictures into comics by supplying the templates, background colors and speech bubbles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/technology/personaltech/transforming-your-photos-into-comics-strips.html', 'snippet': 'Several apps will help you turn your pictures into comics by supplying the templates, background colors and speech bubbles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE way a comic book artist can convey so much emotion, drama and narrative with just a few simple lines has always amazed me. Now, if you want to put a comic strip together and provide your own drama and emotion, there are many mobile apps that can do the basic artwork for you.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transforming Your Photos Into Comic Strips', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Transforming Your Photos Into Comic Strips', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eaton, Kit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T19:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f4cfc8b-f375-5590-bc3f-e92f6a07079c', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f4cfc8b-f375-5590-bc3f-e92f6a07079c'}, {'abstract': 'The online-only radio station East Village Radio will shut down next week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/east-village-radio-to-close-citing-licensing-costs/', 'snippet': 'The online-only radio station East Village Radio will shut down next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'East Village Radio, a commercial-free Internet radio station broadcasting from a storefront on First Avenue in Manhattan, said on Wednesday that it would be shutting down next week, blaming the high cost of music licenses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'East Village Radio to Close, Citing Licensing Costs', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T19:33:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33a206be-2b27-5ca0-914b-a5b8b4127ac1', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33a206be-2b27-5ca0-914b-a5b8b4127ac1'}, {'abstract': 'Hedge fund managers don’t benefit from the carried interest tax advantage that are the focus of proposed legislation, Victor Fleischer writes in the Standard Deduction column. Instead, many use Bermuda-based reinsurance companies to avoid taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/why-hedge-funds-dont-worry-about-carried-interest-tax-rules/', 'snippet': 'Hedge fund managers don’t benefit from the carried interest tax advantage that are the focus of proposed legislation, Victor Fleischer writes in the Standard Deduction column. Instead, many use Bermuda-based reinsurance companies to avoid taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hedge fund managers don’t use the carried interest tax loophole. They need something more exotic.', 'source': 'The Ne