al-pm/13nytnow-funeral-pm-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Evening Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T21:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas and Victoria Shannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ed866b1-9942-5577-8697-9b2fa4796afb', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ed866b1-9942-5577-8697-9b2fa4796afb'}, {'abstract': 'A new track by Bob Dylan, “Full Moon and Empty Arms,” was a hit for Frank Sinatra nearly 70 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/dylan-records-a-sinatra-hit/', 'snippet': 'A new track by Bob Dylan, “Full Moon and Empty Arms,” was a hit for Frank Sinatra nearly 70 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is Bob Dylan channeling his inner Sinatra? Or is it his inner Rachmaninoff? On Wednesday, Mr. Dylan’s website, bobdylan.com, posted what appears to be the cover of the singer’s forthcoming album, “Shadows in the Night,” as well as a single track – a gently sung cover of “Full Moon and Empty Arms,” in an ensemble dominated by a country-tinged steel guitar part. The song, written in 1945 by Buddy Kaye and Ted Mossman, is based on a theme from the third movement of Rachmaninoff’s Piano Concerto No. 2, and was a hit for Frank Sinatra in 1946.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dylan Records a Sinatra Hit', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sinatra, Frank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T21:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c92f15fc-eb49-5997-8d36-d1427d66ca63', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c92f15fc-eb49-5997-8d36-d1427d66ca63'}, {'abstract': 'The new design for the Philadelphia Museum of Art will be unveiled July 1 at the museum.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/14/gehry-design-for-philadelphia-museum-of-art-to-be-displayed/', 'snippet': 'The new design for the Philadelphia Museum of Art will be unveiled July 1 at the museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The architect Frank Gehry’s design for a renovation and expansion of the Philadelphia Museum of Art will be unveiled on July 1 in an exhibition at the museum on Benjamin Franklin Parkway. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gehry Design for Philadelphia Museum of Art to Be Displayed', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gehry, Frank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Museum of Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '20