ole-j-bufford-at-the-metropolitan-room.html', 'snippet': 'Carole J. Bufford, originally inspired by Bessie Smith, brings the blues to the Metropolitan Room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The singer Carole J. Bufford’s love affair with the blues began when she was 13 years old and discovered Bessie Smith on a two-disc set, she recalled last Thursday at the Metropolitan Room. She has immersed herself in the genre ever since. And this supremely confident performer has brought her accumulated know-how to her new show, “Shades of Blue.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Singing the Blues Is a Performer’s Pleasure', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Singing the Blues Is a Performer’s Pleasure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bufford, Carole J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T21:31:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/652de380-6efb-5e66-b30d-aa21e7e36a39', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/652de380-6efb-5e66-b30d-aa21e7e36a39'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Spencer Finch, commissioned by the National September 11 Memorial Museum, has created a skyscape of as many hues as lives lost at ground zero.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/arts/design/spencer-finch-turned-to-the-heavens-to-honor-the-dead.html', 'snippet': 'The artist Spencer Finch, commissioned by the National September 11 Memorial Museum, has created a skyscape of as many hues as lives lost a