her-on-leftover-women/', 'snippet': 'In her new book, Leta Hong Fincher argues that gender inequality is growing in China and identifies a key area where that can be seen — property ownership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the 1949 Communist revolution, Mao Zedong declared that “Women hold up half the sky.” It was a phrase that caught the imagination in China and the world. Yet as socialism has crumbled and a Leninist state, married with elements of a market economy, steers the country, women’s position is slipping, as Leta Hong Fincher examines in her new book, “Leftover Women: The Resurgence of Gender Inequality in China.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14sino-hong01/14sino-hong01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14sino-hong01/14sino-hong01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 747}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14sino-hong01/14sino-hong01-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 823, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14sino-hong01/14sino-hong01-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1133, 'width': 910, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14sino-hong01/14sino-hong01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/14/world/14sino-hong01/14sino-hong01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', '