lls turned out to be both reflective and transparent. The floor inside was bare, more pristine than its outskirts. The audience sat on either side of this structure, two groups facing each other, just one of many mirror images that appeared over the next hour.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/ZOE/ZOE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/ZOE/ZOE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 683}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/ZOE/ZOE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/ZOE/ZOE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/ZOE/ZOE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/ZOE/ZOE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/ZOE/ZOE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Swirl of Duality and Dueling Identities', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Swirl of Duality and Dueling Identities ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': '3LD Art & Technology Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shuey, Juniper', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scofield, Zoe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T22:39:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f72c12a-5f8d-5fff-a6d2-eed52ac0fe92', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f72c12a-5f8d-5fff-a6d2-eed52ac0fe92'}, {'abstract': 'The relatively few Americans who move to Canada often find that they enjoy the country’s more liberal policies and free health care, though there are adjustments to make.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/business/retirementspecial/the-trade-offs-of-relocating-north-to-canada.html', 'snippet': 'The relatively few Americans who move to Canada often find that they enjoy the country’s more liberal policies and free health care, though there are adjustments to make.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S a nearby country where most natives speak English and there are few major cultural differences from the United States. Yet the number of Americans choosing to head north to retire in Canada has remained low — reaching a high of 1,675 in 2008 (for immigrants older than 49), then dipping to 1,060 in 2011, and rising again in 2013 to an estimated 1,565.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/business/retirementspecial/15EXPATS/EXPATS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legac