/desk-clocks-faces-of-another-era.html', 'snippet': 'You may not need them to check the time anymore, but traditional ones still look good and rank as collectibles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even in the age of the smartphone, there’s value in a traditional desk clock. True, it’s no longer necessary from a functional standpoint, but as Gideon Mendelson pointed out, that’s not the only reason to have a clock.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Desk Clocks: Faces of Another Era', 'kicker': 'Shopping With Gideon Mendelson', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Faces of Another Era', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKeough, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mendelson, Gideon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T23:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84976379-1432-50b9-b75d-4e68ed03ccdd', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84976379-1432-50b9-b75d-4e68ed03ccdd'}, {'abstract': 'How long does it take to fall madly in love with a neglected 19th-century house? For one woman, a nanosecond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/greathomesanddestinations/holleywood-ending.html', 'snippet': 'How long does it take to fall madly in love with a neglected 19th-century house? For one woman, a nanosecond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Helen Klein Ross, a novelist and poet, and her husband, Donald K. Ross, a lawyer, lived on the Upper West Side with their two daughters and were content to spend weekends in an 1810 clapboard farmhouse in Amenia, N.Y. But that was before they were seduced by Holleywood.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holleywood Ending', 'kicker': 'On Location: Lakeville, Conn.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holleywood Ending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lakeville (Conn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Louie, Elaine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T23:03:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6654e62f-0899-57a0-95b6-0fb128137084', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6654e62f-0899-57a0-95b6-0fb128137084'}, {'abstract': 'Flowers, shrubs and trees have their own fashion cycles. Here, a guide to horticultural has-beens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/garden/youre-planting-that-old-thing.html', 'snippet': 'Flowers, shrubs and trees have their own fashion cycles. Here, a guide to horticultural has-beens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Catalpa Tree Appreciation Society needs fresh blood. There are no me