th Master Limited Partnerships, Get a Piece of the Pipeline', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Master Limited Partnerships, Get a Piece of the Pipeline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-14T23:55:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Retirement', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Wasik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Wasik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/931adc7b-b2fb-5bc8-b183-4c9529be56f2', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/931adc7b-b2fb-5bc8-b183-4c9529be56f2'}, {'abstract': 'But it does need to change how it searches for personal names.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/opinion/dont-force-google-to-forget.html', 'snippet': 'But it does need to change how it searches for personal names.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMBRIDGE, Mass. — THE European Court of Justice ruled on Tuesday that Europeans have a limited “right to be forgotten” by search engines like Google. According to the ruling, an individual can compel Google to remove certain reputation-harming search results that are generated by Googling the individual’s name. The court is trying to address an important problem — namely, the Internet’s ability to preserve indefinitely all its information about you, no matter how unfortunate or misleading — but it has devised a poor solution.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Force Google to ‘Forget’', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Force Google to ‘Forget’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zittrain, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Court of Justice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T00:02:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Zittrain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zittrain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/43b136b2-3704-5465-9fc5-84ba0d5354a0', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43b136b2-3704-5465-9fc5-84ba0d5354a0'}, {'abstract': 'Narendra Modi, the front-runner in the race for prime minister, has made the cleanup of the river that flows through Varanasi a metaphor for his campaign as he seeks to stamp out corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/world/asia/ganges-river-revered-soiled-and-symbol-of-an-indian-election-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'Narendra Modi, the front-runner in the race for prime minister, has made the cleanup of the river that flows through Varanasi a metaphor for his campaign as he seeks to stamp out corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARANASI, India — For centuries, Hindus have brought their dead to banks of the Ganges River in this ancient city, with the promise that if their bodies are burned on the riverfront, their souls will escape the constant cycle of rebirth and attain moksha, or salvation. Transporting their souls is the goddess of the river, whose ebbs and flows have run through thousands of years of civilization.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/world/15VARANASI/15VARANASI-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/15/world/15VARANASI/15VARANASI-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/world/15VARANASI/15VARANASI-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/world/15VARANASI/15VARANASI-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/world/15VARANASI/15VARANASI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/15/world/15VARANASI/15VARANASI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/world/15VARANASI/15VARANASI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ganges River: Revered, Soiled and Symbol of an Indian Election Campaign', 'kicker': 'Varanasi Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A River Is Revered, Fouled, and the Symbol of an Election Campaign', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ganges River', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Varanasi (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kejriwal, Arvind', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aam Aadmi Party (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T00:03:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shreeya Sinha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shreeya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sinha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07aa990a-4429-5377-b8b8-f9c8c8b563ee', 'word_count': 1153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07aa990a-4429-5377-b8b8-f9c8c8b563ee'}, {'abstract': 'Boko Haram is not the only problem desperate Nigerians are facing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/opinion/the-kidnapping-of-a-country.html', 'snippet': 'Boko Haram is not the only problem desperate Nigerians are facing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHIBOK, Nigeria — THE road to Chibok is eerily quiet, lined with checkpoints manned by civilians, many of them teenagers, wielding rusty rifles and serving as added security for an area that has little. In this northeast Nigeri