g wires, setting up antennas, signing up customers and getting government licenses makes it hard for new players to get into a business dominated by former monopolies with deep pockets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping the Wireless Business Competitive', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keeping the Wireless Business Competitive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio Spectrum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T01:04:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/15d5ca33-df56-5e09-8d63-83596ace9d23', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15d5ca33-df56-5e09-8d63-83596ace9d23'}, {'abstract': 'Some parents are creating accounts for their babies on Facebook, Twitter, Instagram and other services, long before those children are able to add posts themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/technology/personaltech/100000002879066/babys-first-tweet.html', 'snippet': 'Some parents are creating accounts for their babies on Facebook, Twitter, Instagram and other services, long before those child