.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, May 15, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“When an institution like the C.D.C. makes a statement, it makes a profound difference to the doctors who are ambivalent.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, May 15, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T03:39:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c33d0fe-8ba9-55f3-8e59-cc85df39eacd', 'word_count': 40, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c33d0fe-8ba9-55f3-8e59-cc85df39eacd'}, {'abstract': 'The captain and three other crew members of the ferry that capsized off the southwestern coast of South Korea in April were indicted on murder charges Thursday, prosecutors said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/world/asia/south-korea-murder-charges-in-ferry-disaster.html', 'snippet': 'The captain and three other crew members of the ferry that capsized off the southwestern coast of South Korea in April were indicted on murder charges Thursday, prosecutors said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The captain and three other crew members of the ferry that capsized off the southwestern coast of South Korea on April 16 were indicted on murder charges on Thursday, prosecutors said. The indictments were among formal charges leveled against 15 crew members of Sewol, the 6,825-ton ferry, after weeks of investigations into the causes of the sinking. As of Thursday, 281 people had been found dead and 23 remained missing. All 15 crew members had previously been arrested on various criminal charges, including accidental homicide. But on Thursday, prosecutors brought the more serious murder charges against the captain, Lee Jun-seok, and three others. They were accused of failing to try to rescue people on board and fleeing the vessel even though they knew that people were in danger and would die without their help. If convicted, the four could face death sentences. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Korea: Murder Charges in Ferry Disaster', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea: Murder Charges in Ferry Disaster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ferries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee Jun-seok', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T03:44:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dc83a92-bef2-5f5e-ae16-d0ea5df095b9', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dc83a92-bef2-5f5e-ae16-d0ea5df095b9'}, {'abstract': 'In this installment of a new series from the photo editors of T, we examine a set of images, taken mostly during the ’70s and ’80s, that capture everyday life in the industrial town of Wilkes-Barre, Pa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/t-magazine/mark-cohen-wilkes-barre-photo.html', 'snippet': 'In this installment of a new series from the photo editors of T, we examine a set of images, taken mostly during the ’70s and ’80s, that capture everyday life in the industrial town of Wilkes-Barre, Pa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekly series, T’s photo editors share the most compelling visual projects they’ve discovered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Secret World of the Photographer Mark Cohen', 'kicker': 'Viewfinder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TCulture', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Liberto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liberto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00827462-3686-5907-8f12-2800c70c25a3', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00827462-3686-5907-8f12-2800c70c25a3'}, {'abstract': 'Mads Refslund takes his crew on a field trip — to the wilderness an hour outside of Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/t-magazine/mads-refslund-foraging-new-jersey-nordic.html', 'snippet': 'Mads Refslund takes his crew on a field trip — to the wilderness an hour outside of Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Danish chef and foraging enthusiast Mads Refslund takes his crew on a field trip — to the wilderness an hour outside of Manhattan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/t-magazine/15forage-rao-slide-V573/15forage-rao-slide-V573-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/15/t-magazine/15forage-rao-slide-V573/15forage-rao-slide-V573-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i