rs like the Waldorf Astoria in Beijing and Barneys New York, is getting a retrospective of its tasteful furniture during New York Design Week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/t-magazine/furniture-yabu-pushelberg.html', 'snippet': 'The architecture and design firm, which is renowned for standout interiors like the Waldorf Astoria in Beijing and Barneys New York, is getting a retrospective of its tasteful furniture during New York Design Week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve had the chance to admire the elegant interiors and furniture design of the Waldorf Astoria in Beijing, the Hazelton Hotel in Toronto or Barneys New York, you’ve been witness to the creative hand of Yabu Pushelberg. Since starting in Toronto 35 years ago, the architecture and design firm has quietly but assertively set the bar for high-end residential, hospitality and retail design. With offices in Toronto and New York and more than 100 employees, Yabu Pushelberg boasts an impressive client list and projects in over 16 countries, including the Edition hotels in London and Miami, the Lane Crawford department store in Shanghai and the Park Hyatt New York and One Madison in New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Elegant, Thoughtful Furniture of Yabu Pushelberg', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felix Burrichter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burrichter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95b56051-179e-5988-a4a4-e2af8c210e64', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95b56051-179e-5988-a4a4-e2af8c210e64'}, {'abstract': 'It seems contrary to common sense, but there is reason to think that people might actually end up paying more per channel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/upshot/why-unbundling-cable-would-not-save-you-money.html', 'snippet': 'It seems contrary to common sense, but there is reason to think that people might actually end up paying more per channel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you have cable TV, you probably don’t watch most of the channels you get. The average American television household receives 189 channels, up from 123 in 2003. But we’re watching only 17.5 of those channels — nearly unchanged from 11 years ago, according to a new report from Nielsen.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/upshot/15up-bundle-illu-promocopy/15up-bundle-illu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/15/upshot/15up-bundle-illu-promocopy/15up-bundle-illu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 346}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/upshot/15up-bundle-illu-promocopy/15up-bundle-illu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/upshot/15up-bundle-illu-promocopy/15up-bundle-illu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1182, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/upshot/15up-bundle-illu-promocopy/15up-bundle-illu-promocopy-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'imag