 him, she can never find happiness in monogamy after she introduces Will (David Ajala) as her fiancé.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T05:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/9112ec02-7438-5f16-9c40-1dd52ce159b5', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9112ec02-7438-5f16-9c40-1dd52ce159b5'}, {'abstract': 'What many voters don’t realize is that their representatives in Parliament actually have very little power over local-level problems like potholes or drainage systems.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/lawmakers-real-powers-cant-match-voters-local-expectations/', 'snippet': 'What many voters don’t realize is that their representatives in Parliament actually have very little power over local-level problems like potholes or drainage systems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI\xa0— In the ancient city of Varanasi, in the state of Uttar Pradesh, voters said they might pass over the opposition Bharatiya Janata Party because their current lawmaker, Murli Manohar Joshi, hadn’t done much over the past decade to develop the town. And in Amethi, the Uttar Pradesh constituency of Rahul Gandhi, the vice president of the Indian National Congress, voters pointed to stagnant, trash-filled pools of water on the city’s main street and spoke of wanting change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xla