ternational/euro-zone-economy-grows-more-slowly-than-expected.html', 'snippet': 'Gross domestic product in the 18 nations rose 0.2 percent in the first quarter of this year, as Germany helped make up for France and Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The European economy maintained its feeble overall growth in the first three months of the year, official data showed on Thursday, as relatively strong performances by Germany and Britain were offset by continued weakness in France and a step backward by Italy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/16euecon-web1/16euecon-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/16/business/16euecon-web1/16euecon-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/16euecon-web1/16euecon-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/16euecon-web1/16euecon-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/16euecon-web1/16euecon-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/16/business/16euecon-web1/16euecon-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/16euecon-web1/16euecon-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro Zone Economy Grows More Slowly Than Expected', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eurostat', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T11:12:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60d07ea3-be25-5fd7-b366-45e8345a9827', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60d07ea3-be25-5fd7-b366-45e8345a9827'}, {'abstract': 'About that European recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/not-on-the-mend/', 'snippet': 'About that European recovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There have been many proclamations that the euro crisis is over, that Europe’s economy is on the mend. Behind these proclamations lie something very real — a huge convergence in interest rates, thanks to the ECB’s support and growing belief that the political risks to the euro have receded — and something more dubious — a modest uptick in debtor-country growth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not On The Mend', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T11:26:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fabe1129-b500-506e-9e44-422260906774', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fabe1129-b500-506e-9e44-422260906774'}, {'abstract': 'Citigroup fired 11 more employees over fraud at its Mexican business. | Chipotle’s two chief executives together earned $50 million last year. | The hedge fund industry talks money at a conference in Las Vegas.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/morning-agenda-cleaning-house-at-citi/', 'snippet': 'Citigroup fired 11 more employees over fraud at its Mexican business. | Chipotle’s two chief executives together earned $50 million last year. | The hedge fund industry talks money at a conference in Las Vegas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A SHAKE-UP AT CITIGROUP \xa0|\xa0 Citigroup is moving quickly to try to put a costly fraud at its Mexican business in the rearview mirror, firing an additional 11 employees, including four high-ranking executives in Mexico, Michael Corkery and Elisabeth Malkin write in DealBook. On Monday afternoon, the board of the bank was briefed on an internal investigation into the $400 million fraud involving a large Banamex client, and by Tuesday evening, the 11 employees in Mexico were fired.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cleaning House at Citi', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T11:27:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ea4482b-2159-56e2-b974-3dc642d11fa6', 'word_count': 1774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ea4482b-2159-56e2-b974-3dc642d11fa6'}, {'abstract': 'Former Treasury secretary Timothy F. Geithner’s memoir offers an inside look at the government’s response to the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/books/review/stress-test-by-timothy-f-geithner.html', 'snippet': 'Former Treasury secretary Timothy F. Geithner’s memoir offers an inside look at the government’s response to the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He’s written a really good book — we might as well get that out of the way, as so much else about Timothy F. Geithner remains unsettled. Geithner served as president of the New York Federal Reserve from late 2003 to 2008 and secretary of the Treasury from 2009 to 2013, and so sat near the center of the American financial system as it prepared to self-destruct. He then had a courtside seat to the global catastrophe. He has rich material to work with, and he has contrived to preserve its freshness. His inability as Treasury secretary to explain himself, or his actions, or the financial crisis, or his beliefs about financial reform, to the wider public will leave many readers, I suspect, feeling they are hearing his voice on these subjects for the first time.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/books/review/25lewis-sub/25lewis-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/books/review/25lewis-sub/25lewis-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/books/review/25lewis-sub/25lewis-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/books/review/25lewis-sub/25lewis-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/books/review/25lewis-sub/25lewis-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/books/review/25lewis-sub/25lewis-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/books/review/25lewis-sub/25lewis-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hot Seat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hot Seat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Stress Test: Reflections on Financial Crises (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T11:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Lewis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/afca77f1-05aa-5441-b8bb-261b4b3e5b42', 'word_count': 2086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afca77f1-05aa-5441-b8bb-261b4b3e5b42'}, {'abstract': 'The future of protecting an open Internet has been the subject of fierce debate, and potential changes to the rules by the Federal Communications Commission could affect your online experience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/technology/100000002881329/how-net-neutrality-works.html', 'snippet': 'The future of protecting an open Internet has been the subject of fierce debate, and potential changes to the rules by the Federal Communications Commission could affect your online experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The future of protecting an open Internet has been the subject of fierce debate, and potential changes to the rules by the Federal Communications Commission could affect your online experience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/multimedia/net-neutrality-explainer/net-neutrality-explainer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/14/multimedia/net-neutrality-explainer/net-neutrality-explainer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/14/multimedia/net-neutrality-explainer/net-neutrality-explainer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo'