ons of crude oil spilling into the street in eastern Los Angeles early Thursday morning, with geysers that were at first spurting up to 50 feet into the air.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pipe Ruptures, Spewing Oil in Los Angeles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T11:48:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eea097be-9504-5aa1-997f-80344a3589b1', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eea097be-9504-5aa1-997f-80344a3589b1'}, {'abstract': 'Kenneth Branagh, who stars in and jointly directs a stage production of “Macbeth,” discusses its genesis on the eve of its New York opening at the Armory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/theater/branagh-brings-his-visceral-macbeth-to-the-armory.html', 'snippet': 'Kenneth Branagh, who stars in and jointly directs a stage production of “Macbeth,” discusses its genesis on the eve of its New York opening at the Armory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any new production of “Macbeth” has a lot to overcome, including history, tradition, expectation and the participants’ own relationship to the material. For the actor and director Kenneth Branagh, this meant years of thinking about the play, biding his time and concocting and discarding various ideas (some cleverer than others) for how to stage it. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18BRANAGH/18BRAANAGH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articl