ile Joshua J. Harris, another co-founder and senior managing director, gave away 200,000 shares.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/2-apollo-global-executives-reduce-their-stakes/', 'snippet': 'Marc J. Rowan, a co-founder and senior managing director of Apollo, sold about $28.6 million shares this week, while Joshua J. Harris, another co-founder and senior managing director, gave away 200,000 shares.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two of the three leaders of Apollo Global Management have reduced their stakes in the private equity firm by a small amount, regulatory filings show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-rowan/dbpix-rowan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-rowan/dbpix-rowan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-rowan/dbpix-rowan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-rowan/dbpix-rowan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1475, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-rowan/dbpix-rowan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-rowan/dbpix-rowan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-rowan/dbpix-rowan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2 Apollo Global Executives Reduce Their Stakes', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Joshua J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowan, Marc J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apollo Global Management', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T13:40:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/978defff-6930-53ba-abab-b7384d72fa56', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/978defff-6930-53ba-abab-b7384d72fa56'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not unusual to hear stories about security officers using shock weapons against students.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/tasers-and-schools-dont-mix/', 'snippet': 'It’s not unusual to hear stories about security officers using shock weapons against students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The police rule by fiat in the hinterlands of Texas. Given that reality, no one is surprised that a Bastrop County grand jury has declined to indict the sheriff’s deputy involved in the case of a high school student who suffered permanent brain damage last fall after being shocked with a Taser. But Adam Loewy, a veteran lawyer representing 17-year-old Noe Niño de Rivera, was particularly angry about what he described as a grand jury that “was a sham process from start to finish.” Mr. Loewy asserted in an email that prosecutors never contacted him, and never met with the victim, his parents or an eye witness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tasers and Schools Don’t Mix', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stun Guns', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T13:56:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d0cdec3-ca9a-503f-9ca6-950be177416c', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d0cdec3-ca9a-503f-9ca6-950be177416c'}, {'abstract': 'The author of “The Noble Hustle: Poker, Beef Jerky, and Death” would like to host Flannery O’Connor, “because I don’t think she knew a lot of black people, or got out of the house that much.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/books/review/colson-whitehead-by-the-book.html', 'snippet': 'The author of “The Noble Hustle: Poker, Beef Jerky, and Death” would like to host Flannery O’Connor, “because I don’t think she knew a lot of black people, or got out of the house that much.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The author of “The Noble Hustle: Poker, Beef Jerky, and Death” would like to host Flannery O’Connor, “because I don’t think she knew a lot of black people, or got out of the house that much.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':