'_id': 'nyt://article/8a18211d-b563-5d28-87db-1965337fa80d', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a18211d-b563-5d28-87db-1965337fa80d'}, {'abstract': 'How a corps of Virginia Military Institute students found themselves on the front lines in the Shenandoah Valley.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/the-cadets-at-new-market/', 'snippet': 'How a corps of Virginia Military Institute students found themselves on the front lines in the Shenandoah Valley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the evening of May 10, 1864, on the first anniversary of the battlefield death of Gen. Thomas “Stonewall” Jackson, who had been a professor at the Virginia Military Institute before the war, some 300 V.M.I. cadets paraded the lush grounds in full dress while bands played and nearby townsfolk came to pay their respects. “Groups of girls in filmy garments set off with bits of color came tripping across the sod; and children and nurses sat about the benches at the guard-tree,” one cadet recalled. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cadets at New Market', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Ulysses S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Robert E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of Northern Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virginia Military Institute', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T15:53:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jed Morrison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morrison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/698ba97e-0016-5655-9324-2c86a307f775', 'word_count': 2007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/698ba97e-0016-5655-9324-2c86a307f775'}, {'abstract': 'A basic online tool for people to ask Google to take down potential harmful links would be in place in about two weeks, a top German regulator said.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/after-european-court-decision-google-works-on-a-link-removal-tool/', 'snippet': 'A basic online tool for people to ask Google to take down potential harmful links would be in place in about two weeks, a top German regulator said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Google will announce by the end of the month a mechanism for consumers to request that links to information about them be removed from the company’s search engine, a leading European regulator said on Thursday. It was one of the first signs that Google was working through how to operate after a court ruling said consumers could make such requests.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/business/15bits-go