been announced, putting the city — and the event’s curator, Jessica Morgan of the Tate Modern — on the map.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/gwangju-biennale-south-korea-jessica-morgan/', 'snippet': 'The lineup for this fall’s Gwangju Biennale has just been announced, putting the city — and the event’s curator, Jessica Morgan of the Tate Modern — on the map.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout most of the past week, Randalls Island seemed the most far-flung art destination anyone in the New York art world was paying attention to. But a dinner at the West Village club Norwood held during Frieze New York shifted attention to a locale halfway around the world. The curator Jessica Morgan of the Tate Modern in London announced the artists participating in her edition of the Gwangju Biennale in South Korea this fall, which runs Sept. 5 though Nov. 9. Founded in 1995, the event is South Korea’s most important international exhibition, and arguably Asia’s as well, and has put the nation’s sixth-largest city on the map. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/t-magazine/15gwangju-mcgarry1/15gwangju-mcgarry1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/15/t-magazine/15gwangju-mcgarry1/15gwangju-mcgarry1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/t-magazine/15gwangju-mcgarry1/15gwangju-mcgarry1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/t-magazine/15gwangju-mcgarry1/15gwangju-mcgarry1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', '