ostage for 105\xa0days while working to bring education to the children of the war-torn region of Darfur, Sudan. In some respects my captivity seems all but a distant memory. The passage of time, however, will never diminish my fond recollections of my only trusted companion during those long, death-defying days—Gabriel García Márquez. With his recent passing, all of the harrowing and heart-tugging memories of our time together came flooding back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Held Hostage in Sudan with Gabriel García Márquez', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T16:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Flavia Wagner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Flavia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wagner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/272b2f35-fbab-5234-92a6-68418eb9067c', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/272b2f35-fbab-5234-92a6-68418eb9067c'}, {'abstract': 'A battle scene from the artist’s first feature film that combines live-action and animation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/t-magazine/100000002882396/clip-jellyfish-eyes-by-takashi-murakami.html', 'snippet': 'A battle scene from the artist’s first feature film that combines live-action and animation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A battle scene from the artist’s first feature film that combines live-action and animation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/multimedia/tmag-murakami/tmag-murakami-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/