'Two weeks after the Pennsylvania Ballet said its artistic director would step down, the executive director is also leaving.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/executive-director-like-artistic-director-is-leaving-pennsylvania-ballet/', 'snippet': 'Two weeks after the Pennsylvania Ballet said its artistic director would step down, the executive director is also leaving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s all change at Pennsylvania Ballet. Just two weeks after the announcement that its artistic director, Roy Kaiser, would leave the company once a successor was found, the troupe has announced that its executive director, Michael Scolamiero, will also depart. He will take up the same position at Miami City Ballet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Executive Director, Like Artistic Director, Is Leaving Pennsylvania Ballet', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scolamiero, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami City Ballet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania Ballet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T16:54:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85fb5928-0116-55f4-a6e5-62ca9e9fc964', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85fb5928-0116-55f4-a6e5-62ca9e9fc964'}, {'abstract': 'T debuts an exclusive clip from the Japanese artist’s first film — tickets for a June 1 screening in New York go on sale today.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/15/exclusive-clip-jellyfish-eyes-takashi-murakami-movie-at-film-society-lincoln-center/', 'snippet': 'T debuts an exclusive clip from the Japanese artist’s first film — tickets for a June 1 screening in New York go on sale today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Takashi Murakami is one of the few artists alive who might genuinely be considered a household name. The Japanese maestro’s hard-edged, big-featured monsters, beauties and flower-faces — famously executed by a vast network of studio assistants, some of whom have spawned their own cult iconographies under the umbrella of his art production and artist management company Kaikai Kiki Co. — are the progenitors of the self-explanatory art movement known as “Superflat,” which has long since exploded beyond the walls of galleries and onto Louis Vuitton bags, Supreme skate decks and any niche product that can be refashioned as a postmodern canvas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Screening | Takashi Murakami Makes a Movie', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T17:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cc5da07-cf18-57dc-a07d-e5acbb1fcc3e', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cc5da07-cf18-57dc-a07d-e5acbb1fcc3e'}, {'abstract': 'BMW says it may build Minis in Mexico; a quadriplegic former IndyCar racer will drive a 2014 Corvette Stingray at the Indianapolis Motor Speedway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/automobiles/wh