ton-obit-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mel Patton, 89, Who Shattered a Leg and Then Sprinting Records, Is Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mel Patton, 89, Who Shattered a Leg and Then Sprinting Records, Is Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patton, Mel (1924-2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T18:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Litsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Litsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/7da2698b-35c1-5fa5-9032-7eae09298901', 'word_count': 1152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7da2698b-35c1-5fa5-9032-7eae09298901'}, {'abstract': 'Arthur Sulzberger Jr., The New York Times’s publisher, denied that a disparity in Jill Abramson’s pay compared with predecessors figured in her being replaced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/business/media/times-issues-response-on-abramson-pay.html', 'snippet': 'Arthur Sulzberger Jr., The New York Times’s publisher, denied that a disparity in Jill Abramson’s pay compared with predecessors figured in her being replaced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after The New York Times announced that it had dismissed Jill Abramson, its first female executive editor, after only 33 months on the job, its publisher was denying reports that her removal was related to complaints about unequal compensation in comparison with her predecess