', 'value': 'Feeney, Krista Bennion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T21:32:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e16f9dae-8c50-5629-bcab-deff8b9c763b', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e16f9dae-8c50-5629-bcab-deff8b9c763b'}, {'abstract': 'A show devoted to Parmigianino’s portrait of a turbaned woman arrives at the Frick cloaked in mystery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/arts/design/parmigianinos-schiava-turca-comes-to-the-frick.html', 'snippet': 'A show devoted to Parmigianino’s portrait of a turbaned woman arrives at the Frick cloaked in mystery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the midst of a frantic week of art fairs and auctions, a splendid Renaissance portrait made a quiet and dignified entrance at the Frick. Parmigianino’s “Schiava Turca,” a painting of an unidentified woman with twinkling hazel eyes and a mischievous half-smile, invites us to settle in for a restorative session of close looking.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/18FRICK1/FRICK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/18FRICK1/FRICK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 770}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/18FRICK1/FRICK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subt