: 'For Edie Falco, star of the Showtime series “Nurse Jackie,” Sunday is a day for “free-floating time” with her son, Anderson, 9, and her daughter, Macy, 6. The children’s godfathers may pay a visit. There may be a movie or a play. There’s usually a meditation class. Ms. Falco, 50, has won four Emmys, one for “Nurse Jackie” and three for her role as Carmela Soprano in “The Sopranos.” A single mother, she lives in the West Village with her children and the family’s rescue dog, Sami, a Brussels griffon. Ms. Falco often rides around town on her electric bike.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18ROUTINE4/18ROUTINE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18ROUTINE4/18ROUTINE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18ROUTINE4/18ROUTINE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18ROUTINE4/18ROUTINE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18ROUTINE4/18ROUTINE4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18ROUTINE4/18ROUTINE4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18ROUTINE4/18ROUTINE4-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Edie Falco: Meditate. Then It’s Time to Play.', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Meditate. Then It’s Time to Play.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Falco, Edie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Nurse Jackie (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T21:58:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kara Mayer Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kara', 'middlename': 'Mayer', 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22edaa35-ed15-530b-8ab5-6dc259407ee0', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22edaa35-ed15-530b-8ab5-6dc259407ee0'}, {'abstract': 'In “A Troublesome Inheritance,” Nicholas Wade argues that races evolved differently, and that scientists should pursue studies of the biological and genetic differences between them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/books/nicholas-wades-a-troublesome-inheritance.html', 'snippet': 'In “A Troublesome Inheritance,” Nicholas Wade argues that races evolved differently, and that scientists should pursue studies of the biological and genetic differences between them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few areas of science have contributed more to human misery than the study of racial difference. In the 1920s, eugenicists from top American universities promoted the sterilization of the unfit and later praised Hitler’s racial codes while advocating laws that would exclude thousands of Jews from our shores.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16BOOKWADE/16BOOKWADE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 515, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16BOOKWADE/16BOOKWADE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 515, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16BOOKWADE/BOOKWADE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16BOOKWADE/BOOKWADE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16BOOKWADE/BOOKWADE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Charging Into the Minefield of Genes and Racial Difference', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charging Into the Minefield of Genes and Racial Difference', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Nicholas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T22:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ar