f the opening-day buzz at the Cannes Film Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/movies/sommeliers-decanting-the-madness-of-cannes.html', 'snippet': 'A shortage of female directors in competition, the film “Timbuktu,” the return of Jean-Luc Godard, and a young director’s suicide were part of the opening-day buzz at the Cannes Film Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES — They know how to put on a good show at the Cannes Film Festival, even when forced to make do with an opening-night dud and the lack of a closing-night selection. No matter how serious and aesthetically high-minded, the festival always banks on its stars. This year Quentin Tarantino will help wrap up the proceedings by introducing a restoration of Sergio Leone’s 1964 red-sauce western, “A Fistful of Dollars.” It’s a celebrity event that will bookend the one delivered on Wednesday, when Nicole Kidman — the star of the widely derided “Grace of Monaco” — drifted down the red carpet, reprising her familiar role as a supernova who transcends her every stinker. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16CANNES/16CANNES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16CANNES/16CANNES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16CANNES/16CANNES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16CANNES/16CANNES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subt