nference-stocks-induce-anxiety/', 'snippet': 'At the hedge fund industry’s annual gathering in Las Vegas, managers voiced concerns about the direction of the stock market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — At the the SkyBridge Alternatives Conference here, hedge fund managers are gathering at the Bellagio hotel to exchange views and ideas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At SALT Conference, Stocks Induce Anxiety', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T23:07:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e596593-b13d-5df5-83ca-43592b742d7f', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e596593-b13d-5df5-83ca-43592b742d7f'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Discoverers,” a history professor takes his children on a family-fraught trip with historical re-enactors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/movies/the-discoverers-directed-by-justin-schwarz.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Discoverers,” a history professor takes his children on a family-fraught trip with historical re-enactors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On paper, “The Discoverers” sounds like “National Lampoon’s Vacation” crossed with a self-help manual. Lewis (Griffin Dunne) is a struggling history professor in Chicago who, à la Grady Tripp in “Wonder Boys,” is preparing to publish a nearly 7,000-page tome. In the sort of excursion that might generously be described as a getaway, he piles his teenage kids, Zoe (Madeleine Martin) and Jack (Devon Graye), into the car, bound for a conference in Portland, Ore. The road trip’s destination suddenly changes when Lewis’s mother takes a turn for the worse.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16DISCOVERERS/DISCOVERERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16DISCOVERERS/DISCOVERERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16DISCOVERERS/DISCOVERERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16DISCOVERERS/DISCOVERERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1037, 'width': 1554, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16DISCOVERERS/DISCOVERERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16DISCOVERERS/DISCOVERERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/16DISCOVERERS/DISCOVERERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Lewis and Clark Inspired', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Discoverers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunne, Griffin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Discoverers (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwarz, Justin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T23:07:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9786b3f5-b25c-547b-84f4-2f977b986dd9', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9786b3f5-b25c-547b-84f4-2f977b986dd9'}, {'abstract': 'The beverage maker and the fast-food chain have had close ties since 1955, to the point where Coca-Cola even has a McDonald’s division.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/business/coke-and-mcdonalds-working-hand-in-hand-since-1955.html', 'snippet': 'The beverage maker and the fast-food chain have had close ties since 1955, to the point where Coca-Cola even has a McDonald’s division.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was early 1955 when Ray Kroc, an ambitious milkshake equipment salesman who had bought the right to expand McDonald’s throughout the country, was opening his first restaurant, in Des Plaines, Ill.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coke and McDonald’s, Growing Together Since 1955 ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coke and McDonald&#8217;s, Growing Together Since 1955 ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelles, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coca-Cola Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-15T23:16:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gelles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38594725-1af2-5931-bb24-20fa52c3f78d', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38594725-1af2-5931-bb24-20fa52c3f78d'}, {'abstract': 'Alzheimer’s, which has been linked to far more deaths than AIDS, has failed to garner the same national outrage and attention, even as AIDS deaths have begun to fall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/nyregion/alzheimers-a-neglected-epidemic.html', 'snippet': 'Alzheimer’s, which has been linked to far more deaths than AIDS, has failed to garner the same national outrage and attention, even as AIDS deaths have begun to fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opening shots of “The Normal Heart,” HBO’s adaptation of Larry Kramer’s 1985 play about the early days of the AIDS crisis in New York, reveal a crew of sinewy and amorous young men disembarking from a ferry on Fire Island on a beautiful July day in 1981. The tableau is meant to suggest the final hour of unburdened desire, the moment before so much youth and beauty would be sacrificed to the cruelest attacks of physiology and cultural indifference.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18BIG_SPAN/18BIG_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18BIG_SPAN/18BIG_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18BIG_SPAN/18BIG_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 10