organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c8d8c35-1436-5c3e-a00a-909cbe64a822', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c8d8c35-1436-5c3e-a00a-909cbe64a822'}, {'abstract': 'Jimmy Page, the founder of Led Zeppelin, has been remastering the group’s entire catalog and says he would love to be onstage playing music again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/17/arts/music/jimmy-page-talks-about-his-old-band-its-legacy-and-himself.html', 'snippet': 'Jimmy Page, the founder of Led Zeppelin, has been remastering the group’s entire catalog and says he would love to be onstage playing music again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Boston last week to deliver the commencement address at the Berklee College of Music, Jimmy Page, the founder of Led Zeppelin, learned to his surprise that the school had a course in which his guitar licks were minutely analyzed. “They go into all these things and deconstruct them,” he said, “the harmonies and the voicings and the progressions, the arrangements.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/page-image/page-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 871, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/page-image/page-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 871}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/page-image/page-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 706, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/arts/page-image/page-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1411, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}