 of the airwaves for purchase in auctions by smaller wireless companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Federal Communications Commission on Thursday adopted new rules governing coming auctions of airwaves for use in mobile broadband, and the agency said it would set aside certain portions of the airwaves for purchase by smaller wireless companies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.C.C. to Help Small Firms Buy Airwaves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.C.C. to Help Small Firms Buy Airwaves ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio Spectrum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyatt, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T00:29:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03c90ff9-a940-588d-8bb0-ed80449fbf10', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03c90ff9-a940-588d-8bb0-ed80449fbf10'}, {'abstract': 'The lawsuit charges that prisoners are routinely executed using “a secret drug formulation obtained from secret sources,” denying the public its rightful access to important information about the criminal justice system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/us/news-groups-sue-for-data-on-missouris-executions.html', 'snippet': 'The lawsuit charges that prisoners are routinely executed using “a secret drug formulation obtained from secret sources,” denying the public its rightful access to important information about the criminal justice system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of news organizations sued the Missouri Department of Corrections on Thursday, arguing that the department is violating the First Amendment by refusing to identify the sources of lethal drugs used in its executions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Groups Sue for Data on Missouri’s Executions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'News Groups Sue for Data on Missouri’s Executions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T00:32:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fad459d5-6351-5940-af1e-628f09ce6a46', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fad459d5-6351-5940-af1e-628f09ce6a46'}, {'abstract': 'False doctrines on climate science have become badges of identity for Republicans, and that’s more frightening than some of the environmental change underway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/opinion/krugman-points-of-no-return.html', 'snippet': 'False doctrines on climate science have become badges of identity for Republicans, and that’s more frightening than some of the environmental change underway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently two research teams, working independently and using different methods, reached an alarming conclusion: The West Antarctic ice sheet is doomed. The sheet’s slide into the ocean, and the resulting sharp rise in sea levels, will probably happen slowly. But it’s irreversible. Even if we took drastic action to limit global warming right now, this particular process of environmental change has reached a point of no return.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 591}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1008, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1881, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Points of No Return', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Points of No Return', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T00:36:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a07fac2-5268-5d95-aae6-0adae8276d1c', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a07fac2-5268-5d95-aae6-0adae8276d1c'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority plans to increase service on the L subway line this fall, adding 33 round trips on Saturdays and 22 round trips on Sundays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/nyregion/mta-expanding-weekend-service-on-the-l-line-to-handle-growing-crowds.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority plans to increase service on the L subway line this fall, adding 33 round trips on Saturdays and 22 round trips on Sundays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The math problem of the New York City subway system is no secret, its remainders spilling onto the platforms where luckless travelers watch full trains come and go.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/nyregion/16ltrain/16ltrain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/16/nyregion/16ltrain/16ltrain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/nyregion/16ltrain/16ltrain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/nyregion/16ltrain/16ltrain-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/nyregion/16ltrain/16ltrain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/16/nyregion/16ltrain/16ltrain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/nyregion/16ltrain/16ltrain-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'M.T.A. Expanding Weekend Service on the L Line to Handle Growing Crowds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'M.T.A. Expanding Weekend Service on the L Line to Handle Growing Crowds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Straphangers Campaign', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T00:41:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f01de7ac-8990-5d65-aece-b3a33286e1d3', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f01de7ac-8990-5d65-aece-b3a33286e1d3'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn Women’s Exchange, a shop selling handmade wares, was founded in Brooklyn Heights in 1854, helping women in need sell needlework and handicrafts without resorting to factory work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/nyregion/for-160-years-always-something-new.html', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn Women’s Exchange, a shop selling handmade wares, was founded in Brooklyn Heights in 1854, helping women in need sell needlework and handicrafts without resorting to factory work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Brooklyn Women’s Exchange, a nonprofit, volunteer-run shop selling handmade wares, the atmosphere is instantly soothing. Rows of baby sweaters in Jordan almond colors hang neatly on a rack. A gangly trio of stuffed rabbits shares table space with a stack of crocheted blankets. Nat King Cole music plays softly in the background. Two volunteers murmur to each other as they sort through a pile of tiny hand-knit bootees in pastel green, lemon and pink. The scent of lavender wafts delicately from the soap display. Call it retail tonic.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For 1