ork Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b46ca9a-26e6-558b-991c-2f8309501cb9', 'word_count': 1898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b46ca9a-26e6-558b-991c-2f8309501cb9'}, {'abstract': 'Concert listings for the New York area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/arts/music/pop-music-listings-for-may-16-22.html', 'snippet': 'Concert listings for the New York area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prices may not reflect ticketing service charges. For full reviews of recent concerts: nytimes.com/music. A searchable guide to these and other shows is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop Music Listings for May 16-22', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T00:51:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e710b2d4-be2c-5933-ad48-295770593598', 'word_count': 1323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e710b2d4-be2c-5933-ad48-295770593598'}, {'abstract': 'A listing of discussions, film screenings, cultural activities and walking tours in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/arts/spare-times-listings-for-may-16-22.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of discussions, film screenings, cultural activities and walking tours in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dance Parade and Festival (Saturday) Why walk down Broadway when you can twist, pirouette and boogie down the thoroughfare with thousands of other quick-stepping souls during this annual free dance celebration? More than 150 groups, demonstrating over 75 styles of dance traditional and contemporary, will be among the professional and amateur hoofers bounding their way from 21st Street to Tompkins Square Park. Setting feet in motion at 1 p.m. will be a ribbon cutting by the event’s grand marshals, the tapper Savion Glover; Jawole Willa Jo Zollar, the artistic director of the Urban Bush Women; and the D.J. and producer Hex Hector. The fun continues in the park from 3 p.m., with performances and lessons. Participants at last year’s spectacle included local members of the Fraternidad Folklórica y Cultural Caporales Universitarios de San Simon, demonstrating Bolivian moves, and the NYC Bhangra Dance Company, displaying Indian styles. The event is free for individuals, but registration is required for participants. Information is at danceparade.org. Now go shine those dancing shoes. (Anne Mancuso)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for May 16-22', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T00:51:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1dbfb12-00dd-5d6a-a4d7-0d0a52724a4f', 'word_count': 2559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1dbfb12-00dd-5d6a-a4d7-0d0a52724a4f'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to classical music concerts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/arts/music/classical-music-listings-for-may-16-22.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to classical music concerts.', 'lead_paragraph': '★ Argento Chamber Ensemble  (Friday and Sunday) This excellent group offers works exploring the possibilities of different instruments, with music for piano, clarinet, viola and voice by Aaron Helgeson, Aaron Einbond, David Fulmer, Berg and Sebastian Currier. Friday at 7:30 p.m., Sunday at 4 p.m., Austrian Cultural Forum, 11 East 52nd Street, Manhattan, 212-319-5300, acfny.org; free, $10 suggested donation. (Schweitzer)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical Music Listings for May 16-22', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T00:51:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/c680cf8b-0173-561d-bb4d-b7e58981310e', 'word_count': 1280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c680cf8b-0173-561d-bb4d-b7e58981310e'}, {'abstract': 'A critical guide to exhibitions and installations in the New York area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/arts/design/art-listings-for-may-16-22.html', 'snippet': 'A critical guide to exhibitions and installations in the New York area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Museums and galleries are in Manhattan unless otherwise noted. Full reviews of recent art shows: nytimes.com/art. A searchable guide to these and many other art shows is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum & Gallery Listings for May 16-22', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_d