4/05/17/world/asia/india-elections.html', 'snippet': 'The Hindu nationalist Bharatiya Janata Party’s enormous victory clearly reflects a rapid change in Indian society as urbanization and economic growth break down old voting patterns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Addressing a euphoric crowd Friday afternoon, Narendra Modi rallied the public to join him in taking on challenges of a vast scale. He has floated the idea of building “a hundred new cities,” of extending a high-speed rail network across the subcontinent and undertaking the herculean task of cleaning the Ganges River.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Narendra Modi’s Ambitious Agenda Will Face Difficult Obstacles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India Delivers Clear Mandate to Hindu Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gandhi, Rahul', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T04:49:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b28c71dc-7f74-5bfa-a1fb-bd1a0f0b1a78', 'word_count': 1219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b28c71dc-7f74-5bfa-a1fb-bd1a0f0b1a78'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Starz) CAPTAIN PHILLIPS (2013) Tom Hanks, above, portrays Richard Phillips, the commander of the Maersk Alabama, an American container ship with a crew of 20 sailors and a cargo including supplies from the United Nations World Food Program, that was seized in the Indian Ocean in April 2009 by four armed Somalis. Barkhad Abdi, a first-time actor who received an Oscar nomination, plays Muse, their leader, whose actions lead to the arrival of the American military and its warships. “The existential realities that inform contemporary Somali piracy turn out to be one of the unexpected themes of ‘Captain Phillips,’ which begins as something of a procedural about men at work and morphs into a jittery thriller even as it also deepens, brilliantly, unexpectedly, into an unsettling look at global capitalism and American privilege and power,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times about this best picture nominee, adapted by the director Paul Greengrass from Mr. Phillips’s book, “A Captain’s Duty: Somali Pirates, Navy SEALS, and Dangerous Days at Sea.” “Phillips is unambiguously a heroic figure, but he’s scarcely the sole point of interest in a movie that steadily and almost stealthily asserts the agonized humanity of his captors.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T05:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 