1e2304a-0fae-59ed-9949-63e4ae024bce'}, {'abstract': 'An ambitious new exhibit shows the many transformations – social, physical and cultural – that have remade Latin America.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/latin-americas-mutating-cities-in-photographs/', 'snippet': 'An ambitious new exhibit shows the many transformations – social, physical and cultural – that have remade Latin America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Evaporados — evaporated — is pasted in huge letters on an expressway wall in Lima, Peru. The artist Eduardo Villanes put them there in 1995, to protest the abduction and murder of nine university students and a professor by a military death squad, as well as the subsequent amnesty granted to the killers by Alberto Fujimori, Peru’s repressive and corrupt president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/20140515-lens-latin-slide-9PJ0/20140515-lens-latin-slide-9PJ0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/20140515-lens-latin-slide-9PJ0/20140515-lens-latin-slide-9PJ0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 901}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/20140515-lens-latin-slide-9PJ0/20140515-lens-latin-slide-9PJ0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/20140515-lens-latin-slide-9PJ0/20140515-lens-latin-slide-9PJ0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1364, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/20140515-lens-l