nough? Then there were the camera crews from CNN and TMZ at their practices.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/17/sports/Y-CLIPPERS/Y-CLIPPERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/17/sports/Y-CLIPPERS/Y-CLIPPERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/17/sports/Y-CLIPPERS/Y-CLIPPERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/17/sports/Y-CLIPPERS/Y-CLIPPERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/17/sports/Y-CLIPPERS/Y-CLIPPERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/17/sports/Y-CLIPPERS/Y-CLIPPERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/17/sports/Y-CLIPPERS/Y-CLIPPERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clippers Can’t Believe Their Surreal Season Has Ended', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clippers Can’t Believe Their Surreal Season Has Come to a Close', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T11:58:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1b71ac4-5e81-5391-ae2e-c2d51a3c87a8', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1b71ac4-5e81-5391-ae2e-c2d51a3c87a8'}, {'abstract': 'In the romantic comedy “Words and Pictures,” Juliette Binoche plays a painter and is a painter: All of the original artwork in the film is hers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/movies/juliette-binoche-brings-own-art-to-words-and-pictures.html', 'snippet': 'In the romantic comedy “Words and Pictures,” Juliette Binoche plays a painter and is a painter: All of the original artwork in the film is hers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the new romantic comedy “Words and Pictures,” a rolling office chair becomes a tool for art creation. Juliette Binoche, playing an art teacher whose rheumatoid arthritis affects her ability to paint, lies on her stomach across the chair, grabs a paintbrush and swivels from one part to another of the canvas on the floor. Passion and pain become a part of each stroke, as Ms. Binoche both plays a visual artist and is one.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18WORDS/18WORDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge'