riginal': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27aff7a6-efeb-583b-91cb-adafa85589b5', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27aff7a6-efeb-583b-91cb-adafa85589b5'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon promotes books from Hachette Books Group while discouraging people from buying them. After the retailer’s aggressive stance became public last week, criticism and complaints mounted. But Amazon seems confident it will get what it wants in the end.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/amazon-vs-hachette-when-does-discouragement-become-misrepresentation/', 'snippet': 'Amazon promotes books from Hachette Books Group while discouraging people from buying them. After the retailer’s aggressive stance became public last week, criticism and complaints mounted. But Amazon seems confident it will get what it wants in t...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For months now, Amazon has been trying to put the screws on Hachette, the smallest of the Big Five publishers, by discouraging people from buying its printed books. Amazon’s goal: force Hachette to give it better terms on e-books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/technology/15bits-amazon3/15bits-amazon3-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/15/technology/15bits-amazon3/15bits-amazon3-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/technology/15bits-amazon3/15bits-amazon3-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 472, 'width': 796, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ran