', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/books/review/0518-bks-FALLOWS/0518-bks-FALLOWS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/books/review/0518-bks-FALLOWS/0518-bks-FALLOWS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/books/review/0518-bks-FALLOWS/0518-bks-FALLOWS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/books/review/0518-bks-FALLOWS/0518-bks-FALLOWS-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 982, 'width': 1408, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/books/review/0518-bks-FALLOWS/0518-bks-FALLOWS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/18/books/review/0518-bks-FALLOWS/0518-bks-FALLOWS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/books/review/0518-bks-FALLOWS/0518-bks-FALLOWS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rising Sun', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rising Sun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fallows, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pilling, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T15:58:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Fallows', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fallows', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/42804965-3313-56bc-9dfb-07579fd25131', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42804965-3313-56bc-9dfb-07579fd25131'}, {'abstract': 'Representative John Conyers Jr., Democrat of Michigan, was denied a place on the ballot this week.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/an-incumbent-falls-afoul-of-election-laws-designed-to-protect-incumbents/', 'snippet': 'Representative John Conyers Jr., Democrat of Michigan, was denied a place on the ballot this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Political pros know better than anyone that election laws are typically crafted by statehouse lawmakers with enough hedges, hurdles and moats to insulate party machines and shield incumbents against insurgent challengers. That’s the nature of the power game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Incumbent Falls Afoul of Election Laws Designed to Protect Incumbents', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conyers, John Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T15:59:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b74961d-a74a-5845-89ed-18cebede8e0b', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b74961d-a74a-5845-89ed-18cebede8e0b'}, {'abstract': 'Vladimir Jurowski, principal conductor of the London Philharmonic Orchestra, will make his New York Philharmonic debut on Wednesday, conducting two colorful works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/arts/music/venerable-poetry-and-a-premiere.html', 'snippet': 'Vladimir Jurowski, principal conductor of the London Philharmonic Orchestra, will make his New York Philharmonic debut on Wednesday, conducting two colorful works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vladimir Jurowski, principal conductor of the London Philharmonic Orchestra, will make his New York Philharmonic debut on Wednesday, conducting two colorful works. The excellent young violinist Janine Jansen will be the soloist in Szymanowski’s shimmering and sumptuous Violin Concerto No. 1, inspired by Tadeusz Micinski’s poem “May Night.” Also on the lineup are selections from Prokofiev’s ballet “Cinderella.” (7:30 p.m. Wednesday and Thursday, 2 p.m. Friday, 8 p.m. Saturday, Avery Fisher Hall, Lincoln Center, 212-875-5656, nyphil.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE4/18GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE4/18GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/