me-slice-of-baloney.html', 'snippet': '“Judge Judy Primetime,” on Tuesday night at 8 on CBS, deciphers the guilty pleasure to be found in her courtroom drama by serving up classic Judyisms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fess up: who hasn’t gawked in awe as Judge Judith Sheindlin slaps sense into a freak show of ne’er-do-wells with rejoinders we only wish we had queued up: “Are you trying to justify to me that you are an idiot?” “Don’t try to teach a pig to sing. It doesn’t work, and it irritates the pig.” “Beauty fades. Dumb is forever.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 805}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 763, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1490, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prime-Time Slice of ‘Baloney!’', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prime-Time Slice of ‘Baloney!’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T16:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d31effb-bf87-57cd-965c-0978ee560a3e', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d31effb-bf87-57cd-965c-0978ee560a3e'}, {'abstract': 'Most people associate Auschwitz with the death camp. But it is also a town, Oswiecim, once home to a vibrant Jewish community in Poland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/arts/design/a-polish-town-before-its-infamy.html', 'snippet': 'Most people associate Auschwitz with the death camp. But it is also a town, Oswiecim, once home to a vibrant Jewish community in Poland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most people associate Auschwitz with the death camp. But it is also a town, Oswiecim, once home to a vibrant Jewish community in Poland. Now, the Museum of Jewish Heritage — A Living Memorial to the Holocaust in Lower Manhattan is examining that history in “A Town Known as Auschwitz: The Life and Death of a Jewish Community,” which explores how Jews and non-Jews coexisted peacefully in Oswiecim (Auschwitz was its German name) for centuries before World War II.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE5/18GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 