inoffs “Superman” and “Justice League”), in various TV incarnations from 1992 to 1999. Call it the Bruce W. Timm brain trust, after its producer and character designer; members included the writer Paul Dini and the voice director Andrea Romano. (And salute its writer Dwayne McDuffie, who died in 2011, and its composer Shirley Walker, who died in 2006.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE3/18SiloGUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE3/18SiloGUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE3/18SiloGUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE3/18SiloGUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE3/18SiloGUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE3/18SiloGUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE3/18SiloGUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Temptress Returns to Tweak His Cowl', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Temptress Returns to Tweak His Cowl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T16:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/575b3df9-5f26-524c-85f6-46dd6d39191c', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/575b3df9-5f26-524c-85f6-46dd6d39191c'}, {'abstract': 'The latest round of Danspace Project’s Platform series, which explores dance through the lens of a particular idea or theme, is dedicated to the work of the choreographer DD Dorvillier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/arts/dance/trolling-the-past-for-fresh-insights.html', 'snippet': 'The latest round of Danspace Project’s Platform series, which explores dance through the lens of a particular idea or theme, is dedicated to the work of the choreographer DD Dorvillier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest round of Danspace Project’s Platform series, which explores dance through the lens of a particular idea or theme, is dedicated to the work of the choreographer DD Dorvillier, who helped define contemporary dance beginning in the 1990s. For more than a decade Ms. Dorvillier lived and worked out of the Matzoh Factory, a loft she shared with the dancer and choreographer Jennifer Monson in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUIDE6/18GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/arts/18GUID