dwater Hospital for chronically ill patients, on Roosevelt Island, was shuttered in December to make room for a science and technology campus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/nyregion/death-of-a-hospital.html', 'snippet': 'The Goldwater Hospital for chronically ill patients, on Roosevelt Island, was shuttered in December to make room for a science and technology campus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1935, with the last inmates from the century-old penitentiary transferred to Rikers Island, a site south of the Queensboro Bridge was cleared for the modern Welfare Hospital for Chronic Diseases, which would become known as Goldwater Hospital.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death of a Hospital', 'kicker': 'Album', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Death of a Hospital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Roosevelt Island (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coler-Goldwater Specialty Hospital and Nursing Facility', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giraudet, Charles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T17:53:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd812c9a-b8ab-5cd1-ba19-32f72ccdf98c', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd812c9a-b8ab-5cd1-ba19-32f72ccdf98c'}, {'abstract': 'After twice failing to catch a stunning early morning vista on Haleakala, the author finally finds her view at the other end of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/travel/forgoing-sunrise-for-sunset-on-mauis-volcano.html', 'snippet': 'After twice failing to catch a stunning early morning vista on Haleakala, the author finally finds her view at the other end of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was standing at the top of Mount Haleakala at 6 o’clock on a March morning, bleary-eyed and nauseated. During the three-hour journey from sea level to 10,000 feet, a group of wretchedly jet-lagged adventurers and I had scissored through almost 40 miles of hairpin turns holding on to our coffee cups and stomachs, stopping to help a disoriented elderly woman, navigating through herds of cows and glumly watching as rain began to splatter the van’s windshield.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SUBEXPLORER10/SUB18EXPLORER10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SUBEXPLORER10/SUB18EXPLORER10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SUBEXPLORER10/SUB18EXPLORER10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SUBEXPLORER10/SUB18EXPLORER10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1380, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SUBEXPLORER10/SUB18EXPLORER10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/18/travel/18SUB