, 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Irwin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Irwin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3649f2d7-b741-5571-9e57-7643afa451df', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3649f2d7-b741-5571-9e57-7643afa451df'}, {'abstract': 'The association named “A Gentleman’s Guide to Love & Murder” best musical and “All the Way” best play.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/drama-league-honors-gentlemans-guide-and-all-the-way/', 'snippet': 'The association named “A Gentleman’s Guide to Love & Murder” best musical and “All the Way” best play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Drama League, an association of thousands of theatergoers nationwide, announced on Friday that “A Gentleman’s Guide to Love & Murder” has won its 2014 award for best musical and “All the Way” has won for best play. At a ceremony to present its 80th annual awards, the league also named “Hedwig and the Angry Inch” best revival of a musical and “The Glass Menagerie” best revival of a play.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drama League Honors ‘Gentleman’s Guide’ and ‘All the Way’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drama League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T18:42:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/283227e5-f4ff-5f57-8fff-d3fd8a4b8236', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/283227e5-f4ff-5f57-8fff-d3fd8a4b8236'}, {'abstract': 'The actress, whose first starring role in an American film takes the big screen today with “The Immigrant,” discusses her costar Joaquin Phoenix and her strategy for getting in character.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/interview-marion-cotillard-on-the-immigrant-movie-james-gray-joaquin-phoenix/', 'snippet': 'The actress, whose first starring role in an American film takes the big screen today with “The Immigrant,” discusses her costar Joaquin Phoenix and her strategy for getting in character.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Marion Cotillard is presented with the notion that after more than 40 films, an Oscar for Best Actress (for “La Vie en Rose”), and roles in some of the last decade’s defining blockbusters, she’s only now leading her first American film, even she seems surprised. Yes, that’s true,” she says with a laugh. “I didn’t even think about it.” But “The Immigrant,” an operatic melodrama directed by James Gray that opens today, hardly feels like it belongs in a 21st century American multiplex. It’s a grandiose throwback to an era when movies dealt with big emotions, not big explosions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/t-magazine/16cotillard-barna/16cotillard-barna-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/16/t-magazine/16cotillard-barna/16cotillard-barna-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/t-magazine/16cotillard-barna/16cotillard-barna-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/t-magazine/16cotillard-barna/16cotillard-barna-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/t-magazine/16cotillard-barna/16cotillard-barna-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/16/t-magazine/16cotillard-barna/16cotillard-barna-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/t-magazine/16cotillard-barna/16cotillard-barna-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. | Marion Cotillard on Her New Role and the Pursuit of Happiness', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotillard, Marion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Immigrant (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T18:46:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Barna', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barna', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b5f233-ec4c-5d7b-a837-3691ee928d5d', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b5f233-e