 1315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5325772-b3a8-5179-bc0e-359cebcd6080'}, {'abstract': 'Timothy F. Geithner’s new book defending his role in the financial crisis is drawing out his detractors and defenders on both sides of the political aisle. A look back on our reporting of the past week’s highs and lows in finance.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/weekend-reading-the-hero-and-the-wall-st-puppet/', 'snippet': 'Timothy F. Geithner’s new book defending his role in the financial crisis is drawing out his detractors and defenders on both sides of the political aisle. A look back on our reporting of the past week’s highs and lows in finance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 4:23 p.m., Saturday | Timothy F. Geithner’s new book defending his role in the financial crisis is drawing out his detractors and defenders on both sides of the political aisle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-verse/dbpix-verse-jumbo.png', 'height': 515, 'width': 476, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-verse/dbpix-verse-superJumbo.png', 'height': 515, 'width': 476, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-verse/dbpix-verse-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-verse/dbpix-verse-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/business/dbpix-verse/dbpix-verse-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Reading: The Hero and the Wall St. Puppet', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T19:40:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Owles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Owles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28638dd7-3d2a-5e67-a43d-93f11bb37c24', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28638dd7-3d2a-5e67-a43d-93f11bb37c24'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees-Pirates game on Friday night was washed away, so now the teams will play an old-fashioned, single-admission doubleheader Sunday afternoon at Yankee Stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/17/sports/baseball/yankees-turn-the-clock-all-the-way-back.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees-Pirates game on Friday night was washed away, so now the teams will play an old-fashioned, single-admission doubleheader Sunday afternoon at Yankee Stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees and the Pittsburgh Pirates might as well wear throwback uniforms this weekend. The opener of their three-game series, scheduled for Friday night, was rained out, and now they are scheduled to play an afternoon game Saturday and an old-fashioned, single-admission doubleheader Sunday afternoon at Yankee Stadium.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rainout Puts Yanks in Old-Time 2-Game Set', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rainout Puts Yanks in Old-Time 2-Game Set', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Pirates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T19:47:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Plutnicki and Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Plutnicki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0dc1b25-474d-529e-b88c-e12b493cb34c', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0dc1b25-474d-529e-b88c-e12b493cb34c'}, {'abstract': 'In romance, it may not actually matter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/opinion/sunday/so-youre-not-desirable.html', 'snippet': 'In romance, it may not actually matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT is one of the hard truths of romance: Desirable people attract other desirable people, while the rest of us — lacking in attractiveness, charisma or success — settle for the best partner who is willing to consider our overtures. In the scientific literature, this idea is enshrined in the concept of mate value, which determines who gets to mate with whom. In popular culture, it is reflected in the choice of comely contestants to vie for the equally comely spouse-to-be on TV shows like “The Bachelor.” Pairing off, it seems, is just one more example that life isn’t fair. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/sunday-review/18GRAY/18GRAY-articleLarge.jpg