: 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b1680c0-ff11-5e24-ba1b-9e89c3b4a734'}, {'abstract': 'If you shoot you’d better hit your mark.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/friday-night-music-arcade-fire-joan-of-arc/', 'snippet': 'If you shoot you’d better hit your mark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Various stuff keeping me frantic, so not much time to seek out new music. But I keep finding new gems from the latest AF album — or actually from the live performances, especially the stripped-down versions, which I often prefer. In this case the final violin dissonance really does it …', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Arcade Fire, Joan of Arc', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T20:08:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9f02ba7-42e7-5cfc-b794-ea8f33a10af8', 'word_count': 51, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9f02ba7-42e7-5cfc-b794-ea8f33a10af8'}, {'abstract': 'The Affordable Care Act has become more popular, a prominent Republican pollster says, so expect Republicans to give up talk about repealing it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/17/upshot/why-gop-will-shift-to-talking-about-fixing-the-heath-care-law.html', 'snippet': 'The Affordable Care Act has become more popular, a prominent Republican pollster says, so expect Republicans to give up talk about repealing it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In response to polling data showing that the Affordable Care Act has become more popular, a prominent Republican pollster said that he expected Republicans to change how they talked about the law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why G.O.P. Will Shift to Talking About Fixing the Heath-Care Law', 'kicker': 'Pulse of the People', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T20:08:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45a5202f-557b-59bd-ab89-cc05012bdcf8', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45a5202f-557b-59bd-ab89-cc05012bdcf8'}, {'abstract': 'Baruch Lebovits, whose prosecution divided the ultra-Orthodox Jewish community in New York, received a two-year sentence in a molestation case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/17/nyregion/brooklyn-cantor-pleads-guilty-in-sexual-abuse-case.html', 'snippet': 'Baruch Lebovits, whose prosecution divided the ultra-Orthodox Jewish community in New York, received a two-year sentence in a molestation case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sexual abuse case that divided the ultra-Orthodox Jewish community in Brooklyn and created rifts in the borough’s district attorney’s office ended on Friday as a once-prominent cantor pleaded guilty to molestation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn Cantor Pleads Guilty in Sexual Abuse Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guilty Plea to Sex Abuse by a Cantor in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clifford, Stephanie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lebovits, Baruch', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hynes, Charles J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T20:11:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66cfce40-43b9-5e96-ba12-c4c3a2d41b41', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66cfce40-43b9-5e96-ba12-c4c3a2d41b41'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/the-gun-report-may-16-2014/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Carolinas, guns are allowed in bars. In Arkansas, you can take a gun into some churches and religious schools. In Indiana, you can keep a gun in your car on school property. In West Virginia, residents with concealed-carry permits can bring firearms into public recreation facilities such as tennis courts and swimming pools. Since the massacre in Newtown, 18 states have passed laws allowing guns in more places—but in only four states can you bring a gun into state legislative chambers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/opinion/open-carry/open-carry-articleLarge.png', 'height': 474, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/16/opinion/open-carry/open-carry-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 474}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/opinion/open-carry/open-carry-jumbo.png', 'height': 808, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/opinion/open-carry/open-carry-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1579, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/opinion/open-carry/open-carry-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/16/opinion/open-carry/open-carry-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/16/opinion/open-carry/open-carry-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: May 16, 2014', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T20:16:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abf78a3b-7278-547f-8bc9-565c5a37a588', 'word_count': 2528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abf78a3b-7278-547f-8bc9-565c5a37a588'}, {'abstract': 'At “Lightscapes,” a garden of more than 7,500 fantastical sculptures animated by light covers 10 acres on the grounds of Van Cortlandt Manor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/nyregion/brightening-the-night-with-a-spring-palette.html', 'snippet': 'At “Lightscapes,” a garden of more than 7,500 fantastical sculptures animated by light covers 10 acres on the grounds of Van Cortlandt Manor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walk beneath an animated rainbow, and then head through a tunnel of swirling fog. Meander past luminescent flowers, gigantic glowing mushrooms and a praying mantis towering more than 12 feet tall. Listen to the beat of a backdrop that blends natural noises with music. Welcome to “Lightscapes,” a fantastical garden of light, color and sound on the grounds of Van Cortlandt Manor.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18WESPOT/18WESPOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18WESPOT/18WESPOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18WESPOT/18WESPOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': No