ase every side. And when you try to please everyone, you often please no one.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/16/did-regulators-break-the-internet-or-did-they-save-it-yes/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Communications Commission’s proposal on network neutrality tries to please every side. And when you try to please everyone, you often please no one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years from now, we’ll look back on this week as the moment federal regulators broke the Internet as we know it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Did Regulators Break the Internet or Did They Save It? Yes.', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Net Neutrality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeler, Thomas E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T21:04:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farhad Manjoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farhad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manjoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19e1c849-87b8-5ae7-9828-9c58a3523748', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19e1c849-87b8-5ae7-9828-9c58a3523748'}, {'abstract': 'Women’s events aren’t just about consciousness-raising anymore. They’re a business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/fashion/how-womens-conferences-can-be-a-business.html', 'snippet': 'Women’s events aren’t just about consciousness-raising anymore. They’re a business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a month before Gloria Steinem’s 80th birthday, but on a Saturday evening in February, on the cliffs at a resort in Southern California, 500 women were helping her celebrate early. Ms. Steinem, the guest of honor, was flanked by her longtime friends Marlo Thomas and Jane Fonda. The three hugged, and then Ms. Thomas raised a glass. “To Gloria,” she said. “The absolutely perfect leader to our revolution.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/fashion/18CONFABS1/18CONFABS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/fashion/18CONFABS1/18CONFABS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/fashion/18CONFABS1/18CONFABS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/fashion/18CONFABS1/18CONFABS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1444, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/fashion/18CONFABS1/18CONFABS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/18/fashion/18CONFABS1/18CONFABS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/fashion/18CONFABS1/18CONFABS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feminism, One Conference at a Time