: 'nyt://article/9e34fe24-d24e-5a6b-9973-1286bc5944f3', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e34fe24-d24e-5a6b-9973-1286bc5944f3'}, {'abstract': '“The System,” Al Jazeera America’s new eight-part series, which begins Sunday night, examines criminal justice in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/17/arts/television/the-system-on-al-jazeera-america-examines-us-justice.html', 'snippet': '“The System,” Al Jazeera America’s new eight-part series, which begins Sunday night, examines criminal justice in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are several issues to consider regarding the premiere of “The System,” Joe Berlinger’s new eight-part series, which begins on Sunday night on Al Jazeera America. The most obvious and probably most pertinent is that the channel is trying to keep up with one of its cable news rivals: It’s bringing in a recognizable figure (Mr. Berlinger is known for feature documentaries like the “Paradise Lost” series about the West Memphis 3 case and “Metallica: Some Kind of Monster”) to do original documentary-style programming before CNN gets its new shows with Lisa Ling, Mike Rowe and John Walsh on the air. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'True Crime, With an Analytic Leaning', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'True Crime, With an Analytic Leaning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlinger, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The System with Joe Berlinger (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-16T21:15:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original'