 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/17/nyregion/17csection/17csection-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/17/nyregion/17csection/17csection-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mother Accuses Doctors of Forcing a C-Section and Files Suit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mother Accuses Doctors of Forcing a C-Section', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malpractice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caesarean Section', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Staten Island University Hospital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dray, Rinat', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-17T00:29:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95eee31a-8a19-5472-ad20-a1b8393fce2d', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95eee31a-8a19-5472-ad20-a1b8393fce2d'}, {'abstract': 'Negotiators for the government and the FARC guerrillas announced their pact, part of broader talks, just a week before a presidential election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/17/world/americas/colombia-and-rebels-agree-on-drug-fight.html', 'snippet': 'Negotiators for the government and the FARC guerrillas announced their pact, part of broader talks, just a week before a presidential election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — Negotiators for the Colombian government and the country’s largest guerrilla group said Friday that they had reached an agreement on ways to fight drug trafficking as part of broader talks aimed at ending five decades of war. The announcement came barely a week before a presidential election that could hinge on how voters view the peace talks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colombia and Rebels Agree on Drug Fight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colombia and Rebels Agree on Drug Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Liberation Army (Colombia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-17T00:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76741129-d752-5707-89bb-408716a12579', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76741129-d752-5707-89bb-408716a12579'}, {'abstract': 'The building on Jericho Turnpike in Syosset that houses Din Din, which has been an Asian restaurant for decades, has had a series of name changes recently.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/nyregion/a-review-of-din-din-in-syosset.html', 'snippet': 'The building on Jericho Turnpike in Syosset that houses Din Din, which has been an Asian restaurant for decades, has had a series of name changes recently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I announced, “We’re going to Din Din,” my dining companions responded, laughing, with baby talk. In fact, the name of the restaurant comes from the “Chinese baby name” of its owner, Sophia Kang, Ms. Kang told me on the telephone after my visits. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18DINELI2/18DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18DINELI2/18DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18DINELI2/18DINELI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18DINELI2/18DINELI2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1484, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18DINELI2/18DINELI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18DINELI2/18DINELI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/nyregion/18