e599920e52', 'word_count': 561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d484b42c-8096-5fc7-91b2-aee599920e52'}, {'abstract': 'A request for further study of a new federal rule on pay for home care workers should be denied.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/17/opinion/no-reason-to-delay-fair-wages.html', 'snippet': 'A request for further study of a new federal rule on pay for home care workers should be denied.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Come Jan. 1, 2015, a new federal rule will require that home care workers be paid at least the minimum wage and time and a half for overtime. This rule would undo an indefensible policy, dating from 1974, that denied home care workers basic labor protections by deeming them “companions” rather than employees. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Reason to Delay Fair Wages', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Reason to Delay Fair Wages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perez, Thomas E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Overtime', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Medicaid Directors', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-17T01:31:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b337e615-2ab5-5196-89e8-7e8351a692e0', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b337e615-2ab5-5196-89e8-7e8351a692e0'}, {'abstract': 'A new prepublication review policy would constrain the ability of officials to comment informally when issues are stirred by leaked information.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/17/opinion/the-slippery-slope-of-secrecy.html', 'snippet': 'A new prepublication review policy would constrain the ability of officials to comment informally when issues are stirred by leaked information.', 'lead_paragraph': '“If you want to keep a secret,” George Orwell advised in “1984,” “you must also hide it from yourself.” So the latest stricture seems to demand from the Office of the Director of National Intelligence, the federal uber-agency of all things secret. The office, which oversees 16 government intelligence agencies, issued a new policy in April that will seriously constrain the existing practice by which officials comment informally to the press and public when obvious issues are stirred by leaked information and unauthorized disclosures. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Slippery Slope of Secrecy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Slippery Slope of Secrecy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clapper, James R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Director of National Intelligence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-17T01:34:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_materia