e police uniform and carrying a gun, the police said. He demanded to see Khalil Ahmad, a member of the minority Ahmadi community who was being held at the station. Mr. Ahmad had been arrested Monday after a dispute with a Muslim shopkeeper escalated and the shopkeeper sought help from local clerics, who accused Mr. Ahmad and three other Ahmadis of blasphemy. When the boy was taken to the detainee’s cell, he shot Mr. Ahmad, who died instantly, the police said. The boy was arrested. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: Boy Kills a Jailed Man Who Was Accused of Blasphemy', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Boy Kills a Jailed Man Who Was Accused of Blasphemy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-17T02:16:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Waqar Gillani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Waqar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/20ea6b2b-83b2-56b3-8587-9e4f1dedf353', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20ea6b2b-83b2-56b3-8587-9e4f1dedf353'}, {'abstract': 'A bizarre cargo of more than 80 exotic reptiles, including four horned vipers and an iguana, attracted the attention of an alert customs official at Frankfurt Airport this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/17/world/europe/germany-the-flight-of-the-iguana.html', 'snippet': 'A bizarre cargo of more than 80 exotic reptiles, including four horned vipers and an iguana, attracted the attention of an alert customs official at Frankfurt Airport this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bizarre cargo of more than 80 exotic reptiles, including four horned vipers and an iguana, attracted the attention of an alert customs official at Frankfurt Airport this week. During a routine inspection of luggage in transit, the official found 50 turtles, 30 arboreal alligator lizards, the snakes and the iguana in one suitcase. Several reptiles were stuffed into cloth bags or boxes, and the snakes were entangled in women’s stockings, said Hans-Jürgen Schmidt, a customs spokesman. The owner of the bag, traveling from Mexico City to Barcelona, was detained Tuesday before boarding his flight to Spain, Mr. Schmidt said. The passenger, a 44-year-old Mexican, who cannot be named under German privacy laws, is under investigation to determine whether he violated laws on the protection of endangered species and the treatment of animals. Three turtles have died, and most of the reptiles, which have been moved to the Frankfurt zoo, were in bad shape, Mr. Schmidt said. The potential sale value of the cargo was as much as $82,000, he said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: The Flight of the Iguana', 'kicker': 'World Briefing ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany: The Flight of the Iguana', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reptiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luggage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-17T02:18:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_na