r me. You don’t forget when a government opens fire at the crowd you’re in. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiananmen, 25 Years Later', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-17T09:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a16f7e89-75a9-542a-b062-7db20d4ab2b4', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a16f7e89-75a9-542a-b062-7db20d4ab2b4'}, {'abstract': 'The death toll in Turkey’s worst mining accident rose to 301 people, as final recovery efforts were hampered by a fire and a gas leak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/world/europe/soma-turkey-mine-explosion.html', 'snippet': 'The death toll in Turkey’s worst mining accident rose to 301 people, as final recovery efforts were hampered by a fire and a gas leak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOMA, Turkey — Rescue workers removed the last remaining bodies from a stricken mine here on Saturday afternoon as the death toll in Turkey’s worst mining accident rose to 301 people, according to the prime minister’s office.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/world/SUB-TURKEY-1/SUB-TURKEY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/world/SUB-TURKEY-1/SUB-TURKEY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None