e': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c4b6cab-5c25-571d-908b-1c8d50335396', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c4b6cab-5c25-571d-908b-1c8d50335396'}, {'abstract': 'New products aim to remove the obstacles to reading and writing effectively on tablet computers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/business/tackling-the-limits-of-touch-screens.html', 'snippet': 'New products aim to remove the obstacles to reading and writing effectively on tablet computers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Touch screens are ubiquitous on tablets and smartphones, but their flat glass surfaces can hinder close reading and accurate typing. People flipping through electronic pages often retain less of what they read than on printed ones, studies suggest. And typing on a flat surface with no physical keys to guide the fingers requires heightened visual attention to avoid typos, draining concentration from the thoughts being expressed.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/business/18-NOVEL-1/18-NOVEL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/business/18-NOVEL-1/18-NOVEL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 643}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/business/18-NOVEL-1/18-NOVEL-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 956, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/business/18-NOVEL-1/18-NOVEL-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1979, 'width': 1847, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype