-5da6-a173-ac2abcf8ed55'}, {'abstract': 'It turns out every building has its own magnetic “fingerprint,” and you can figure out what it looks like with the compass of an iPhone. Merge that information with public maps, and we may see a movement to make all our spaces as public as roads. Think Yelp reviews of your couch.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/mapping-our-interiors/', 'snippet': 'It turns out every building has its own magnetic “fingerprint,” and you can figure out what it looks like with the compass of an iPhone. Merge that information with public maps, and we may see a movement to make all our spaces as public as roads. ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sure, that’s your office cubicle. Your corner store. Maybe even the layout of your furniture in your living room. But that doesn’t mean that soon we won’t all be peering at it, too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/17/technology/17bits-atlasmagnetic/17bits-atlasmagnetic-articleLarge.png', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/17/technology/17bits-atlasmagnetic/17bits-atlasmagnetic-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/17/technology/17bits-atlasmagnetic/17bits-atlasmagnetic-jumbo.png', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/17/technology/17bits-atlasmagnetic/17bits-atlasmagnetic-superJumbo.png', 'height': 918, 'width': 1497, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/17/technology/17bi