anielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'IVORY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/27e0674f-c116-57c2-86c0-73e62cb55b16', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/27e0674f-c116-57c2-86c0-73e62cb55b16'}, {'abstract': 'Day in and day out, the long-term unemployed are coping with upended lives, struggling to squeeze back into a work force that has squeezed them out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/nyregion/still-working-to-find-a-job.html', 'snippet': 'Day in and day out, the long-term unemployed are coping with upended lives, struggling to squeeze back into a work force that has squeezed them out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every night, Sharon Cabelly power-pedals on the exercise bicycle in her bedroom, clearing her head of any angst or anxiety. Then, before bed, she recites her favorite psalms, praying first for others in need and finally for her own peace of mind.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/nyregion/19working-web/19working-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/19/nyregion/19working-web/19working-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/nyregion/19working-web/19working-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/nyregion/19working-web/19working-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJum