 theaters, good for No. 1 at the box office.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/18/a-big-godzilla-has-a-big-weekend/', 'snippet': 'This remake took in an estimated $93.2 million in tickets at North American theaters, good for No. 1 at the box office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fatty? Oh, yes. A remake of “Godzilla” took in an estimated $93.2 million in tickets at North American theaters over the weekend, a huge No. 1 total that left this version of the radioactive lizard – mocked online in recent weeks for being too chubby – with the last laugh. (Or at least roar.) “Godzilla,” powered in part by strong Imax and 3-D screenings, cost a reported $195 million to make, with tax credits bringing the net cost closer to $160 million. Legendary Pictures and Warner Brothers collaborated on the picture, but Legendary put up 75 percent of the budget and will thus reap an outsize share of the profits.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/movies/18godzilla/18godzilla-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/18/movies/18godzilla/18godzilla-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 250}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/movies/18godzilla/18godzilla-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/movies/18godzilla/18godzilla-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 854, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/movies/18godzilla/18godzilla-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/18/movies/18godzilla/18godzilla-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/18/movies/18godzilla/18godzilla-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Big ‘Godzilla’ Has a Big Weekend', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Godzilla’ Goes on a Rampage in Its Opening Weekend', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamm, Jon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-18T16:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b62bc3ad-16c2-554c-ba26-348224abb2b0', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b62bc3ad-16c2-554c-ba26-348224abb2b0'}, {'abstract': 'The Kentucky Derby and Preakness winner is unbeaten while wearing a nasal strip, but the New York stewards disallowed the breathing aid for a previous Triple Crown contender.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/sports/california-chrome-could-skip-belmont-over-equipment-ruling.html', 'snippet': 'The Kentucky Derby and Preakness winner is unbeaten while wearing a nasal strip, but the New York stewards disallowed the breathing aid for a previous Triple Crown contender.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — Would the owners of California Chrome scrap a historic Triple Crown bid over an equ