 widespread adoption of popular concepts like “minimum viable products,” “data-driven decisions” and “failing fast.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When ‘Going Lean’ Goes Wrong', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newsletters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Robert J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RJMetrics Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-18T19:32:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert J. Moore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81f088fc-89db-51bf-9ad1-4ea444c33830', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81f088fc-89db-51bf-9ad1-4ea444c33830'}, {'abstract': 'Reince Priebus said that the questions were valid in any presidential campaign by Mrs. Clinton.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/us/politics/gop-chairman-says-clintons-health-and-age-are-fair-issues.html', 'snippet': 'Reince Priebus said that the questions were valid in any presidential campaign by Mrs. Clinton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Reince Priebus, the chairman of the Republican National Committee, insisted on Sunday that Hillary Rodham Clinton’s health and age were fair targets for inquiry ahead of a possible 2016 presidential run, as both he and Karl Rove, the Republican strategist who injected those questions into the debate, suggested that such scrutiny might dissuade her from running.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Chairman Says Clinton’s Health and Age Are Fair Issues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Priebus, Reince R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Meet the Press (TV Program)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-18T19:49:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Knowlton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knowlton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13718a2d-1242-5ca4-bfff-99a57585580a', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13718a2d-1242-5ca4-bfff-99a57585580a'}, {'abstract': 'Jérôme Kerviel resumed his pilgrimage from Rome late Sunday, ahead of a midnight deadline for him to turn himself in to the French authorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/business/international/convicte