 more slowly, researchers in two studies reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time, researchers have found drugs that can slow the decline of people with a fatal lung disease, idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drugs Found to Aid Breathing in a Fatal Lung Disease', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Disease That’s Fatal, 2 Drugs Help Lungs Cope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Idiopathic Pulmonary Fibrosis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grady, Denise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'InterMune Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boehringer Ingelheim GmbH', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-18T21:27:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8919bdf7-6145-5502-b2ef-0c7908ed1ef4', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8919bdf7-6145-5502-b2ef-0c7908ed1ef4'}, {'abstract': 'J. R. R. Tolkien’s translation of “Beowulf” is being published on Thursday, 88 years after its making.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/books/jrr-tolkiens-translation-of-beowulf-is-published.html', 'snippet': 'J. R. R. Tolkien’s translation of “Beowulf” is being published on Thursday, 88 years after its making.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s more to J. R. R. Tolkien than wizards and hobbits. The author of “The Lord of the Rings” and “The Hobbit” was also an Oxford University professor specializing in languages like Old Norse and Old English. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/jptolkien/jptolkien-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/jptolkien/jptolkien-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 780}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/jptolkien/jptolkien-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/jptolkien/jptolkien-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1575, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/jptolkien/jptolkien-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/jptolkien/jptolkien-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/jptolkien/jptolkien-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waving His Wand at ‘Beowulf’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Waving His Wand at ‘Beowulf’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilsdorf, Ethan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolkien, J R R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Beowulf (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Translation and Interpreters', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-18T21:28:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Gilsdorf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilsdorf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdf4b50a-f5b1-5c0c-8ea0-50656520e8f6', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdf4b50a-f5b1-5c0c-8ea0-50656520e8f6'}, {'abstract': 'Denis R. McDonough said that the president has ordered a check of whether reforms are needed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/us/politics/obama-angry-over-falsification-of-veterans-affairs-data-chief-of-staff-says.html', 'snippet': 'Denis R. McDonough said that the president has ordered a check of whether reforms are needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama is “madder than hell” about reports that some medical facilities run by the Department of Veterans Affairs have falsified data to hide substantial delays for veterans to see doctors, and he has demanded that the department’s leaders “fix these things,” the White House chief of staff said in an interview aired Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Angry Over Falsification of Veterans Affairs Data, Chief of Staff Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonough, Denis R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-18T21:32:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Knowlton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knowlton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5648f2a4-4d92-522f-9aec-0b5d80f5b58c', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5648f2a4-4d92-522f-9aec-0b5d80f5b58c'}, {'abstract': 'In Emmanuelle Huynh’s “A Vida Enorme/épisode 1,” disembodied voices, male and female, converse in Portuguese and French; the couple appears later, shirtless, in a restive dance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/arts/dance/emmanuelle-huynh-presents-sensuous-show-at-st-marks-church.html', 'snippet': 'In Emmanuelle Huynh’s “A Vida Enorme/épisode 1,” disembodied voices, male and female, converse in Portuguese and French; the couple appears later, shirtless, in a restive dance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you don’t speak Portuguese or French, it’s hard to understand, in the conventional sense, the first half of Emmanuelle Huynh’s “A Vida Enorme/épisode 1.” For about 20 minutes, two disembodied voices, male and female, converse in those voluptuous languages, broadcast from a stack of speakers in the middle of the otherwise empty space. The only activity happens in the form of light, which slowly fades and intensifies, singling out features of the sanctuary at St. Mark’s Church. The program contains English translations of the text, by the Portuguese poet Herberto Hélder, but how necessary are these? The sensuousness of the voices, their texture, say a lot in themselves. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First, Voices, Then Bodies', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First, Voices, Then Bodies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huynh, Emmanuelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-18T21:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/72af4415-91f4-51be-bcf8-8247421e3363', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72af4415-91f4-51be-bcf8-8247421e3363'}, {'abstract': 'Big retailers are set to report their earnings for the start of the year, and the Fed will release minutes of its last meeting, offering clues to policy makers’ goals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/business/economic-reports-for-the-week-of-may-19.html', 'snippet': 'Big retailers are set to report their earnings for the start of the year, and the Fed will release minutes of its last meeting, offering clues to policy makers’ goals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MAJOR RETAILERS SET TO REPORT EARNINGS', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports for the Week of May 19', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Week Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Target Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sears Holdings Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Best BUY Company Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-18T21:38:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa22e7a7-8462-56ac-b723-92ef531e2173', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa22e7a7-8462-56ac-b723-92ef531e2173'}, {'abstract': 'The city of North Miami and the board of the Museum of Contemporary Art there cannot agree on the museum’s future, leaving it in limbo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/arts/design/north-miami-fights-to-keep-its-art-museum.html', 'snippet': 'The city of North Miami and the board of the Museum of Contemporary Art there cannot agree on the museum’s future, leaving it in limbo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NORTH MIAMI, Fla. — Anyone looking to meet the director of the tiny but highly regarded Museum of Contemporary Art here has two choices. Head into the museum, where its interim director, Alex Gartenfeld, has an office. Or go next door to City Hall, where the city manager’s appointee to the same position, Babacar M’Bow, is essentially working in exile.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/jpfeud1/jpfeud1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/jpfeud1/jpfeud1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/jpfeud1/jpfeud1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {