 'nyt://article/7ab70d94-f45f-5c65-a598-a0ee6a327732'}, {'abstract': '“Red Army,” the story of the dominant Soviet hockey team of the 1970s and 1980s, is among the notable contenders at the Cannes Film Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/movies/red-army-is-among-the-notables-at-festival.html', 'snippet': '“Red Army,” the story of the dominant Soviet hockey team of the 1970s and 1980s, is among the notable contenders at the Cannes Film Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES, France — “Gabe! Gabe!” Slava Fetisov, the former ice hockey god, was yelling across the sun-splashed courtyard at the director Gabe Polsky. A loud mechanical noise had begun whirring near Mr. Fetisov as he was being interviewed about “Red Army,” Mr. Polsky’s documentary about the rise and fall of Soviet hockey that is playing at the Cannes Film Festival. Mr. Fetisov — who helped lead the Soviet team to two Olympic gold medals and one silver as well as seven world championships in the 1970s and ’80s — wanted his director to deal with it. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/cannes1/cannes1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/cannes1/cannes1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/cannes1/cannes1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/cannes1/cannes1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1075, 'width': 1482, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/cannes1/cannes1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/cannes1/cannes1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/cannes1/cannes1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spotted at Cannes: Ice to Go With Steam', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spotted at Cannes: Ice to Go With Steam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Red Army (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fetisov, Slava', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polsky, Gabe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-18T21:49:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df8bcfc6-25cc-5fe6-b3a6-8f5f1364be42', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df8bcfc6-25cc-5fe6-b3a6-8f5f1364be42'}, {'abstract': 'City Ballet’s season is studded with debuts and revelations from younger dancers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/arts/dance/debuts-at-new-york-city-ballet.html', 'snippet': 'City Ballet’s season is studded with debuts and revelations from younger dancers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dancing of New York City Ballet this spring has abounded in debuts and revelations. The illustrious Sara Mearns has reached new heights of eloquence. At two performances over the weekend she finally conquered the lofty ballerina role of the adagio second movement of George Balanchine’s “Symphony in C.” It’s a part she’s danced for years, but with a certain tension that has held her back. This time, partnered superlatively by Jared Angle (making his debut in this part), she demonstrated a tragic glamour and courage that bound everyone in her spell. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/nycb/nycb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/nycb/nycb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/nycb/nycb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/nycb/nycb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/nycb/nycb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/19/arts/nycb/nycb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 