ers killed a man in a Brooklyn apartment on Sunday, the police said, after he lunged at the officers with a pair of scissors.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Police Officers Shoot and Kill a Brooklyn Man', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Police Officers Shoot and Kill a Brooklyn Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flatbush (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osbourne, Broadie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T12:54:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9523184-07af-5784-b3a6-7334c0097f5a', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9523184-07af-5784-b3a6-7334c0097f5a'}, {'abstract': 'Hyon Song-wol was reported to be a former girlfriend of the country’s leader, Kim Jong-un.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/world/asia/north-korean-performer-reported-executed-appears-on-television.html', 'snippet': 'Hyon Song-wol was reported to be a former girlfriend of the country’s leader, Kim Jong-un.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — Hyon Song-wol is not quite North Korea’s version of Beyoncé. But as a popular singer and leader of the nation’s best-known girl band, which often performs in miniskirts, she attracts plenty of attention. Last Friday, millions watched on national television as she saluted the country’s leader, Kim Jong-un, for his “heavenly trust and warm care” in promoting the arts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/world/NORTH/NORTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/20/world/NORTH/NORTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/world/NORTH/NORTH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/world/NORTH/NORTH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 906, 'width': 1879, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/world/NORTH/NORTH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/20/world/NORTH/NORTH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/world/NORTH/NORTH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cheating Death, and the Rumor Mill, in North Korea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cheating Death, and Rumor Mill, in North Korea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Intelligence Service (South Korea)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ri Sol-ju', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hyon Song-wol', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T13:24:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9efc5a12-692e-5e4b-ba77-9ce8f5bd8cc8', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9efc5a12-692e-5e4b-ba77-9ce8f5bd8cc8'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Lyman, who is moving to Warsaw to reopen the Times’s bureau in Central and Eastern Europe, is finding the city a treat and the language a test.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/05/19/the-education-of-a-foreign-correspondent/', 'snippet': 'Rick Lyman, who is moving to Warsaw to reopen the Times’s bureau in Central and Eastern Europe, is finding the city a treat and the language a test.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rick Lyman, who has been a reporter and editor at The Times since 1997, is reopening its bureau in Central and Eastern Europe. He will be based in Warsaw and responsible for covering more than a dozen nations in the region, from Estonia and the other Baltic States down to Slovenia on the Italian border. A former international correspondent, based in South Africa, he has most recently been a national correspondent based in New York, but has previously been an editor, a political correspondent and the Houston bureau chief and covered both the movie industry in Los Angeles and the theater in New York. We asked him about his approach to his new beat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/warsaw/warsaw-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/warsaw/warsaw-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/warsaw/warsaw-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/warsaw/warsaw-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/warsaw/warsaw-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/warsaw/warsaw-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/15/blogs/warsaw/warsaw-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Education of a Foreign Correspondent', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', '