rchitecture on Apiece Apart’s worth-bookmarking blog\xa0and in their seasonal printed zine — with better things to do than fret about what to throw on in the morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/t-magazine/19apiece-hartman/19apiece-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/19/t-magazine/19apiece-hartman/19apiece-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/t-magazine/19apiece-hartman/19apiece-hartman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/t-magazine/19apiece-hartman/19apiece-hartman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/t-magazine/19apiece-hartman/19apiece-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/19/t-magazine/19apiece-hartman/19apiece-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/t-magazine/19apiece-hartman/19apiece-hartman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apiece Apart Debuts With J. Crew', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T14:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ff60d51-8fb1-5801-873f-4e63d1b9d745', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ff60d51-8fb1-5801-873f-4e63d1b9d745'}, {'abstract': 'The X refers to an extra-fast, higher-capacity version of LTE available on about half of Verizon’s network, including in New York and Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/verizon-wireless-names-faster-part-of-its-network-xlte/', 'snippet': 'The X refers to an extra-fast, higher-capacity version of LTE available on about half of Verizon’s network, including in New York and Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Data-guzzling smartphones and tablets are so ubiquitous that even Verizon Wireless, the No. 1 American phone carrier, was getting crushed by network traffic\xa0last year in big cities like New York. The company now says it has fixed its network in problematic areas, and this week it is introducing an advertising campaign to make consumers aware of improved portions of its network.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/business/19bits-verizon/19bits-verizon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/19/business/19bits-verizon/19bits-verizon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/business/19bits-verizon/19bits-verizon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'sub