e': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T16:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c08afafc-9482-5eaf-b6a8-3d834b213729', 'word_count': 1457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c08afafc-9482-5eaf-b6a8-3d834b213729'}, {'abstract': 'A group of American creative talents, including Pharrell Williams, Kelly Wearstler and Rafael de Cárdenas, created their own versions of the iconic Bourgie table lamp, which are on view at the Italian design brand’s SoHo store this week.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/kartell-icff-pharrell-williams-kelly-wearstler-rafael-de-cardenas-snarkitecture-assume-vivid-astro-focus/', 'snippet': 'A group of American creative talents, including Pharrell Williams, Kelly Wearstler and Rafael de Cárdenas, created their own versions of the iconic Bourgie table lamp, which are on view at the Italian design brand’s SoHo store this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After 65 years producing plastic furniture, lighting and accessories, it’s safe to say that the Italian company Kartell knows a thing or two about how to elevate the utilitarian material into fashionable design. The trick? Balancing plastic’s cold and industrial characteristics with familiar, classic silhouettes. Philippe Starck’s Ghost chairs for the brand — shaped in the style of French Louis XVI — have reportedly sold over 1.5 million units. Another historically inspired icon, Ferruccio Laviani’s Bourgie table lamp featuring a baroque base and a corrugated shade, celebrates 10 years in production this year. It has also been a best seller in transparent, colored and metallic versions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Kartell, There’s Still a Great Future in Plastics', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Cardenas, Rafael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kravitz, Lenny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kartell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T16:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Rubinstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubinstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06094ea3-d5d9-5463-aac4-1d97d496c8dd', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06094ea3-d5d9-5463-aac4-1d97d496c8dd'}, {'abstract': 'Jonathan Martin, The Times’s national political correspondent on Senate minority leader, Mitch McConnell’s challenge in Kentucky’s Tuesday G.O.P. primary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000002888859/times-minute-kentucky8217s-primary-day.html', 'snippet': 'Jonathan Martin, The Times’s national political correspondent on Senate minority leader, Mitch McConnell’s challenge in Kentucky’s Tuesday G.O.P. primary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Martin, The Times’s national political correspondent on Senate minority leader, Mitch McConnell’s challenge in Kentucky’s Tuesday G.O.P. primary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/multimedia/nytm-051914-noon/nytm-051914-noon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/19/multimedia/nytm-051914-noon/nytm-0519