 among the reasons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/upshot/asian-americans-have-had-the-sharpest-shift-toward-democrats.html', 'snippet': 'A new Gallup study cites religion, immigration policy and President Obama as among the reasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Asian-Americans make up the racial or ethnic group that has shifted most strongly toward the Democratic Party since 2000. They are also the country’s fastest-growing racial or ethnic group by percentage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asian-Americans Have Had the Sharpest Shift Toward Democrats', 'kicker': 'A Survey Says', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T17:14:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Megan Thee-Brenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thee-Brenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6614aef-e87e-5136-a4b8-1345c6fe5048', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6614aef-e87e-5136-a4b8-1345c6fe5048'}, {'abstract': 'Would Rubio’s emerging policy agenda take the G.O.P. back to Bushism?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/marco-rubio-as-george-w-bush/', 'snippet': 'Would Rubio’s emerging policy agenda take the G.O.P. back to Bushism?', 'lead_paragraph': 'While Rand Paul has been trying to map out a heretofore-uncharted path to the presidency, his potential rival Marco Rubio has been playing more of an inside game, delivering a series of policy speeches — on poverty, on higher education, and most recently on entitlement reform\xa0— that make him seem more presidential to the kind of Washingtonian “thought leaders” (those are ironic quotation marks, people) who care about such things.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marco Rubio As George W. Bush', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T17:27:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/011743f6-4334-5a2b-b217-63cce59466ac', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/011743f6-4334-5a2b-b217-63cce59466ac'}, {'abstract': 'Jill Abramson, the former executive editor of The New York Times, made her first public appearance since her 