', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e73015b-4965-5739-841c-9f909182cfc4', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e73015b-4965-5739-841c-9f909182cfc4'}, {'abstract': 'For some of us, the apparent perfect symmetry of nature suggests an inventor. But evolution is messier and more roughshod than our own machines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/science/creation-in-the-eye-of-the-beholder.html', 'snippet': 'For some of us, the apparent perfect symmetry of nature suggests an inventor. But evolution is messier and more roughshod than our own machines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I remember the chill I felt, 27 years ago, when I picked up the latest edition of Scientific American magazine. Pictured on the cover was an object of unnerving beauty — a cutaway of a perfect blue sphere meticulously assembled from tiny identical parts and studded around the circumference with precisely placed green antennas. Inside this flawlessly honed outer shell was a smaller inner sphere, reddish tan in color, and suspended at its center was an ivory capsule, built from hundreds of still tinier spheres.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/science/20JOHN/20JOHN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/20/science/20JOHN/20JOHN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 708}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/science/20JOHN/20JOHN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 868, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/science/20JOHN/20JOHN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 1203, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/science/20JOHN/20JOHN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/20/science/20JOHN/20JOHN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/science/20JOHN/20JOHN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Creation, in the Eye of the Beholder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Creation, in the Eye of the Beholder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, George', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution (Biology)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paley, William (1743-1805)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T19:34:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c851d8f-7af1-5fbb-96f0-8b7488f2a8bb', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c851d8f-7af1-5fbb-96f0-8b7488f2a8bb'}, {'abstract': 'Officials fear that some soccer fans will carry dengue fever, now an epidemic in Brazil, back to their home countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/health/with-world-cup-in-brazil-risk-of-spreading-a-virus.html', 'snippet': 'Officials fear that some soccer fans will carry dengue fever, now an epidemic in Brazil, back to their home countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Public health authorities are worried about a confluence of events set to happen soon: Brazil is suffering the world’s worst epidemic of dengue fever, with 1.4 million cases last year. And the country is about to play host to the World Cup, which attracts tourists by the millions. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With World Cup in Brazil, Risk of Spreading a Virus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With World Cup in Brazil, Risk of Spreading a Virus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dengue Fever', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T19:34:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f6a9aa9-2fa5-5628-b685-657affce7514', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f6a9aa9-2fa5-5628-b685-657affce7514'}, {'abstract': 'Following a gift of Cubist artworks valued at more than $1 billion, the Metropolitan Museum of Art is looking to improve its layout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/arts/design/in-mets-future-a-redesigned-modern-art-wing.html', 'snippet': 'Following a gift of Cubist artworks valued at more than $1 billion, the Metropolitan Museum of Art is looking to improve its layout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art is planning to rebuild its wing for Modern and contemporary art — possibly from scratch — to create new, showcase galleries for its expanded collection from those periods, Met officials have confirmed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20MET2/20MET2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20MET2/20MET2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20MET2/20MET2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20MET2/20MET2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1377, 'width': 1963, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20MET2/20MET2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20MET2/20MET2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20MET2/20MET2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width'