ytimes.com/2014/05/19/exploring-the-social-and-environmental-challenges-as-brazil-prepares-for-two-sports-spectacles/', 'snippet': 'A short film explores Brazil’s struggle over the impacts of back-to-back mega-sports events: this year’s World Cup and the 2016 Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the fourth year in a row, a team of graduate and undergraduate communication students at Pace University has created a compelling short documentary focused on efforts to mesh human progress with the environment. (I admit a bias here, given that I co-teach the documentary course that produces these films with Pace Prof. Maria Luskay.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/blogs/dotpacedallas/dotpacedallas-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 573, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/blogs/dotpacedallas/dotpacedallas-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 573, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/blogs/dotpacedallas/dotpacedallas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/19/blogs/dotpacedallas/dotpacedallas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/19/blogs/dotpacedallas/dotpacedallas-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sewage in Rio Waters and Other Challenges as Brazil Prepares for Sports Spectacles', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2016)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sewers and Sewage', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pace University', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South America', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T20:26:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0341938f-62b7-5392-b794-c9227cb9aff2', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0341938f-62b7-5392-b794-c9227cb9aff2'}, {'abstract': 'Prevention and maintenance are keys for illnesses like asthma, but higher levels of cost-sharing cause people to delay or avoid treatment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/upshot/why-patients-with-chronic-illnesses-should-pay-less.html', 'snippet': 'Prevention and maintenance are keys for illnesses like asthma, but higher levels of cost-sharing cause people to delay or avoid treatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most health care plans ask that you spend some money out of your pocket whenever you use the health care system. This is known as cost-sharing, and it exists because research has shown us that people are, in general, less likely to spend their own money than someone else’s. Cost-sharing works its way into insurance today through co-pays, deductibles and co-insurance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/upshot/20UP-Costsharing-copy/20UP-Costsharing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/20/upshot/20UP-Costsharing-copy/20UP-Costsharing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/upshot/20UP-Costsharing-copy/20UP-Costsharing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/upshot/20UP-Costsharing-copy/20UP-Costsharing-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/upshot/20UP-Costsharing-copy/20UP-Costsharing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/20/upshot/20UP-Costsharing-copy/20UP-Costsharing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/upshot/20UP-Costsharing-copy/20UP-Costsharing-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'People With Chronic Illness Fare Worse Under Cost-Sharing', 'kicker': 'The New Health Care', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "State Children's Health Insurance Program (S-CHIP)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JAMA Pediatrics (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T20:28:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron E. Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7573be42-e77d-52e1-a403-ef475909f7e1', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7573be42-e77d-52e1-a403-ef475909f7e1'}, {'abstract': 'Shortstop Lennie Merullo, 97, who has been invited back to Wrigley Field to be honored in June, is the only person alive to have worn a Cubs uniform in a World Series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/sports/baseball/cubs-last-link-to-world-series-is-still-proud-of-his-scars.html', 'snippet': 'Shortstop Lennie Merullo, 97, who has been invited back to Wrigley Field to be honored in June, is the only person alive to have worn a Cubs uniform in a World Series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'READING, M