: 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Denk, Jeremy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozart, Wolfgang Amadeus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T20:36:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Erik Braund and Ashley Maas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Braund', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f57f4ddd-f5f2-52b4-bd55-80ddc77eb0f1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f57f4ddd-f5f2-52b4-bd55-80ddc77eb0f1'}, {'abstract': 'On Saturday, the Tribeca New Music Festival presented an evening of polished pop that featured the soprano Mellissa Hughes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/arts/music/poetry-in-motion-a-tribeca-new-music-concert-at-the-cell.html', 'snippet': 'On Saturday, the Tribeca New Music Festival presented an evening of polished pop that featured the soprano Mellissa Hughes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tribeca New Music Festival is one of the most clearly defined brands in New York’s teeming new-music scene. The festival’s preferred label is “avant pop,” defined as the merging of pop culture taste and classically honed craft. Saturday’s “Poetry in Motion,” an evening of new vocal music presented as part of a five-concert series at the Cell in Chelsea, was in many ways a typical sample. The songs by Andrew Norman, Christopher Cerrone, Jacob Cooper, Eric Shanfield and Ted Hearne were compact, direct and elegant; the soprano Mellissa Hughes performed them with grace and razor-sharp emotional acuity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subt