': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/85097525-d5dd-5577-b33a-2babcbfa02f5', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85097525-d5dd-5577-b33a-2babcbfa02f5'}, {'abstract': 'The Swiss bank, which has large investment banking operations in New York, will also pay about $2.6 billion in penalties and hire an independent monitor for up to two years.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/credit-suisse-set-to-plead-guilty-in-tax-evasion-case/', 'snippet': 'The Swiss bank, which has large investment banking operations in New York, will also pay about $2.6 billion in penalties and hire an independent monitor for up to two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 10:12 p.m. | Credit Suisse has done what no other bank of its size and significance has done in over two decades: plead guilty to criminal wrongdoing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Credit Suisse Pleads Guilty in Felony Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Swiss Bank Pleads Guilty in Felony Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawsky, Benjamin M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BNP Paribas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Credit Suisse Group AG', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'o