aptured the city’s vogue for old-time music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/arts/music/new-york-hot-jazz-festival-takes-over-players-club.html', 'snippet': 'Sunday’s New York Hot Jazz Festival captured the city’s vogue for old-time music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few minutes before midnight on Sunday night, Bria Skonberg was onstage in the ballroom at the Players club, trumpet aloft, playing a punchy solo on the 1930s novelty tune “I’ll Be Glad When You’re Dead, You Rascal You.” Two rooms over, in a parlor overlooking Gramercy Park, the ragtime piano specialist Dalton Ridenhour and the clarinetist Dennis Lichtman were leading an old-time jam. In both rooms, and in a library upstairs, well-turned-out young couples danced among the crowd. It was about 11 hours into the second New York Hot Jazz Festival, and the energy was far from flagging.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Young, Fresh Crowd Comes Out Bouncing', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Young, Fresh Crowd Comes Out Bouncing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-19T21:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdb5e3fd-c6d6-5f13-90a2-743944512cde', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdb5e3fd-c6d6-5f13-90a2-743944512cde'}, {'abstract': 'Letters to the editor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.