 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/078990c7-9195-5f30-8f48-64bdd7508952'}, {'abstract': 'Many employers say they offer telecommuting and flexible work hours to employees, but in fact are cutting back on time for child leave or to care for an ill parent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/business/for-workers-less-flexible-companies.html', 'snippet': 'Many employers say they offer telecommuting and flexible work hours to employees, but in fact are cutting back on time for child leave or to care for an ill parent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He calls it one of the bright spots of his week: Before Jared Dalton, 32, starts his workday as a manager at Ernst & Young, the big accounting firm, he dresses his 5-month-old daughter, Olivia, and then places her on her tummy to play. Since he works from home on Mondays and Tuesdays, he can spend an extra hour with Olivia and an extra hour working — time that would otherwise be lost commuting into Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/FLEX/FLEX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/20/business/FLEX/FLEX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/FLEX/FLEX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/FLEX/FLEX-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/FLEX/FLEX-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/20/business/FLEX/FLEX-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/FLEX/FLEX-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Workers, Less Flexible Companies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Workers, Less Flexible Companies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernard, Tara Siegel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telecommuting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T00:22:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c49e212e-92c5-5e89-b418-2d606f4a2617', 'word_count': 1315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c49e212e-92c5-5e89-b418-2d606f4a2617'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets’ pitchers collectively went 0 for 64 at the plate to start the season, setting a modern record and stirring talk of extending the designated hitter rule to the National League.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/sports/baseball/now-not-batting-for-the-mets-a-sorely-needed-designated-hitter.html', 'snippet': 'The Mets’ pitchers collectively went 0 for 64 at the plate to start the season, setting a modern record and stirring talk of extending the designated hitter rule to the National League.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mets’ Bartolo Colon swung and missed, his body twisting so violently that his helmet fell off and he nearly toppled over. He sheepishly fetched his headgear from the dirt a few feet away, and then he returned to the batter’s box to take another hack. He feebly struck out swinging to end the embarrassment. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/sports/Y-METS/Y-METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/20/sports/Y-METS/Y-METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/sports/Y-METS/Y-METS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/sports/Y-METS/Y-METS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 999, 'width': 1499, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/sports/Y-METS/Y-METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/20/sports/Y-METS/Y-METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/sports/Y-METS/Y-METS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Not Batting for the Mets, a Sorely Needed Designa