’s visitors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/business/media/miami-area-hotel-brings-its-past-to-forefront.html', 'snippet': 'Print ads in a $1 million campaign link the Biltmore’s historic past and illustrious guests to today’s visitors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE BILTMORE, an upscale resort in Coral Gables, Fla., is running its first ad campaign in 10 years to attract guests from the United States and overseas.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/ADCO/ADCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/20/business/ADCO/ADCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 689}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/ADCO/ADCO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 892, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/ADCO/ADCO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1766, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/ADCO/ADCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/20/business/ADCO/ADCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/ADCO/ADCO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Miami Area Hotel Brings Its Past to Forefront', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Miami Hotel Brings Its Past to Forefront', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levere, Jane L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Biltmore Hotel (Coral Gables, Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T00:52:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane L. Levere', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Levere', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe7cbbbc-8b07-5df8-ad3f-4b1cc831c2e1', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe7cbbbc-8b07-5df8-ad3f-4b1cc831c2e1'}, {'abstract': 'Republican primaries around the country have largely degenerated into self-parodies, with the radicalism of 2010 and 2012 very much alive in 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/opinion/primary-day-on-the-far-side.html', 'snippet': 'Republican primaries around the country have largely degenerated into self-parodies, with the radicalism of 2010 and 2012 very much alive in 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wearing a black leather vest that barely covered the cigar tucked into his pocket, a man named Harley Brown was allowed to join the debate among candidates for governor of Idaho last week, holding forth on discrimination against bikers and the presidential seal tattooed on his shoulder after God told him he would one day occupy the White House. Another candidate, Walt Bayes, railed against “a bunch of eastern idiots” pushing the country toward Sodom and Gomorrah. If you thought that this was nothing but a stunt designed by Gov. Butch Otter to distract attention from his real opponent, you’d be right. But you’d also be missing the larger point: Republican primaries around the country have largely degenerated into self-parodies. They may lack the flowing beards of Mr. Brown and Mr. Bayes, but many of the other candidates in the party’s primaries — a large number of which will take place on Tuesday — are running on ideas only slightly less extreme.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Primary Day on the Far Side', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Primary Day on the Far Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T00:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8907a8f3-7b00-5352-a5bb-5ee4ceb848e9', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8907a8f3-7b00-5352-a5bb-5ee4ceb848e9'}, {'abstract': 'After years of declining to charge big banks, prosecutors are now seeking to criminally punish the banks without putting them out of business and wreaking havoc on the financial system.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/feeling-the-force-of-the-law/', 'snippet': 'After years of declining to charge big banks, prosecutors are now seeking to criminally punish the banks without putting them out of business a