zled on the racetrack. Afterward, though, his team stole the show. The fairy-tale run of his working-class owners, Steve and Carolyn Coburn and Perry and Denise Martin, has captured even the most casual fan’s attention. At 77, the trainer Art Sherman finally made it to the sport’s biggest stage. His 41-year-old jockey, Victor Espinoza, battled back from a slump to partake in his second Triple Crown run. Most important, they are all having fun. Following are excerpts from their post-Preakness news conference, where they were cracking jokes as if they were part of an improv show.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Savoring the Magic, One Run at a Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Savoring the Magic, One Run at a Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoppert, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'California Chrome (Race Horse)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coburn, Steve', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherman, Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Espinoza, Victor', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Perry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T02:48:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e3914fa-53a7-55e6-8799-a010cf155b5a', 'word_count': 1675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e3914fa-53a7-55e6-8799-a010cf155b5a'}, {'abstract': 'A city agency changes several policies to reduce what the new Human Resources Administration commissioner described as a punitive approach to welfare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/nyregion/rejecting-bloomberg-policies-new-york-city-will-ease-some-hurdles-to-public-assistance.html', 'snippet': 'A city agency changes several policies to reduce what the new Human Resources Administration commissioner described as a punitive approach to welfare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new commissioner of New York City’s Human Resources Administration on Monday announced a set of sweeping changes that would remove some work requirements and other barriers to receiving public assistance, cheering advocates for the poor and underscoring the sharp change in direction by Mayor Bill de Blasio away from the welfare policies of his predecessor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/nyregion/WELFARE/WELFARE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/20/nyregion/WELFARE/WELFARE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/nyregion/WELFARE/WELFARE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/nyregion/WELFARE/WELFARE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/nyregion/WELFARE/WELFARE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 