onent-of-us-entry-in-wwii-is-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Stuart was an heir to the Quaker Oats business and as a law student in 1940 helped found the America First Committee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert D. Stuart Jr., whose long career as a top executive for the family business, Quaker Oats, was preceded by his founding, with a handful of fellow Yale law students, of the America First Committee, the catalyst for a potent and polarizing movement opposing the nation’s entry into World War II, died on May 8. He was 98.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/Stuart-Obit/Stuart-Obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/20/business/Stuart-Obit/Stuart-Obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 685}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/Stuart-Obit/Stuart-Obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 898, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/Stuart-Obit/Stuart-Obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1815, 'width': 1590, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/Stuart-Obit/Stuart-Obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/20/business/Stuart-Obit/Stuart-Obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/business/