//artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/in-performance-jeremy-denk/', 'snippet': 'The pianist Jeremy Denk performs Mozart’s Rondo in F (K. 494).', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s In Performance video features the pianist Jeremy Denk playing Mozart’s Rondo in F (K. 494). Mr. Denk, who was awarded the Avery Fisher Prize in March, will be the music director of next month’s Ojai Music Festival in California.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Jeremy Denk', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Denk, Jeremy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T12:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b852a2a6-c285-56c3-995c-178655952383', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b852a2a6-c285-56c3-995c-178655952383'}, {'abstract': 'Russ Leatherman, the well-known voice of Moviefone, will be providing short video reviews of movies to HitFix.com, an entertainment news site.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/business/media/more-than-just-a-booming-voice-mr-moviefone-is-now-on-video.html', 'snippet': 'Russ Leatherman, the well-known voice of Moviefone, will be providing short video reviews of movies to HitFix.com, an entertainment news site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Helloooo, and welcome to Mr. Moviefone’s new gig.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Than Just a Booming Voice, Mr. Moviefone Is Now on Video', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Moviefone Is Now on Video', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moviefone Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leatherman, Russ', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HitFix', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T12:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab80eb5b-fc94-5f2e-80cf-70752526a2c1', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab80eb5b-fc94-5f2e-80cf-70752526a2c1'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a risk that a focus on small details in these critiques might suggest a lack of perspective, a trees/forest problem. But getting the small things right, consistently, contributes to the overall polish, clarity and authority of our writing.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/the-small-stuff/', 'snippet': 'There’s a risk that a focus on small details in these critiques might suggest a lack of perspective, a trees/forest problem. But getting the small things right, consistently, contributes to the overall polish, clarity and authority of our writing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a risk that a focus on small details in these critiques might suggest a lack of perspective, a trees/forest problem. And I realize that proper use of hyphens is a small detail in the broad scope of our journalistic efforts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Small Stuff', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T12:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c1b3a43-9669-5a0e-8e34-c1dd1cd12dec', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c1b3a43-9669-5a0e-8e34-c1dd1cd12dec'}, {'abstract': 'Credit Suisse is the first bank in decades to plead guilty to criminal wrongdoing. | A look at a disclosure rule that gives investors a wide reporting window. | What AT&T’s deal for DirecTV means. | Examining Pfizer’s “final” offer for AstraZeneca.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/morning-agenda-credit-suisses-felony-plea/', 'snippet': 'Credit Suisse is the first bank in decades to plead guilty to criminal wrongdoing. | A look at a disclosure rule that gives investors a wide reporting window. | What AT&T’s deal for DirecTV means. | Examining Pfizer’s “final” offer for AstraZeneca...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Credit Suisse has done what no other bank of its size and significance has done in more than two decades: plead guilty to criminal wrongdoing, DealBook’s Ben Protess and Jessica Silver-Greenberg write. “In a sign that banking giants are no longer immune from criminal charges, despite concerns that financial institutions have grown so large and interconnected that they are too big to jail, federal prosecutors demanded that Credit Suisse’s parent company plead guilty to helping thousands of American account holders hide their wealth,” they write.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Credit Suisse’s Felony Plea', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T12:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0de7823-2fcb-5922-aa2f-05837b6c165d', 'word_count': 2207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0de7823-2fcb-5922-aa2f-05837b6c165d'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister David Cameron and his home secretary praised the terrorism conviction in New York of Mostafa Kamel Mostafa, but some Muslims in London expressed concern.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/world/europe/from-david-cameron-a-sense-of-justice-delayed-but-achieved-british-cleric.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister David Cameron and his home secretary praised the terrorism conviction in New York of Mostafa Kamel Mostafa, but some Muslims in London expressed concern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The conviction of a radical British Muslim cleric in New York this week drew praise from the British prime minister and home secretary on Tuesday, but some Muslims in the London neighborhood where the cleric once preached said they were troubled by his prosecution.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Officials Welcome Cleric’s Conviction, but Some Britons Are Wary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Praise and Concern in Britain Over Cleric’s Terror Conviction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mostafa, Mostafa Kamel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'T