tter on Tuesday seeking to explain himself to subscribers of the Munich Philharmonic, the orchestra he is set to take over as music director in 2015-16.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gergiev, Under Fire for Support of Putin, Seeks to Reassure Munich', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gergiev Seeks to Reassure Munich', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gergiev, Valery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Munich Philharmonic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T15:28:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cba8bbaf-52d4-56a6-beda-7bb778cd7c2d', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cba8bbaf-52d4-56a6-beda-7bb778cd7c2d'}, {'abstract': 'Bloggers who approach time-craft with the devotion of biblical exegetes and thousands of devotees turned up last weekend for the Time Crafters fair at the Park Avenue Armory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/fashion/watch-fair-included-Tag-Heuer-Bulgari-Chopard-Hublot.html', 'snippet': 'Bloggers who approach time-craft with the devotion of biblical exegetes and thousands of devotees turned up last weekend for the Time Crafters fair at the Park Avenue Armory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They stop time, ring time, contain time, split its measure into infinitesimally calibrated segments. They are sleek and golden, burnished to Fred Astaire elegance or else bulky and steroidal, as cartoonish as Hulk Hogan. By far the majority of watches fall into some commercially secure Goldilocks middle ground, serviceable mechanical manacles locked in vestigial fashion to millions of wrists. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/fashion/22WATCHESSPAN/22WATCHESSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/21/fashion/22WATCHESSPAN/22WATCHESSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/fashion/22WATCHESSPAN/22WATCHESSPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/fashion/22WATCHESSPAN/22WATCHESSPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/fashion/22WATCHESSPAN/22WATCHESSPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/21/fashion/22WATCHESSPAN/22WATCHESSPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/fashion/22WATCHESSPAN/22WATCHESSPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Latest in Watches: The Old Way to Tell Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Latest in the Old Way to Tell Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conventions, Fairs and Trade Shows', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T15:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3487004c-d208-548a-8c94-839a1c7437e5', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3487004c-d208-548a-8c94-839a1c7437e5'}, {'abstract': 'India has the highest number of newborn deaths in the world — nearly 780,000 babies under 28 days old die every year, with many deaths happening within 24 hours of birth, according to a series on newborn survival in The Lancet that was published Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/lancet-study-calls-for-action-to-prevent-millions-of-newborn-deaths/', 'snippet': 'India has the highest number of newborn deaths in the world — nearly 780,000 babies under 28 days old die every year, with many deaths happening within 24 hours of birth, according to a series on newborn survival in The Lancet that was published T...', 'lead_paragraph': 'URAGAHALLI, India — About a year ago, Nagarathna, who uses only one name, was admitted to a local government hospital on the outskirts of India’s information technology hub of Bangalore, when she went into labor. A bone-rattling ride on a motorized three-wheeler transported her to the facility located a few miles from her village.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ