icane Sandy, the River Café is casting its romantic spell once more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/dining/restaurant-review-the-river-cafe-at-fulton-ferry.html', 'snippet': 'After a museum-quality restoration in the wake of Hurricane Sandy, the River Café is casting its romantic spell once more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in the 1960s, when nobody except rats, longshoremen and gangsters needing to dispose of a wayward bookie saw much value in the Brooklyn waterfront, Michael O’Keeffe saw romance. He saw enough flowers for a year of proms, he saw a piano player massaging a Steinway, he saw a curtain of glass framing the Brooklyn Bridge and the lights of Fortress Manhattan on the other side. All of this he saw floating on a barge in the East River. After pleading for permits for 12 years, he persuaded City Hall to see it, too, and in 1977 the River Café dropped anchors.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/dining/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/21/dining/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/dining/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/dining/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/dining/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/21/dining/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/dining/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6/20140521-REST-slide-FFD6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Old Flame Reignited', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Old Flame Reignited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'River Cafe (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Keeffe, Michael (Restaurateur)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T18:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f964d667-f554-52a9-b646-dd1201e68a40', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f964d667-f554-52a9-b646-dd1201e68a40'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio’s solution in his contract with New York teachers was to promise retroactive pay now and pay it later. States and cities routinely fudge the numbers like this.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/upshot/de-blasio-and-new-york-promises-now-payments-later.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio’s solution in his contract with New York teachers was to promise retroactive pay now and pay it later. States and cities routinely fudge the numbers like this.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For nearly his last five years as mayor of New York City, Michael Bloomberg and the United Federation of Teachers failed to agree on a contract for the city’s public schoolteachers. By the time Bill de Blasio took office as mayor in January, the teachers were demanding billions in retroactive pay increases for the years they didn’t have a contract and therefore didn’t get base pay increases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/21UP-Budget-copy/21UP-Budget-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/21UP-Budget-copy/21UP-Budget-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/21UP-Budget-copy/21UP-Budget-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/21UP-Budget-copy/21UP-Budget-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1460, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/21UP-Budget-copy/21UP-Budget-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/21UP-Budget-copy/21UP-Budget-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/21UP-Budget-copy/21UP-Budget-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is a Balanced Budget Anyway?', 'kicker': 'Settling Accounts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Federation of Teachers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T18:58:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Barro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a624aae6-ff30-5f62-8160-768198619a8d', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a624aae6-ff30-5f62-8160-768198619a8d'}, {'abstract': 'Susan Parker said getting burned with the previous distribution agreements taught her to be stronger when negotiating the new ones.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/a-manufacturer-learns-hard-lessons-about-negotiating/', 'snippet': 'Susan Parker said getting burned with the previous distribution agreements taught her to be stronger when negotiating the new ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the most recent meeting of the She Owns It business group, Susan Parker talked about recent changes at her company,\xa0Bari Jay. These included hiring new designers and negotiating new distribution agreements.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Manufacturer Learns Hard Lessons About Negotiating', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T19:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1b69be6-c07d-5af7-a227-789aca9a2e73', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1b69be6-c07d-5af7-a227-789aca9a2e73'}, {'abstract': 'The conceptual New York-based designer Mary Ping and the Paris-based jeweler of Pièce à Conviction have teamed up for a five-piece capsule collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/perfect-pairing-collaboration-sculptural-jewelry-mary-ping-piece-a-conviction/', 'snippet': 'The conceptual New York-based designer Mary Ping and the Paris-based jeweler of Pièce à Conviction have teamed up for a five-piece capsule collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The spare, witty jewelry of Pièce à Conviction is little-known in the United States, but the New York-based designer Mary Ping\xa0has been collecting it for a decade, ever since she first discovered the ahead-of-its-time “floating”-style rings in a shop in Paris. “I don’t remember the name of the store,” says Ping, who designs\xa0Slow and Steady Wins the Race\xa0as well as a namesake line. “Which is a testament to how struck by the rings I was, because I remember everything.” After years spent wearing the jewelry\xa0daily in her Manhattan studio — and getting asked about it “all the time” — Ping worked up the courage to approach the line’s designer, Ghislain Ryckebusch, about collaborating. Ryckebusch invited her to his home and studio in Fontainebleau to work together, and the striking, sculptural results — a five-piece capsule collection including rings, bracelets and a necklace — will debut Thursday evening at Creatures of Comfort in New York, with more designs to follow in future seasons. “These really are pieces that hum and breathe. There is a rhythm, a balance,” Ping says. “They are unique punctuation marks.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/t-magazine/21conviction-hartman/21conviction-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/21/t-magazine/21conviction-hartman/21conviction-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/t-magazine/21conviction-hartman/21conviction-hartman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/t-magazine/21conviction-hartman/21conviction-hartman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1207, 'width': 1811, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp