': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Parliament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Front (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farage, Nigel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Pen, Marine', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crimea (Ukraine)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Political Capital Institute', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chauprade, Aymeric', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T19:01:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/720f16d9-db3f-5850-8ff2-4323c9bc100b', 'word_count': 1281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/720f16d9-db3f-5850-8ff2-4323c9bc100b'}, {'abstract': 'A survey of young doctors finds that they overwhelmingly would not choose heroic resuscitation measures if they had a terminal illness.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/do-not-resuscitate-what-young-doctors-would-choose/', 'snippet': 'A survey of young doctors finds that they overwhelmingly would not choose heroic resuscitation measures if they had a terminal illness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The researcher was presenting her findings to a room full of geriatricians, at the American Geriatrics Society annual scientific meeting last week in Orlando, Fla. So a slide revealing one particular statistic didn’t cause an audible gasp or murmur. Talking to geriatricians about end-of-life treatment practically defines preaching to the choir, as a member of the audience told me later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Not Resuscitate: What Young Doctors Would Choose', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T19:02:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f176f26-1e55-55c5-a0f8-635eed529fab', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f176f26-1e55-55c5-a0f8-635eed529fab'}, {'abstract': 'Jameis Winston, the Heisman Trophy winner who has been accused of rape by a former student, did not attend the hearing, which focused on two of his teammates who witnessed part of the sexual encounter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/sports/ncaafootball/florida-state-holds-hearing-connected-to-jameis-winston-allegations.html', 'snippet': 'Jameis Winston, the Heisman Trophy winner who has been accused of rape by a former student, did not attend the hearing, which focused on two of his teammates who witnessed part of the sexual encounter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly a year and a half after a student at Florida State accused the future Heisman Trophy winner Jameis Winston of rape, the