ing back its fundraising efforts, and promising to move to the political sidelines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Enough Room at the Democratic Cash Trough', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organizing for Action', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T19:08:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/067e2ccd-ccde-5507-99ff-795b618145f3', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/067e2ccd-ccde-5507-99ff-795b618145f3'}, {'abstract': 'From packing to tipping, booking flights to buying beverages, here’s some budget-friendly advice for those going to Brazil for the giant soccer tournament that kicks off next month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/travel/bound-for-the-world-cup-tips-to-save-you-money.html', 'snippet': 'From packing to tipping, booking flights to buying beverages, here’s some budget-friendly advice for those going to Brazil for the giant soccer tournament that kicks off next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The monthlong, 32-country soccer tournament known as the World Cup kicks off on June 12 in Brazil. And guess where the most tickets have been sold, outside of Brazil that is? Defying all logic, it’s the United States, the only country in the world you have to start an article about the World Cup by explaining what it is, when it starts and where it’s being played.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-frugal-top/25-frugal-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-frugal-top/25-frugal-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-frugal-top/25-frugal-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-frugal-top/25-frugal-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-frugal-top/25-frugal-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-frugal-top/25-frugal-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-frugal-top/25-frugal-top-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bound for the World Cup? Tips to Save You Money', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T19:11:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef504ea0-28c7-5033-b6fd-a4067779cd80', 'word_count': 1254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef504ea0-28c7-5033-b6fd-a4067779cd80'}, {'abstract': 'Can’t make it to the World Cup this summer? A soccer trip to Vancouver, Seattle or Portland could be a fine substitute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/travel/soccer-as-spectacle-in-the-pacific-northwest.html', 'snippet': 'Can’t make it to the World Cup this summer? A soccer trip to Vancouver, Seattle or Portland could be a fine substitute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last thing I remember clearly, sometime around 4 a.m., was wondering how many people had fallen down the vertiginous back-hallway stairs that are the only way in or out of the Railway Club, the oldest continuously operating bar in Vancouver, British Columbia, a drinking and former gambling establishment that has seen its share of idiots and drunkards since it opened in 1931.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-pursuits-top-sf/25-pursuits-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-pursuits-top-sf/25-pursuits-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 538}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-pursuits-top-sf/25-pursuits-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-pursuits-top-sf/25-pursuits-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1836, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-pursuits-top-sf/25-pursuits-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-pursuits-top-sf/25-pursuits-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-pursuits-top-sf/25-pursuits-top-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soccer as Spectacle in the Pacific Northwest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soccer (the Fans, Not the Players) as Spectacle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Portland Timbers (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Whitecaps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Sounders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vancouver (British Columbia)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Northwestern States (US)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-20T19:12:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Rhodes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rhodes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8e42a67-e978-5873-bee5-611aac8046c6', 'word_count': 1758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8e42a67-e978-5873-bee5-611aac8046c6'}, {'abstract': 'Toward a unified theory of this White House’s foreign policy struggles.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/obamas-indecision-points/', 'snippet': 'Toward a unified theory of this White House’s foreign policy struggles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wrote my Sunday column on President Obama’s foreign policy, which seems to be failing to achieve its objectives just about everywhere one might reasonably look. (And the column went to press before the latest turn of events\xa0in post-Qaddafi Libya,\xa0the latest sour news on the Iranian nuclear talks, and the acknowledgment from administration officials that actually, in its latest incarnations, al Qaeda may not actually be on “the path to defeat” after all.) In limning these failures, however, I diagnosed without prescribing: I’m not sure I have a grand unified theory of what’s going wrong\xa0 — “events, dear boy, events” probably doesn’t count — so it’s hard to offer a clear account of everything the president should be doing differently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Indecision Points', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank':