l', 'snippet': 'The collision between a freight train collided and a passenger train near Moscow on Tuesday also injured 25.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A freight train collided with a passenger train near Moscow on Tuesday, killing at least six people and injuring 25. Russian officials said the crash occurred near the town of Naro-Fominsk, southwest of Moscow, when the train carrying about 400 passengers was on its way to Chisinau, Moldova. Russian television said the Moscow-bound freight train was operated by an unidentified Ukrainian company. The poor state of the tracks or the freight train is considered a possible cause of the crash, investigators said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Train Crash Kills Six Near Moscow', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Train Crash Kills Six Near Moscow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freight (Cargo)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T01:54:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Odynova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Odynova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/718128c0-ee62-5b16-9e9e-f0fc7484b2b2', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/718128c0-ee62-5b16-9e9e-f0fc7484b2b2'}, {'abstract': 'Mike Buckley offers us a twofer.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/20/long-long-stories/', 'snippet': 'Mike Buckley offers us a twofer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY’S PUZZLE — Today’s puzzle by Mike Buckley reminds us that if a one-word homophone is punny, then a two-word homophone is even punnier. Don’t you just love a twofer?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Long, Long Stories', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T02:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad18a197-02da-57cb-9043-f0f85b8ff9d2', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad18a197-02da-57cb-9043-f0f85b8ff9d2'}, {'abstract': 'Trent Lott, John B. Breaux and Tom Daschle support more use of remote digital technology to help care for patients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/us/politics/ex-senators-on-both-sides-of-aisle-join-forces-on-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'Trent Lott, John B. Breaux and Tom Daschle support more use of remote digital technology to help care for patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As a Republican senator, Trent Lott was among those who successfully dug in against the Clinton-era health overhaul. Tom Daschle, then the Senate Democratic leader, fought Republicans on their prescription drug plan. John B. Breaux, a centrist Democrat who led a blue-ribbon Medicare commission, often found himself at odds with both parties.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/0