subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lott, Trent', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breaux, John B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daschle, Tom', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T02:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01ac916b-e7ab-5f9f-ab41-aa51581405d1', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01ac916b-e7ab-5f9f-ab41-aa51581405d1'}, {'abstract': 'A study showed that 30 percent of the drinkers are women, despite an officially enforced Islamic prohibition on alcoholic beverages, a medical toxicologist said Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/world/middleeast/iran-more-than-one-million-said-to-defy-alcohol-ban.html', 'snippet': 'A study showed that 30 percent of the drinkers are women, despite an officially enforced Islamic prohibition on alcoholic beverages, a medical toxicologist said Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Despite an officially enforced Islamic prohibition on alcoholic beverages, more than one million Iranians are drinkers, a medical toxicologist said Tuesday. The toxicologist, Dr. Reza Afshari, president of the Asia Pacific Association of Medical Toxicology, was quoted by the Iranian Students’ News Agency as saying the finding was based on a yearlong study that ended in March 2013. It also showed that 30 percent of the drinkers are women. Dr. Afshari spoke at what the news agency called the first conference on alcohol abuse in Iran, a reflection of the government’s acknowledgment of the problem. Alcohol consumption, possession and production have been illegal since the 1979 Islamic Revolution, but smuggled and homemade liquor is said to be widely available. Government officials have said at least 200,000 Iranians are alcoholics. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: More Than One Million Said to Defy Alcohol Ban', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: More Than One Million Said to Defy Alcohol Ban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Afshari, Reza', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T02:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef8980d5-df71-5acd-8c61-460148f06307', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef8980d5-df71-5acd-8c61-460148f06307'}, {'abstract': 'Blackhawks goaltender Corey Crawford has struggled to shake the sense he’s the beneficiary of a loaded roster, but he’s excelled in this year’s playoffs and teammates refer to him as their backbone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/sports/hockey/blackhawks-stand-behind-corey-crawford-as-their-goalie.html', 'snippet': 'Blackhawks goaltender Corey Crawford has struggled to shake the sense he’s the beneficiary of a loaded roster, but he’s excelled in this year’s playoffs and teammates refer to him as their backbone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — On the ice at Boston’s TD Garden, minutes after he had won his first Stanley Cup last year, Blackhawks goaltender Corey Crawford was approached by a local television host for an interview. He had been one of Crawford’s fiercest critics during the season and through the playoffs, repeatedly questioning whether Crawford was a championship-caliber goalie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/sports/Y-BLACKHAWKS/Y-BLACKHAWKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/21/sports/Y-BLACKHAWKS/Y-BLACKHAWKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/sports/Y-BLACKHAWKS/Y-BLACKHAWKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/sports/Y-BLACKHAWKS/Y-BLACKHAWKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/sports/Y-BLACKHAWKS/Y-BLACKHAWKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/21/sports/Y-BLACKHAWKS/Y-BLACKHAWKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/sports/Y-BLACKHAWKS/Y-BLACKHAWKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning the Cup, and Starting to Win Over Critics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winning the Cup, and Starting to Win Over Critics ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Blackhawks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crawford, Corey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T02:04:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69dd0e21-2860-50f2-aa9c-fb54e15c9ef4', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69dd0e21-2860-50f2-aa9c-fb54e15c9ef4'}, {'abstract': 'New York Republicans are energized at the prospect of taking on Attorney General Eric T. Schneiderman, whose name recognition has remained mediocre.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/nyregion/gop-sees-chance-as-schneiderman-seeks-2nd-term-as-attorney-general.html', 'snippet': 'New York Republicans are energized at the prospect of taking on Attorney General Eric T. Schneiderman, whose name recognition has remained mediocre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Eric T. Schneiderman, the state attorney general, has a big problem for an incumbent seeking a second term: Many New Yorkers barely seem to know his name.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/nyregion/y-jpSCHNEIDERMAN/y-jpSCHNEIDERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/21/nyregion/y-jpSC