is wisdom at a hefty price. | Credit Suisse sees business as usual after its guilty plea. | Examining the latest dispute over the sale of Red Lobster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INVERSION DIVERSION \xa0|\xa0 A group of 14 senators introduced a bill on Tuesday that would essentially disallow any more so-called inversions for two years, slowing down the rush by United States corporations to reincorporate overseas to lower their tax bills, DealBook’s David Gelles writes. The bill would give Congress time to pursue broad changes in the corporate tax code that could make the United States rates more competitive with other countries, reducing the incentive for companies to move overseas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inversion Diversion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T11:33:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0a02661-aa72-51bc-afb7-7978fe67f06d', 'word_count': 2213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0a02661-aa72-51bc-afb7-7978fe67f06d'}, {'abstract': 'It took more than 30 years for Larry Kramer’s play “The Normal Heart,” about gay New Yorkers struggling with AIDS, to be turned into a movie. But for the playwright, there is still work to be done.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/television/100000002892340/larry-kramer-the-fighting-heart.html', 'snippet': 'It took more than 30 years for Larry Kramer’s play “The Normal Heart,” about gay New Yorkers struggling with AIDS, to be turned into a movie. But for the playwright, there is still work to be done.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took more