i': 'nyt://article/55b8758e-992e-5a4e-9ab7-98170b8a8e31'}, {'abstract': 'Theodore Roosevelt, who considered Abraham Lincoln “my great hero,” might have been inspired by a memorial parade honoring Lincoln after his assassination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/upshot/when-tr-saw-lincoln.html', 'snippet': 'Theodore Roosevelt, who considered Abraham Lincoln “my great hero,” might have been inspired by a memorial parade honoring Lincoln after his assassination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Look at the open second-floor window between shutters in this photograph, and you will see two little boys. President Theodore Roosevelt’s widow, Edith, identified one of them as her husband at the age of 6, looking down from his grandfather’s Union Square mansion onto the coffin of the assassinated Abraham Lincoln on Broadway in New York in April 1865.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/upshot/22UP-Teddy-copy/22UP-Teddy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 618, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/22/upshot/22UP-Teddy-copy/22UP-Teddy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 618}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/upshot/22UP-Teddy-copy/22UP-Teddy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 994, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/upshot/22UP-Teddy-copy/22UP-Teddy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1988, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/upshot/22UP-Teddy-copy/22UP-Teddy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/22/upshot/22UP-Teddy-copy/22UP-Teddy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/upshot/22UP-Teddy-copy/22UP-Teddy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When T.R. Saw Lincoln', 'kicker': 'HistorySource', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Theodore', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Union Square (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T14:58:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Beschloss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beschloss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Web Log', '_id': 'nyt://article/29bbee20-8293-5d33-ba87-d93e3b2585a0', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29bbee20-8293-5d33-ba87-d93e3b2585a0'}, {'abstract': 'A look back at coverage of Larry Kramer’s 1985 play about the AIDS crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/decades-of-the-normal-heart/', 'snippet': 'A look back at coverage of Larry Kramer’s 1985 play about the AIDS crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been almost 30 years since Larry Kramer’s play “The Normal Heart,” an angry and autobiographical drama about gay men and the AIDS crisis, opened at the Public Theater. On Sunday, HBO will broadcast its new film version, starring Mark Ruffalo as the outspoken activist Ned Weeks, a character based on Mr. Kramer, and Matt Bomer as Felix, his lover who is dying of AIDS. Read more about it here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Decades of ‘The Normal Heart’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Edward I', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kramer, Larry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mantello, Joe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rich, Frank', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Gay Men's Health Crisis", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T15:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/541491ee-6509-50a8-820f-b4c4bba1a481', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/541491ee-6509-50a8-820f-b4c4bba1a481'}, {'abstract': 'The world economy is expected to continue to sputter in the near future, at a time when more young people are entering the job market than ever before.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/upshot/united-nations-forecasts-persistently-high-unemployment-for-the-young.html', 'snippet': 'The world economy is expected to continue to sputter in the near future, at a time when more young people are entering the job market than ever before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The clouds of the global financial crisis may have lifted, but six years later, the world economy is not creating nearly as many jobs as it was before 2008, a United Nations report on Wednesday concluded, nor is it expected to in the near term. That is a particularly worrisome fact at a time when more young people are entering the job market than ever before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/22UP-JOBS/22UP-JOBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/22UP-JOBS/22UP-JOBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/22UP-JOBS/22UP-JOBS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/22UP-JOBS/22UP-JOBS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/22UP-JOBS/22UP-JOBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/22UP-JOBS/22UP-JOBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/upshot/22UP-JOBS/22UP-JOBS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'United Nations Forecasts Persistently High Unemployment for the Young', 'kicker': 'A Recovery That Needs a Recovery', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T15:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a29fb8e5-1cd6-58af-984e-cde2fde2f3bc', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a29fb8e5-1cd6-58af-984e-cde2fde2f3bc'}, {'abstract': 'Americans for Prosperity wants to stop the deal that would help the city’s pensioners.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/the-koch-brothers-hit-detroit-while-its-down/', 'snippet': 'Americans for Prosperity wants to stop the deal that would help the city’s pensioners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last five months, a deal has come together that would solve some of the most contentious issues in Detroit’s bankruptcy. It would minimize the pension cuts for 30,000 retirees and city workers, save the city’s art collection and give a reasonable amount of money to the city’s bondholders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Koch Brothers Kick Detroit While It’s Down', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [