jor': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T16:40:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marisa Meltzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meltzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b0e2b7c-eeb7-5962-80aa-71d9bb5e38e3', 'word_count': 1592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b0e2b7c-eeb7-5962-80aa-71d9bb5e38e3'}, {'abstract': 'To ship through Shyp, you first download the firm’s iPhone app and enter in your payment data.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/technology/personaltech/use-an-app-pay-a-fee-and-ship-almost-anything.html', 'snippet': 'To ship through Shyp, you first download the firm’s iPhone app and enter in your payment data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PACKAGING and shipping an item isn’t the worst task in the world, but it isn’t exactly fun, either. Say you’re sending a gift to your grandmother. First, you have to find a box. Then you need tape, one of those household items that is almost never where you thought you’d put it. You might also need to weigh and measure the box, and research which shipper fits your budget and delivery preferences. Then you either have to go to the web to order a shipping label or hurry over to the post office to wait in line.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/business/22gadgetwise-web2/22gadgetwise-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/22/business/22gadgetwise-web2/22gadgetwise-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/business/22gadgetwise-web2/22gadgetwise-web2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/business/22gadgetwise-web2/22gadgetwise-web2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/business/22gadgetwise-web2/22gadgetwise-web2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/22/business/22gadgetwise-web2/22gadgetwise-web2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/business/22gadgetwise-web2/22gadgetwise-web2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Painless Shipping In a Few Easy Steps', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Painless Shipping in a Few Easy Steps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manjoo, Farhad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delivery Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shyp Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T16:43:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farhad Manjoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farhad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manjoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60e3ec96-c879-5b8f-85cb-8ddc61b4ccbb', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60e3ec96-c879-5b8f-85cb-8ddc61b4ccbb'}, {'abstract': 'Excerpts from a conversation with the two singer-songwriters.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/q-and-a-conor-oberst-and-lorde-find-common-ground/', 'snippet': 'Excerpts from a conversation with the two singer-songwriters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Growing up in the suburbs of Omaha turns out not to have been much different than growing up in the suburbs of Auckland, at least to hear Conor Oberst, a Nebraskan, and Lorde, a New Zealander, tell it: both had to make their own fun. The two musicians and mutual fans bonded over their similarly forthright lyrical styles, in a conversation on Monday. They also shared a love for the debut albums of the British acts the Arctic Monkeys and the Streets, a certain distaste for social media (although Lorde, born Ella Yelich-O’Connor, has more than 1.6 million Twitter followers), and discussed the high and low points of touring. Here are more excerpts from their conversation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20lorde/20lorde-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20lorde/20lorde-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 626}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20lorde/20lorde-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 983, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20lorde/20lorde-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1918, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20lorde/20lorde-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20lorde/20lorde-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/20/arts/20lorde/20lorde-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Conor Oberst and Lorde Find Common Ground', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lorde', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oberst, Conor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T16:50:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/110ce7f6-4c5c-58fe-ae58-4a2714848491', 'word_count': 1285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/110ce7f6-4c5c-58fe-ae58-4a2714848491'}, {'abstract': 'Meet Madison Krekel wearing a bolo tie she bought at a flea market, socks with sushi printed on them and a Cramps T-shirt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/fashion/brooklyn-street-style-bushwick.html', 'snippet': 'Meet Madison Krekel wearing a bolo tie she bought at a flea market, socks with sushi printed on them and a Cramps T-shirt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Getting off at the Morgan Avenue stop on the L train in Brooklyn is like stepping into a vintage version of New York City. The area is home to fledgling artists, industrial-looking buildings dripping in street art and the sounds of musicians practicing from nearby studios. Madison Krekel blends in easily wearing a bolo tie she bought at a flea market, socks with sushi printed on them and a Cramps T-shirt. Originally from Oakland, Calif., she moved to the area four years ago and recently dyed her hair green as a way to welcome spring. This interview has been edited.\xa0', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/fashion/22INTERSECTION3/22zINTERSECTION3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/22/fashion/22INTERSECTION3/22zINTERSECTION3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/fashion/22INTERSECTION3/22zINTERSECTION3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/fashion/22INTERSECTION3/22zINTERSECTION3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/fashion/22INTERSECTION3/22zINTERSECTION3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/22/fashion/22INTERSECTIO