, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koblin, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T17:44:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Koblin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koblin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f95763b-0849-5a4d-b36f-f6be76d1c374', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f95763b-0849-5a4d-b36f-f6be76d1c374'}, {'abstract': 'For a one-man show in Manhattan, Loudon Wainwright III will draw on the writings of his father, a magazine columnist who died in 1988.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/loudon-wainwright-to-join-father-in-posthumous-collaboration-for-stage-show/', 'snippet': 'For a one-man show in Manhattan, Loudon Wainwright III will draw on the writings of his father, a magazine columnist who died in 1988.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Loudon Wainwright III has always been a first-class storyteller, but in the 44 years since his eponymous debut album, his métier has mostly been the four-minute, folk-tinged pop song. Now he is broadening his canvas. In “Surviving Twin,” an 80-minute one-man show that opens at the Westside Theater in Manhattan on June 9, Mr. Wainwright will sing favorites from his catalog, as well as several new songs that he plans to include on his next album, “Haven’t Got the Blues (Yet),” due in September. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype':