at Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Virginia C. McGuire', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Virginia', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McGuire', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c738292e-6bbb-5d16-a0ea-8a8921aa9e76', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c738292e-6bbb-5d16-a0ea-8a8921aa9e76'}, {'abstract': 'The suspects included two police officers, two registered nurses, a paramedic, an au pair and an individual who served as both a den master with the Boy Scouts of America and a Little League baseball coach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/nyregion/dozens-arrested-in-new-york-state-child-pornography-investigation.html', 'snippet': 'The suspects included two police officers, two registered nurses, a paramedic, an au pair and an individual who served as both a den master with the Boy Scouts of America and a Little League baseball coach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It began in Westchester County with the arrest of a police chief who was teaching classes about sexual abuse at a Roman Catholic church. The investigation soon swept up many others who were swapping files of children forced into explicit sexual acts: two registered nurses, a Brooklyn rabbi, a New York City police officer, a paramedic and a Boy Scout leader.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/nyregion/CHILD/CHILD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/22/nyregion/CHILD/CHILD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/nyregion/CHILD/CHILD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 