e': 'persons', 'value': 'Cloepfil, Brad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Cardenas, Rafael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meier, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Van Alen Institute', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T19:36:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/016de784-359f-5bd4-8122-ae913f35e74e', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/016de784-359f-5bd4-8122-ae913f35e74e'}, {'abstract': 'The Cannaregio area is filled with a diverse range of local shops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/travel/browsing-in-boutiques-near-venices-grand-canal.html', 'snippet': 'The Cannaregio area is filled with a diverse range of local shops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to shopping, travelers to Venice tend to stick to the big-brand Italian chain stores near touristy San Marco Square, but the city’s homegrown boutique scene warrants far more attention than it gets. The Cannaregio area, for example, is filled with a diverse range of local shops along narrow alleys and in small piazzas. Situated off the Grand Canal and a 10-minute walk from the Rialto Bridge, this is a residential enclave where middle- and upper-class families have lived for generations and to which Venetians regularly flock for retail excursions.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-foraging-top/25-foraging-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-foraging-top/25-foraging-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 585}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-foraging-top/25-foraging-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 998, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-foraging-top/25-foraging-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1997, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-foraging-top/25-foraging-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-foraging-top/25-foraging-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25-foraging-top/25-foraging-top-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Browsing in Boutiques Near Venice’s Grand Canal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off the Beaten Canal in Cannaregio', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T19:39:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814ead22-5f5c-5ab5-883e-e39a2f4b4904', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814ead22-5f5c-5ab5-883e-e39a2f4b4904'}, {'abstract': 'Over the past six years, a number of cafes and art collectives have opened along Halsey Street, giving the city a denser downtown culture district.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/travel/exploring-cafes-and-culture-in-downtown-newark.html', 'snippet': 'Over the past six years, a number of cafes and art collectives have opened along Halsey Street, giving the city a denser downtown culture district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ceramic fire-breathing dragons in the window of Gifts East West, a curio shop owned by Ing and John Watts, have seen neighbors come and go during their 40-year tenure at 57 Halsey Street in Newark. Today the dragons look out to an empty lot and a mural painted on a wall of a shuttered department store, Hahne & Company, which last saw customers in the late 1980s. In two years the building will house a Whole Foods Market, with mixed-income rental apartments stacked above it. Another construction site across the street is for the Prudential Tower, which will give the financial services giant a new home next year, with room for retail as well.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25HEADS4/25HEADS4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25HEADS4/25HEADS4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/travel/25HEADS4/25