,” outsold the new Michael Jackson album “Xscape,” for which producers used old vocals to make new songs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In one of the odder contests in recent pop history, the Black Keys have narrowly beaten Michael Jackson for the No. 1 spot on the new Billboard album chart.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Black Keys’s Latest Tops Michael Jackson', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T20:19:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c56fc939-1eb1-5dea-8e95-2cd923a5a8ee', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c56fc939-1eb1-5dea-8e95-2cd923a5a8ee'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Tom Corbett said that a challenge to a decision striking down the state’s ban on gay marriage would be unlikely to succeed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/us/pennsylvania-governor-will-not-appeal-same-sex-marriage-ruling.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Tom Corbett said that a challenge to a decision striking down the state’s ban on gay marriage would be unlikely to succeed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Tom Corbett of Pennsylvania said Wednesday that he would not appeal a judge’s ruling striking down Pennsylvania’s ban on same-sex marriage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/us/SAMESEX-REFER/SAMESEX-REFER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/22/us/SAMESEX-REFER/SAME