-turn-to-disease.html', 'snippet': 'Contaminated water has covered homes, towns and fields, leading to fears of intestinal ailments, respiratory infections, skin diseases, hepatitis and perhaps worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OBRENOVAC, Serbia — For five days, as rain pelted the Balkans and the waters rose, Jovanka Sreckovic, 85, waited in bed in her tiny house, barely a hut, beside the Sava River. Ms. Sreckovic, unable to walk, had no food, no water, no medicine and no electricity, and felt herself sinking into sickness with nothing but a children’s book about Jesus to pass the time.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Worries Turn to Disease as Waters Recede in Balkans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Worries Turn to Disease as Waters Recede in Balkans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Balkan States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyman, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T21:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Lyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e9b6b85-0dc5-5feb-88f0-0b0e9eaa5d4c', 'word_count': 1222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e9b6b85-0dc5-5feb-88f0-0b0e9eaa5d4c'}, {'abstract': 'How to braise, grill or smoke them any time of year (but especially no