age', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/fashion/22RIOTERS/22zSUPEREFER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/22/fashion/22RIOTERS/22zSUPEREFER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/fashion/22RIOTERS/22zSUPEREFER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From a Prison Cell to the Red Carpet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From a Prison Cell to the Red Carpet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennett, Jessica', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alyokhina, Maria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolokonnikova, Nadezhda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T21:26:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Bennett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83fd5637-ad8b-559a-bfca-14625587c82f', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83fd5637-ad8b-559a-bfca-14625587c82f'}, {'abstract': 'The just-opened Molitor is a five-star renovation of a legendary Art Deco public pool in the 16th Arondissement.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/paris-swimming-hotel-molitor-jean-philippe-nuel-architect/', 'snippet': 'The just-opened Molitor is a five-star renovation of a legendary Art Deco public pool in the 16th Arondissement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The just-opened Molitor\xa0hotel is making a splash (quite literally) in Paris this season. Even in its new incarnation as a nautically themed 124-room luxury hotel, the site of the mythic Piscine Molitor — a vintage Art Deco public swimming pool — hasn’t entirely lost the aura of erotic possibility that made it beloved, in a tongue-in-cheek sort of way, by generations of Parisians. The three-story cement complex with sleek ocean-liner-like architecture and two pools — one indoor and heated, one outdoor — was originally designed by the architect Lucien Pollet and inaugurated in 1929 in the heart of the silk-stocking 16th Arrondissement, Paris’s Upper East Side, by the American Olympic gold medalists Aileen Wiggin and Johnny Weissmuller — who spent a summer here working as a lifeguard and giving swimming lessons before he went on to win the role of Tarzan in the film of the same name a few years later.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/t-magazine/22molitor-lobrano2/22molitor-lobrano2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/22/t-magazine/22molitor-lobrano2/22molitor-lobrano2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/t-magazine/22molitor-lobrano2/22molitor-lobrano2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/t-magazine/22molitor-lobrano2/22molitor-lobrano2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1620, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/t-magazine/22molitor-lobrano2/22molitor-lobrano2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/22/t-magazine/22molitor-lobrano2/22molitor-lobrano2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/t-magazine/22molitor-lobrano2/22molitor-lobrano2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Paris, A Sexy New Swimming Hotel Is Making Waves', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Accommodations: Splash Opening', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ART DECO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming Pools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T21:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b9a1fa2-7233-5811-aa55-993002a6fca4', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b9a1fa2-7233-5811-aa55-993002a6fca4'}, {'abstract': '“Gaîté Parisienne,” a ballet set in 19th-century Paris, returned to the Metropolitan Opera House for the first time since 1999.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/arts/dance/american-ballet-theater-performs-gaite-parisienne.html', 'snippet': '“Gaîté Parisienne,” a ballet set in 19th-century Paris, returned to the Metropolitan Opera House for the first time since 1999.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1988, when American Ballet Theater debuted a new production of Leonide Massine’s “Gaîté Parisienne,” one of the most popular ballets of the 1940s and ’50s, some people were shocked by the cartoonish sets by Zack Brown and the clashing colors in the costumes by Christian Lacroix. But the designers had the right idea. If a modern production of this comical character ballet is not to become a quaint evocation of mid-19th-century French cafe culture, it must not be afraid of being vulgar. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/22ABT1/22ABT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/22ABT1/22ABT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/22ABT1/22ABT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1023, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/22ABT1/22ABT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1970, 'width': 1971, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/22ABT1/22ABT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/22ABT1/22ABT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thu