 the coverage of science, sports, style, home and dining.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/05/21/how-arthur-gelb-helped-reinvent-the-modern-times/', 'snippet': 'During his tenure on The Times’s masthead, Mr. Gelb worked to put in place several of the daily sections that expanded the coverage of science, sports, style, home and dining.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arthur Gelb, who died Tuesday at the age of 90, held many titles in his years with The Times. He was a critic, chief cultural correspondent, metropolitan editor, deputy managing editor and managing editor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Arthur Gelb Helped Reinvent the Modern Times', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelb, Arthur', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T22:46:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erika Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0c49ae8-6c53-5434-a3ed-0291abd94ac7', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0c49ae8-6c53-5434-a3ed-0291abd94ac7'}, {'abstract': 'The psychological devastation of the Civil War was much more widespread than we think.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/21/the-civil-war-and-p-t-s-d/', 'snippet': 'The psychological devastation of the Civil War was much more widespread than we think.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edson Bemis was a hard man to kill. Rebel soldiers tried three times, and three times they failed. At the Battle of Antietam, a musket ball ripped through his left arm. Two years later, in the horrible fighting in the Wilderness, he was shot in the abdomen, just above the groin. The ball was never extracted, remaining in his body until the day he died. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Civil War and P.T.S.D.', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traumatic Brain Injury', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-21T22:47:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dillon Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dillon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f677abc5-f557-59a1-b2ae-25b504b563a9', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f677abc5-f557-59a1-b2ae-25b504b563a9'}, {'abstract': 'The poll by The New York Times, NY1 and Siena College was conducted May 15 through 20 with 678 likely Democratic primary voters throughout the 13th Congressional District.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytim