 times for veterans are disgraceful. If true, President Obama has to punish those responsible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When America sends men and women to fight, it owes them an enduring debt, starting with competent and timely health care and disability benefits when they leave active duty. President Obama expressed outrage on Wednesday at recent charges of wrongdoing in the Department of Veterans Affairs’ health care system. He also dispatched his deputy chief of staff to Phoenix to assess explosive allegations that government workers falsified data to hide long wait times for veterans needing to see doctors. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Troubles With Veterans’ Health Care', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Troubles With Veterans’ Health Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shinseki, Eric K', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffin, Richard J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Falsification of Data', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T00:58:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac4db05c-d1b0-5dc7-a8da-478c45b7549d', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac4db05c-d1b0-5dc7-a8da-478c45b7549d'}, {'abstract': 'Before the Senate votes on the judicial nomination of David Barron, the public should be able to see the drone memos that justified the killing of an American citizen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/opinion/the-senate-foolishly-rushes-in.html', 'snippet': 'Before the Senate votes on the judicial nomination of David Barron, the public should be able to see the drone memos that justified the killing of an American citizen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate is unnecessarily rushing to vote on President Obama’s nomination of David Barron for a seat on the United States Court of Appeals for the First Circuit in Boston, even though the public has yet to see documents written by Mr. Barron that have raised legitimate concern among civil liberties advocates on both the left and the right. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Senate Foolishly Rushes In', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Senate Foolishly Rushes In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barron, David J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appeals Courts (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourteenth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Anwar al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Targeted Killings', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T01:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/80ece9d9-7670-5cf6-9bcc-e26e4ad3efa8', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80ece9d9-7670-5cf6-9bcc-e26e4ad3efa8'}, {'abstract': 'The problems that Europe has endured in the past several years demonstrate the need more than ever for unity and that the parliamentary elections matter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/opinion/testing-time-for-european-unity.html', 'snippet': 'The problems that Europe has endured in the past several years demonstrate the need more than ever for unity and that the parliamentary elections matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The elections to the European Parliament, taking place Thursday through Sunday, are second only to India’s in size. Europe has 380 million registered voters, but turnout has been declining with every European Union parliamentary election since the first one in 1979, and it is likely to dip sharply below the 43 percent of registered voters in the last one in 2009.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Testing Time for European Unity', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Testing Time for European Unity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Parliament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elec