.M. (FX) X-MEN TAKEOVER THURSDAY With the release of “X-Men: Days of Future Past” on Friday, the network presents a trilogy of films about Marvel’s mutant superheroes, as well as interviews with cast members of the latest installment. The lineup begins with “X-Men Origins: Wolverine” (2009), followed by “X-Men: The Last Stand” (2006) at 7:15, and “X-Men: First Class” (2011) at 10. Hugh Jackman, above (who portrays Logan/Wolverine), Ellen Page (Kitty Pryde/Shadowcat), Patrick Stewart (Prof. Charles Xavier), James McAvoy (Charles Xavier), Michael Fassbender (Erik Lehnsherr/Magneto) and Peter Dinklage (Bolivar Trask) discuss the challenges facing the mutants of the future, how they prepare to play their characters and what they took away from the experience of making this latest film.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T05:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f41445a-e70e-59a9-8817-54e8083cc9e1', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f41445a-e70e-59a9-8817-54e8083cc9e1'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on May 22, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/pageoneplus/corrections-may-22-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on May 22, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: May 22, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dde15c7b-1500-5f73-bf9c-5a54f22dc596', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dde15c7b-1500-5f73-bf9c-5a54f22dc596'}, {'abstract': 'Adam M. Segal, an expert on China and cybersecurity at the Council on Foreign Relations, discussed the clash between the United States and China over cyberspying.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/q-a-adam-segal-on-china-cyberspies-and-the-moral-high-ground/', 'snippet': 'Adam M. Segal, an expert on China and cybersecurity at the Council on Foreign Relations, discussed the clash between the United States and China over cyberspying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, the United States took its most aggressive step yet in trying to curb what it calls Chinese state-sponsored hacking attacks aimed at stealing trade secrets from American corporations. The Justice Department on Monday announced an indictment against five members of the People’s Liberation Army accused of corporate cyberespionage. United States officials say the five men belong to Unit 61398, which operates out of an office tower on the outskirts of Shanghai.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/world/22sino-cyber02/22sino-cyber02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/22/world/22sino-cyber02/22sino-cyber02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/