_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/420eed10-8217-5c63-a3bd-f7b61e76bd86', 'word_count': 1086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/420eed10-8217-5c63-a3bd-f7b61e76bd86'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon likes to say it is obsessed with its customers. It ranks high on the Reputation Institute’s annual survey of the most reputable companies. It’s also one of the hardest companies for customers to give up.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/one-womans-lonely-boycott-of-amazon/', 'snippet': 'Amazon likes to say it is obsessed with its customers. It ranks high on the Reputation Institute’s annual survey of the most reputable companies. It’s also one of the hardest companies for customers to give up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated with new reporting on Amazon’s relationship with a book publisher, Hachette. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/technology/22bits-amazon/22bits-amazon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/22/technology/22bits-amazon/22bits-amazon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 652}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/technology/22bits-amazon/22bits-amazon-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 943, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/technology/22bi