 skin feel cleaner and more hydrated.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/julia-scott-on-going-suds-free-for-28-days/', 'snippet': 'Julia Scott went soapless for 28 days to test the claim by AOBiome that a living bacterial skin tonic would make her skin feel cleaner and more hydrated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the Health Issue this week, Julia Scott tested the claim by AOBiome that a living bacterial skin tonic composed of billions of cultivated Nitrosomonas eutropha, an ammonia-oxidizing bacteria, would make her skin feel cleaner and more hydrated. Part of her experiment included these headshots she took of herself. Scott recently talked about what it was really like not to shower with soap products for a month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/magazine/Bacteria1/Bacteria1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/magazine/Bacteria1/Bacteria1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/magazine/Bacteria1/Bacteria1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/21/magazine/Bacteria1/Bacteria1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/21/magazine/Bacteria1/Bacteria1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Julia Scott on Discovering What She Smells Like After 28 Soapless Days', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biotechnology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shampoos and Hair Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T11:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannie Choi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Choi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c50c516c-1b87-5504-a8cf-dcbe5ed4b9e0', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c50c516c-1b87-5504-a8cf-dcbe5ed4b9e0'}, {'abstract': 'Another 13 officials awaited help as insurgents continued to besiege a district government complex in a remote corner of northern Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/world/asia/afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Another 13 officials awaited help as insurgents continued to besiege a district government complex in a remote corner of northern Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Taliban insurgents captured 27 of 40 police officers and officials who had taken refuge in a bunker, the government and the insurgents said on Thursday, as the Taliban continued to besiege a district government complex in a remote corner of northern Afghanistan that until last year had been considered one of the safest parts of the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '27 Captured by Taliban Amid Siege', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '27 Captured by Taliban Amid Siege', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nordland, Rod', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Directorate of Security (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mujahid, Zabiullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T11:02:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5b0367d-7361-5b1b-90db-ef04a0186e76', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5b0367d-7361-5b1b-90db-ef04a0186e76'}, {'abstract': 'An attack on a Ukrainian military checkpoint that left at least 16 soldiers dead complicates a presidential vote Sunday, when few polling centers are expected to be open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/world/europe/ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'An attack on a Ukrainian military checkpoint that left at least 16 soldiers dead complicates a presidential vote Sunday, when few polling centers are expected to be open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DONETSK, Ukraine — When two armed men on Thursday afternoon barged into the small yellow schoolroom that has served as Inna Mashenskaya’s makeshift election office, she stood up straight and began to argue. But when one of them, wearing sunglasses, patted the knife that was hanging from his belt, she stopped talking and surrendered control of her polling center.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/23UKRAINE/23UKRAINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/23/world/23UKRAINE/23UKRAINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/23UKRAINE/23UKRAINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/23UKRAINE/23UKRAINE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/23UKRAINE/23UKRAINE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/23/world/23UKRAINE/23UKRAINE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/23UKRAINE/23UKRAINE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Violence and Doubts About Credibility as a Troubled Ukraine Election Nears', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Violence and Doubts About Credibility as a Troubled Ukraine Election Nears', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Donetsk (Ukraine)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Luhansk (Ukraine)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T11:02:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise and Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/242403c2-8972-558f-bae3-377f41eb0713', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/242403c2-8972-558f-bae3-377f41eb0713'}, {'abstract': 'What happens when you leave cleanliness up to your microbiome?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/magazine/my-no-soap-no-shampoo-bacteria-rich-hygiene-experiment.html', 'snippet': 'What happens when you leave cleanliness up to your microbiome?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For most of my life, if I’ve thought at all about the bacteria living on my skin, it has been while trying to scrub them away. But recently I spent four weeks rubbing them in. I was Subject 26 in testing a living bacterial skin tonic, developed by AOBiome, a biotech start-up in Cambridge, Mass. The tonic looks, feels and tastes like water, but each spray bottle of AO+ Refreshing Cosmetic Mist contains billions of cultivated Nitrosomonas eutropha, an ammonia-oxidizing bacteria (AOB) that is most commonly found in dirt and untreated water. AOBiome scientists hypothesize that it once lived happily on us too — before we started washing it away with soap and shampoo — acting as a built-in cleanser, deodorant, anti-inflammatory and immune booster by feeding on the ammonia in our sweat and converting it into nitrite and nitric oxide.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25bacteria1/mag-25Bacteria-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25bacteria1/mag-25Bacteria-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25bacteria1/mag-25Bacteria-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25bacteria1/mag-25Bacteria-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25bacteria1/mag-25Bacteria-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25bacteria1/mag-25Bacteria-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25bacteria1/mag-25Bacteria-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My No-Soap, No-Shampoo, Bacteria-Rich Hygiene Experiment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wash on the Wild Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AOBiome LLC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Probiotics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cleansers, Detergents and Soaps', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T11:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e4ef3c0-8dd7-5134-a58f-e02c110c412e', 'word_count': 2502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e4ef3c0-8dd7-5134-a58f-e02c110c412e'}, {'abstract': 'Bessel van der Kolk wants to change the way we heal a traumatized mind — by starting with the body.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/magazine/a-revolutionary-approach-to-treating-ptsd.html', 'snippet': 'Bessel van der Kolk wants to change the way we heal a traumatized mind — by starting with the body.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bessel van der Kolk sat cross-legged on an oversize pillow in the center of a smallish room overlooking the Pacific Ocean in Big Sur. He wore khaki pants, a blue fleece zip-up and square wire-rimmed glasses. His feet were bare. It was the third day of his workshop, “Trauma\xad Memory and Recovery of the Self,” and 30 or so workshop participants — all of them trauma victims or trauma therapists — lined the room’s perimeter. They, too, sat barefoot on cushy pillows, eyeing van der Kolk, notebooks in hand. For two days, they had listened to his lectures on the social history, neurobiology and clinical realities of post-traumatic stress disorder and its lesser-known sibling, complex trauma. Now, finally, he was about to demonstrate an actual therapeutic technique, and his gaze was fixed on the subject of his experiment: a 36-year-old Iraq war veteran named Eugene, who sat directly across from van der Kolk, looking mournful and expectant.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25memory_nocap/25memory_ss-slide-XZ1K-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25memory_nocap/25memory_ss-slide-XZ1K-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 477}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25memory_nocap/25memory_ss-slide-XZ1K-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 814, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25memory_nocap/25memory_ss-slide-XZ1K-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1627, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25memory_nocap/25memory_ss-slide-XZ1K-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25memory_nocap/25memory_ss-slide-XZ1K-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25memory_nocap/25memory_ss-slide-XZ1K-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Revolutionary Approach to Treating PTSD', 'kicker': 'The Health Issue', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Do You Heal a Traumatized Mind?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Interlandi, Jeneen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van der Kolk, Bessel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memory', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T11:32:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeneen Interlandi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeneen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Interlandi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/594991c2-6350-57c6-aa39-ca982a1ba9e5', 'word_count': 6595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/594991c2-6350-57c6-aa39-ca982a1ba9e5'}, {'abstract': 'China’s JD.com is set to begin trading. | Two American tobacco giants are said to be in talks to merge. | The Lehman estate is trying to sell a stake in the hedge fund D.E. Shaw. | Another view on Timothy F. Geithner’s book.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/morning-agenda-a-thirst-for-china/', 'snippet': 'China’s JD.com is set to begin trading. | Two American tobacco giants are said to be in talks to merge. | The Lehman estate is trying to sell a stake in the hedge fund D.E. Shaw. | Another view on Timothy F. Geithner’s book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American investors are hungry for a Chinese Internet company, and it isn’t the Alibaba Group, China’s e-commerce giant. Instead, JD.com, an online retailer aspiring to become that country’s answer to Amazon.com, exceeded expectations for its initial public offering on Wednesday, raising $1.78 billion, DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced writes. Even though the company has lost money for the last several years, its stock sale valued the company at $25.7 billion. Shares in JD.com will begin trading on the Nasdaq stock exchange on Thursday under the symbol JD.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Thirst for China', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T11:34:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a50ef59-fbd6-51be-956a-1e25625d0e5d', 'word_count': 1954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a50ef59-fbd6-51be-956a-1e25625d0e5d'}, {'abstract': 'The question was never whether he would keep the Genesis Prize money, but to whom he would give it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/nyregion/bloomberg-wins-1-million-prize.html', 'snippet': 'The question was never whether he would keep the Genesis Prize money, but to whom he would give it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Two very, very rich Americans who recently left very, very high-profile jobs flew to Israel this week, each on a private plane. The less-rich one hosted a ceremony Thursday night where the more-rich one got a $1 million prize from a quartet of Russian oligarchs. Then he gave it back.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/BLOOMBERG/BLOOMBERG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/23/world/BLOOMBERG/BLOOMBERG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 490}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/BLOOMBERG/BLOOMBERG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/BLOOMBERG/BLOOMBERG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1672, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/BLOOMBERG/BLOOMBERG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/23/world/BLOOMBERG/BLOOMBERG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/BLOOMBERG/BLOOMBERG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg, in Israel, Wins a $1 Million Prize, and Then Gives It Back', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bloomberg, in Israel, Wins 