d80-0161dc95dc45', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ce89265-b188-546a-bd80-0161dc95dc45'}, {'abstract': 'What, precisely, did James Craig have in mind when he spoke favorably of citizens arming themselves as an extra protection against violence?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/detroits-police-chief-stands-his-ground/', 'snippet': 'What, precisely, did James Craig have in mind when he spoke favorably of citizens arming themselves as an extra protection against violence?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What, precisely, did Detroit police chief James Craig have in mind when he spoke favorably of citizens arming themselves as an extra protection against violence in his battered city? The chief wound up on the cover of a National Rifle Association magazine this month after he stressed his pro-gun position, telling America’s 1st Freedom: that he was celebrating the rise of “good Americans, good Detroiters” carrying firearms because they were “fed up with being victims.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detroit’s Police Chief Stands His Ground', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vigilantes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Craig, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T15:05:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '