The online Chinese retailer JD.com started life as a publicly traded company with a rousing start, closing up 10 percent on the Nasdaq on Thursday. At that price, shareholders valued the company at more than $28.6 billion, more than other American technology names like Twitter and LinkedIn.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JD.com Has Rousing Start in Trading Debut', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strong Market Debut for JD.com Shows Allure of Chinese E-Commerce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alibaba Group Holding Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JD.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T15:41:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d352be3d-eee5-591e-96cf-7a064287cfb9', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d352be3d-eee5-591e-96cf-7a064287cfb9'}, {'abstract': 'Supporters of Narendra Modi in Karnataka said that they had sent a ticket to Pakistan to a celebrated writer who spoke out against his candidacy.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/modi-activists-in-karnataka-tell-bangalore-writer-to-go-to-pakistan/', 'snippet': 'Supporters of Narendra Modi in Karnataka said that they had sent a ticket to Pakistan to a celebrated writer who spoke out against his candidacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a book launch at a college in Bangal