uddenly Have a Wedding to Plan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbett, Thomas W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T17:52:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Hurdle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hurdle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4358bcb3-9d43-5ca1-8393-1b1a5afa2ec7', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4358bcb3-9d43-5ca1-8393-1b1a5afa2ec7'}, {'abstract': 'New York City’s health department completed a pilot project that used the website to identify unreported food-borne illnesses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/dining/reviews-on-yelp-help-track-illness.html', 'snippet': 'New York City’s health department completed a pilot project that used the website to identify unreported food-borne illnesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a particularly bad restaurant meal, you may be moved to post a review on the website Yelp, warning other diners. But now someone else is listening in: New York City health officials, who may try to track you down if you complain that the meal made you sick.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yelp Reviews Help Track Food Illnesses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yelp Reviews Help Track Food Illnesses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organiza