is film featuring Michael C. Hall and Sam Shepard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this video, the director Jim Mickle narrates a sequence from “Cold in July.” The film takes place in 1989 and features Michael C. Hall as a man who has killed a burglar who broke into his home. That act sets off a series of events in this twisty thriller. Here, Mr. Hall’s character appears at the funeral of the man he killed, with surprising results. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anatomy of a Scene: Video of ‘Cold in July’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Michael C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mickle, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shepard, Sam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T20:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f994319-ff5c-5402-acde-cf28a0b71146', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f994319-ff5c-5402-acde-cf28a0b71146'}, {'abstract': 'John Creten shares with T the processes and inspirations behind some of the pieces in his new outdoor sculpture installation.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/belgian-sculptor-johan-creten-antwerp-middelheim-museum/', 'snippet': 'John Creten shares with T the processes and inspirations behind some of the pieces in his new outdoor sculpture installation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A storm is brewing at Middelheim Museum, a sculpture park outside of Antwerp, Belgium. “The Storm,” to be exact. It’s the Belgian sculptor Johan Creten’s newest show, an outdoor installation of 25 monumental works cast in bronze, clay and resin. Creten’s work speaks to the storm within us all, as individuals and as a society, and deals with his usual themes: nature, the female form, power, politics and spirituality. As a preview to what is, to date, his largest and most ambitious exhibition, which opens this Saturday under the moody Flemish sky, the Paris-based artist talks to T about the processes and inspiration behind some of the works on view.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Belgian Sculptor Takes Antwerp by Storm', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTWERP (BELGIUM)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T20:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gay Gassmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gassmann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3a9bcd4-edf8-5eb5-94bd-4956255cb56c', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3a9bcd4-edf8-5eb5-94bd-4956255cb56c'}, {'abstract': 'Amnesia seemed to be in force as the House Financial Services Committee met this week for a hearing on “the dangers” of financial regulation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/business/the-financial-crisis-already-forgotten.html', 'snippet': 'Amnesia seemed to be in force as the House Financial Services Committee met this week for a hearing on “the dangers” of financial regulation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael S. Barr, a law professor at the University o