5fc-55d8-a8b5-f64f2914fde6', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eae43be-a5fc-55d8-a8b5-f64f2914fde6'}, {'abstract': 'Anthony W. Marx, president and chief executive of the New York Public Library, earned $781,000 — including housing, tuition and other compensation — in his first full year.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/22/library-reveals-presidents-salary/', 'snippet': 'Anthony W. Marx, president and chief executive of the New York Public Library, earned $781,000 — including housing, tuition and other compensation — in his first full year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony W. Marx earned $781,000 — including housing, tuition and other compensation — in his first full year as president and chief executive of the New York Public Library, according to the library’s most recent tax returns. According to the library’s Form 990, Mr. Marx’s base salary for 2012 was $491,000, considerably lower than that of his predecessor, Paul LeClerc, who was making $667,000 when he left the library, in 2011. More recent salary figures are not available. Library salaries have been a topic of discussion in recent months as New York City officials review the salary of Thomas W. Galante, who gets about $391,000 as the director of the Queens Library system. Mr. Marx and other officers are paid with private funds.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Library Reveals President’s Salary', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Library Reveals President’s Salary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marx, Anthony W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T21:31:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65b893fb-52fd-5a37-965c-57bb702e261c', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65b893fb-52fd-5a37-965c-57bb702e261c'}, {'abstract': 'The arrival of Alejandro Jodorowsky’s new feature would be grounds for excitement even if the movie, “The Dance of Reality,” were not something very close to a masterpiece.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/movies/the-dance-of-reality-jodorowskys-comeback-film.html', 'snippet': 'The arrival of Alejandro Jodorowsky’s new feature would be grounds for excitement even if the movie, “The Dance of Reality,” were not something very close to a masterpiece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chilean-born filmmaker Alejandro Jodorowsky has recently been the subject of a revelatory documentary — “Jodorowsky’s Dune,” directed by Frank Pavich — about a movie he never made. There are a lot of those: Since his heyday in the early ’70s as a midnight cult-film pioneer with “El Topo” and “The Holy Mountain,” Mr. Jodorowsky’s semimythic status as a cinematic wild man has outstripped his productivity as a director. So the arrival of a new feature — his first since 1990 — would be grounds for excitement even, if the movie in question, “The Dance of Reality,” were not something very close to a masterpiece.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23DANCE/23DANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23DANCE/23DANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23DANCE/23DANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23DANCE/23DANCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23DANCE/23DANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23DANCE/23DANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23DANCE/23DANCE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Family Memoir in a Dreamscape', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Family Memoir in a Dreamscape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jodorowsky, Alejandro', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Dance of Reality (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T21:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2085a8ba-28a6-5e70-ab6c-fed0b1aa06ac', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2085a8ba-28a6-5e70-ab6c-fed0b1aa06ac'}, {'abstract': 'Music festival season is here, beginning at MetLife Stadium on Memorial Day weekend and ending just before Labor Day on Randalls Island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/arts/music/a-selection-of-summer-music-festivals.html', 'snippet': 'Music festival season is here, beginning at MetLife Stadium on Memorial Day weekend and ending just before Labor Day on Randalls Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York brims with summer entertainment, and that includes more choices than ever for those whose idea of it is to escape into a “lost weekend” of music festival revelry. Nearby options include the freewheeling Mountain Jam at Hunter Mountain (June 5-8), the folk and singer-songwriter hub Clearwater’s Great Hudson River Revival in Croton-on-Hudson (June 21-22), the hip-hop- and rock-centric Made in America weekend in Philadelphia (Aug. 30-31) and many more. Here are six of the most-anticipated destination festivals in the region.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FEST1/23FEST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FEST1/23FEST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FEST1/23FEST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FEST1/23FEST1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FEST1/23FEST1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 7