, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time (Magazine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sports Illustrated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN SOCIETY OF MAGAZINE EDITORS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pearlstine, Norman', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T21:43:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39a081ef-c484-5f84-aa27-78cfa2ce0d12', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39a081ef-c484-5f84-aa27-78cfa2ce0d12'}, {'abstract': 'The question of what is innate and what can be learned arises in the exhibition “Self-Taught Genius: Treasures From the American Folk Art Museum.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/arts/design/inspiration-made-concrete-in-self-taught-genius-exhibition.html', 'snippet': 'The question of what is innate and what can be learned arises in the exhibition “Self-Taught Genius: Treasures From the American Folk Art Museum.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is there such a thing as artistic genius? In high-culture circles, it used to be taken for granted that there was, and there was a well-established canon of great artworks to prove it, from Leonardo’s “Mona Lisa” to Jackson Pollock’s drip paintings. Then, at the end of the 1960s, scholars like Linda Nochlin, author of “Why Have There Been No Great Women Artists?,” began to wonder why the canon consisted almost exclusively of works by male Caucasians. Is genius something that only white men are capable of? After that, belief in genius pretty much disappeared from serious art-historical discourse, except when it was disparaged as a patriarchal myth. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FOLK1/23FOLK1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FOLK1/23FOLK1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FOLK1/23FOLK1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FOLK1/23FOLK1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FOLK1/23FOLK1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FOLK1/23FOLK1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/23FOLK1/23FOLK1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Confederacy of Mavericks', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Confederacy of Mavericks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, '