nding-the-thai-coup/', 'snippet': 'Thomas Fuller, who is covering the coup for The Times, recommends what to read on the political dynamics of Thai society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Thai military overthrew the country’s elected government on Thursday. It was the second time in a decade that the military has seized control. We asked Thomas Fuller, who is covering the coup for The Times, to recommend what to read on the political dynamics of Thai society. Here is his suggestion:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Understanding the Thai Coup', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Chris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pasuk Phongpaichit', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thaksin Shinawatra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T22:04:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Insider Staff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Insider', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d498191-64bf-5484-9719-ca1e659c484f', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d498191-64bf-5484-9719-ca1e659c484f'}, {'abstract': '69th Street, from Lexington to Third, is notable among surviving stable streets — where the smells and noise of horses were isolated their owners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/realestate/architecture-for-the-upper-east-side-horse.html', 'snippet': '69th Street, from Lexington to Third, is notable among surviving stable streets — where the smells and noise of horses were isolated their owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The legacies of the horse in New York include the stable street, where the well-to-do isolated their private stables to avoid the smells and noise, inflicting them instead on their lesser neighbors. Although the mansions they served are in most cases gone, a few of these stable streets survive, and one of the most significant is 69th Street, from Lexington to Third Avenues. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/realestate/25SCAPES2/25SCAPES2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 220, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/realestate/25SCAPES2/25SCAPES2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 220}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/realestate/25SCAPES2/25SCAPES2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/realestate/25SCAPES2/25SCAPES2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/realestate/25SCAPES2/25SCAPES2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/realestate/25SCAPES2/25SCAPES2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/realestate/25SCAPES2/25SCAPES2-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 