 [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/abd84d44-86d1-5f40-ab23-76aa34d26f52', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abd84d44-86d1-5f40-ab23-76aa34d26f52'}, {'abstract': 'Cristiano Ronaldo, who helped lead Real Madrid to the Champions League title, had to be nudged into leaving the insulation of Madeira for a better opportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/sports/soccer/recalling-a-young-cristiano-ronaldo-who-clung-to-his-roots.html', 'snippet': 'Cristiano Ronaldo, who helped lead Real Madrid to the Champions League title, had to be nudged into leaving the insulation of Madeira for a better opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FUNCHAL, Portugal — The roads of Madeira twist together like licorice ropes, their spindly curves beginning at the seashore and rising up the steps of this steep island in a maze reminiscent of Rio de Janeiro’s favelas. The slow climb here comes with a similar feeling to the Brazilian shanties, too: one of utter insulation, a complete removal from the tourist areas that lie below.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/sports/23RONALDO2/23RONALDO2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/23/sports/23RONALDO2/23RONALDO2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/sports/23RONALDO2/23RONALDO2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type