 help prevent an apocalyptic battle a half-century away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even compared with other self-serious superhero franchises — the brooding “Dark Knight” saga, the agonized “Amazing Spider-Man,” the hectic “Avengers” house party — the X-Men series wears its allegorical heart on its sleeve. In chronicling the adventures of a despised minority with extraordinary powers, the movies, like the Marvel comic books before them, poke around in some interesting social and political hot zones. The central conflict is the endless moral and political argument between Professor X and Magneto: in other words, between the accommodationist idea that the mutants should fight for the moral redemption of the humans, and the militant insistence that they should defend their own interests by any means necessary. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving Their Future, in Bell-Bottoms', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saving Their Future, in Bell-Bottoms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'X-Men: Days of Future Past (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singer, Bryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T23:07:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e9050ee-cc4c-5f23-8e4c-b91d53885bfd', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e9050ee-cc4c-5f23-8e4c-b91d53885bfd'}, {'abstract': 'In “Cold in July,” Michael C. Hall, Sam Shepard and Don Johnson are unlikely amigos, banding against evil.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/movies/michael-c-hall-and-sam-shepard-star-in-cold-in-july.html', 'snippet': 'In “Cold in July,” Michael C. Hall, Sam Shepard and Don Johnson are unlikely amigos, banding against evil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pulpy neo-noir “Cold in July” should propel the filmmaking team of Jim Mickle and Nick Damici further up the blood-spattered, zombie-infested hierarchy of B-movie auteurs with Hollywood ambitions. Last year, they advanced a few feet with their remake of the 2011 Mexican cannibal fest, “We Are What We Are,” which followed two microbudget cult favorites: the post-apocalyptic “Stake Land” (2011), and “Mulberry St.” (2007), a medical horror flick.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monsters (the Human Kind) Slithering Through East Texas', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Monsters (the Human Kind) Slithering Through East Texas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mickle, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Michael C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shepard, Sam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Don', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lansdale, Joe R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaw, Vinessa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Cold in July (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damici, Nick', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-22T23:19:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b80fd40a-db5e-5d19-8330-53d310e83fa4', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b80fd40a-db5e-5d19-8330-53d310e83fa4'}, {'abstract': 'No matter the temperature, New York is the place to be. Here’s a summer guide to make the most of it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/nyregion/what-to-do-in-new-york-city-in-summer-2014.html', 'snippet': 'No matter the temperature, New York is the place to be. Here’s a summer guide to make the most of it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Winter was no picnic, but the amnesia that summer provides is just around the corner. The season’s lodestar, Macy’s Fourth of July fireworks show, is moving back to the East River, guided by the wishes of the Brooklynite mayor, Bill de Blasio. To witness another spectacle, find the camping gear and clear your calendar to ensure a ticket to “King Lear,” starring John Lithgow and Annette Bening, the Public Theater’s free Shakespeare in the Park production. No matter the temperature, New York is the place to be. Here’s a summer guide to make the most of it.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25SUMMER1/25SUMMER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 871, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25SUMMER1/25SUMMER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 871}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25SUMMER1/25SUMMER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 706, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25SUMMER1/25SUMMER1-sup