times.com/2014/05/23/arts/music/new-york-times-critics-respond-to-glyndebourne-fat-reviews.html', 'snippet': 'Anthony Tommasini, the chief classical music critic of The New York Times, and Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim, a classical music critic for The Times, respond to the attention the opera singer Tara Erraught has gotten for her size, not her voice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The reviews of the production of “Der Rosenkavalier” that opened this year’s Glyndebourne opera festival in England have gone viral, but not in a way that either the performers or the critics who wrote them probably expected. At issue: the way several prominent male critics harped on the shape, and not just the sound, of the young mezzo-soprano portraying Octavian: Tara Erraught.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24OCTAVIAN/24OCTAVIAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 896, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24OCTAVIAN/24OCTAVIAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 896}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24OCTAVIAN/24OCTAVIAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24OCTAVIAN/24OCTAVIAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1373, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24OCTAVIAN/24OCTAVIAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24OCTAVIAN/2