rs are scrambling to find just the right words to describe a costly bureaucratic blunder that came to light on Wednesday, thanks to some digging by the satirical weekly Le Canard Enchaîné. Was the foul-up only “comically tragic,” as a French transportation minister sheepishly described it, a “vaudeville farce,” as a rail worker’s union saw it, or a howler verging on madness as a leading French newspaper suggested.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Gap to Mind', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Gap to Mind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SNCF (Societe Nationale des Chemins de fer Francais)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RFF (Reseau Ferre de France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T01:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bed95d54-233b-5209-ab32-a6a08bd19bf0', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bed95d54-233b-5209-ab32-a6a08bd19bf0'}, {'abstract': 'After attending a science event, Abdullah Assem refused to leave Los Angeles after his chaperones refused to give him assurances that he would be safe back in Egypt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/us/path-to-an-asylum-request-from-egypt-jail-to-california-fair.html', 'snippet': 'After attending a science event, Abdullah Assem refused to leave Los Angeles after his chaperones refused to give him assurances that he would be safe back in Egypt.', 'lead_paragraph':