ls and organizations affiliated with Al Qaeda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/world/sanctions-imposed-against-boko-haram.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations Security Council on Thursday added Boko Haram, the Nigerian extremist group, to its Al Qaeda Sanctions List, a blacklist of individuals and organizations affiliated with Al Qaeda.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United Nations Security Council on Thursday added Boko Haram, the Nigerian extremist group, to its Al Qaeda Sanctions List, a blacklist of individuals and organizations affiliated with Al Qaeda. The designation subjects Boko Haram members to penalties that include a freeze on assets, a travel ban and an arms embargo. Nigeria had sought the designation as part of a broader response to a wave of attacks on schools and other targets by the group and its kidnapping of nearly 300 schoolgirls last month. The Security Council designation announcement cited the group’s avowed affinity and collaboration with Al Qaeda and its “violent insurgency utilizing terrorist tactics.” The designation was welcomed by Samantha Power, the United States ambassador, who said the Council’s action had “helped to close off important avenues of funding, travel and weapons to Boko Haram, and shown global unity against their savage actions.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sanctions Imposed Against Boko Haram', 'kicker': 'World Briefing ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sanctions Imposed Against Boko Haram', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacklisting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T02:28:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd830dd7-6bdd-57ab-904d-14fadcfd7de4', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd830dd7-6bdd-57ab-904d-14fadcfd7de4'}, {'abstract': 'Suicide bombers and car bombs killed at least 35 Shiite pilgrims and wounded dozens more in attacks in Baghdad on Thursday, security officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/world/middleeast/iraq-bombings-kill-at-least-35-pilgrims.html', 'snippet': 'Suicide bombers and car bombs killed at least 35 Shiite pilgrims and wounded dozens more in attacks in Baghdad on Thursday, security officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Suicide bombers and car bombs killed at least 35 Shiite pilgrims and wounded dozens more in attacks in Baghdad on Thursday, security officials said. The pilgrims were on their way to the shrine of a Shiite saint in Kadhimiya, in northern Baghdad, to commemorate the anniversary of his death. A day earlier, Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki urged the security forces to protect pilgrims traveling to the shrine. The deadliest attack took place in the Ur neighborhood of eastern Baghdad, where a car bomb exploded near a tent for pilgrims, killing 14 people, including four children, security officials said. “We need a new government that is able to protect us from those terrorists that are the enemies of God,” said a man wounded in the Ur bombing, Jafar al-Musawi. An attack in central Baghdad by a suicide bomber killed 12 pilgrims and wounded 26, and in the western Baghdad neighborhood of Mansour, a car bomb killed nine people and wounded 20, officials said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Bombings Kill at Least 35 Pilgrims', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Bombings Kill at Least 35 Pilgrims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilgrimages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T02:32:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Duraid Adnan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Duraid', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Adnan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9be504bc-358a-56bd-bda1-5f71c6f5fc85', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9be504bc-358a-56bd-bda1-5f71c6f5fc85'}, {'abstract': 'Former President Alfonso Portillo was sentenced in Federal District Court in Manhattan on Thursday to nearly six years in prison for conspiring with others to launder millions of dollars through United States bank accounts, federal prosecutors said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/world/americas/guatemala-ex-president-sentenced.html', 'snippet': 'Former President Alfonso Portillo was sentenced in Federal District Court in Manhattan on Thursday to nearly six years in prison for conspiring with others to launder millions of dollars through United States bank accounts, federal prosecutors sai...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Former President Alfonso Portillo was sentenced in Federal District Court in Manhattan\xa0on Thursday to nearly six years in prison for conspiring with others to launder millions of dollars through United States bank accounts, federal prosecutors said. Mr. Portillo, 62, who was extradited to the United States in May 2013 after fighting extradition for three years, pleaded guilty in March before Judge Robert P. Patterson Jr. In court\xa0on Thursday, speaking through an interpreter, he apologized and said that he felt “profoundly remorseful and embarrassed,” adding, “God and history will know whether I was a good or bad man during my time on this earth,” The Associated Press reported. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guatemala: Ex-President Sentenced', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guatemala: Ex-President Sentenced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Portillo, Alfonso', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guatemala', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Laundering', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T02:33:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5d8e09f-fd71-5f15-a2cb-a3ef7df0527a', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5d8e09f-fd71-5f15-a2cb-a3ef7df0527a'}, {'abstract': 'Kathy Hochul bounded up the stairs to the podium, full of vim, vigor and enthusiasm when she was nominated as the Democratic candidate for lieutenant governor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/nyregion/nod-smile-and-wave-while-you-can-wink.html', 'snippet': 'Kathy Hochul bounded up the stairs to the podium, full of vim, vigor and enthusiasm when she was nominated as the Democratic candidate for lieutenant governor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELVILLE, N.Y. — Kathy Hochul bounded up the stairs to the podium, full of vim, vigor and enthusiasm. She’d just been nominated as the Democratic candidate for lieutenant governor, replacing our current Lt. Gov. What’shisname.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nod, Smile and Wave While You Can (Wink!)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nod, Smile and Wave While You Can (Wink!)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hochul, Kathleen C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T02:35:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20616848-7bfc-5c9c-8019-0ffb98a62d51', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20616848-7bfc-5c9c-8019-0ffb98a62d51'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, May 23, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-friday-may-23-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, May 23, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There was a huge financial crisis that rocked the world, and it didn’t matter to us if the frauds occurred within the four corners of our district or around the globe.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, May 23, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T02:36:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/c04e8016-43ec-50fc-ba87-798288478b70', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c04e8016-43ec-50fc-ba87-798288478b70'}, {'abstract': 'Max Pacioretty, who grew up in New Canaan, Conn., was a devoted fan of the Rangers before becoming one of the Canadiens’ top scorers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/sports/hockey/the-canadiens-max-pacioretty-a-rangers-fan-no-longer.html', 'snippet': 'Max Pacioretty, who grew up in New Canaan, Conn., was a devoted fan of the Rangers before becoming one of the Canadiens’ top scorers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like so many others his age in the New York region, Max Pacioretty became a Rangers fan during the spring of 1994 as the team surged to a title.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/sports/CITY-PACIORETTY/CITY-PACIORETTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/23/sports/CITY-PACIORETTY/CITY-PACIORETTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/sports/CITY-PACIORETTY/CITY-P