kes-fight-against-us-base-to-washington.html', 'snippet': 'Despite reports of progress in relocating a Marine base on Okinawa, the mayor of its designated future home insists he will keep trying to block the plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — To some, the long-stalled agreement to relocate a United States Marine base from a heavily populated area of Okinawa, Japan, to a smaller city might finally be seeing the light of day. During his visit to Japan in April, Secretary of Defense Chuck Hagel said, “We look forward to the facility’s construction beginning soon.” A few weeks later at a news conference in Tokyo, President Obama and Prime Minister Shinzo Abe agreed that progress had been made.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/world/24okinawa-cnd01/24okinawa-cnd01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/24/world/24okinawa-cnd01/24okinawa-cnd01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 810}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/world/24okinawa-cnd01/24okinawa-cnd01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 759, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/world/24okinawa-cnd01/24okinawa-cnd01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1518, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/world/24okinawa-cnd01/24okinawa-cnd01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/24/world/24okinawa-cnd01/24okinawa-cnd01-thumbStandard-v2