odern antiretroviral drugs could alter the epidemic much as birth control changed the culture in the ’60s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRETEND it’s 1960, and the Food and Drug Administration has just done something startling. It has taken a drug it had previously approved for infertility — brand name Enovid — and approved it for the opposite use: birth control.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are We Ready for H.I.V.’s Sexual Revolution?', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Are We Ready for H.I.V.’s Sexual Revolution?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autoimmune Diseases', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Truvada (Drug)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T11:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/282e2003-46e4-52f3-9886-a4a288784c0c', 'word_count': 1208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/282e2003-46e4-52f3-9886-a4a288784c0c'}, {'abstract': 'In search of a cocktail that brings a smoky flavor indoors without annoying the neighbors or setting off a smoke alarm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/24/upshot/for-apartment-dwellers-a-memorial-day-barbecue-in-a-glass.html', 'snippet': 'In search of a cocktail that brings a smoky flavor indoors without annoying the neighbors or setting off a smoke alarm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s Memorial Day weekend, which marks the official start of barbecue season. But as my colleague Neil Irwin has noted, the recent uptick in housing construction is almost entirely about apartment construction. That means, in coming years, a declining percentage of American households will have a backyard to grill in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/upshot/24twist/24twist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/24/upshot/24twist/24twist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/upshot/24twist/24twist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/upshot/24twist/24twist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/upshot/24twist/24twist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/24/upshot/24twist/24twist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/upshot/24twist/24twist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Apartment Dwellers, a Memorial Day Barbecue in a Glass', 'kicker': 'Upshot With a Twist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barbecue', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorial Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T11:12:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Barro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eaee9ce-d74d-543d-8fd6-277fc7ecf7c4', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eaee9ce-d74d-543d-8fd6-277fc7ecf7c4'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking ever-higher payments from publishers to bolster its anemic bottom line, Amazon is holding books and authors hostage on two continents by delaying shipments and raising prices.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/amazon-escalates-its-battle-against-hachette/', 'snippet': 'Seeking ever-higher payments from publishers to bolster its anemic bottom line, Amazon is holding books and authors hostage on two continents by delaying shipments and raising prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amazon’s power over the publishing and bookselling industries is unrivaled in the modern era. Now it has started wielding its might in a more brazen way than ever before.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Publishers Fight Amazon, Books Vanish', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Publishers Fight Amazon, Books Vanish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowling, J K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stone, Brad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bonnier Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hachette Book Group', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T11:24:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld and Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a21bbd77-f906-538e-8848-ca2ef2f14a37', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a21bbd77-f906-538e-8848-ca2ef2f14a37'}, {'abstract': 'Conservative Islamic voters are just like any others: They want their governments to represent their values.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/24/opinion/more-democratic-less-liberal.html', 'snippet': 'Conservative Islamic voters are just like any others: They want their governments to represent their values.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — After being ousted from power last July, Egypt’s Muslim Brotherhood, the Arab world’s original Islamist movement, faces an existential moment. The group has been targeted with extreme repression, prompting a wave of commentary about the failure — or even death — of political Islam.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source'