: 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5414f5c6-79df-50ca-a2b1-9b2cc8494ca5', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5414f5c6-79df-50ca-a2b1-9b2cc8494ca5'}, {'abstract': 'A quiz administered to measure knowledge of contemporary political figures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/upshot/december-2011-political-awareness-quiz.html', 'snippet': 'A quiz administered to measure knowledge of contemporary political figures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In research about voters who split their tickets, Lynn Vavrek came up with a quiz to test political awareness. These questions, which were fielded in December 2011, asked a representative sample of 45,000 people about legislative and executive branch leaders. Her article is here. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'December 2011 Political Awareness Quiz', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T11:28:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e2b6ae5-ef1d-5215-8eeb-1bb8c86d5ad2', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e2b6ae5-ef1d-5215-8eeb-1bb8c86d5ad2'}, {'abstract': 'Voters who split their ticket know less and matter more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/upshot/the-power-of-political-ignorance.html', 'snippet': 'Voters who split their ticket know less and matter more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Split-ticket voting is quite rare for top offices like president and senator. But those who do choose candidates from different parties on Election Day have at least one thing in common: They know less about politics than people who vote the straight party line.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/upshot/25upshot/25upshot-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/upshot/25upshot/25upshot-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/upshot/25upshot/25upshot-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/upshot/25upshot/25upshot-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1301, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/upshot/25upshot/25upshot-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/upshot/25upshot/25upshot-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/upshot/25upshot/25upshot-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Power of Political Ignorance', 'kicker': 'Voter Behavior', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Power of Political Ignorance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vavreck, Lynn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T11:28:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Vavreck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vavreck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4616f54e-6cda-5a5a-9b23-3215f8e499a1', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4616f54e-6cda-5a5a-9b23-3215f8e499a1'}, {'abstract': 'Brian Page, a teacher in Ohio, took students in his personal finance and economics class out into the real world for lessons on high-cost lending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/24/your-money/a-high-school-field-trip-to-a-pawn-shop.html', 'snippet': 'Brian Page, a teacher in Ohio, took students in his personal finance and economics class out into the real world for lessons on high-cost lending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'READING, Ohio — The last time Brian Page had to file the paperwork to evict a tenant from a rental property he and his wife own, he noticed all the check-cashing services and pawn shops on his drive home from the courthouse. A clerk tipped him off to what was going on: Every day, lots of people leave court with checks they’ve received in legal settlements. They often stop to cash their checks right away, paying a big fee for the privilege, and then go shopping with the money.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Class Field Trip Stops at a Local Pawnshop', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Class Field Trip Stops at a Local Pawnshop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieber, Ron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Page, Brian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T11:41:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68cec1ce-4cc4-55ef-8032-aa40e34c7a08', 'word_count': 1446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68cec1ce-4cc4-55ef-8032-aa40e34c7a08'}, {'abstract': 'A new malaria vaccine strategy emerges from studies of blood in resistant Tanzanian toddlers.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/research-on-malaria-resistant-children-in-tanzania-leads-to-new-vaccine-approach/', 'snippet': 'A new malaria vaccine strategy emerges from studies of blood in resistant Tanzanian toddlers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The quest for effective malaria vaccines has been long and challenging, so it’s important not to overplay a single study. But there is real promise in fresh findings reported by researchers in Science today. The work centers on a parasite protein, named PfSEA-1 by the authors, that was isolated after analysis of blood samples in resistant and susceptible Tanzanian toddlers. Paul Rodgers has a really nice piece on the paper in Forbes. Here’s an excerpt:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/27/science/27GLOB_SPAN/27GLOB_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/27/science/27GLOB_SPAN/27GLOB_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargew