th a rousing start. | Credit Suisse found an unlikely opponent in Alexandria, Va. | Barclays has been fined in a gold price fixing case. | The anticipated merger between two large legal firms has ...', 'lead_paragraph': ' JD.COM STARTS HOT \xa0|\xa0 The online Chinese retailer JD.com started life as a publicly traded company with a rousing start, closing up 10 percent on the Nasdaq stock exchange on Thursday, DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced writes. At that price, shareholders valued the company at more than $28.6 billion, more than other United States technology names like Twitter and LinkedIn. Shares of the retailer closed at $20.90 for each American depositary receipt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hot Start for JD.com', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T11:53:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fe7ed5e-67f8-554c-88e6-21f50bbe2ea9', 'word_count': 2058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fe7ed5e-67f8-554c-88e6-21f50bbe2ea9'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '2 A.M. (LMN) WINTER’S BONE (2010) Jennifer Lawrence received her first Oscar nomination for her role as Ree Dolly, a teenager living in the Ozarks of southwestern Missouri who goes in search of her meth-cooking father after he puts up the family home to cover his bail and disappears. But her efforts to find him place her in a terrible dilemma: either betray the code of silence that keeps her clan proudly on the wrong side of the law or face destitution. (Above from left, Ashlee Thompson, Ms. Lawrence and Isaiah Stone in the film.) John Hawkes plays her uncle, whose silent menace soon erupts into violence, though he’s more compassionate than most. The harshness in Debra Granik’s “regional-realist morality tale,” based on the novel by Daniel Woodrell, “is not there to illuminate a sociological condition,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “Something more primal, almost Greek in its archaic power, is at stake in ‘Winter’s Bone,’ and its visual and emotional starkness do not feel like simple badges of authenticity.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/586d39f0-113b-52f9-af03-d0aeca69ecb1', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/586d39f0-113b-52f9-af03-d0aeca69ecb1'}, {'abstract': 'There has been no escaping the sonic shifts that have been reconfiguring country music of late: the country-rap crossover.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/arts/music/country-music-opens-its-ears.html', 'snippet': 'There has been no escaping the sonic shifts that have been reconfiguring country music of late: the country-rap crossover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — About a year and a half ago, as the country superstar Blake Shelton was working on songs for his latest album, “Based on a 