overished north of Argentina, sex traffickers search among the vulnerable for targets. Typically, they lure women with deceitful job offers and then traffic them to big cities, mining towns and agricultural regions, where they are forced into sex slavery.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/24-ARGENTINA/24-ARGENTINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/23/world/24-ARGENTINA/24-ARGENTINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/24-ARGENTINA/24-ARGENTINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/24-ARGENTINA/24-ARGENTINA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/24-ARGENTINA/24-ARGENTINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/23/world/24-ARGENTINA/24-ARGENTINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/world/24-ARGENTINA/24-ARGENTINA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Desperate Mother’s Search Leads to a Fight Against Sex Trafficking', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Desperate Mother’s Search Leads to a Fight Against Sex Trafficking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T15:18:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Gilbert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilbert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48ad1eea-96cf-5530-a833-0832698d5876', 'word_count': 1287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48ad1eea-96cf-5530-a833-0832698d5876'}, {'abstract': 'A lawsuit by Harper Lee against a museum in Alabama, which appeared to have been settled, has been scheduled to go to trial in November.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/judge-rules-that-harper-lee-can-renew-suit-against-museum/', 'snippet': 'A lawsuit by Harper Lee against a museum in Alabama, which appeared to have been settled, has been scheduled to go to trial in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wheels of justice apparently turn quickly in Alabama. When lawyers for Harper Lee filed to reinstate her lawsuit against the Monroe County Heritage Museum for what she says is the unauthorized marketing of merchandise based on her 1960 novel, “To Kill a Mockingbird,” a federal judge said that he needed more information. (The lawyers sought to reinstate the suit because, they said, the museum was backtracking on an out-of-court agreement reached in February.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Rules That Harper Lee Can Renew Suit Against Museum', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Rules Harper Lee Can Renew Lawsuit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Harper', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monroe County Heritage Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T15:20:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5331c7df-2d42-56b6-a22a-5b4f9311833b', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5331c7df-2d42-56b6-a22a-5b4f9311833b'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers on bicycles can go beyond the boundaries of the subway map when searching for a place to live.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/realestate/bikes-change-your-brooklyn-apartment-hunt.html', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers on bicycles can go beyond the boundaries of the subway map when searching for a place to live.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was cheaper rent that initially drew Jesse Warner-Levine, 34, and Hallie Nickelson, 33, to Wallabout, a fairly isolated Brooklyn neighborhood on the fringe of Clinton Hill near the Brooklyn Navy Yard. But it was bicycling that made them stay. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/realestate/25cover3/25cover3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy