 including Longo, Tunde Adebimpe of TV on the Radio and Monica Lewinsky, revealed secrets about their own kitchens.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/after-hours-robert-longo-tunde-adebimpe-cindy-sherman-monica-lewinsky-the-kitchen/', 'snippet': 'Since the night was hosted by the arts space the Kitchen, some of the guests, including Longo, Tunde Adebimpe of TV on the Radio and Monica Lewinsky, revealed secrets about their own kitchens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York artist Robert Longo may be most famous for his black-and-white Men in the Cities images of the early ’80s — which became such icons of yuppiedom that they appeared in Patrick Bateman’s apartment in the film adaptation of “American Psycho.” Like other New York art-world royalty, including Cindy Sherman, Philip Glass, Bill T. Jones, Laurie Anderson and Vito Acconci, he has long been a champion of the 43-year-old arts space The Kitchen, where he worked as a video curator for four years beginning in 1977.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Hours | A Family-Style Fete to Honor Robert Longo', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jonas, Joan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewinsky, Monica S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Longo, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherman, Cindy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T15:30:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb7a84f7-cdcb-5063-ad2f-7e91ea72e77c', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb7a84f7-cdcb-5063-ad2f-7e91ea72e77c'}, {'abstract': 'Schwa Fire is a new online magazine about language and life.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/new-online-magazine-honors-the-mighty-schwa/', 'snippet': 'Schwa Fire is a new online magazine about language and life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The schwa — the vowel sound at the end of the word “America,” represented in dictionary pronunciation guides with a backward and upside down “e” (ə) — is the most common vowel sound in the English language. And now it is also the namesake of a new online magazine about language and life.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Online Magazine Honors the Mighty Schwa', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Online Magazine Honors the Mighty Schwa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T15:49:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4b5758d-5cb7-5bc2-b40c-38aafdf1aaad', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4b5758d-5cb7-5bc2-b40c-38aafdf1aaad'}, {'abstract': 'The director of “Leviathan” said he had shown the film to Russia’s culture minister, who didn’t like it but who did not rule out government money for future projects.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/cannes-film-festival-a-movie-that-challenges-putin/', 'snippet': 'The director of “Leviathan” said he had shown the film to Russia’s culture minister, who didn’t like it but who did not rule out government money for future projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES — The Russian director Andrey Zvyagintsev’s latest film, “Leviathan,” tells the story of Kolia, a man fighting to keep his seaside house in a justice system all but beholden to a corrupt local mayor. The family drama can be read as the story of Job filtered through Chekhov, but also as a scathing indictment of Russia under President Vladimir Putin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/leviathan/leviathan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 498, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/leviathan/leviathan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 498}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/leviathan/leviathan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 850, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/leviathan/leviathan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1699, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/leviathan/leviathan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/leviathan/leviathan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/arts/leviathan/leviathan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}]