 {'main': 'HP’s Whitman on PC Decline and Job Cuts', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitman, Margaret C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T17:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a206fbce-dda6-55bc-9316-efbcf71240be', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a206fbce-dda6-55bc-9316-efbcf71240be'}, {'abstract': 'Timothy M. Dolan, the archbishop of New York and once the go-to American cardinal for many in the Vatican, is navigating changes in the Roman Catholic world wrought by the election of Pope Francis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/24/nyregion/a-new-role-for-cardinal-dolan-in-a-shifting-catholic-church.html', 'snippet': 'Timothy M. Dolan, the archbishop of New York and once the go-to American cardinal for many in the Vatican, is navigating changes in the Roman Catholic world wrought by the election of Pope Francis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cardinal Timothy M. Dolan lives in a 19th-century Madison Avenue mansion that connects to St. Patrick’s Cathedral. A cook and two housekeepers serve him and three other priests. A driver chauffeurs him around, though in a Chrysler minivan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/DOLAN/DOLAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', '