e': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b5b8bf7-6882-5961-a0bd-08caa1827a92', 'word_count': 1554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b5b8bf7-6882-5961-a0bd-08caa1827a92'}, {'abstract': '“In stark contrast to the Orange Revolution of 2004, few people in Ukraine are in a celebratory mood,” said Kyle Crichton, the editor in charge of coverage there. He went on to explain why.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/05/23/a-quick-take-on-ukraine-from-the-international-desk/', 'snippet': '“In stark contrast to the Orange Revolution of 2004, few people in Ukraine are in a celebratory mood,” said Kyle Crichton, the editor in charge of coverage there. He went on to explain why.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s the likely takeaway from the presidential election in Ukraine on Sunday? We asked Kyle Crichton, the editor in charge of coverage there, to weigh in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Quick Take on Ukraine From the International Desk', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crichton, Kyle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Donetsk (Ukraine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kiev (Ukraine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Luhansk (Ukraine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T17:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kyle Crichton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kyle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crichton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf4a8608-975c-5183-9fba-7cbf16ee973e', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf4a8608-975c-5183-9fba-7cbf16ee973e'}, {'abstract': 'His show at his new West Coast gallery, Regen Projects, includes his signature folded wall-mounted pieces and sculptures made with Angeleno rocks that remind him of his native country.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/new-exhibition-the-mexican-artist-gabriel-kuri-regen-projects-los-angeles/', 'snippet': 'His show at his new West Coast gallery, Regen Projects, includes his signature folded wall-mounted pieces and sculptures made with Angeleno rocks that remind him of his native country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Yorkers might recognize the work of Gabriel Kuri from the wheat-pasted posters that were plastered around town in 2011, when his signature repurposed tickets and receipts were the graphic identity of that year’s Armory Show. The Mexican artist is known for incorporating a range of detritus and found objects into his practice, combining man-made and organic materials to hint at a borderless global economy of objects. Eight months ago, he became one of a number of prominent artists to relocate to Los Angeles, moving from Brussels, where he’d spent the last decade. His first show at Regen Projects, his new West Coast gallery, opens Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/t-magazine/23mcgarry-kuri2/23mcgarry-kuri2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/23/t-magazine/23mcgarry-kuri2/23mcgarry-kuri2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/t-magazine/23mcgarry-kuri2/23mcgarry-kuri2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/t-magazine/23mcgarry-kuri2/23mcgarry-kuri2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1298, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/t-magazine/23mcgarry-kuri2/23mcgarry-kuri2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/23/t-magazine/23mcgarry-kuri2/23mcgarry-kuri2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/23/t-magazine/23mcgarry-kuri2/23mcgarry-kuri2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With a New Exhibition, the Mexican Artist Gabriel Kuri Makes His Home in L.A.', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T17:21:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, '