rce': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lucinda Williams, Rufus Wainwright and Norah Jones to Perform at the Clearwater Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clearwater Festival Announces Lineup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seeger, Pete', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shimabukuro, Jake', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wainwright, Rufus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Lucinda', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hudson River Sloop Clearwater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Croton-on-Hudson (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T17:39:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15d03bd2-24af-5dcd-a57d-3f60896319d8', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15d03bd2-24af-5dcd-a57d-3f60896319d8'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times asked Cardinal Timothy M. Dolan, New York’s archbishop, how the election of Pope Francis has changed the diocese and his personal life.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/cardinal-dolan-reflects-on-the-pope-francis-effect-in-his-life-and-work/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times asked Cardinal Timothy M. Dolan, New York’s archbishop, how the election of Pope Francis has changed the diocese and his personal life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cardinal Timothy M. Dolan, New York’s archbishop, traveled to Rome for the canonization of two popes, stayed on to speak at a communications conference there, jetted to Jordan to see the work of a Catholic charity he chairs, and once home, spoke at two graduations in the diocese — all in the past month. In other words, it was a typically busy month for him. So when The New York Times asked him, through a spokesperson, how the election of Pope Francis had changed the diocese and his own personal life, he asked that we submit a series of written questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/24DOLAN-CITYROOM/24DOLAN-CITYROOM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/24DOLAN-CITYROOM/24DOLAN-CITYROOM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/24DOLAN-CITYROOM/24DOLAN-CITYROOM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/24DOLAN-CITYROOM/24DOLAN-CITYROOM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/24DOLAN-CITYROOM/24DOLAN-CITYROOM-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/24DOLAN-CITYROOM/24DOLAN-CITYROOM-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/24DOLAN-CITYROOM/24DOLAN-CITYROOM-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cardinal Dolan Reflects on the ‘Pope Francis Effect’ in his Life and Work', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolan, Timothy M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T17:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c4373af-2d3d-5b2a-a03b-e6b4a321a1a9', 'word_count': 1466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c4373af-2d3d-5b2a-a03b-e6b4a321a1a9'}, {'abstract': 'Families that can flee New York City’s brutal summers by escaping to the beach or the mountains can engender ill will in those who cannot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/nyregion/sympathy-for-the-working-mother.html', 'snippet': 'Families that can flee New York City’s brutal summers by escaping to the beach or the mountains can engender ill will in those who cannot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One morning recently I received a call from a friend who told me she had decided to leave her job after many years, one in which she commanded a lot of authority and was very well paid, to begin a new and as yet undetermined phase; she was taking advantage of a lucrative buyout her company had offered. I pointed out the fortuitous timing — it was May, which meant she would have the summer off, which meant she could leave the city, which meant she would be envied by a great number of people (arguably this year more than others because The Farmers’ Almanac is predicting a summer so hot, wet and muggy that New York will essentially feel like Biloxi, Miss.).', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1455, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/nyregion/25BIG/25BIG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sympathy for the Working Mother', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sympathy for the Working Mother', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T17:49:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87c002a6-f92f-5fe0-9c6d-7425af4e1df2', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87c002a6-f92f-5fe0-9c6d-7425af4e1df2'}, {'abstract': 'The State Department appeared to go out of its way to pit one investigation into the Benghazi attacks against a new one being conducted by a select committee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/24/us/politics/kerry-agrees-to-testify-on-benghazi-with-caveats.html', 'snippet': 'The State Department appeared to go out of its way to pit one investigation into the Benghazi attacks against a new one being conducted by a select committee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Secretary of State John Kerry agreed on Friday to testify before the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform over the 2012 attacks on the American diplomatic mission in Benghazi, Libya, possibly exacerbating tensions between Republicans over competing inquiries.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/us/BENGHAZI/BENGHAZI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLa