t': 'What I needed after grading.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/friday-night-music-beirut/', 'snippet': 'What I needed after grading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Continuing on the grumpy old man theme, may I say how much I hate what passes for handwriting? Not only did I have trouble making out what they wrote, I had trouble figuring out who wrote it — when the blue book appears to come from a student named “grzzmph”, entering his grade in the spreadsheet is hard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Beirut', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-23T21:46:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f422e1b-d3e3-5fb6-9359-1ac319d1e719', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f422e1b-d3e3-5fb6-9359-1ac319d1e719'}, {'abstract': 'Kyle Bean, a conceptual artist in London, designed and constructed the “electrified body” that can be seen on this week’s cover. He recently talked about his creative process.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/under-cover-body-building/', 'snippet': 'Kyle Bean, a conceptual artist in London, designed and constructed the “electrified body” that can be seen on this week’s cover. He recently talked about his creative process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To illustrate Michael Behar’s cover story about how electricity delivered through the nervous system might be used to fight disease, the magazine’s art department turned to Kyle Bean, a conceptual artist in London. Gail Bichler, the art director, and Jason Sfetko, a designer, chose Bean because, in Bichler’s words, he “makes graphically striking dimensional pieces.” Bean, for his part, says that after reading Behar’s story, he was inspired by scientific diagrams in old textbooks to make the “electrified body” seen on this week’s cover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25cover_text/25cover_text-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25cover_text/25cover_text-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 730}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25cover_text/25cover_text-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 842, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25cover_text/25cover_text-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1684, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25cover_text/25cover_text-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25cover_text/25cover_text-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/magazine/25cover_text/25cover_text-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Cover: Body Building', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': N