f1f-bd7a-62b44f3a202d'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Exercise Was Beneficial, Sir,” Nicolas Bouchaud played the French critic and editor Serge Daney, who died in 1992.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/24/theater/a-critics-life-in-the-exercise-was-beneficial-sir.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Exercise Was Beneficial, Sir,” Nicolas Bouchaud played the French critic and editor Serge Daney, who died in 1992.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Cannes festival has recently reminded us, the French adore movies. And that enthusiasm was on delightful display onstage and in the audience Thursday at Gould Hall, at “The Exercise Was Beneficial, Sir” (“La Loi du Marcheur” is the French title), Nicolas Bouchaud’s solo portrayal of the editor and critic Serge Daney. (It was the end of a two-night run.) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24EXERCISE/24EXERCISE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 465, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24EXERCISE/24EXERCISE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 465}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24EXERCISE/24EXERCISE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 793, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24EXERCISE/24EXERCISE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1587, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/arts/24EXERCISE/24EXERCISE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail'