o powerful that lights dimmed when the switch was thrown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man who had shot to death his four young children, for reasons known only to him, sat in the wooden chair reserved for him at the Riverbend Maximum Security Institution in Nashville. His body was strapped tight and his head was freshly shaved, to enhance the conductivity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/us/CHAIR/CHAIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/24/us/CHAIR/CHAIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/us/CHAIR/CHAIR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/us/CHAIR/CHAIR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1106, 'width': 1887, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/us/CHAIR/CHAIR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/24/us/CHAIR/CHAIR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/us/CHAIR/CHAIR-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Specter of Past Executions Resurfaces in Tennessee', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Specter of Past Executions Resurfaces in Tennessee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holton, Daryl Keith (1961-2007)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-24T01:33:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c5232a8-ad69-58af-9a62-c9bf10194b2c', 'word_count': 1049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c5232a8-ad69-58af-9a62-c9bf10194b2c'}, {'abstract': 'Ukraine’s east is more deeply divided than at any point in the country’s history, and residents say it is possible that Sunday’s presidential election will do little to change that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/24/world/europe/calm-streets-mask-deep-divisions-in-donetsk.html', 'snippet': 'Ukraine’s east is more deeply divided than at any point in the country’s history, and residents say it is possible that Sunday’s presidential election will do little to change that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DONETSK, Ukraine — To the casual observer, this is not a city at war. Masked men are confined to a few buildings in the center of town, where children on in-line skates pass by. City workers tend to flowers in meticulously planted parks. Crowded open-air cafes spill onto sidewalks and into parks. Pfizer is holding a conference at the Ramada, where grilled sea bass is on the menu.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/world/24DONETSK/24DONETSK-articleLarge.jpg', 'h