, 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/24KOMODO2web/24KOMODO2web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/24KOMODO2web/24KOMODO2web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/24/nyregion/24KOMODO2web/24KOMODO2web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dragons Return to the Bronx Zoo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Zoo Wildlife Conservation Park', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Komodo Dragons (Lizards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-24T02:46:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f68b16a-709f-51d9-a4f1-0ba0fa075d89', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f68b16a-709f-51d9-a4f1-0ba0fa075d89'}, {'abstract': 'What reporters miss when they only talk to the people who are right in front of them.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/23/why-journalists-need-to-squint/', 'snippet': 'What reporters miss when they only talk to the people who are right in front of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you squint, and peer into the dark back room of the bamboo hut, you can barely make them out. Women huddled together in a cluster peek out from behind an open kitchen door. As the camera shoots back and forth between a community leader and the only villager with formal English training—both men—the women take turns retreating further into the scenery so they might shush the crying baby.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Journalists Need to Squint', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-24T02:48:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Sganga', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sganga', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14c3fdeb-e2ed-5cd1-8922-3a5fc596659b', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14c3fdeb-e2ed-5cd1-8922-3a5fc596659b'}, {'abstract': 'With voting for the European Parliament ending on Sunday, the elections will provide the best indicator yet of the depth of disillusionment in southern Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/24/world/europe/europes-right-and-left-on-march-to-populism.html', 'snippet': 'With voting for the European Parliament ending on Sunday, the elections will provide the best indicator yet of the depth of disillusionment in southern Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — For weeks, Beppe Grillo, the Italian political insurgent, has crisscrossed the nation in what might be called his vitriol tour. He has let loose zesty, bellowing insults against journalists, businessmen, Italian politicians and Angela Merkel, the German chancellor and avatar of European austerity. He has even taken a swipe at Dudu, the fluffy white poodle belonging to former Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima