ine': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc947bab-8d53-5587-9a37-c9648fd7f3ba', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc947bab-8d53-5587-9a37-c9648fd7f3ba'}, {'abstract': 'Pin boys once kept the game rolling at bowling alleys nationwide. But as a former one recently discovered, the job isn’t yet extinct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/jobs/on-work-strikes-spares-and-bruised-shins.html', 'snippet': 'Pin boys once kept the game rolling at bowling alleys nationwide. But as a former one recently discovered, the job isn’t yet extinct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In high school, I had one of the rarer jobs for a teenager in modern America. The time-honored types of teenage employment — jobs in fast food or in retailing at the mall — didn’t exist in the rural Pennsylvania town where I grew up. The few positions for restaurant servers, grocery stockers and cashiers were filled mostly by older women who needed that work to get by. Strangely, the job readily available to me was at the town bowling alley, where I worked one night a week as a pin boy. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/business/25-ONWORK/25-ONWORK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/business/25-ONWORK/25-ONWORK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 475}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/business/25-ONWORK/25-ONWORK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/business/25-ONWO