cle/1b122c16-08f2-5139-9dca-d943c3d98775', 'word_count': 1325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b122c16-08f2-5139-9dca-d943c3d98775'}, {'abstract': 'The option for dialogue on cyberissues should remain open, even as the Justice Department pursues its legal case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/opinion/sunday/america-china-and-the-hacking-threat.html', 'snippet': 'The option for dialogue on cyberissues should remain open, even as the Justice Department pursues its legal case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over several years of trying to persuade China to stop cyberattacks against corporate America, the Obama administration has gotten nowhere. What officials say is the most aggressive effort by any country to steal secrets from some of the most prominent and successful American companies is still going strong. Losses are estimated at billions of dollars in profits and thousands of jobs.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America, China and the Hacking Threat', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'America, China and the Hacking Threat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Industrial Espionage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-24T18:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_materia