 a result of all the changes it has made, that has not followed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CONCORD, N.C. — Marcos Ambrose, the Tasmanian Nascar driver and road course ace who has raced for small and midsize teams throughout his six-year Sprint Cup career, has never qualified for the annual playoff. But this may be his year. With a new qualifying format putting stronger emphasis on winning, Ambrose figures he has perhaps his best shot at making the expanded 16-team field for the playoff, the Chase for the Sprint Cup.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wins-First Mentality Has Not Lifted Nascar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wins-First Mentality Has Not Lifted Nascar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nascar Sprint Cup Series', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-24T19:34:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Viv Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Viv', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1af063ad-628e-5902-a795-4434b527c38e', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1af063ad-628e-5902-a795-4434b527c38e'}, {'abstract': 'Early election results showed the government coalition parties, Fine Gael and Labour, had each lost significant levels of support.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/world/europe/sinn-fein-benefits-as-ireland-moves-left.html', 'snippet': 'Early election results showed the government coalition parties, Fine Gael and Labour, had each lost significant levels of support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN — Ireland has taken a decisive step to the left in local and European elections, where early returns on Saturday showed that the big winners were Sinn Fein, formerly the political wing of the Irish Republican Army, and Socialist independent candidates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sinn Fein Benefits as Ireland Moves Left', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sinn Fein', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADAMS, GERRY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-24T19:39:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Dalby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dalby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca8c1f86-fb9f-5f60-b56f-0dbba17728d2', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca8c1f86-fb9f-5f60-b56f-0dbba17728d2'}, {'abstract': 'The president is expected to chart in a speech at West Point a middle course between isolationism and military intervention in international conflicts, from Syria’s civil war to Russia’s incursions in Ukraine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/world/obama-to-detail-a-broader-foreign-policy-agenda.html', 'snippet': 'The president is expected to chart in a speech at West Point a middle course between isolationism and military intervention in international conflicts, from Syria’s civil war to Russia’s incursions in Ukraine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama, seeking to answer criticism that he has forsaken America’s leadership role, plans to lay out a retool