ole': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dff7f9a-0dbe-5b5d-b60e-624d890ff266', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dff7f9a-0dbe-5b5d-b60e-624d890ff266'}, {'abstract': 'A program of rarely performed works investigates the fervent embrace of belligerent nationalism by composers after the outbreak of World War I.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/arts/music/composers-struck-by-homeland-fever.html', 'snippet': 'A program of rarely performed works investigates the fervent embrace of belligerent nationalism by composers after the outbreak of World War I.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A century after the outbreak of World War I, the fervent embrace of belligerent nationalism by educated Europeans continues to puzzle and fascinate historians. The conductor and scholar Leon Botstein investigates this question in a fascinating program of rarely performed works by composers swept up in nationalist movements. The American Symphony Orchestra will be joined by the Collegiate Chorale Singers and three fine soloists: the pianist Blair McMillen, the bass Denis Sedov and the tenor Corey Bix. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE6/25GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE6/25GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE6/25GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE6/25GUIDE6-