'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fa17952-ec6c-53cb-9277-c66855cfe4d4', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fa17952-ec6c-53cb-9277-c66855cfe4d4'}, {'abstract': 'The British painter Joseph Mallord William Turner revolutionized the stodgy tradition of marine painting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/arts/design/when-seascapes-left-stodgy-behind.html', 'snippet': 'The British painter Joseph Mallord William Turner revolutionized the stodgy tradition of marine painting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether you agree with the Victorian critic John Ruskin that the British painter Joseph Mallord William Turner was a talent on par with Shakespeare, you have to acknowledge that Turner revolutionized the stodgy tradition of marine painting. On Saturday, more than 100 of his seascapes — including his frothy, experimental renderings of wind-whipped oceans — will go on view at the Peabody Essex Museum in Salem, Mass.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE4/25GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE4/25GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE4/25GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE4/25GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1518, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE4/25GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE4/25GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE4/25GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Seascapes Left Stodgy Behind', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Seascapes Left Stodgy Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Joseph Mallord William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-24T20:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acadba12-add6-5ffc-b139-4faac65b7b2e', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acadba12-add6-5ffc-b139-4faac65b7b2e'}, {'abstract': 'Frederic Franklin, who died at 99 last May, was one of modern ballet’s most irrepressible figures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/arts/dance/leaping-to-honor-a-first-name-guy.html', 'snippet': 'Frederic Franklin, who died at 99 last May, was one of modern ballet’s most irrepressible figures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost everyone involved with dance knew him, and they all just called him Freddie. Frederic Franklin, who died at 99 last May, was one of modern ballet’s most irrepressible figures. He was always onstage, performing mime roles in his later years. Blessed with an amazing memory and an ability to communicate, he also staged ballets, including American Ballet Theater’s “Coppélia,” the 19th-century comic classic, which the company will dance in his honor. (7:30 p.m. Friday, 2 p.m. and 8 p.m. Saturday, Metropolitan Opera House, Lincoln Center; 212-362-6000, abt.org.) From the Horse’s Mouth, a group that brings dance people together, is presenting three evenings dedicated to Franklin, featuring reminiscences, films and videos. Participants will vary from night to night, and presentations will emphasize his contributions to male dancing. (7:30 p.m. Friday through Sunday, Schimmel Center for the Arts, Pace University, 3 Spruce Street, between Park Row and Gold Street, Lower Manhattan; 212-346-1715, schimmel.pace.edu.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE1/25GUIDE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE1/25GUIDE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE1/25GUIDE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE1/25GUIDE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE1/25GUIDE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE1/25GUIDE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE1/25GUIDE1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaping to Honor a First-Name Guy', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leaping to Honor a First-Name Guy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-24T20:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d52fc8c5-ce77-5e4b-ae2d-587d10c8a396', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d52fc8c5-ce77-5e4b-ae2d-587d10c8a396'}, {'abstract': 'Theo Croker has a new album, “Afrophysicist,” showing his breadth, with plush funk and rock idioms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/25/arts/music/young-man-with-a-horn.html', 'snippet': 'Theo Croker has a new album, “Afrophysicist,” showing his breadth, with plush funk and rock idioms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The jazz trumpeter Theo Croker is the grandson of Doc Cheatham, who played the same instrument with great beauty and economy until his death at the age of 91 in 1997. In a reverse of the typical trumpeter’s story, Cheatham seemed to reach his peak in the last phase of his life. Mr. Croker, 29, may have learned something from his grandfather’s pacing. He started with plenty of promise and made a very good record in his early 20s (“The Fundamentals,” on Left Sided), but rather than speed-track his career, he worked in Shanghai for seven years, in clubs and on TV. He has a new album, “Afrophysicist” (DDB/Sony), showing his breadth, with plush funk and rock idioms, some subtle and complex new-jazz ones, a ballad standard (“Moody’s Mood for Love”) and high-wire soloing. He’ll play this week with his band DVRK Funk, including the pianist Sullivan Fortner and the drummer Kassa Overall, with the singer Dee Dee Bridgewater as guest. (7:30 and 9:30 p.m. Tuesday and Wednesday, Jazz Standard, 116 East 27th Street, Manhattan, 212-576-2232, jazzstandard.com.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE5/25GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE5/25GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE5/25GUIDE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE5/25GUIDE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE5/25GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE5/25GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/25/arts/25GUIDE5/25GUIDE5-thum