': 'It was the fourth United States Championship victory in five years for both Gata Kamsky and Irina Krush.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a struggle for them, but both Gata Kamsky and Irina Krush successfully defended their national titles on Tuesday by winning three-way playoffs at the United States Championship in St. Louis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Champs Retain Titles in Playoffs After Late Rallies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Champs Retain Titles in Playoffs After Late Rallies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClain, Dylan Loeb', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kamsky, Gata', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krush, Irina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akobian, Varuzhan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-25T01:53:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60a969d7-7bee-5d7f-8e86-958f380f4c33', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60a969d7-7bee-5d7f-8e86-958f380f4c33'}, {'abstract': 'Put a few primary “Orphan Black” characters in a normal environment, with regular people, and see what kind of shenanigans ensue.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/24/orphan-black-recap-so-a-clone-walks-into-a-bar/', 'snippet': 'Put a few primary “Orphan Black” characters in a normal environment, with regular people, and see what kind of shenanigans ensue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the highlights from the first season of “Orphan Black” came in Episode 6, when Sarah (Tatiana Maslany), Felix (Jordan Gavaris), Paul (Dylan Bruce) and Victor (Michael Mando) crashed a neighborhood potluck at Alison’s home. In the midst of this suburban party — while guests congregated in the living room and kitchen, laughing, drinking and listening to ’90s pop hits like “Lovefool” by The Cardigans — the clones and their associates engaged in and/or tried to cover up various forms of torture in the basement and the garage. The resulting juxtaposition from that setup illustrated how different the clones’ lives are from the rest of the general populace. It was also a goldmine for both comedy and dramatic tension. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/orphanblack0206/orphanblack0206-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/orphanblack0206/orphanblack0206-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/orphanblack0206/orphanblack0206-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/orphanblack0206/orphanblack0206-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/orphanblack0206/orphanblack0206-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/22/arts/orphanblack020