his 25th-anniversary broadcast from the West Lawn of the United States Capitol, which will commemorate the 70th anniversary of the World War II D-Day invasion on the beaches at Normandy. The “American Idol” winner Caleb Johnson will sing the national anthem. Danielle Bradbery, Megan Hilty, Jackie Evancho and Anthony Kearns will perform with the National Symphony Orchestra, above, conducted by Jack Everly. Other participants include former Secretary of State Colin L. Powell, the actress Dianne Wiest, members of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, the Army Herald Trumpets, the Army Chorus, the Soldiers’ Chorus of the United States Army Field Band, the Navy Band Sea Chanters and the Air Force Singing Sergeants. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-25T15:27:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0bf1019-db3b-56fc-b388-313c7c93e5bc', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0bf1019-db3b-56fc-b388-313c7c93e5bc'}, {'abstract': 'Elliot Rodger, the 22-year-old who the police said killed six people near the campus of the University of California, Santa Barbara, expressed his frustration in an autobiography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/05/25/us/shooting-document.html', 'snippet': 'Elliot Rodger, the 22-year-old who the police said killed six people near the campus of the University of California, Santa Barbara, expressed his frustration in an 