ain': 'Obama Surprises Troops in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-25T22:56:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'Reuters', 'person': [], 'organization': 'Reuters'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/adb790fe-754a-5c3d-b075-95e22eaa726a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/adb790fe-754a-5c3d-b075-95e22eaa726a'}, {'abstract': 'The contemporary choreographer John Heginbotham will receive the eighth annual Jacob’s Pillow Dance Award.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/26/arts/dance/jacobs-pillow-prize-is-announced.html', 'snippet': 'The contemporary choreographer John Heginbotham will receive the eighth annual Jacob’s Pillow Dance Award.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The contemporary choreographer John Heginbotham, above, will receive the eighth annual Jacob’s Pillow Dance Award. Mr. Heginbotham is to accept the award, which comes with a cash prize of $25,000, on June 14, the opening night of this year’s Jacob’s Pillow Dance Festival. His company, Dance Heginbotham, will also perform a new work called “Chalk and Soot” at the festival, from July 30 to Aug. 3. Jacob’s Pillow, in Becket, Mass., established the award in 2007 to recognize outstanding contributions to dance. Previous recipients include last year’s winner, Michelle Dorrance; Crystal Pite; and Bill T. Jones.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '