: 'nyt://article/30287e5d-4845-53a2-b4d6-6023e48f6510'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Jacobs reports from Yushu, a town in Qinghai Province in China’s west that was flattened by an earthquake four years ago, that the vast rebuilding effort has alienated many there.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/26/renovation-and-controversy-at-the-roof-of-the-world/', 'snippet': 'Andrew Jacobs reports from Yushu, a town in Qinghai Province in China’s west that was flattened by an earthquake four years ago, that the vast rebuilding effort has alienated many there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years and $7.2 billion later, Yushu, a city high on the Tibetan Plateau that was leveled by a calamitous earthquake, has been largely made whole, as I reported from there recently. There are thousands of new homes, dozens of schools and impressive-looking museums. The reconstruction effort was made all the more challenging by the city’s isolation and thin air.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Renovation and Controversy at the Roof of the World', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuns', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Andrew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yushu (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-26T12:07:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', '