nippet': 'Did the French economist, in using a simple spreadsheet program, use the right tool for the job of analyzing economic inequality over time?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like Carmen Reinhart and Kenneth Rogoff before him, Thomas Piketty has had questions  raised about his analysis; in his case, his work on wealth inequality. Though I can’t knowledgeably comment on the questions or the analysis, I can comment on the technology that Ms. Reinhardt, Mr. Rogoff and Mr. Piketty chose to do their work: the spreadsheet. This choice can increase the chances of error in complex analysis, but it also can make finding errors by nonexperts easier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thomas Piketty and Spreadsheets', 'kicker': 'Numbers, Numbers', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thomas Piketty and Spreadsheets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piketty, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reinhart, Carmen M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogoff, Kenneth S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-26T14:26:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Frakt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frakt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cebe5cdf-26fa-5637-852a-62cb490939a5', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cebe5cdf-26fa-5637-852a-62cb490939a5'}, {'abstract': 'One hundred fifty years after the first burial at Arlington, the national cemetery is running short of room.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/26/in-eighteen-hundred-sixty-four-the-burying-began-arlington-ceme