: 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-26T15:08:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'A.J. Chavar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chavar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/7def2c16-57d7-50d1-b565-bd569039b6e8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/7def2c16-57d7-50d1-b565-bd569039b6e8'}, {'abstract': 'Can willpower save Europe?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/26/european-green-lanterns/', 'snippet': 'Can willpower save Europe?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sitting in a room listening to EU officials reacting to the European Parliament elections — and it seems to me that they’re deep in denial. Barroso just declared that the euro had nothing to do with the crisis, that it was all failed policies at the national level; a few minutes ago he said that Europe’s real problem is a lack of political will.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Green Lanterns', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-26T15:13:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e032bad3-413b-5ab4-aaa7-7a6c9f62bb47', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e032bad3-413b-5ab4-aaa7-7a6c9f62bb47'}, {'abstract': 'Deductibles and co-pays keep health spending down while not harming health for most people, but in this area, more may not be better.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/27/upshot/health-care-cost-sharing-works-up-to-a-point.html', 'snippet': 'Deductibles and co-pays keep health spending down while not harming health for most people, but in this area, more may not be better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My colleague Aaron Carroll wrote last week that directly charging consumers for part of their health care costs (the practice known as cost-sharing) can harm the health of poorer or sicker people. But for the rest of us, it seems to reduce spending without harming health. This is the basic conclusion of a famous 1970s experiment funded by the RAND Corporation that randomly assigned families to different levels of responsibility for medical costs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/upshot/27up-costsharingsub/27up-costsharingsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/27/upshot/27up-costsharingsub/27up-costsharingsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/upshot/27up-costsharingsub/27up-costsharingsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/upshot/27up-costsharingsub/27up-costsharingsub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1150, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/upshot/27up-costsharingsub/27up-costsharingsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/27/upshot/27up-costsharingsub/27up-costsharingsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/upshot/27up-costsharingsub/27up-costsharingsub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Care Cost-Sharing Works — Up to a Point', 'kicker': 'The New Health Care', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rand Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-26T15:24:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Frakt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frakt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb49e1c8-2bcc-500f-ae8d-afb3a2797f5d', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb49e1c8-2bcc-500f-ae8d-afb3a2797f5d'}, {'abstract': 'Two new wind turbine installations have gone up recently, and at least half a dozen more are on the horizon, though it remains to be seen how popular they will become.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/27/nyregion/turbines-pop-up-on-new-york-roofs-along-with-questions-of-efficiency.html', 'snippet': 'Two new wind turbine installations have gone up recently, and at least half a dozen more are on the horizon, though it remains to be seen how 