age', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/science/27TIER/27TIER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/27/science/27TIER/27TIER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/science/27TIER/27TIER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/science/27TIER/27TIER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/science/27TIER/27TIER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/27/science/27TIER/27TIER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/science/27TIER/27TIER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Win the Lottery (Happily)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Win the Lottery (Happily)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tierney, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Happiness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-26T19:01:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Tierney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tierney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c2b2389-713c-5251-9448-0b899247ec5d', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c2b2389-713c-5251-9448-0b899247ec5d'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Phillips’s “Becoming Freud: The Making of a Psychoanalyst” comments on the first 50 years of Freud’s 83-year life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/27/books/becoming-freud-recounts-the-psychoanalysts-first-50-years.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Phillips’s “Becoming Freud: The Making of a Psychoanalyst” comments on the first 50 years of Freud’s 83-year life.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Becoming Freud: The Making of a Psychoanalyst,” by the English psychoanalyst, editor and writer Adam Phillips, is about the first 50 years of Freud’s 83-year life. This short, dense book is partly a group of abbreviated biographical commentaries, partly about Freud’s career and writings until 1906. It uses both ordinary language and literary terminology to replace traditional psychoanalytic terms and jargon, although Mr. Phillips’s understanding and theorizing are familiar and generally conformable. It is also a less-than-perfect performance.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/arts/book/book-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 886, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/27/arts/book/book-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 886}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width