Behind the Cover Story: Michael Behar on ‘Star Trek,’ Acupuncture and Bioelectronics', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACUPUNCTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nerves and Nervous System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalai Lama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GlaxoSmithKline PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-26T21:47:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d269fba5-fffc-5335-8dd2-4e76e0283fa9', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d269fba5-fffc-5335-8dd2-4e76e0283fa9'}, {'abstract': 'New releases include albums by Lee Bains III & the Glory Fires, Sleaford Mods and Owen Pallett.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/27/arts/music/new-albums-from-lee-bains-iii-the-glory-fires-sleaford-mods-and-owen-pallett.html', 'snippet': 'New releases include albums by Lee Bains III & the Glory Fires, Sleaford Mods and Owen Pallett.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From Lynyrd Skynyrd to the Black Crowes to the Drive-By Truckers, Southern rockers have been acutely self-conscious about where they come from, writing songs steeped in history, local color, memories, everyday life, expectations and paradoxes. Lee Bains III & the Glory Fires, a four-man band from Alabama, proudly join the Southern-rock tradition of wild-eyed music hitched to serious deliberation. “Dereconstructed,” the band’s second album, ponders Southern identity in a welter of cranked-up guitars, bristling drums and rasping, hollering vocals. It’s pandemonium with a conscience.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/arts/jpnewmusic4/jpnewmusic4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/27/arts/jpnewmusic4/jpnewmusic4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/arts/jpnewmusic4/jpnewmusic4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/arts/jpnewmusic4/jpnewmusic4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1458, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/arts/jpnewmusic4/jpnewmusic4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/27/arts/jpnewmusic4/jpnewmusic4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/arts/jpnewmusic4/jpnewmusic4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Southern Rock, Proudly Revised', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Southern Rock, Proudly Revised', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pallett, Owen', 'rank': 4