//article/7aaea54c-f95e-544c-aa72-7af7b483c432'}, {'abstract': 'Narendra Modi was sworn in on Monday as India’s prime minister. Among those attending the ceremony was Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif of Pakistan, hinting that the two countries may revive a moribund peace process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/27/world/asia/india-prime-minister-narendra-modi-swearing-in-ceremony.html', 'snippet': 'Narendra Modi was sworn in on Monday as India’s prime minister. Among those attending the ceremony was Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif of Pakistan, hinting that the two countries may revive a moribund peace process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Outside the sandstone palace that was built for the viceroy of British-ruled India, before a crowd that included corporate titans, Bollywood heartthrobs and saffron-robed Hindu holy men, Narendra Modi, the son of a provincial tea-seller, was sworn in on Monday as India’s prime minister.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/world/INDIA/INDIA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/27/world/INDIA/INDIA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/world/INDIA/INDIA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/world/INDIA/INDIA-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/world/INDIA/INDIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/27/world/INDIA/INDIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/world/INDIA/INDIA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Signs of Diplomacy as Indian Leader Is Sworn In', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Signs of Diplomacy as Indian Leader Is Sworn In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-26T23:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7c1e762-d6d8-5dc2-8c78-1128d86142ac', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7c1e762-d6d8-5dc2-8c78-1128d86142ac'}, {'abstract': 'In a series of cases, immigrants have been questioned and detained in courthouses, eroding their willingness to participate in the judicial system, advocates and politicians say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/27/nyregion/advocates-seek-to-make-courthouses-off-limits-for-immigration-officials.html', 'snippet': 'In a series of cases, immigrants have been questioned and detained in courthouses, eroding their willingness to participate in the judicial system, advocates and politicians say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rosario Socope, a Guatemalan immigrant in the country illegally, had an unwelcome surprise waiting for her when she attended a pretrial hearing on a felony charge at a courthouse in Brooklyn this month. As she stepped out of the courtroom into a public hallway, she was approached by immigration agents seeking to deport her.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Advocates Seek to Make Courthouses Off Limits for Immigration Officials', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Push to Keep Immigration Authorities Out of Courts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Semple, Kirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Immigration and Customs Enforcement (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-27T00:13:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd55cb12-3823-5476-b9b7-cbea8a74ba2b', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd55cb12-3823-5476-b9b7-cbea8a74ba2b'}, {'abstract': 'Ethical Electric, a start-up founded by a former Washington political operative, allows customers to sign up for electricity from renewable sources.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/27/business/energy-environment/applying-the-lessons-of-politics-to-green-power.html', 'snippet': 'Ethical Electric, a start-up founded by a former Washington political operative, allows customers to sign up for electricity from renewable sources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Over the years, Tom Matzzie — by working as a political operative on John Kerry’s 2004 presidential campaign and on building the antiwar movement that helped usher President Obama into office — became convinced that the key to creating change was to make it easy for people to participate.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/business/Power/Power-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/27/business/Power/Power-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/business/Power/Power-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/business/Power/Power-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1403, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/business/Power/Power-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/27/business/Power/Power-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '