pher Pierpaolo Ferrari, release a book capturing avant-garde furniture from the late ’60s in often-outrageous tableaux.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a photograph in “1968: Radical Italian Furniture” — the new book (out May 31) by the artist and provocateur Maurizio Cattelan and his frequent collaborator, the photographer Pierpaolo Ferrari — of a woman dressed in pink trousers, standing on top of a desk. Crouched down expertly in heels, she stares blankly into the camera and urinates — quite deliberately, it seems — onto the piece of furniture beneath her.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf | A Surrealist Ode to a Radical Era in Furniture Design', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revolutionary Design', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cattelan, Maurizio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-27T14:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gazelle Emami', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gazelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Emami', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/722c9e0d-46ba-57ab-87f7-dedb64c759a9', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/722c9e0d-46ba-57ab-87f7-dedb64c759a9'}, {'abstract': 'The talk-show host will make a rare appearance outside his television show.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/27/letterman-to-moderate-seinfeld-discussion/', 'snippet': 'The talk-show host will make a rare appearance outside his television show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that David Letterman is staring retirement in the eye, he’s suddenly considering all kinds of opportunities he probably thought he’d 