, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06b54756-1a23-5569-ae97-f1ef241a695b', 'word_count': 1698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06b54756-1a23-5569-ae97-f1ef241a695b'}, {'abstract': 'Hector Xavier Monsegur, who prosecutors said helped the F.B.I. take down an aggressive group of hackers, was given a greatly reduced sentence of time served.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/28/nyregion/hacker-who-helped-disrupt-cyberattacks-is-allowed-to-walk-free.html', 'snippet': 'Hector Xavier Monsegur, who prosecutors said helped the F.B.I. take down an aggressive group of hackers, was given a greatly reduced sentence of time served.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York man whose cooperation helped the authorities infiltrate the shadowy world of computer hacking and disrupt at least 300 cyberattacks on targets that included the United States military, courts and private companies was given a greatly reduced sentence on Tuesday of time served and allowed to walk free.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hacker Who Helped Disrupt Cyberattacks Is Allowed to Walk Free', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hacker Who Became a Federal Informer Is Allowed to Walk Free', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monsegur, Hector Xavier', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anonymous (Internet Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preska, Loretta A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-27T16:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c901edc-920b-5f3c-8191-65ef419468bb', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c901edc-920b-5f3c-8191-65ef419468bb'}, {'abstract': 'The 82-year-old Japanese artist, who created the ephemeral installation currently on view at the Glass House in New Canaan, Conn., talks about her preferred material and the relationship between art and nature.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/27/q-and-a-fujiko-nakaya-glass-house-veil-robert-rauschenberg/', 'snippet': 'The 82-year-old Japanese artist, who created the ephemeral installation currently on view at the Glass House in New Canaan, Conn., talks about her preferred material and the relationship between art and nature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last 40 years, the Japanese artist Fujiko Nakaya has been installing sculptures made of fog throughout the world—in fields and forests, in public plazas and atop parking garages, even in a park designed for kids. A new fog sculpture called “Veil” is on view at the Glass House in New Canaan, Conn., through Nov. 30. To create it, the 82-year-old artist spent nearly a year testing wind patterns and carefully calibrating the 800 mist-generating nozzles that are now installed across the landscape. The temporary sculpture alternately envelops and reveals Philip Johnson’s iconic modernist structure, creating an effect that is at once romantic and contemporary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/27/t-magazine/27miller-nakaya/27miller-nakaya-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/27/t-magazine/27miller-nakaya/27miller-nakaya-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth