:24:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e00b20a-0676-5fe6-9210-55c47738db14', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e00b20a-0676-5fe6-9210-55c47738db14'}, {'abstract': 'The ubiquitous multihyphenate kicked off his “G I R L” show at Emmanuel Perrotin’s new space with a party and not-so-secret performance.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/27/pharrell-curated-exhibition-paris-girl-emmanuel-perrotin-marina-abramovic/', 'snippet': 'The ubiquitous multihyphenate kicked off his “G I R L” show at Emmanuel Perrotin’s new space with a party and not-so-secret performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WhoPharrell Williams was in Paris last night to fete the exhibition he curated\xa0at\xa0the new Emmanuel Perrotin space there: “G I R L,” inspired by Williams’s new album of the same name. The multitasking man of the moment referred to the process of putting the exhibition together as “another day of school for Pharrell Williams.” The artists Daniel Arsham, Sophie Calle, Marina Abramovic, JR, Mr. and Laurent Grasso, who contributed works to the show, were on hand, as were the fashion-world luminaries Haider Ackermann, Peter Lindbergh, Alber Elbaz and Vanessa Bruno. The Korean superstar rapper G-Dragon arrived with his entourage, including the stylist Xin Yang, who will be launching his own line of too-cool-for-school men’s wear in Paris next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art and Fashion Stars Toast a Pharrell-Curated Exhibition in Paris', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMOVIC, MARINA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elbaz, Alber', 'ran