organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f79e282-05fe-545d-b170-8b506c8f46b6', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f79e282-05fe-545d-b170-8b506c8f46b6'}, {'abstract': 'In “Gebo and the Shadow,” a family struggles with a relative’s long disappearance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/28/movies/gebo-and-the-shadow-directed-by-manoel-de-oliveira.html', 'snippet': 'In “Gebo and the Shadow,” a family struggles with a relative’s long disappearance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The family in “Gebo and the Shadow,” Manoel de Oliveira’s 2012 film adaptation of a play by the early-20th-century Portuguese writer Raul Brandão, has been stuck in a limbo of anguish and tedium. A young man named João (Ricardo Trêpa) has been missing for eight years, and every evening his father, Gebo (Michael Lonsdale), loses himself in ledgers and business documents. João’s mother (Claudia Cardinale) and wife (Leonor Silveira) bring Gebo coffee and pester him for news of the prodigal. João’s fate is ambiguous, which makes the grief and anxiety of his wife and mother all the more acute, and his father’s evasiveness all the more troubling.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/28GEBO/28GEBO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/28GEBO/28GEBO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 321}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/28GEBO/28GEBO-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 548, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/28GEBO/28