mation-flows-s-e-c-faces-difficulty-bottling-it-up/', 'snippet': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission is caught trying to control too much information and monitoring information it can’t even see or hear, Steven Davidoff writes in the Deal Professor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wall Street, information is “the most valuable commodity,” to quote a line from the 1987 movie “Wall Street.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/28/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1114, 'width': 1114, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/28/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Information Flows, S.E.C. Faces Difficulty Bottling It Up', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Information Flows, S.E.C. Faces Difficulty Bottling It Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-27T22:06:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c5c343a-a9c0-5efd-8249-414fbe09e4f4', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c5c343a-a9c0-5efd-8249-414fbe09e4f4'}, {'abstract': 'DanceAfrica delivered rousing performances by groups from Buffalo, Madagascar and Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/28/arts/dance/groupe-bakomanga-and-asase-yaa-perform-at-danceafrica.html', 'snippet': 'DanceAfrica delivered rousing performances by groups from Buffalo, Madagascar and Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter the lineup at DanceAfrica, one performer always delivers: Charles (known as Chuck) Davis, the revered and beloved master of ceremonies, who founded the festival in 1977 and who, it was recently announced, will step down as director in 2016. Can anyone charm and command a crowd as he does? On Monday afternoon at the Brooklyn Academy of Music’s Howard Gilman Opera House, even his “no flash photography” announcement drew wild cheers from the audience. His successor, Abdel R. Salaam, has a tough act to follow.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/dance1/dance1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/dance1/dance1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/dance1/dance1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/dance1/dance1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/dance1/dance1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/dance1/dance1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/arts/dance1/dance1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'African Dance, Rhythms and Folksy Beats, Pitched to Fill a Basket', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'African Dance, Rhythms and Folksy Beats, Pitched to Fill a Basket', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DanceAfrica (Danc