e have warned Western journalists to stay away from the square.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Even by the standards of the clampdowns that routinely mark politically sensitive dates in China, the approach this year to June 4, the anniversary of the day in 1989 when soldiers brutally ended student-led protests in Tiananmen Square, has been particularly severe.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/world/CRACKDOWN-1/CRACKDOWN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/28/world/CRACKDOWN-1/CRACKDOWN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/world/CRACKDOWN-1/CRACKDOWN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/world/CRACKDOWN-1/CRACKDOWN-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/world/CRACKDOWN-1/CRACKDOWN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/28/world/CRACKDOWN-1/CRACKDOWN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/world/CRACKDOWN-1/CRACKDOWN-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiananmen Square Anniversary Prompts Campaign of Silence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tiananmen Square Anniversary Prompts Campaign of Silence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tiananmen Square (Beijing)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wu, Vivian', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pu Zhiqiang', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yu Fangqiang', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hao Jian', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xu Youyu', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-28T00:29:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bf3bdb6-46ca-57c7-b07a-cf76441328bb', 'word_count': 1274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bf3bdb6-46ca-57c7-b07a-cf76441328bb'}, {'abstract': 'A “special rapporteur on the right to food” confirms how mainstream what once seemed like radical thinking about diet has become.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/28/opinion/bittman-foods-big-picture-guy.html', 'snippet': 'A “special rapporteur on the right to food” confirms how mainstream what once seemed like radical thinking about diet has become.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wish Olivier de Schutter had the power to match the acuity of his analysis, but it’s great that we’ve had an advocate whose vision is as broad as that of the corporations who have for the last 50 years determined global food policy. Since 2008, the human rights lawyer has had the title of United Nations special rapporteur on the right to food. (His second three-year term ends this week.) This is obviously not a genius marketing title and, even worse, the position carries no real power.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bittman-circular/bittman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bittman-circular/bittman-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bittman-circular/bittman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bittman-circular/bittman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bittman-circular/bittman-circular-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Food’s Big-Picture Guy', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Schutter, Olivier', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-28T00:29:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/27a03e09-f89c-5412-a08f-ec50ae3e7a96', 'word_count': 1234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27a03e09-f89c-5412-a08f-ec50ae3e7a96'}, {'abstract': 'With the Supreme Court’s ruling against Florida’s strict I.Q. rule, the momentum continues in limiting the use of capital punishment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/28/opinion/the-shrinking-death-penalty.html', 'snippet': 'With the Supreme Court’s ruling against Florida’s strict I.Q. rule, the momentum continues in limiting the use of capital punishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twelve years after it banned the execution of intellectually disabled people, the Supreme Court on Tuesday clarified and thus reaffirmed the essence of its ruling by striking down a Florida law requiring that a defendant claiming that condition show an I.Q. score of 70 or below.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline':