torney general suggested Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. hinted Tuesday that the Justice Department might choose not to jail a New York Times reporter for defying a subpoena forcing him to discuss his confidential sources — even as the Obama administration continues to pursue the right to do so before the Supreme Court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holder Hints Reporter May Be Spared Jail in Leak', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holder Hints Reporter May Be Spared Jail in Leak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News Sources, Confidential Status of', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subpoenas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attorneys General', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Risen, James', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'State of War: The Secret History of the CIA and the Bush Administration (Book)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sterling, Jeffrey Alexander', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'or