m a 4-1 deficit to tie the score in the second period, the Canadiens responded with three consecutive goals and forced a Game 6.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTREAL — There was no celebration for the Rangers on Tuesday night, no triumphant passage to the Stanley Cup finals. Instead, there was nastiness, chaotic defense and uncharacteristically flawed goaltending, with Henrik Lundqvist chased from the nets by a deluge of Montreal goals and with his substitute, Cam Talbot, faring little better. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/sports/RANGERS2/RANGERS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/28/sports/RANGERS2/RANGERS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/sports/RANGERS2/RANGERS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/sports/RANGERS2/RANGERS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1446, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/sports/RANGERS2/RANGERS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/28/sports/RANGERS2/RANGERS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/sports/RANGERS2/RANGERS2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thu