many of whom had been hospitalized for dementia or stroke complications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — A fire broke out at a hospital annex in South Korea early Wednesday, killing 21 people and injuring seven others and further rattling a country still traumatized by a recent ferry disaster. The police were holding a patient in connection with the fire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Patient Is Held After Fire at South Korea Hospital Kills 21', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Patient Is Held After Fire at South Korea Hospital Kills 21', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARSON', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-28T06:33:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca14e60f-70d7-5934-8e00-f002898481c1', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca14e60f-70d7-5934-8e00-f002898481c1'}, {'abstract': 'A spate of elderly suicides has followed announcement of a government phase-out of full burials in favor of cremation around the city of Anqing, the Chinese news media reported.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/28/elderly-suicides-reported-after-city-announces-phase-out-on-burials/', 'snippet': 'A spate of elderly suicides has followed announcement of a government phase-out of full burials in favor of cremation around the city of Anqing, the Chinese news media reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Officials in China have a rule and target for almost everything\xa0— the legacy of thousands of years of bureaucratic thinking and the Communist Party’s own planned economy — even for a person’s final resting place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elderly Suicides Reported After City Announces Phase-out on Burials', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cremation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beijing News, The', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Daily', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Anhui (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-28T07:07:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72fefc28-ef7c-5ddf-9c80-9e9021df4fa1', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72fefc28-ef7c-5ddf-9c80-9e9021df4fa1'}, {'abstract': 'The drug maker said the British regulator had opened a formal criminal inquiry into its “commercial practices.” The company gave no further details.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/business/international/glaxosmithkline-under-investigation-by-serious-fraud-office.html', 'snippet': 'The drug maker said the British regulator had opened a formal criminal inquiry into its “commercial practices.” The company gave no further details.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British drugmaker GlaxoSmithKline said late Tuesday that the Serious Fraud Office of Britain had opened a formal criminal investigation into its “commercial practices.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'GlaxoSmithKline Under Investigation by Serious Fraud Office', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GlaxoSmithKline PLC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Serious Fraud Office (United Kingdom)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-28T08:10:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fed4cf9b-a3cb-5ac0-b7ca-f94c997f79bd', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fed4cf9b-a3cb-5ac0-b7ca-f94c997f79bd'}, {'abstract': 'Can you calculate the amount of water used by residents of a California town during the summer months?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/28/test-yourself-math-may-28-2014/', 'snippet': 'Can you calculate the amount of water used by residents of a California town during the summer