bd0-6ae5f0a102c8'}, {'abstract': 'Europe’s voters send a message of dismay with the governing parties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/opinion/the-fringe-gets-bigger.html', 'snippet': 'Europe’s voters send a message of dismay with the governing parties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As expected, angry Europeans across the Continent delivered a drubbing to establishment parties in elections to the European Parliament that ended on Sunday. It was not only fringe parties in smaller states that did it: Marine Le Pen’s National Front in France and Nigel Farage’s UKIP (U.K. Independence Party) in Britain each took about a quarter of the votes in their countries, the second- and third-biggest economies in the European Union.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fringe Gets Bigger', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fringe Gets Bigger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Parliament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-28T11:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a319591-74f2-5b06-b450-4ca372216309', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a319591-74f2-5b06-b450-4ca372216309'}, {'abstract': 'The investment firm, long known for its shareholder activism, agreed to invest $150 million into Magnum Hunter