 from the Middle East to Africa, The Times’s Mark Landler reports. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s News in Washington: Obama to Outline Foreign Policy Agenda', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dewhurst, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gruenberg, Martin J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-28T12:05:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8ffb972-a62f-5a6c-aeac-91062b161cb4', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8ffb972-a62f-5a6c-aeac-91062b161cb4'}, {'abstract': 'Valeant Pharmaceuticals has raised its takeover bid for Allergan. | An offer by Pilgrim’s Pride sets up a potential battle over Hillshire Brands. | Pimco has brought back a former top executive. | Fabrice Tourre said that he would not appeal his case in higher court.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/28/morning-agenda-valeant-turns-up-the-heat/', 'snippet': 'Valeant Pharmaceuticals has raised its takeover bid for Allergan. | An offer by Pilgrim’s Pride sets up a potential battle over Hillshire Brands. | Pimco has brought back a former top executive. | Fabrice Tourre said that he would not appeal his c...', 'lead_paragraph': 'VALEANT RAISES BID FOR ALLERGAN \xa0|\xa0 Valeant Pharmaceuticals on Wednesday raised its takeover bid for Allergan, turning up the heat in its pursuit of the Botox maker, Michael J. de la Merced writes in DealBook. The new offer comes on the heels of a separate deal in which Nestlé will buy the sales rights to some of Valeant’s skin care products for $1.4 billion. It also arrives a day after Allergan unveiled a more pointed defense against the takeover bid, questioning the sustainability of its unwanted suitor’s business model and stock price. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Valeant Turns Up the Heat', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-28T12:06:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3896317-bde0-5e48-a07b-747a5f59070a', 'word_count': 1874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3896317-bde0-5e48-a07b-747a5f59070a'}, {'abstract': 'The former justice’s decision, after a string of revelations that tarnished his image, is a blow to the beleaguered government of President Park Geun-hye.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/world/asia/presidents-choice-for-south-korea-premier-steps-aside.html', 'snippet': 'The former justice’s decision, after a string of revelations that tarnished his image, is a blow to the beleaguered government of President Park Geun-hye.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — A former justice handpicked to be South Korea’s new prime minister stepped aside on Wednesday, dealing a blow to President Park Geun-hye’s efforts to regroup her government in the wake of a fatal ferry disaster.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The N