 guru offers advice on the best approach to sending online stationery.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/28/jenna-lyons-j-crew-paperless-post-e-cards/', 'snippet': 'To mark a new collaboration between J. Crew and Paperless Post, the creative guru offers advice on the best approach to sending online stationery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since Jenna Lyons took the reins as creative director at J. Crew, the brand has launched a seemingly endless stream of covetable designer collaborations in clothing, accessories and beauty products. Now, the brand is bringing its casual-chic aesthetic to the realm of digital correspondence. In a project launched this week with Paperless Post, Lyons has overseen a line of electronic stationery that includes thank-you notes, invites and greetings. The overall tone of the language is one Lyons deems essential for any e-card: “humor and a touch of sarcasm.” A birthday card reads, “Happy… Whatever Age You Wish You Were”; another says, “Thinking of You… But Not in a Creepy Stalker Kind of Way.” The design is quintessentially J. Crew, too, with neon hues, bold prints and carefully chosen fonts that are as tasteful yet playful as the looks in the catalog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/t-magazine/28lyons-bobb1/28lyons-bobb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/28/t-magazine/28lyons-bobb1/28lyons-bobb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/t-magazine/28lyons-bobb1/28lyons-bobb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image