pet': 'Kristina McCain, a gynecologist, has used the CerviScope to treat poor women in other countries, many of them former sex slaves. Her stories hint at how the product can be useful in the field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You don’t often hear about cervical cancer killing women in the United States, where Pap smears are routine, but in the developing world, it is one of the most lethal cancers for women. While reporting my article that appeared in the May 25 magazine — about how David Walmer, a fertility specialist, created a device to help prevent cervical cancer despite knowing next to nothing about the disease — I spoke to a gynecologist named Kristina McCain. Her experience abroad using a field-test model of the CerviScope to treat poor women, many of them former sex slaves, hints at how the finished product can be useful.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/magazine/Cerviscope1/Cerviscope1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/28/magazine/Cerviscope1/Cerviscope1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/magazine/Cerviscope1/Cerviscope1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/magazine/Cerviscope1/Cerviscope1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/magazine/Cerviscope1/Cerviscope1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/28/magazine/Cerviscope1/Cerviscope1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/28/magazine/Cerviscope1/Cerviscope1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The CerviScope in the Field', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cervical Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walmer, David K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-28T18:09:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bonnie Rochman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bonnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rochman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96b7513a-344c-5492-913a-28ade9cb117e', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96b7513a-344c-5492-913a-28ade9cb117e'}, {'abstract': 'The band’s album “Ghost Stories” sold 383,000 copies, marking its fourth consecutive No. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/28/coldplay-hits-no-1/', 'snippet': 'The band’s album “Ghost Stories” sold 383,000 copies, marking its fourth consecutive No. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coldplay’s latest album, “Ghost Stories” (Parlophone/Atlantic), enters the Billboard 200 chart at No. 1 this week, with sales of 383,000 for the week ending May 25, just six days after the album was released. Of that total, 245,000 (or 64 percent) of the album’s sales were as digital downloads, according to Nielsen SoundScan.', 'print_sect