unt': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a5ad4dd-4fdd-54dc-8aba-eb2045b8a89d'}, {'abstract': 'In his new book, Pieter Estersohn, an architectural photographer, captures the elegance of Kentucky horse country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/garden/bluegrass-portraits-with-a-twist.html', 'snippet': 'In his new book, Pieter Estersohn, an architectural photographer, captures the elegance of Kentucky horse country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pieter Estersohn, a veteran architecture and interiors photographer, really stretched himself for his new book, “Kentucky: Historic Houses and Horse Farms of Bluegrass Country” ($60; Monacelli Press). For aerial shots of barns and thoroughbreds, as well as portraits of historic homes, he made five extended visits to Lexington over two years. At one point, he insisted on removing the passenger-side door of a helicopter he was riding in. “I was cantilevered out, contorting my body for three hours in 20-degree temperatures to get those images,” he recalled recently during lunch not far from his home and studio near Gramercy Park.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/29QNA1-copy/29QNA1-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 468, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/29QNA1-copy/29QNA1-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 468}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/29QNA1-copy/29QNA1-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/29QNA1-copy/29QNA1-copy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1396, 'width': 1789, 'subType': 'supe