'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1115be5a-25d7-5d64-b1a8-3b621097d03b', 'word_count': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1115be5a-25d7-5d64-b1a8-3b621097d03b'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of blaming politics for the Supreme Court we have, perhaps we should place on the court some of the blame for our politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/opinion/greenhouse-polar-vision.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of blaming politics for the Supreme Court we have, perhaps we should place on the court some of the blame for our politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost any commentary on the Supreme Court these days will include an observation about how polarized the court is: how for the first time in history, all the Republican-appointed justices (there are five) are to the right of all the Democratic appointees, and how the two groups diverge (Justice Anthony M. Kennedy occasionally excepted) in many of the court’s most ideologically charged cases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth':