88070d426'}, {'abstract': 'The World Trade Center site in Lower Manhattan negotiates its dual roles as a memorial and a part of a living city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/arts/design/finding-space-for-the-living-at-a-memorial.html', 'snippet': 'The World Trade Center site in Lower Manhattan negotiates its dual roles as a memorial and a part of a living city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some fences have come down at the World Trade Center. The site isn’t finished yet, but there’s no longer the regime of barricades and snaking line to see the pair of matching fountains approximating the footprints of the former towers. The other morning, New York’s police commissioner, William J. Bratton, trailed by seconds, marched under the rows of swamp white oaks toward the newly opened Sept. 11 museum.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Space for the Living at a Memorial', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Space for the Living at a Memorial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimmelman, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National September 11 Memorial and Museum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-28T22:42:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kimmelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kimmelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repo