 [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristof, Nicholas D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rohingya (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T00:35:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/59c7e7a9-2e37-585b-891f-44b61f181dd9', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59c7e7a9-2e37-585b-891f-44b61f181dd9'}, {'abstract': 'We’re finally making headway against childhood obesity. We can’t stop now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/opinion/michelle-obama-on-attempts-to-roll-back-healthy-reforms.html', 'snippet': 'We’re finally making headway against childhood obesity. We can’t stop now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN we began our Let’s Move! initiative four years ago, we set one simple but ambitious goal: to end the epidemic of childhood obesity in a generation so that kids born today will grow up healthy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Campaign for Junk Food', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Campaign for Junk Food', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lunch and Breakfast Programs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T00:37:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Obama', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Obama', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9b85e4a-f7c5-59d6-9d4d-d63b67c4ec54', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9b85e4a-f7c5-59d6-9d4d-d63b67c4ec54'}, {'abstract': 'Federal health officials said Wednesday that an Illinois man who met with an Indiana man who later fell ill with Middle East Respiratory Syndrome did not pick up the virus from him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/us/health-officials-reverse-diagnosis-of-mers-in-illinois-man.html', 'snippet': 'Federal health officials said Wednesday that an Illinois man who met with an Indiana man who later fell ill with Middle East Respiratory Syndrome did not pick up the virus from him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reversing an earlier announcement, federal health officials said Wednesday that an Illinois man who met with an Indiana man who later fell ill with Middle East Respiratory Syndrome, or MERS, did not pick up the virus from him. Officials from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention said a first lung sample from the Illinois man had tested negative for the coronavirus that causes MERS, but two preliminary blood samples had then tested positive for antibodies to it. That led the C.D.C. to announce on May 17 that the man had been infected but had not fallen ill; this would have been the first transmission of the virus within the United States. On Wednesday, they said that a more sensitive blood test that takes at least five days to produce results showed that he never had the virus. The most likely explanation, one of the officials said, is that the preliminary test had cross-reacted with antibodies the man had to a previous coronavirus infection. At least six coronaviruses are known to infect humans: Four normally cause common cold symptoms, while the other two, MERS and SARS, are more serious. Only two MERS cases have been found in the United States — the Indiana man and another in Florida. Both had recently arrived after working in Saudi hospitals where there have been hundreds of cases since March. Thus far, C.D.C. officials said, extensive testing indicates that the two men did not pass on the virus to any family members or health care workers treating them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Officials Reverse Diagnosis of MERS in Illinois Man', 'kicker': 'National Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Health Officials Reverse Diagnosis of MERS in Man From Illinois', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'MERS (Middle East Respiratory Syndrome)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T00:37:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b456cd6-738c-5cb8-814c-ea0fc4c960b8', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b456cd6-738c-5cb8-814c-ea0fc4c960b8'}, {'abstract': 'Trying to recalculate monthly bills by paying separate companies for high-speed Internet, cable television and landline telephone service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/technology/personaltech/finally-breaking-up-the-cable-bundles.html', 'snippet': 'Trying to recalculate monthly bills by paying separate companies for high-speed Internet, cable television and landline telephone service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’M in a relationship that just hasn’t been working out. I still want to be connected, just not as connected as before.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/business/GADGET/GADGET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/29/business/GADGET/GADGET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 744}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/business/GADGET/GADGET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 826, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/business/GADGET/GADGET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1651, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/business/GADGET/GADGET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75