e, While Losing Her Peace of Mind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothenberg, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bacsinszky, Timea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T00:56:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ccda7ca-25a2-5948-b6ea-36670daa6e49', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ccda7ca-25a2-5948-b6ea-36670daa6e49'}, {'abstract': 'Fearing the worst from Republicans, President Obama backs away from a review on deportations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/opinion/adding-delay-to-immigration-failure.html', 'snippet': 'Fearing the worst from Republicans, President Obama backs away from a review on deportations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama asked the homeland security secretary, Jeh Johnson, in March to review the administration’s immigration enforcement policies. He was under intense pressure from immigrant advocates, frustrated at Congress’s inaction on reform, who were imploring him to act on his own to end or slow the pace of deportations. Now he’s backing off and asking Mr. Johnson to delay the review. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adding Delay to Immigration Failure', 'kicker': 'A Discouraging Day | Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adding Delay to Immigration Failure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jeh C', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T00:59:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c68e6c20-ce8f-55f5-a5f8-c8cc86409fac', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c68e6c20-ce8f-55f5-a5f8-c8cc86409fac'}, {'abstract': 'The lawsuit will claim that between 2009 and 2012, the number of new mortgages in minority neighborhoods of Providence, R.I., fell 63 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/business/santander-to-face-suit-claiming-bias-in-mortgages.html', 'snippet': 'The lawsuit will claim that between 2009 and 2012, the number of new mortgages in minority neighborhoods of Providence, R.I., fell 63 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the housing bubble expanded in the early 2000s, mortgage lenders aggressively handed out money in black and Hispanic neighborhoods, though often at exorbitant rates and in ways that made the loans unaffordable to more vulnerable borrowers. Now, the pendulum has swung the other way, raising concerns that some banks are shutting out blacks and Hispanics in favor of white homeowners. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santander Bank to Face Suit Claiming Bias in Mortgages', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Santander to Face Suit Claiming Bias in Mortgages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dewan, Shaila K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Banco Santander S A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Providence (RI)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T00:59:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaila Dewan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dewan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bcda42b-0aea-5a40-9bc1-45ffb5ef03a8', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bcda42b-0aea-5a40-9bc1-45ffb5ef03a8'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s commencement speech at West Point provided little new insight into how he plans to lead in the next two years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/opinion/president-obama-misses-a-chance-on-foreign-affairs.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s commencement speech at West Point provided little new insight into how he plans to lead in the next two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama and his aides heralded his commencement speech at the United States Military Academy at West Point on Wednesday as a big moment, when he would lay out his foreign policy vision for the remainder of his term and refute his critics. The address did not match the hype, was largely uninspiring, lacked strategic sweep and is unlikely to quiet his detractors, on the right or the left.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Obama Misses a Chance on Foreign Affairs', 'kicker': 'A Discouraging Day | Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Obama Misses a Chance on Foreign Affairs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Military Academy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commencement Speeches', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T01:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/df5921c3-1093-5a16-bb04-a7f05f1c79b1', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df5921c3-1093-5a16-bb04-a7f05f1c79b1'}, {'abstract': 'The state ethics board voted to fine the National Organization for Marriage $50,250 for keeping its donors secret during the campaign, in 2009, to repeal a law legalizing gay marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/us/maine-ethics-panel-fines-group-opposed-to-same-sex-marriage.html', 'snippet': 'The state ethics board voted to fine the National Organization for Marriage $50,250 for keeping its donors secret during the campaign, in 2009, to repeal a law legalizing gay marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The state ethics board voted Wednesday to fine the National Organization for Marriage $50,250 for keeping its donors secret during the successful campaign, in 2009, for a referendum to repeal a law legalizing same-sex marriage. The Maine Commission on Governmental Ethics and Election Practices said the group contributed about $2 million to that campaign but did not register with the commission as a ballot committee, in violation of election law. The organization has argued that its donors did not specifically earmark contributions for the campaign and so it did not have to make disclosures about them to the commission. It said it would appeal. The fine is the highest imposed by the ethics board, which will also direct the group to register as a ballot question committee and to list its contributions. Voters in Maine legalized same-sex marriage with another ballot question in 2012. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maine: Ethics Panel Fines Group Opposed to Same-Sex Marriage', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maine: Ethics Panel Fines Group Opposed to Same-Sex Marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Organization for Marriage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T01:10:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a67d0ed1-fa3d-5cd0-bf18-8a4f663a21d3', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a67d0ed1-fa3d-5cd0-bf18-8a4f663a21d3'}, {'abstract': 'Opponents of government policies that have spurred the growth of renewable energy are pushing back on mandates nationwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/business/energy-environment/a-pushback-on-green-power.html', 'snippet': 'Opponents of government policies that have spurred the growth of renewable energy are pushing back on mandates nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As renewable energy production has surged in recent years, opponents of government policies that have helped spur its growth have pushed to roll back those incentives and mandates in state after state.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/business/jpGREEN/jpGREEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/29/business/jpGREEN/jpGREEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/busine