_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/894bfeb9-5424-5de1-ad42-c47fd768e4fd'}, {'abstract': 'Not long after The Times reported an increase in the percentage of workers belonging to unions, the trend turned firmly in the other direction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/upshot/union-membership-has-declined-since-the-1970s.html', 'snippet': 'Not long after The Times reported an increase in the percentage of workers belonging to unions, the trend turned firmly in the other direction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times has converted all of its 1964 issues into a digitized, searchable format. Each week, The Upshot will unearth an item from 50 years ago and put it in the light of today. “U.S. Finds Unions Gaining Members, Reversing Trend” appeared on May 25, 1964, and can be seen in its original format on TimesMachine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Union Membership Was Rising', 'kicker': 'Archive Dive', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T18:24:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Flippen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flippen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d00348f-a267-50f7-a7d8-6a572191e90b', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d00348f-a267-50f7-a7d8-6a572191e90b'}, {'abstract': 'The theater will present seven American premieres from around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/lionboy-and-pinocchio-among-highlights-of-new-victory-theater-season/', 'snippet': 'The theater will present seven American premieres from around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a house specializing in works for families and young audiences, the New Victory Theater may seem an unlikely place for Complicite, the British company known for shows that combine surreal imagery and psychological intensity. But the 2013 production of “Lionboy,” Marcelo Dos Santos’s adaptation of material from Zizou Corder’s “Lionboy” novels – Complicite’s first family production in its 31-year history – will be coming to the New Victory in January. “Lionboy,” a highlight of the New Victory’s 2014-15 season, will run from Jan. 23 to Feb. 1.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Lionboy’ a Highlight of New Victory Theater Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Victory Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T18:26:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38738682-c4ac-5cc5-b51b-76e60d5ece73', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38738682-c4ac-5cc5-b51b-76e60d5ece73'}, {'abstract': 'Japan, in return, said it would start lifting sanctions it had imposed on the North, which in 2002 admitted the abductions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/world/asia/north-korea-agrees-to-investigate-fate-of-japanese-abducted-decades-ago.html', 'snippet': 'Japan, in return, said it would start lifting sanctions it had imposed on the North, which in 2002 admitted the abductions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — North Korea has agreed to open a new investigation into the fate of Japanese citizens abducted by its agents during the Cold War, the two countries said Thursday, signaling a possible diplomatic breakthrough in an emotional issue that has divided Japan and the North.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea Will Investigate Fate of Abducted Japanese ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea Will Investigate Fate of Abducted Japanese', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T18:29:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09b046cb-302f-5d01-ade9-e1b6c93105cf', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09b046cb-302f-5d01-ade9-e1b6c93105cf'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Whitehead’s new memoir is about his participation in the World Series of Poker.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/surviving-at-the-poker-tables-colson-whitehead-talks-about-the-noble-hustle/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Whitehead’s new memoir is about his participation in the World Series of Poker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Colson Whitehead’s new memoir, “The Noble Hustle: Poker, Beef Jerky and Death,” began as an assignment for the online magazine Grantland, which commissioned him to compete in and write about the World Series of Poker in Las Vegas. In the book, Mr. Whitehead writes about his anhedonic personality (“I have a good poker face because I am half dead inside,” it begins), his training with the help of a coach named Helen Ellis and his fate at the high-stakes tables. I recently spoke to Mr. Whitehead in a phone interview. Below are edited excerpts from the conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/books/29whitehead/29whitehead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 787, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/29/books/29whitehead/29whitehead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 787}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/books/29whitehead/29whitehead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 781, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/books/29whitehead/29whitehead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1562, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/books/29whitehead/29whitehead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/29/books/29whitehead/29whitehead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/books/29whitehead/29whitehead-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumb