be sure to check out the MalPaso Dance Company at the Joyce Theater. Also, there is a BookCon at the Javits Center and Ubisoft’s new adventure game, “Watch Dogs” is now available.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Video', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Weekend: A Cuban Dance Troupe', 'kicker': 'The New York Times News Minute', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T19:26:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christian Roman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daf5def2-657c-517e-bc08-ddf3b2707e8e', 'word_count': 19, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daf5def2-657c-517e-bc08-ddf3b2707e8e'}, {'abstract': 'Pamela Skaist-Levy and Gela Nash-Taylor share advice from their new business book, “The Glitter Plan.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/juicy-couture-on-how-to-succeed-in-business-the-glitter-plan-book/', 'snippet': 'Pamela Skaist-Levy and Gela Nash-Taylor share advice from their new business book, “The Glitter Plan.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Not only are we designing 1o collections a year now,” Pamela Skaist-Levy says, “but there’s a crazy big-player bidding war to turn our book into a TV show.” She’s referring to “The Glitter Plan,” out today. It’s the first memoir from the designer and her longtime business partner, Gela Nash-Taylor, the co-founders of Juicy Couture. Written in collaboration with the journalist Booth Moore, the book tells the story of two best friends who took a simple idea and turned it into one of the most successful fashion companies in history. “We didn’t go to Harvard Business School,” Nash-Taylor says. “Or any business school, for that matter. But we wanted to inspire and work off of an idea that came from a real passion to empower.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/t-magazine/29juicy-bobb1/29juicy-bobb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/29/t-magazine/29juicy-bobb1/29juicy-bobb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/t-magazine/29juicy-bobb1/29juicy-bobb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/t-magazine/29juicy-bobb1/29juicy-bobb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1116, 'width': 1675, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/t-magazine/29juicy-bobb1/29juicy-bobb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/29/t-magazine/29juicy-bobb1/29juicy-bobb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/t-magazine/29juicy-bobb1/29juicy-bobb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rules of Style | The Founders of Juicy Couture on How to Succeed in Business', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Special Delivery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'k