e': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monet, Claude', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levinson, David W', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T20:33:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcc4dc49-48a6-55ef-84f2-4233b71f3bf2', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcc4dc49-48a6-55ef-84f2-4233b71f3bf2'}, {'abstract': '“Object of Devotion,” an exhibition of medieval English alabaster sculptures at the Museum of Biblical Art, prompts reflection on why so many objects of this kind were willfully destroyed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/arts/design/object-of-devotion-an-exhibition-of-alabaster-sculptures.html', 'snippet': '“Object of Devotion,” an exhibition of medieval English alabaster sculptures at the Museum of Biblical Art, prompts reflection on why so many objects of this kind were willfully destroyed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A hotly debated issue among theologians in medieval Europe concerned what has since been called “the cult of images.” The controversy turned on beliefs about how people related to and used images of Christian subjects rendered by painters and sculptors. Proponents of images argued that they were educational and edifying. Iconoclasts feared that people would become enthralled by images and fall into the sin of idolatry. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30BIBLICAL1/B