rden/diffa-marks-3-decades-of-designers-fighting-aids.html', 'snippet': 'At its latest fund-raiser, a panel including Ruben and Isabel Toledo and Terrence McNally spoke of how the disease had affected their industries in the early, terrifying years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The charity known as the Design Industries Foundation Fighting AIDS, or Diffa, turned 30 in April.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/01seen/01seen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/01seen/01seen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/01seen/01seen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/01seen/01seen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/01seen/01seen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/01seen/01seen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/garden/01seen/01seen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diffa Marks 3 Decades of Designers Fighting AIDS', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '30 Years of Fighting AIDS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Penelope', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Design Industries Foundation Fighting Aids', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T21:06:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Penelope Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Penelope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8861c3ad-31e8-5a28-97f2-ffa1500f2e64', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8861c3ad-31e8-5a28-97f2-ffa1500f2e64'}, {'abstract': 'The Library of America chronicles the history of American responses to Shakespeare from 1776 to the present day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/books/review/shakespeare-in-america-edited-by-james-shapiro.html', 'snippet': 'The Library of America chronicles the history of American responses to Shakespeare from 1776 to the present day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who is the American Shakespeare? The question has an odd, anxious quality that it wouldn’t quite have if applied to Germany, say, or Russia. It’s not just that in those cases, there is an answer ready at hand (Goethe, Pushkin), but that in the international context we know what the question means. Who is the founding poet to whom all subsequent writers must relate? Who established the parameters of the language within or against which all subsequent writers labor? Understood that way, the answer to the question for America isn’t an American at all: It’s \xadWilliam Shakespeare himself.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01MILLMAN/01MILLMAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01MILLMAN/01MILLMAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 554}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01MILLMAN/01MILLMAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 946, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01MILLMAN/01MILLMAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1759, 'width': 1904, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01MILLMAN/01MILLMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01MILLMAN/01MILLMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01MILLMAN/01MILLMAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Shakespeare', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Our Shakespeare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Shakespeare in America: An Anthology From the Revolution to Now (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shapiro, James S (1955- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T21:07:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Millman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Millman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb6c3bf2-cc38-5e12-ac0c-d649409d4239', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb6c3bf2-cc38-5e12-ac0c-d649409d4239'}, {'abstract': 'A curator is seeking information about Ida O’Keeffe, a painter and younger sister of Georgia O’Keeffe, for the exhibition about the sister in the shadows planned for the Dallas Museum of Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/arts/design/a-sister-in-the-shadow-of-georgia-okeeffe.html', 'snippet': 'A curator is seeking information about Ida O’Keeffe, a painter and younger sister of Georgia O’Keeffe, for the exhibition about the sister in the shadows planned for the Dallas Museum of Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Georgia O’Keeffe was disappointed in her painter sister Ida O’Keeffe. “A wasted life,” she told the family when Ida died in 1961, at 71. The Dallas Museum of Art will tell Ida’s side of the story with an exhibition scheduled for 2017, “Ida O’Keeffe: Escaping Georgia’s Shadow.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30ANTIQUES1/ANITQUES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 460, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30ANTIQUES1/ANITQUES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 460}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo'