which is one element, is achieved by way of the magician’s method, which is another; method is hidden in misdirection, and a reconstruction is attempted afterward, by the audience. “A magician seeks to choreograph a way through the trick with these component parts,” Strauss explains. “If he does so he will have achieved magic. If not, he is a failure.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '45', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01-bks-Hendrix/0601-bks-Hendrix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01-bks-Hendrix/0601-bks-Hendrix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1000}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01-bks-Hendrix/0601-bks-Hendrix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01-bks-Hendrix/0601-bks-Hendrix-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1499, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01-bks-Hendrix/01-bks-Hendrix-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01-bks-Hendrix/01-bks-Hendrix-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01-bks-Hendrix/01-bks-Hendrix-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType