_date': '2014-05-29T23:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurel Graeber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graeber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bea2fcd-6f88-5a95-bf46-2aaf6fea490e', 'word_count': 4735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bea2fcd-6f88-5a95-bf46-2aaf6fea490e'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to street fairs, parades, literary events, performances and walking tours in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/arts/spare-times-for-may-30-june-5.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to street fairs, parades, literary events, performances and walking tours in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSING WORKS STREET FAIR AND OTHER EVENTS (Sunday, Monday and Wednesday) Books — and the people whose lives revolve around them — are the stars of several events at this SoHo bookstore at 126 Crosby Street, near Houston Street. Thousands of donated books, records and CDs can be scooped up for $1 each at a street fair, a fund-raiser for outreach programs run by Housing Works, on Sunday from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for May 30-June 5', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-29T23:23:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/998b1110-7b28-5d8e-959c-e8dac4a6c0b9', 'word_count': 2780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/998b1110-7b28-5d8e-959c-e8dac4a6c0b9'}, {'abstract': 'Kelly Reichardt’s “Night Moves” stars Jesse Eisenberg, Dakota Fanning and Peter Sarsgaard as young Oregonians plotting to blow up a dam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/movies/night-moves-tracks-three-eco-terrorists-in-oregon.html', 'snippet': 'Kelly Reichardt’s “Night Moves” stars Jesse Eisenberg, Dakota Fanning and Peter Sarsgaard as young Oregonians plotting to blow up a dam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Realism is too imprecise a term for Kelly Reichardt’s filmmaking. She is a more of a materialist, determined to capture how the world looks, how it feels and, at a granular level of detail, how it works. Her stories tend to be simple and starkly told. In “Old Joy,” two friends take a camping trip that tests their intimacy and raises painful, unspoken questions about their identities as 21st-century American men. In “Wendy and Lucy,” a young woman and her dog are stranded by car trouble en route to Alaska. In “Meek’s Cutoff,” settlers in mid-19th-century Oregon lose their way. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30NIGHTMOVES/30NIGHTMOVES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30NIGHTMOVES/30NIGHTMOVES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30NIGHTMOVES/30NIGHTMOVES-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30NIGHTMOVES/30NIG