m, directed by Jon S. Baird and featuing James McAvoy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A scene from the film, directed by Jon S. Baird and featuing James McAvoy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30FILTH/30FILTH-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30FILTH/30FILTH-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30FILTH/30FILTH-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30FILTH/30FILTH-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30FILTH/FILTH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30FILTH/FILTH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30FILTH/FILTH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clip: ‘Filth’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T00:32:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Magnolia Pictures', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Magnolia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pictures', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/40a3dcfc-29e8-5af7-986f-8f6fe8ddb304', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/40a3dcfc-29e8-5af7-986f-8f6fe8ddb304'}, {'abstract': 'A program offering legal counsel for every indigent immigrant would be cost-effective by reducing waste in courts and jails, a New York City Bar Association report says.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/nyregion/study-favors-free-counsel-to-navigate-deportation.html', 'snippet': 'A program offering legal counsel for every indigent immigrant would be cost-effective by reducing waste in courts and jails, a New York City Bar Association report says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year, tens of thousands of people appear in immigration court to fight deportation orders without a lawyer to assist them. Many are poor and adrift, unable to speak English or understand the laws determining their fate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Public Defender System for Immigrants Facing Deportation Would Pay for Itself, Study Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Says Public Defender System for Immigrants Facing Deportation Would Pay for Itself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Bar Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Semple, Kirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Defenders and Court-Appointed Lawyers (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Aid for the Poor (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Immigrant Family Unity Project', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NERA Economic Consulting', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T00:36:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fc49a53-0938-5242-a303-6c110ba8acc4', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fc49a53-0938-5242-a303-6c110ba8acc4'}, {'abstract': 'In “Filth,” James McAvoy plays an over-the-top Scottish police detective who is going insane while looking for a promotion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/movies/filth-stars-james-mcavoy-as-an-insane-detective.html', 'snippet': 'In “Filth,” James McAvoy plays an over-the-top Scottish police detective who is going insane while looking for a promotion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James McAvoy goes whole hog in “Filth,” an adaptation of a 1998 novel by Irvine Welsh, the Scottish author of “Trainspotting.” And by whole hog, I mean exactly that. His character, Bruce Robertson, who narrates the film, is an Edinburgh police detective sergeant on a catastrophic downward spiral. As he loses his sanity, he suggests a wounded wild boar on the rampage, dragging his entrails behind him as he charges around in circles. Compared with this maniac, the rotten policeman of two “Bad Lieutenant” films is a garden-variety bad boy. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dirty Cop. No, Really Dirty.', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dirty Cop. No, Really Dirty.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAvoy, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welsh, Irvine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Filth (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baird, Jon S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T00:36:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/823e4c8e-ac42-5309-b2ff-d94e4b767330', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/823e4c8e-ac42-5309-b2ff-d94e4b767330'}, {'abstract': 'Before a deadly ferry sinking in April, the South Korean island of Jindo was known largely for one thing: its dogs, famous for their loyalty and homing instinct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/world/asia/an-island-marred-by-a-ferry-disaster-and-sustained-by-jindo-dogs.html', 'snippet': 'Before a deadly ferry sinking in April, the South Korean island of Jindo was known largely for one thing: its dogs, famous for their loyalty and homing instinct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DONJI-RI, South Korea — This hamlet of cinder-block huts with blue and red roofs slumbered in a drowsy repose. Weeds with yellow flowers grew in the corners of dusty front yards and through cracks in the pavement of deserted alleys. The town’s only “hagwon,” a private cram school, stood empty, because so many families with school-age children had moved away.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None