rl': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/29/realty-investors-flock-to-spain/', 'snippet': 'Private equity firms and banks are descending on Spain, teaming up and competing for huge loan portfolios left over from 2008’s market collapse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As one of the most moribund housing markets in Europe, Spain has become a magnet for global bargain hunters. Real estate prices are down as much as 50 percent from their peak during a housing bubble, and investors from Asia to the United States and Britain are flocking to Spain to try to catch the uptick.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Global Investors Looking for Real Estate Bargains Flock to Spain', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Realty Investors Flock to Spain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sareb SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T01:14:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a23dd087-0851-546c-8921-7741de3efd9f', 'word_count': 1491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a23dd087-0851-546c-8921-7741de3efd9f'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama laid out his approach to dealing with aggressive autocratic rulers this week, but his vision is ill-suited for the challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/opinion/brooks-the-autocracy-challenge.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama laid out his approach to dealing with aggressive autocratic rulers this week, but his vision is ill-suited for the challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to remember, but back in the early 1990s there was a debate about how nations should emerge from Communism — the Russian way or the Chinese way. The Russians did political and economic reform together. The Chinese just did economic reform.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1003, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1891, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumb