ed (but Pageboys Abound)', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Boys Allowed (but Pageboys Abound)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crops for Girls (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koenig, Leah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "D'Amico, Michael", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T01:26:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leah Koenig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koenig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58b01d23-a95e-56a7-89b0-f1ce7f0491d2', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58b01d23-a95e-56a7-89b0-f1ce7f0491d2'}, {'abstract': 'In “Lucky Them,” a journalist tries to give her career a lift by catching up with a long-missing musician.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/movies/lucky-them-stars-toni-collette.html', 'snippet': 'In “Lucky Them,” a journalist tries to give her career a lift by catching up with a long-missing musician.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Lucky Them,” a seen-better-days critic, Ellie Klug (Toni Collette), writes for a seen-better-days magazine that covers alternative rock as if it were the only music in the pop universe. Ellie ignores deadlines and the marketplace, and is burdened by the kind of integrity that looks more like self-destructiveness. (In the real world, she would have been fired years ago.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':