dline': {'main': 'At Core of Church-State Clash, Unease Over Christianity’s Rising Influence in China', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Ian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wenzhou (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T01:47:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonah M. Kessel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76d3527a-3239-5c85-bdf0-714b62144450', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76d3527a-3239-5c85-bdf0-714b62144450'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel has told reporters that he would decide soon whether to accept a months-old offer to resettle six prisoners in Uruguay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/us/hagel-sets-his-own-timetable-on-deciding-guantanamo-transfers.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel has told reporters that he would decide soon whether to accept a months-old offer to resettle six prisoners in Uruguay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel, who is under pressure from within the Obama administration to step up his pace in approving the transfer of low-level Guantánamo Bay detainees, has told reporters that he would decide soon whether to accept a months-old offer to resettle six prisoners in Uruguay. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Pressure, Hagel Promises to Act on Guantánamo Transfers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Under Pressure, Hagel Promises to Act on Guantánamo Transfers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uruguay', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T01:49:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage and Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52b35a39-ae74-54dc-be95-6bc52f858e1f', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52b35a39-ae74-54dc-be95-6bc52f858e1f'}, {'abstract': '“The Hornet’s Nest” follows Mike Boettcher, a broadcast journalist, embedded with American troops in Afghanistan during Operation Strong Eagle III.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/movies/the-hornets-nest-follows-journalists-into-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': '“The Hornet’s Nest” follows Mike Boettcher, a broadcast journalist, embedded with American troops in Afghanistan during Operation Strong Eagle III.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the history of the long war in Afghanistan is written, Kunar Province, the mountainous region near the Pakistan border that has been a Taliban stronghold, will fill more than one chapter. It is already a film source: “Lone Survivor,” the Mark Wahlberg feature, and “Restrepo,” the Oscar-nominated 2010 documentary, both take place there. (Another new film, “Korengal,” revisits the “Restrepo” troops.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30HORNETSNEST/HORNETS-NEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30HORNETSNEST/HORNETS-NEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30HORNETSNEST/HORNETS-NEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30HORNETSNEST/HORNETS-NEST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30HORNETSNEST/30HORNETSNEST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30HORNETSNEST/30HORNETSNEST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30HORNETSNEST/30HORNETSNEST-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Into a Taliban Stronghold', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hornet’s Nest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "The Hornet's Nest (Movie)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salzberg, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tureaud, Christian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T01:55:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e244959-08ea-5682-a78e-a01d575efa7c', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e244959-08ea-5682-a78e-a01d575efa7c'}, {'abstract': 'Ayn Rand’s pedantic novella “Anthem” gets a goofy, spoofy and exuberant musical adaptation at the Culture Project.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/theater/a-spoofy-spin-on-ayn-rands-anthem.html', 'snippet': 'Ayn Rand’s pedantic novella “Anthem” gets a goofy, spoofy and exuberant musical adaptation at the Culture Project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would be folly to adapt Ayn Rand’s pedantic novella “Anthem“ as a straight stage drama, though some have recently tried. Far better to give that belabored paean to individualism a goofy, spoofy spin, as “The Anthem,” an exuberant musical adaptation at the Culture Project, does. The source material may be hopelessly schematic, but the show pours on dazzling trimmings, including a critical element absent in Rand’s didactic prose: humor. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30ANTHEM/ANTHEM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30ANTHEM/ANTHEM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30ANTHEM/ANTHEM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30ANTHEM/ANTHEM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 2028, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30ANTHEM/ANTHEM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30ANTHEM/ANTHEM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/arts/30ANTHEM/ANTHEM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Songs, Jokes and Twirls? Just Don’t Tell Ayn Rand', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kick