aph': '11 P.M. (TV5Monde) MONSIEUR HIRE (1989) When a young woman is killed in a Paris suburb, the police immediately suspect the resident loner (Michel Blanc), a tailor who was once jailed for indecent exposure, and whom nobody seems to like. Sandrine Bonnaire plays his pretty neighbor, who never thinks to pull down the shades on the windows facing his, whether she’s dressing or undressing or even making love to her ne’er-do-well boyfriend. This French melodrama, directed by Patrice Leconte from a novel by Georges Simenon, “has the makings of a first-rate psychological study,” Vincent Canby wrote in The New York Times. But here, he added, Mr. Leconte’s normally lighthearted touch “is both artificial and heavy, filled with movie gestures that are not entirely fresh.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T05:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe83aaa9-247f-5875-8160-c116ab8dad43', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe83aaa9-247f-5875-8160-c116ab8dad43'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey’s highest court ruled Thursday that a government ban on the video-sharing site YouTube was unconstitutional and a violation of freedom of expression.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/world/europe/turkish-court-says-youtube-ban-is-unconstitutional.html', 'snippet': 'Turkey’s highest court ruled Thursday that a government ban on the video-sharing site YouTube was unconstitutional and a violation of freedom of expression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turkey’s highest court ruled Thursday that a government ban on the video-sharing site YouTube was unconstitutional and a violation of freedom of expression. The Constitutional Court sent its ruling to the Telecommunications Authority, but it was not immediately clear whether the agency would lift the ban. Last month, the government removed a ban on Twitter a day after the court issued a similar ruling. YouTube was blocked in Turkey on March 27 after recordings from a secret meeting between Foreign Ministry officials detailing plans for possible military intervention against Syria were leaked to the site. The telecommunications agency said the ban was a “precautionary administrative measure” amid concerns over national security.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkish Court Says YouTube Ban Is Unconstitutional', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey: Court Says YouTube Ban Is Unconstitutional', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yeginsu, Ceylan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T05:28:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ceylan Yeginsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ceylan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yeginsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/597e196c-d78b-5164-b3f8-54a551415c29', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/597e196c-d78b-5164-b3f8-54a551415c29'}, {'abstract': 'The government is hiring growing numbers of bureaucrats to join its civil service, while also targeting those “naked officials” who send their families abroad while enjoying the perks of the job back home.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/naked-officials-feel-heat-of-china-anticorruption-drive/', 'snippet': 'The government is hiring growing numbers of bureaucrats to join its civil service, while also targeting those “naked officials” who send their families abroad while enjoying the perks of the job back home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bureaucracy is something of a national obsession in China, where it’s an old and honored tradition, with a secure government job regularly ranking as the most popular employment choice of many of the country’s elite students.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/world/30sino-officials01/30sino-officials01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/30/world/30sino-officials01/30sino-officials01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/world/30sino-officials01/30sino-officials01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/world/30sino-officials01/30sino-officials01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/world/30sino-officials01/30sino-officials01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': '