_id': 'nyt://article/250bc1e7-ce8a-5736-8aec-c823d0983357', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/250bc1e7-ce8a-5736-8aec-c823d0983357'}, {'abstract': 'If consumers thought about stolen coins or other small antiquities like they do about poached ivory they would buy a lot less.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/opinion/egypts-looted-antiquities.html', 'snippet': 'If consumers thought about stolen coins or other small antiquities like they do about poached ivory they would buy a lot less.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 2011, Egypt’s police force and other governmental authorities, overwhelmed by political upheaval, have let their protection of the country’s thousands of archaeological sites and museums fall to a bare minimum. Looters have taken full advantage of this opportunity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Looted Antiquities', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Buy Egyptian Coins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arts and Antiquities Looting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Egyptian Civilization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T10:57:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erin Thompson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thompson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aaeaf53-add6-596e-8922-0014f373027a', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aaeaf53-add6-596e-8922-0014f373027a'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Lattman discusses what it was like to oversee coverage of the firing of The Times’s executive editor, Jill Abramson, five months after he became the paper’s media editor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/05/30/we-met-the-story-and-it-was-us/', 'snippet': 'Peter Lattman discusses what it was like to oversee coverage of the firing of The Times’s executive editor, Jill Abramson, five months after he became the paper’s media editor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes a story hits very close to home. Sometimes it lands on top of you. Peter Lattman, a former DealBook reporter, became media editor late last year. Earlier this month, he was placed in the particularly tricky position of having to oversee coverage of the firing of The Times’s executive editor, Jill Abramson, which was announced on May 14. Since the dust appears to have settled – at least for now – we asked him to discuss what that was like.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/blogs/dean/dean-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/29/blogs/dean/dean-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/blogs/dean/dean-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/blogs/dean/dean-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/blogs/dean/dean-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/29/blogs/dean/dean-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/blogs/dean/dean-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'We Met the Story, and It Was Us', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMSON, JILL', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baquet, Dean', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sulzberger, Arthur Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T10:59:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Insider Staff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Insider', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/122f89af-e1dc-567e-9552-89abfaec8cd3', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/122f89af-e1dc-567e-9552-89abfaec8cd3'}, {'abstract': 'Two Dots, a new game from the maker of Dots, debuted in the top 10 of the Apple store on Thursday. The game makers said the first version of the game had now been played more than six billion times.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/dots-a-highly-addictive-game-now-has-two-dots/', 'snippet': 'Two Dots, a new game from the maker of Dots, debuted in the top 10 of the Apple store on Thursday. The game makers said the first version of the game had now been played more than six billion times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was a little groggy and tired this morning, and that’s entirely my own fault. I was up most of the night playing\xa0TwoDots,\xa0a new version of Dots,\xa0the highly addictive iOS game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/technology/bits-twodots/bits-twodots-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/technology/bits-twodots/bits-twodots-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/technology/bits-twodots/bits-twodots-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/29/technology/bits-twodots/bits-twodots-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/29/technology/bits-twodots/bits-twodots-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dots, a Highly Addictive Game, Now Has a Successor', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Betaworks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T11:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a218f61-3861-56bb-8c37-140af0ee99c1', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a218f61-3861-56bb-8c37-140af0ee99c1'}, {'abstract': 'What happens when a business owner fires a Brilliant Jerk — and then decides to rehire him?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/return-of-the-brilliant-jerk/', 'snippet': 'What happens when a business owner fires a Brilliant Jerk — and then decides to rehire him?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It caused a bit of a stir (and elicited more than 150 comments) when I wrote in 2012 that, no matter how painful it may be, fast-growth entrepreneurs have to fire the “Brilliant Jerk” if they want to take their companies to the next level. Now we have a surprising postscript to add: what happens when the business owner decides to rehire the Brilliant Jerk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Return of the Brilliant Jerk', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T11:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cliff Oxford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cliff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oxford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74513d01-bb01-5d3e-b4a8-d7afc9130f1f', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74513d01-bb01-5d3e-b4a8-d7afc9130f1f'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon used to take margin from its suppliers so it could sell things more cheaply. Now, it needs the margin for itself.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/why-is-amazon-squeezing-hachette-maybe-it-really-needs-the-money/', 'snippet': 'Amazon used to take margin from its suppliers so it could sell things more cheaply. Now, it needs the margin for itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the course of nearly two decades, Amazon has hewed to a consistent philosophy: It’s all about the customer. The retailer is so devoted to its customers that it takes the profits that would normally go to shareholders and gives them to shoppers in the form of faster delivery and lower prices. It was a brilliant strategy that has propelled the company to the top ranks of American businesses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/business/30bits-amazon1alt/30bits-amazon1alt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/30/business/30bits-amazon1alt/30bits-amazon1alt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/business/30bits-amazon1alt/30bits-amazon1alt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/business/30bits-amazon1alt/30bits-amazon1alt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/business/30bits-amazon1alt/30bits-amazon1alt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/30/business/30bits-amazon1alt/30bits-amazon1alt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumb