ons', 'value': 'Tomljanovic, Ajla', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T11:32:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naila-Jean Meyers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naila-jean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meyers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b72b6bac-5dc8-5ba6-b79a-fd268cbd12eb', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b72b6bac-5dc8-5ba6-b79a-fd268cbd12eb'}, {'abstract': 'American partnering with local strongmen hurts the fight against the Taliban.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/opinion/the-wrong-afghan-friends.html', 'snippet': 'American partnering with local strongmen hurts the fight against the Taliban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a checkpoint on a dirt road in southeastern Afghanistan in 2012, Rahim Sarobi, a farmer, braked to a stop behind a knot of idling cars. Up ahead, Afghan gunmen were piled into the back of a Toyota Hilux. On the ground, tied to the rear fender by their wrists, lay two bloodied men, laboring to breathe.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/sunday-review/0601WAR/0601WAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/sunday-review/0601WAR/0601WAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/sunday-review/0601WAR/0601WAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/sunday-review/0601WAR/0601WAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1529, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/sunday-review/0601WAR/0601WAR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/sunday-review/0601WAR/0601WAR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/sunday-review/0601WAR/0601WAR-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wrong Afghan Friends', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Wrong Friends in Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T11:33:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anand Gopal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anand', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gopal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4895a2ef-b53a-5751-9172-db40952b583d', 'word_count': 1225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4895a2ef-b53a-5751-9172-db40952b583d'}, {'abstract': 'Hillshire Brands finds itself in the middle of a bidding war. | Some colleges are offering a real-world experience of philanthropy. | Realty investors are flocking to Spain. | Dish Network said it would allow its customers to make payments in Bitcoin.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/morning-agenda-food-fight/', 'snippet': 'Hillshire Brands finds itself in the middle of a bidding war. | Some colleges are offering a real-world experience of philanthropy. | Realty investors are flocking to Spain. | Dish Network said it would allow its customers to make payments in Bitc...', 'lead_paragraph': ' FOOD FIGHT \xa0|\xa0 A week ago, many shareholders of Hillshire Brands were complaining about its planned acquisition of Pinnacle Foods, the maker of Birds Eye frozen vegetables. But in the last week, Hillshire ‒ the home of its namesake lunch meats, Ball Park hot dogs and Jimmy Dean sausages ‒ has gone from would-be pursuer to pursued, David Gelles and Michael J. de la Merced write in DealBook. On Thursday, Tyson Foods bid $6.8 billion for the company, only two days after a $6.4 billion proposal by Pilgrim’s Pride, one of the country’s big poultry producers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Fight', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T11:40:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c71ace3-4760-5114-8244-18be2fab292a', 'word_count': 1832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c71ace3-4760-5114-8244-18be2fab292a'}, {'abstract': 'Eager to benefit from the insights of some of the nation’s top designers, video game creators are flocking to graduate programs in their field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/arts/video-games/talented-designers-stream-into-mfa-video-game-programs.html', 'snippet': 'Eager to benefit from the insights of some of the nation’s top designers, video game creators are flocking to graduate programs in their field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the eighth floor of a building in Downtown Brooklyn, college students gather regularly — in a library, no less — to play video games. They aren’t procrastinating. They’re doing their homework.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01VIDEO5/01VIDEO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01VIDEO5/01VIDEO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 670}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01VIDEO5/01VIDEO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 917, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01VIDEO5/01VIDEO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1498, 'width': 1341, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01VIDEO5/01VIDEO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01VIDEO5/01VIDEO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01VIDEO5/01VIDEO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Master of the Game (Diploma Says So)', 'kic