act': 'This is a particularly good time for lovers of cinematic dragons, thanks to advances in animation software and live-action visual effects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/movies/dragons-on-screens-big-and-small-flex-new-muscles.html', 'snippet': 'This is a particularly good time for lovers of cinematic dragons, thanks to advances in animation software and live-action visual effects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a particularly good time for lovers of cinematic dragons. Thanks to advances in animation software and live-action visual effects, and a growing skill set among the artists who use them, scores of scaly beasts are taking over screens big and small: There’s “Maleficent,” which opened Friday, featuring a CGI homage to the dragon from Disney’s 1959 animated classic “Sleeping Beauty”; “How to Train Your Dragon 2” this month, which revisits the Viking fliers of the 2010 original; the current “Godzilla,” starring an honorary dragon if there ever was one; and “Game of Thrones,” whose threesome of dragons will continue to terrorize goats and assorted humans through the season finale on June 15.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01DRAGONS3/25DRAGONS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01DRAGONS3/25DRAGONS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01DRAGONS3/25DRAGONS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01DRAGONS3/25DRAGONS3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 815, 'wid