expands.html', 'snippet': 'A voluntary program in Bay Ridge, Brooklyn, is the latest phase of the city’s plan to convert residents into composters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first week or so, the brown bins hunkered on the streets like alien capsules that had fallen to Earth: gingerly stepped around, uneasily eyed, tenaciously ignored. One was pressed into service as a wastebasket for empty liquor bottles. Another was unceremoniously tossed in a street-corner trash can.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31COMPOST/31COMPOST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31COMPOST/31COMPOST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31COMPOST/31COMPOST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31COMPOST/31COMPOST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31COMPOST/31COMPOST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31COMPOST/31COMPOST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31COMPOST/31COMPOST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City Trying to Help Households Turn Waste Into Compost', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Plan for Less Trash: Turn New Yorkers Into Composters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compost', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanitation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Windsor Terrace (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bay Ridge (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T14:16:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d56b3d1-803b-5d93-9782-1d1807fe4f2c', 'word_count': 1304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d56b3d1-803b-5d93-9782-1d1807fe4f2c'}, {'abstract': 'Glen Duncan’s “By Blood We Live,” the conclusion of a supernatural trilogy, is among the season’s horror books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/books/review/glen-duncans-by-blood-we-live-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Glen Duncan’s “By Blood We Live,” the conclusion of a supernatural trilogy, is among the season’s horror books.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Reading a book is a dangerous thing,” says Remshi, the protagonist of Glen Duncan’s BY BLOOD WE LIVE (Knopf, $25.95), speaking, you might say, the wisdom of the ages: He’s the world’s oldest vampire, 20,000 years young, give or take. “A book,” he goes on to say, “can make you find room in yourself for something you never thought you’d understand. Or worse, something you never wanted to understand.” Although it’s always risky to attribute the thoughts of a fictional character to its creator, it’s a reasonably safe bet that this bloodsucker’s sentiments aren’t far from those of the novelist, who has made a habit of writing books about things most of us would rather not understand too well. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16HORRORSUB/0616HORRORSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16HORRORSUB/0616HORRORSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16HORRORSUB/0616HORRORSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16HORRORSUB/0616HORRORSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 1948, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16HORRORSUB/16HORRORSUB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16HORRORSUB/16HORRORSUB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16HORRORSUB/16HORRORSUB-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Horror', 'kicker': 'Summer Reading', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Horror', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Glen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMahon, Jennifer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Susan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hermanson, Marie', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grey, S L', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hannah, Sophie (1971- )', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T14:27:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terrence Rafferty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rafferty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/80fbd694-6b3b-5fbd-8c7e-bc0dcd5682d2', 'word_count': 2171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80fbd694-6b3b-5fbd-8c7e-bc0dcd5682d2'}, {'abstract': 'Summer’s cookbooks include star vehicles, travelogues and vegetarian manifestoes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/books/review/laura-b-russells-brassicas-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Summer’s cookbooks include star vehicles, travelogues and vegetarian manifestoes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cookbooks come in all sorts. Some offer new twists on old recipes or update a familiar cuisine. Others are lavishly tricked out, with production values worthy of “Masterpiece Theatre.” Still others have the brute functionality of car-repair manuals. There are star-vehicle cookbooks, travelogue cookbooks, definitive magnum-opus cookbooks and “I love America” cookbooks, not to mention quasi-\xadreligious farm-to-table, vegan and vegetarian manifestoes.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16COOKINGSUB/0616COOKINGSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16COOKINGSUB/0616COOKINGSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16COOKINGSUB/0616COOKINGSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16COOKINGSUB/0616COOKINGSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1465, 'width': 1949, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16COOKINGSUB/16COOKINGSUB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16COOKINGSUB/16COOKINGSUB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/16COOKINGSUB/16COOKINGSUB-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooking', 'kicker': 'Summer Reading', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cooking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T14:27:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/adebf075-0f8c-57d4-86c6-e12fd245c970', 'word_count': 2335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adebf075-0f8c-57d4-86c6-e12fd245c970'}, {'abstract': 'Ballmer, the former Microsoft chief, agreed to pay three times what the franchise was recently valued at, but the team’s bottom line should benefit from television deals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/sports/basketball/steven-a-ballmers-2-billion-play-for-clippers-is-a-big-bet-on-the-nba.html', 'snippet': 'Ballmer, the former Microsoft chief, agreed to pay three times what the franchise was recently valued at, but the team’s bottom line should benefit from television deals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Men with vast fortunes who have bought professional teams as toys are not uncommon. Whether they considered the franchises sound investments is almost beside the point.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/sports/31clippers-1/31clippers-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/31/sports/31clippers-1/31c