/06/01/books/review/reading-goals-for-the-dog-days.html', 'snippet': 'People at The Times share their summer reading plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s that time of year for guilty reading, but the leisurely months also offer an opportunity for more ambitious projects. I asked people at The Times if they had any goals for the coming weeks.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01OPENBOOK/0602-bks-OPEN-BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 265, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01OPENBOOK/0602-bks-OPEN-BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 265}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01OPENBOOK/0602-bks-OPEN-BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 1019, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01OPENBOOK/0602-bks-OPEN-BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 1019, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01OPENBOOK/0602-bks-OPEN-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01OPENBOOK/0602-bks-OPEN-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01OPENBOOK/0602-bks-OPEN-BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reading Goals for the Dog Days', 'kicker': 'Open Book', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reading Goals for the Dog Days', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T14:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a48ca9b-8316-5ea2-b1e2-4f0bd033e911', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a48ca9b-8316-5ea2-b1e2-4f0bd033e911'}, {'abstract': 'Bob Mankoff, The New Yorker’s cartoon editor, has written a book of memoir, cartoon history and shoptalk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/books/review/bob-mankoffs-how-about-never-is-never-good-for-you.html', 'snippet': 'Bob Mankoff, The New Yorker’s cartoon editor, has written a book of memoir, cartoon history and shoptalk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bob Mankoff is The New Yorker’s cartoon editor as well as a cartoonist himself. “I may not have the best job in the world, but I’m in the running,” he writes in the introduction to his book “How About Never — Is Never Good for You? My Life in Cartoons,” which is not just a charming memoir but also a charming grab bag of cartoon history, cartoon theory (nothing too woolly) and shoptalk. The title is taken from Mankoff’s best-known drawing. Businessman on phone, consulting datebook: “No, Thursday’s out. How about never — is never good for you?” As its author points out — false modesty is not one of his faults — that line has entered the vernacular, alongside other classics from the magazine such as “I say it’s spinach, and I say the hell with it” (drawing by Carl Rose, caption by E. B. White); “Well, back to the old drawing board” (Peter Arno); and “On the Internet, nobody knows you’re a dog” (Peter Steiner).', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01HANDY/01HANDY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01HANDY/01HANDY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01HANDY/01HANDY-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01HANDY/01HANDY-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1159, 'width': 1650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01HANDY/01HANDY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01HANDY/01HANDY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/books/review/01HANDY/01HANDY-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Comic Relief', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comic Relief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Handy, Bruce', 'rank': 2, 'm