les and Ben Ratliff discuss this year’s inductees and the challenges of creating a rock canon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rock Hall’s Class of 2014, Or: The Revenge of Kiss', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T17:29:01+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/e8d795b1-fb6f-5699-8608-450d38e7e214', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/e8d795b1-fb6f-5699-8608-450d38e7e214'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of building traditional Sun Belt retirement communities, developers seek to lure older people who want to remain active or continue to work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/your-money/rethinking-the-retirement-community.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of building traditional Sun Belt retirement communities, developers seek to lure older people who want to remain active or continue to work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Rikki Selby began shopping for a retirement home, the 66-year-old sought a community where she could make friends with people her own age. But Ms. Selby had no interest in the kind of sprawling Sun Belt development that offers thousands of houses to older people. “In those places, everybody is old, and you don’t see young faces in the supermarket,” said Ms. Selby, who recently retired as a financial planner.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/business/31retiring-pic1/31retiring-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/31/business/31retiring-pic1/31retiring-pic1-articleLarge