rm to another can be successful, Jeffrey Goldfarb of Reuters Breakingviews writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/a-private-equity-perennial-that-may-flourish/', 'snippet': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts’ $1.6 billion acquisition of the landscaping company Brickman Group may show how the sale of a company by one private equity firm to another can be successful, Jeffrey Goldfarb of Reuters Breakingviews writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Henry Kravis, a co-founder of Kohlberg Kravis Roberts, is cultivating private equity perennials. Buyout shops like his are selling companies to each other at a breakneck pace. It’s easy to be skeptical about these so-called secondaries. But K.K.R.’s $1.6 billion acquisition of the landscaping company Brickman Group may turn out to be an example of how such deals can flourish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/business/dbpix-kravis/dbpix-kravis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/31/business/dbpix-kravis/dbpix-kravis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/business/dbpix-kravis/dbpix-kravis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/business/dbpix-kravis/dbpix-kravis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1310, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/business/dbpix-kravis/dbpix-kravis-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/31/business/dbpix-kravis/dbpix-kravis-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/business/dbpix-kravis/dbpix-kravis-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Private Equity Perennial That May Flourish', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Leonard I', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kravis, Henry R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Leonard Green & Partners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ValleyCrest Cos', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T20:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Goldfarb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldfarb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d37a456-4eb5-5756-a697-45bb662a2f4f', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d37a456-4eb5-5756-a697-45bb662a2f4f'}, {'abstract': 'The Swedish duo Klara and Johanna Soderberg, who have a new album due out on June 10, talk about their musical childhood and their affinity for the raw directness of country songs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/arts/music/klara-and-johanna-soderberg-explain-their-affinity-for-folk.html', 'snippet': 'The Swedish duo Klara and Johanna Soderberg, who have a new album due out on June 10, talk about their musical childhood and their affinity for the raw directness of country songs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s just another modern-day discovery story: two Swedish sisters, harmonizing since childhood in perfect twangy English, introduced to the rest of the world via YouTube thanks to their covers of indie ballads and Johnny Cash classics. Klara and Johanna Soderberg were 15 and 17 when that happened, in 2008, and since then, they have toured the globe with their own spare guitar-driven songs, impressing the likes of Jack White (who produced a single for them) and Conor Oberst (who included them on his latest album). The sisters, now 21 and 23, record as First Aid Kit; their third album, “Stay Gold,” a major-label debut that adds the Omaha Symphony Orchestra to their lovelorn country-folk, will be released June 10 on Columbia Records, with a sold-out show on June 11 at Webster Hall.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 758}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 812, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1623, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sisters Strumming in the Darkness', 'kicker': 'Snapshot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sisters Strumming in the Darkness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soderberg, Johanna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soderberg, Klara', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T20:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/82c26de5-6bd6-5a1a-93c3-3c5e5552f006', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82c26de5-6bd6-5a1a-93c3-3c5e5552f006'}, {'abstract': 'Officials say the Azraq camp for Syrian refugees, in a remote, dusty expanse of Jordan, could grow even bigger than the Zaatari camp, which shelters more than 100,000 Syrians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/world/middleeast/new-refugee-camp-in-jordan-absorbs-flood-from-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Officials say the Azraq camp for Syrian refugees, in a remote, dusty expanse of Jordan, could grow even bigger than the Zaatari camp, which shelters more than 100,000 Syrians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AL AZRAQ REFUGEE CAMP, Jordan — His face was bright red from the desert sun, and his son’s eyes, blank with exhaustion, gazed into the distance. Bahjat Sheikh, 58, and his family had crossed the Jordanian border to safety after an arduous two-and-a-half-day journey, mostly on foot, from the central Syrian city of Hama.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/world/31JORDAN/31JORDAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/31/world/31JORDAN/31JORDAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/world/31JORDAN/31JORDAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/world/31JORDAN/31JORDAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1296, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/world/31JORDAN/31JORDAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/31/world/31JORDAN/31JORDAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/world/31JORDAN/31JORDAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name'