 citizens of the Internet, the rise of Brooke Candy, 24, will sound familiar. A former stripper, Candy’s image proliferated through likes and retweets when a 2012 music video she appeared in — Grimes’s “Genesis” — went viral. A sword-wielding Barbarella for the Tumblr generation, Candy, clad in cyberpunk princess body armor and neon pink braids — then her trademark look — postured and snarled with primal confidence. The mysterious Candy then revealed her true self several months later, when she uploaded the video to “Das Me,” an abrasive yet empowering hip-hop churner that introduced her as a brash, talented M.C.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30candy-barna/30candy-barna-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30candy-barna/30candy-barna-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30candy-barna/30candy-barna-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30candy-barna/30candy-barna-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30candy-barna/30candy-barna-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30candy-barna/30candy-barna-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumb