sionally produced to ones that are crowdsourced, using data and updates provided by contributors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/automobiles/mapping-apps-follow-the-crowd.html', 'snippet': 'Telenav, a navigation services company, is switching from maps that are professionally produced to ones that are crowdsourced, using data and updates provided by contributors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Think of it as the hive approach to car navigation systems: One driver, like a worker bee, finds the quickest way from Point A to Point B and then shares that route with all the other drivers. It’s the basic idea behind all crowdsourcing, the sharing of free user-generated content to create information like restaurant ratings and contractor recommendations. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/automobiles/Maps/Maps-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/automobiles/Maps/Maps-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/automobiles/Maps/Maps-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/automobiles/Maps/Maps-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1107, 'width': 1916, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/automobiles/Maps/Maps-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/automobiles/Maps/Maps-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/automobiles/Maps/Maps-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mapping Apps Follow the Crowd', 'kicker': 'Technology', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mapping Apps Follow the Crowd', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdsourcing (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TeleNav, Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T21:46:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John R. Quain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Quain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfe5c2e6-f838-50e4-aabf-04766aebb4a2', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfe5c2e6-f838-50e4-aabf-04766aebb4a2'}, {'abstract': 'The Vakhtangov State Academic Theater’s “Eugene Onegin” at City Center is a play with music and dance, composed of scenes from the Pushkin novel in verse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/theater/eugene-onegin-a-blended-version-at-city-center.html', 'snippet': 'The Vakhtangov State Academic Theater’s “Eugene Onegin” at City Center is a play with music and dance, composed of scenes from the Pushkin novel in verse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regret haunts the memories of men who’ve outgrown their brash younger selves, but oh, what pretty pictures torment makes. A glossy, mirrored wall as dark as anthracite looms over the action in the Vakhtangov State Academic Theater’s arrestingly beautiful “Eugene Onegin,” at City Center, and a cloud of white mist floats above the stage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31EUGENE1/31EUGENE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31EUGENE1/31EUGENE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31EUGENE1/31EUGENE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31EUGENE1/31EUGENE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31EUGENE1/31EUGENE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31EUGENE1/31EUGENE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31EUGENE1/31EUGENE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unappreciated Love, the Russian Variety', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unappreciated Love, the Russian Variety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Center Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Eugene Onegin (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vakhtangov Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuminas, Rimas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pushkin, Aleksandr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T21:57:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Collins-Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins-Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/091badfb-6c7c-515d-aa06-2900dd675700', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/091badfb-6c7c-515d-aa06-2900dd675700'}, {'abstract': 'Several design luminaries, including Tory Burch and Christian Louboutin, spoke at commencement ceremonies recently. T rounds up their words, which are worth listening to no matter your age.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/05/30/rules-of-style-collected-wisdom-from-this-years-crop-of-fashion-industry-graduation-speakers/', 'snippet': 'Several design luminaries, including Tory Burch and Christian Louboutin, spoke at commencement ceremonies recently. T rounds up their words, which are worth listening to no matter your age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s that time of year again, when the world’s most successful people travel around the country to give university commencement speeches. This year, a handful of fashion-industry heavy-hitters joined in the tradition.\xa0From the shoe designer Christian Louboutin’s address to the student body at F.I.T. to the lecture given by Steven Kolb of the C.F.D.A. at Kendall College of Art and Design, the speeches of several design luminaries suggested that slow and steady, more often than not, wins the race. Here, some of their collected words of wisdom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30grads-bobb/30grads-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30grads-bobb/30grads-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30grads-bobb/30grads-bobb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30grads-bobb/30grads-bobb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30grads-bobb/30grads-bobb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30grads-bobb/30grads-bobb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/30/t-magazine/30grads-bobb/30grads-bobb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Collected Wisdom From This Year’s Crop of Fashion-Industry Graduation Speakers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T22:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Bobb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bobb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca7982c3-2f9a-55f6-9a39-9fb14656f508', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca7982c3-2f9a-55f6-9a39-9fb14656f508'}, {'abstract': 'In “Deepest Man,” a play by James Scruggs, a man whose wife drowns confronts his traumas by submerging them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/theater/in-deepest-man-an-immersion-into-a-watery-beyond.html', 'snippet': 'In “Deepest Man,” a play by James Scruggs, a man whose wife drowns confronts his traumas by submerging them.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Twilight Zone” meets media critique meets psychological portraiture in James Scruggs’s “Deepest Man,” a thought-provoking experiment at the 3LD Art & Technology Center. Given that the show comes from 3-Legged Dog — a company known for integrating performance, video and effects — it is unsurprising that the piece, loaded with abstraction and supernatural traces, is a visual marvel. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/arts/deepest/deepest-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/03/arts/deepest/deepest-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 275}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/arts/deepest/deepest-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/arts/deepest/deepest-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 940, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/arts/deepest/deepest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/03/arts/deepest/deepest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/arts/deepest/deepest-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Way Over His Head', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Way Over His Head', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scruggs, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '3LD Art & Technology Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Deepest Man (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '3-Legged Dog', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T22:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab585682-e6a1-5932-9617-a8844a11aea4', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab585682-e6a1-5932-9617-a8844a11aea4'}, {'abstract': 'The view from the many vantage points at Half Moon in Dobbs Ferry is inspiring. But the experience with the food and the service can vary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/nyregion/a-review-of-half-moon-in-dobbs-ferry.html', 'snippet': 'The view from the many vantage points at Half Moon in Dobbs Ferry is inspiring. But the experience with the food and the service can vary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Particularly dramatic and romantic at sunset, the view from the Half Moon restaurant’s many vantage points is inspiring. As one of my dining companions observed, there is something about sunset on water that makes one wax Hallmarky. The promenade deck is so close to the Hudson River that when the wind is up, guests might be refreshed by the spray from a crashing wave. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Prime View of Sunset', 'kicker': 'Dining Review | Westchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Prime View of Sunset', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Half Moon (Dobbs Ferry, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dobbs Ferry (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fort Pond Bay Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-30T22:04:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By M. H. Reed', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/79ebae9d-bf7c-5c1b-bbd2-43a5aed97efa', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79ebae9d-bf7c-5c1b-bbd2-43a5aed97efa'}, {'abstract': 'A move by the British education minister Michael Gove to ensure that students read more British literature comes at the expense of American works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/books/goodbye-steinbeck-all-hail-shelley.html', 'snippet': 'A move by the British education minister Michael Gove to ensure that students read more British literature comes at the expense of American works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — When government shapes a nation’s literary education, politics inevitably plays a role. That has come clear in the case of the influential and controversial British minister of education, Michael Gove, who was accused of jingoism this week for new syllabus requirements that have led to the removal of classic American works like “To Kill a M