i': 'nyt://article/a379b71d-ac02-5257-ab56-44084ddd64d2'}, {'abstract': 'H K Gruber’s opera “Gloria — A Pig Tale” opened at the Metropolitan Museum of Art on Thursday as part of the 11-day NY Phil Biennial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/arts/music/gloria-a-pig-tale-brings-opera-to-the-met-museum.html', 'snippet': 'H K Gruber’s opera “Gloria — A Pig Tale” opened at the Metropolitan Museum of Art on Thursday as part of the 11-day NY Phil Biennial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before conducting the staged production of H K Gruber’s anarchic opera “Gloria — A Pig Tale” that opened at the Metropolitan Museum of Art on Thursday night, the second event of the 11-day NY Phil Biennial, Alan Gilbert told the audience that he had thought a lot about what to say to prepare people for the wild piece they were about to hear. But, he explained, he had decided to say nothing, other than to warn audience members that this opera might not sound like anything else they had ever heard.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31PIGTALE/31PIGTALE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31PIGTALE/31PIGTALE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 508}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31PIGTALE/31PIGTALE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 867, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/arts/31PIGTALE/31PIGTALE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1734, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type