first for Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/world/americas/conviction-in-terrorism-case-in-canada.html', 'snippet': 'A jury on Friday convicted a former security guard from Toronto of attempting to join a foreign terrorist organization, a first for Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A jury on Friday convicted a former security guard from Toronto of attempting to join a foreign terrorist organization, a first for Canada. Prosecutors and the police said that the man, Mohamed Hassan Hersi, a Canadian born in Somalia, was heading to join the Somali extremist group Shabab when he was arrested at Toronto’s airport in 2011. Mr. Hersi, who was holding a one-way ticket to Cairo, has maintained that he was going overseas to study Arabic. Long before his arrest, Mr. Hersi had been the subject of an extensive police investigation after the company that employed Mr. Hersi as a guard found in one of his uniforms a USB memory stick that contained what were described as extremist materials. Mr. Hersi was also convicted of encouraging an undercover police officer to participate in terrorism. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conviction in Terrorism Case in Canada', 'kicker': 'World Briefing ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Conviction in Terrorism Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hersi, Mohamed Hassan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-31T00:19:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname