 for the well-being of its citizens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been more than six weeks since nearly 300 schoolgirls were kidnapped by the Boko Haram extremist group in Nigeria. The militants have spent the last five years wreaking havoc and killing civilians — about 4,000 have died — in the northeastern section of the country. But it took a horrifying mass abduction to touch hearts around the world and persuade Nigeria — whose president, Goodluck Jonathan, initially rejected outside help — to join with other countries to try to find them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dealing With Boko Haram', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dealing With Boko Haram', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jonathan, Goodluck', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-31T01:26:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7cc8230-f5f4-5381-bc0b-961fe88d0140', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7cc8230-f5f4-5381-bc0b-961fe88d0140'}, {'abstract': 'Leslie Ross is swapping her crammed Lower East Side studio, where she has spent years building bassoons and inventing unusual instruments, for a sprawling factory in Maine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/nyregion/bassoon-maker-is-leaving-lower-east-side-for-cheaper-rent-in-maine.html', 'snippet': 'Leslie Ross is swapping her crammed Lower East Side studio, where she has spent years building bassoons and inventing unusual instruments, for a sprawling factory in Maine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are not many places to sit amid the jumble of metal tools, piles of maple and boxwood boards, and bassoons crowding — and even hanging from the ceiling of — Leslie Ross’s studio on the Lower East Side. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31BASSOON1/31BASSOON1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31BASSOON1/31BASSOON1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31BASSOON1/31BASSOON1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31BASSOON1/31BASSOON1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31BASSOON1/31BASSOON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31BASSOON1/31BASSOON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/nyregion/31BASSOON1/31BASSOON1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 