g', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/424ce163-d15f-52ec-9ac0-1f06f797c5de', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/424ce163-d15f-52ec-9ac0-1f06f797c5de'}, {'abstract': 'After a ruling that says states can no longer rely on a fixed I.Q. cutoff to decide intellectual competency, the likelihood increased that some inmates will have a chance to avoid execution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/31/us/on-death-row-with-low-iq-and-new-hope-for-a-reprieve.html', 'snippet': 'After a ruling that says states can no longer rely on a fixed I.Q. cutoff to decide intellectual competency, the likelihood increased that some inmates will have a chance to avoid execution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — For Ted Herring, who has spent 32 years on Florida’s death row for murdering a store clerk, signs of intellectual disability arose early and piled up quickly: He repeated first grade and got D’s and F’s through fourth grade. He read like a fourth grader at 14 and did not know that summer followed spring.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Death Row With Low I.Q., and New Hope for a Reprieve', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Death Row With Low I.Q., and New Hope for a Reprieve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intelligence and Intelligence Tests (IQ)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Lizette', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Retardation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida'