severe economic distress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/opinion/sunday/egypts-latest-military-strongman.html', 'snippet': 'The newly elected president, Abdel Fattah el-Sisi, will have to take bold action to rescue a country in severe economic distress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was never any suspense about who would win Egypt’s presidential election last week. Abdel Fattah el-Sisi, until recently the military chief and controlling force behind the government, always had the upper hand — the army’s loyalty, the subservient media and the lack of real competition after he jailed or intimidated all serious opposition. He got more than 95 percent of the vote.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Latest Military Strongman', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt’s Latest Military Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sisi, Abdel Fattah el-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-31T18:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d9d4934-5d04-5490-905a-3a2325472d5f', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d9d4934-5d04-5490-905a-3a2325472d5f'}, {'abstract': 'Too often, companies hide dangers from regulators by reaching legal settlements that are conditioned on silence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/opinion/sunday/secrecy-that-kills.html', 'snippet': 'Too often, companies hide dangers from regulators by reaching legal settlements that are conditioned on silence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the maddening aspects of the General Motors safety scandal is the company’s maneuvering to conceal vital information about an ignition switch defect from government regulators and the public. The defect is linked to 13 deaths and many serious injuries. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Secrecy That Kills', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Secrecy That Kills', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Lindsey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blumenthal, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defective Products', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liability for Products', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-31T18:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization':