 Gulch that killed 12 colleagues and changed Forest Service practices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late in the afternoon of Aug. 5, 1949, 15 young men working for the United States Forest Service parachuted into a remote area near the Missouri River north of Helena, Mont., on the eastern side of the Rockies, prepared to battle what they thought to be an easily manageable forest fire. They were tragically wrong. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/us/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/31/us/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/us/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/us/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2046, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/us/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/31/us/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit/BULLDOG-Sallee-1-Obit-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/us/BULLDOG-Sallee-1