ple who lived in the scattered villages below. “It was a wall of water and debris,” one survivor remembered. “It looked like it was about 25 or 30 foot high coming running at us. And it was just black-looking. It was just rumbling and roaring and the houses was popping and snapping and they was breaking up.” In the end, 125 people lost their lives and more than 4,000 lost their homes. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Flinching State of Mind', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Our Flinching State of Mind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luhrmann, T M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erikson, Kai T', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Better Angels of Our Nature (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Isla Vista, Calif, Massacre (2014)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Isla Vista (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-05-31T18:37:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By T. M. Luhrmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'T.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecc75884-9b4a-5c36-918e-3804e2026bda', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecc75884-9b4a-5c36-918e-3804e2026bda'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bailey worked at the Moulin Rouge, the first integrated hotel and casino in Las Vegas, and was named the first chairman of the Nevada Equal Rights Commission.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/01/us/bob-bailey-entertainer-who-helped-integrate-las-vegas-dies-at-87.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bailey worked at the Moulin Rouge, the first integrated hotel and casino in Las Vegas, and was named the first chairman of the Nevada Equal Rights Commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bob Bailey, a Las Vegas entertainer, television personality and civil rights activist who helped break down racial barriers for decades, beginning when he arrived in 1955 to serve as an M.C. and singer at the Moulin Rouge, the city’s first integrated hotel and casino, died on May 24 in Las Vegas. He was 87. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/us/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/us/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/us/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/us/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1135, 'width': 818, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/us/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/us/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/us/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit/BULLDOG-Bailey-Obit-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'ma